{"topic": "Stroke", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "A patient presents with symptoms of an ischemic stroke and is not eligible for tPA or mechanical thrombectomy. What is the primary focus of their management?", "options": {"A": "Hemodynamic optimization and neurologic monitoring", "B": "Pharmacotherapy with anticoagulants", "C": "Surgical intervention to restore blood flow", "D": "Physical therapy and rehabilitation"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary focus of management for a patient with ischemic stroke who is not eligible for tPA or mechanical thrombectomy is hemodynamic optimization and neurologic monitoring. This involves admitting the patient to the ICU stroke service for blood pressure management and frequent neurologic checks, with the goal of maximizing cerebral perfusion and preventing further complications.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Surgery_Schwartz_12249", "title": "Surgery_Schwartz", "span_text": "Patients not eligible for tPA or mechanical thrombectomy require hemodynamic optimization and neurologic monitoring. Admit such patients to the ICU stroke service for blood pres-sure management and frequent neurologic checks."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_22127", "InternalMed_Harrison_19619", "Neurology_Adams_12314", "First_Aid_Step2_1046", "pubmed23n0014_10562", "pubmed23n0026_6003", "pubmed23n0022_2751", "Gynecology_Novak_7505", "Surgery_Schwartz_12249", "Obstentrics_Williams_8258", "InternalMed_Harrison_25125", "pubmed23n0027_11294", "InternalMed_Harrison_3884", "pubmed23n0039_410", "Neurology_Adams_6349", "pubmed23n0025_1541", "pubmed23n0007_7129", "Surgery_Schwartz_7972", "InternalMed_Harrison_25535", "InternalMed_Harrison_8606", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5954", "InternalMed_Harrison_25924", "pubmed23n0014_2828", "pubmed23n0011_9856", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1218", "pubmed23n0019_13460", "pubmed23n0022_10689", "Surgery_Schwartz_748", "pubmed23n0004_9746", "pubmed