{"topic": "Stroke", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "A patient with a history of primary thrombocytosis is being considered for long-term management. What can be said about the effectiveness of plateletpheresis in this context?", "options": {"A": "Plateletpheresis can produce acute lowering of elevated platelet counts, but may not be effective for long-term control.", "B": "Plateletpheresis is the first line of therapy for primary thrombocytosis.", "C": "Plateletpheresis is only used in emergency situations.", "D": "Plateletpheresis is not a viable treatment option for primary thrombocytosis."}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's platelet count can be lowered acutely with plateletpheresis, but the rate of platelet production may be too rapid to allow for long-term control by pheresis alone.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0015_9962", "title": "Long-term plateletpheresis in the management of primary thrombocytosis", "span_text": "Although intensive pheresis at the rate of four to five procedures per week produced rapid lowering of the patient's platelet count, continued therapy at the rate of two to three procedures a week failed to maintain these counts, and platelets gradually rose to pretreatment levels."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_1218", "Surgery_Schwartz_748", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5954", "pubmed23n0011_9856", "pubmed23n0019_13460", "First_Aid_Step2_319", "pubmed23n0014_2828", "InternalMed_Harrison_25924", "pubmed23n0022_10689", "InternalMed_Harrison_13636", "pubmed23n0015_9962", "pubmed23n0004_9746", "pubmed23n0013_7566", "pubmed23n0031_4281", "pubmed23n0002_2549", "Surgery_Schwartz_6929", "InternalMed_Harrison_874", "InternalMed_Harrison_19005", "pubmed23n0035_5", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6275", "Surgery_Schwartz_13529", "pubmed23n0034_7849", "Surgery_Schwartz_4220", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3830", "pubmed23n0015_10462", "InternalMed_Harrison_12598", "pubmed23n0022_7464