{"topic": "Maternal Health", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "A 25-year-old pregnant woman at 28 weeks gestation presents with a history of smoking one pack of cigarettes per day. What is the most significant risk to her fetus?", "options": {"A": "Low birth weight", "B": "Preterm birth", "C": "Placenta previa", "D": "Perinatal mortality"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Maternal smoking has been shown to increase the risk of low birth weight, preterm birth, and perinatal mortality. However, the most significant risk to the fetus is low birth weight, as it can lead to a range of health problems.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0031_9913", "title": "Perinatal events associated with maternal smoking during pregnancy", "span_text": "Maternal smoking had the strongest effect on birthweight in the 8 factor regression, and birth less than 2500 gm increased directly with smoking level from 20% to 340% in 37 data subgroups."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0017_3532", "Obstentrics_Williams_5624", "Obstentrics_Williams_6655", "pubmed23n0001_2108", "Obstentrics_Williams_4093", "Obstentrics_Williams_4187", "Obstentrics_Williams_3655", "pubmed23n0031_9913", "Obstentrics_Williams_1", "pubmed23n0036_10089", "pubmed23n0029_3275", "Obstentrics_Williams_8496", "InternalMed_Harrison_10844", "Obstentrics_Williams_3541", "InternalMed_Harrison_4259", "Obstentrics_Williams_6343", "Surgery_Schwartz_5057", "Obstentrics_Williams_6506", "pubmed23n0018_6648", "Surgery_Schwartz_8013", "Pediatrics_Nelson_239", "Obstentrics_Williams_3656", "pubmed23n0024_1190", "Obstentrics_Williams_6743", "pubmed23n0018_1674"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_3655", "pubmed23n0031_9913", "Obstentrics_Williams_1", "pubmed23n0036_10089", "pubmed23n0029_3275", "Obstentrics_Williams_8496", "InternalMed_Harrison_10844", "Obstentrics_Williams_3541", "InternalMed_Harrison_4259", "Obstentrics_Williams_6