{"topic": "Anemia", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 9-year-old girl presents with anemia due to iron deficit, what should be considered in the differential diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "Intestinal tuberculosis", "B": "Crohn's disease", "C": "Sickle cell anemia", "D": "Both A and B"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "The girl's symptoms of anemia due to iron deficit could be indicative of either intestinal tuberculosis or Crohn's disease, and a thorough differential diagnosis is necessary to determine the correct diagnosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0019_7011", "title": "[Intestinal tuberculosis and differential diagnosis against Crohn's disease in children (author's transl)]", "span_text": "The case of a 9-year-old girl treated elsewhere for anemia due to iron deficit is described. The first diagnosis of Crohn's disease made by us and for which the girl received treatment had to be revised, because an intestinal tuberculosis was later accepted to be the correct diagnosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"search_terms": ["anemia", "differential diagnosis", "intestinal tuberculosis", "Crohn's disease"], "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_9331", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1924", "pubmed23n0015_4995", "Surgery_Schwartz_10044", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2154", "pubmed23n0017_11402", "pubmed23n0010_6579", "InternalMed_Harrison_8213", "Pathology_Robbins_2867", "pubmed23n0020_5155", "pubmed23n0019_7011"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_9331", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1924", "pubmed23n0015_4995", "Surgery_Schwartz_10044", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2154", "pubmed23n0017_11402", "pubmed23n0010_6579", "InternalMed_Harrison_8213", "Pathology_Robbins_2867", "pubmed23n0020_5155", "pubmed23n0019_7011"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"verified_by": "expert", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Anemia Dia