{"topic": "Osteoporosis", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "A 55-year-old Caucasian woman with a family history of osteoporosis and a small body frame is considering hormone replacement therapy. What is the primary reason to consider bone mineral density screening for this patient?", "options": {"A": "To monitor the effectiveness of hormone replacement therapy", "B": "To assess her risk of osteoporosis due to her high-risk profile", "C": "To evaluate her response to calcium and vitamin D supplements", "D": "To diagnose other medical conditions associated with osteoporosis"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Bone mineral density screening is recommended for high-risk women, such as those with a family history of osteoporosis, small body frame, and Caucasian or Asian race. This patient's profile puts her at increased risk, making screening essential to inform treatment decisions.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Gynecology_Novak_6497", "title": "Gynecology_Novak", "span_text": "Bone mineral density screening should be considered for high-risk women (Table 34.3). Nonmodifiable risk factors include age, family history, Asian or Caucasian race, history of a prior fracture, small body frame, early menopause, and prior oophorectomy."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "database", "doc_ids": ["Gynecology_Novak_6497"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Gynecology_Novak_6497"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteoporosis Screening screening early detection risk assessment screening test sensitivity specificity guideline population screening high-risk preventive care follow-up diagnostic threshold", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 3148.6511249968316, "llm_ms": 4442.3334170132875, "verification_ms": 808.9448749960866, "extra_instructions": "", "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Gynecology_Novak_6497"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 10.0, "verification": 20.0, "llm": 4442.3334170132875}}}
{"topic": "Osteoporosis", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the primary consideration when determining the effectiveness of a screening test for osteoporosis in a general population?", "options": {"A": "The test's ability to detect the disease at an early stage", "B": "The test's specificity and sensitivity in relation to the disease's prevalence", "C": "The test's cost and availability in relation to the population's socioeconomic status", "D": "The test's ability to predict the disease's progression and mortality"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The effectiveness of a screening test is highly dependent on its specificity and sensitivity, particularly in relation to the disease's prevalence in the population being screened. A test with high specificity and sensitivity is more likely to accurately identify individuals with the disease, while minimizing false positives and false negatives.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_5978", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Specificity is at least as important to the ultimate feasibility and success of a screening test as sensitivity."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0002_11976", "pubmed23n0021_8317", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "InternalMed_Harrison_315", "pubmed23n0037_11153", "pubmed23n0014_5461", "pubmed23n0014_9461", "pubmed23n0024_423", "InternalMed_Harrison_5978", "pubmed23n0019_6075", "InternalMed_Harrison_7533", "pubmed23n0002_12168", "pubmed23n0002_10757", "InternalMed_Harrison_5983", "pubmed23n0024_2387", "pubmed23n0020_10076", "First_Aid_Step2_800", "pubmed23n0010_1929", "pubmed23n0033_9269", "Surgery_Schwartz_2204", "pubmed23n0014_9775", "pubmed23n0035_6904", "InternalMed_Harrison_5976", "InternalMed_Harrison_312", "pubmed23n0028_2115", "pubmed23n0028_12412", "Obstentrics_Williams_1848", "pubmed23n0028_3223", "pubmed23n0020_6341", "Obstentrics_Williams_1980", "pubmed23n0017_9264", "pubmed23n0025_10220", "G