{"topic": "Dehydration", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "A patient is receiving intravenous hyperalimentation and develops hyperosmolar hyperglycemic nonketotic dehydration, what is the primary mechanism by which this condition can be prevented?", "options": {"A": "Providing exogenous insulin sufficient to prevent glucosuria", "B": "Increasing the rate of intravenous fluid administration", "C": "Administering oral hypoglycemic medications", "D": "Restricting carbohydrate intake"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Prevention of osmotic diuresis secondary to glucosuria and, therefore, prevention of hyperosmolar hyperglycemic nonketotic dehydration is achieved by providing exogenous insulin sufficient to prevent glucosuria.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0004_8866", "title": "A review of hypersomolar hyperglycemic nonketotic dehydration (HHND): etiology, pathophysiology and prevention during intravenous hyperalimentation", "span_text": "Prevention of osmotic diuresis secondary to glucosuria and, therefore, prevention of HHND is achieved by providing exogenous insulin sufficient to prevent glucosuria."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0004_8866"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0004_8866"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Dehydration Prevention prevention prophylaxis risk reduction screening vaccination primary prevention secondary prevention lifestyle modification counseling public health early detection follow-up", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 3763.3354169956874, "llm_ms": 1069.3120409850962, "verification_ms": 1089.789167017443, "extra_instructions": "", "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "