{"topic": "Dehydration", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "A community health program aims to reduce the incidence of dehydration among its residents. Which of the following strategies would be most effective in achieving this goal?", "options": {"A": "Providing education on proper hydration and heat exhaustion prevention", "B": "Implementing a vaccination program against dehydration-related illnesses", "C": "Conducting regular screenings for dehydration in the community", "D": "Distributing medication to prevent dehydration"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Education on proper hydration and heat exhaustion prevention is a key component of primary prevention, which aims to prevent disease or injury before it occurs. This approach can help individuals take proactive steps to reduce their risk of dehydration, such as drinking plenty of water, avoiding strenuous activity in hot weather, and recognizing the signs of dehydration.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0022_5545", "title": "Medicine, health and prevention", "span_text": "Education on suhc a general scale is only possible by a constant exchange of information and close collaboration between experts in various health-related fields, politicians, laymen, adults and children."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"search_terms": ["dehydration prevention", "community health program"], "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0023_10307", "pubmed23n0029_7030", "InternalMed_Harrison_21040", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "pubmed23n0014_766", "First_Aid_Step2_800", "InternalMed_Harrison_19033", "pubmed23n0031_8336", "InternalMed_Harrison_294", "pubmed23n0029_7031", "pubmed23n0022_5545", "First_Aid_Step2_237", "pubmed23n0037_11153", "InternalMed_Harrison_10759", "InternalMed_Harrison_25306", "pubmed23n0022_6533", "pubmed23n0024_2414", "pubmed23n0020_3101", "pubmed23n0014_768", "InternalMed_Harrison_322", "Gynecology_Novak_839", "pubmed23n0024_1190", "InternalMed_Harrison_17264", "Gynecology_Novak_728", "p