{"topic": "Pimple", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the main task of a medical officer in preventive medicine at the cantonal level?", "options": {"A": "Early detection of diseases", "B": "Planning of programmes in primary prevention, mainly in the field of health-education", "C": "Support, evaluation and coordination of already existing activities on the field of public health", "D": "Counseling of state and local authorities in questions of preventive medicine"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The main task of a medical officer in preventive medicine at the cantonal level is planning of programmes in primary prevention, mainly in the field of health-education.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0023_10307", "title": "[Task of a cantonal preventive health officer]", "span_text": "In the new health-law of the canton of St.Gall, early detection of diseases will be delegated to physicians in private practice. At the cantonal level, a health officer will thus have the following tasks: 1. Planning of programmes in primary prevention, mainly in the field of health-education, for state or private authorities."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_13659", "pubmed23n0050_7411", "pubmed23n0023_10307", "pubmed23n0014_766", "pubmed23n0029_7030", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "InternalMed_Harrison_19033", "pubmed23n0049_13658", "First_Aid_Step2_237", "InternalMed_Harrison_21040", "pubmed23n0049_3247", "First_Aid_Step2_800", "pubmed23n0037_11153", "pubmed23n0022_5545", "pubmed23n0049_9258", "pubmed23n0031_8336", "pubmed23n0043_4593", "pubmed23n0029_7031", "pubmed23n0020_3101", "InternalMed_Harrison_10759", "pubmed23n0049_3300", "pubmed23n0043_6323", "pubmed23n0048_7714", "InternalMed_Harrison_294", "InternalMed_Harrison_25306", "pubmed23n0049_8703", "pubmed23n0047_5386", "pubmed23n0022_6533", "pubmed23n0050_5486", "pubmed23n0050_7903", "Gynecology_Novak_839", "pubmed23n0023_10306", "pubmed23n0024_