{"topic": "malaria", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A patient returns from a trip to a region where malaria is common, presenting with fever and flu-like symptoms. What is the most reliable and definitive test for diagnosing malaria in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Differential stained thick and thin blood smear", "B": "FAST-ELISA for schistosomal antibodies", "C": "Complete blood count with differential", "D": "Liver function tests"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The differential stained thick and thin blood smear is the most reliable and definitive test for diagnosing malaria, as it allows for the direct visualization of the parasites in the blood.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0060_6118", "title": "Laboratory diagnosis of malaria", "span_text": "Presently the differential stained thick and thin blood smear, examined under the microscope, remains the most reliable and definitive test for diagnosis of malaria."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "pubmed", "query": "malaria diagnosis", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_12697", "InternalMed_Harrison_16947", "pubmed23n0060_6118", "InternalMed_Harrison_9718"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_16947", "pubmed23n0060_6118", "InternalMed_Harrison_9718", "InternalMed_Harrison_12697"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "malaria Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7236.504957982106, "llm_ms": 830.3902079933323, "verification_ms": 1099.7515000053681, "extra_instructions": "", "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_check