{"topic": "Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A patient with a history of chronic bronchitis and emphysema presents with symptoms of airflow obstruction. What is the primary radiologic feature that can be expected in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Lung hyperinflation", "B": "Pulmonary nodules", "C": "Pleural effusion", "D": "Cardiomegaly"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary radiologic feature of COPD is lung hyperinflation, which can be seen on chest radiographs. This is due to the air trapping that occurs as a result of the airflow obstruction.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0029_6485", "title": "Definition, differentiation, and classification of COPD", "span_text": "The radiologic manifestations of COPD are multiple, varied, and in many instances nonspecific. The primary radiologic feature in COPD is lung hyperinflation."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0031_1734", "pubmed23n0054_1438", "pubmed23n0062_11087", "pubmed23n0021_11110", "pubmed23n0029_6485", "pubmed23n0017_4708", "Gynecology_Novak_3379", "pubmed23n0030_1621", "pubmed23n0060_4832", "pubmed23n0044_5060", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1924", "pubmed23n0018_10703", "pubmed23n0051_9435", "pubmed23n0061_8494", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3004", "pubmed23n0044_10139", "Gynecology_Novak_5476", "pubmed23n0029_360", "pubmed23n0043_15626", "pubmed23n0045_2021", "pubmed23n0028_2093", "pubmed23n0058_15056", "InternalMed_Harrison_26020", "pubmed23n0054_9863", "pubmed23n0036_7426", "pubmed23n0049_6708", "pubmed23n0062_11242", "pubmed23n0062_8258", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3292", "InternalMed_Harrison_2580", "pubmed23n0015_4995", "pubmed23n0053_16472", "pubmed23n0016_5876", "pubmed23n0006_1007", "pubmed23n0026_2893", "pubmed23n0012_40", "pubmed23n0024_5709", "pubmed23n0035_5697", "InternalMed_Harrison_19673", "InternalMed_Harrison_19881", "InternalMed_Harrison_23259", "InternalMed_Harrison_31359", "pubmed23n0017_629", 