{"topic": "Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 55-year-old man with a long history of smoking comes to the clinic with complaints of chronic cough and shortness of breath. Which of the following tests would be most useful in confirming the diagnosis of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease?", "options": {"A": "Chest X-ray", "B": "Pulmonary function tests", "C": "Complete blood count", "D": "Electrocardiogram"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Pulmonary function tests, such as spirometry, are essential for diagnosing chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) as they measure lung function, specifically the forced expiratory volume (FEV1) and forced vital capacity (FVC), which are critical for assessing airflow obstruction.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0016_5876", "title": "Pulmonary function tests in a community hospital", "span_text": "Screening spirometric pulmonary function tests were performed in 300 consecutive ambulatory patients in a community hospital. A high incidence of moderate to very severe chronic obstructive lung disease was found, 66% of smokers and 38% of nonsmokers."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2023-02-20T14:30:00Z", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0058_15056", "pubmed23n0028_2093", "pubmed23n0049_6708", "pubmed23n0054_9863", "pubmed23n0062_11242", "InternalMed_Harrison_26020", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3292", "pubmed23n0036_7426", "pubmed23n0015_4995", "pubmed23n0016_5876", "pubmed23n0026_2893", "InternalMed_Harrison_2580", "pubmed23n0012_40", "pubmed23n0006_1007", "pubmed23n0062_8258", "InternalMed_Harrison_19673", "InternalMed_Harrison_19881", "InternalMed_Harrison_31359", "pubmed23n0017_629", "pubmed23n0035_5697", "pubmed23n0053_16472", "pubmed23n0024_5709", "InternalMed_Harrison_23259", "pubmed23n0029_54", "pubmed23n0061_4359", "pubmed23n0027_1630", "InternalMed_Harrison_25595", "pubmed23n0020_1117", "pubmed23n0057_24290", "pubmed23n0062_8891", "pubmed23n0054_13137"