{"topic": "High blood pressure", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the primary goal of therapy in managing high blood pressure?", "options": {"A": "To reduce systolic and diastolic blood pressure by 20 mmHg and 10 mmHg, respectively, every 24 h until blood pressure is normal", "B": "To minimize the use of antihypertensive medication", "C": "To maximize the use of lifestyle modifications", "D": "To reduce blood pressure as quickly as possible"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary goal of therapy in managing high blood pressure is to reduce systolic and diastolic blood pressure by 20 mmHg and 10 mmHg, respectively, every 24 h until blood pressure is normal. This is because uncontrolled high blood pressure can lead to serious complications such as heart disease, stroke, and kidney disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_22127", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "The goal of therapy is to reduce systolic and diastolic blood pressure by 20 mmHg and 10 mmHg, respectively, every 24 h until blood pressure is normal."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_20077", "pubmed23n0058_19509", "InternalMed_Harrison_21652", "pubmed23n0042_12959", "pubmed23n0022_11986", "InternalMed_Harrison_22127", "pubmed23n0042_11206", "pubmed23n0057_2115", "pubmed23n0052_2664", "pubmed23n0058_459", "pubmed23n0061_19780", "pubmed23n0048_4049", "pubmed23n0027_10752", "pubmed23n0039_410", "InternalMed_Harrison_19619", "pubmed23n0027_15242", "pubmed23n0061_1343", "pubmed23n0042_9725", "First_Aid_Step2_319", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1119", "pubmed23n0049_16234", "pubmed23n0019_13460", "pubmed23n0057_2114", "pubmed23n0045_7641", "pubmed23n0062_12872", "pubmed23n0063_2014", "pubmed23n0014_2828", "pubmed23n0049_3166", "InternalMed_Harrison_1268", "pubmed23n0057_21089", "pubmed23n0045_10082", "pubmed23n0013_7566", "pubmed23n0061_19896", "pubmed23n0052_7559", "InternalMed_Harrison_10724", "pubmed2