{"topic": "High blood pressure", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "A patient with refractory hypertension and renal disease is being considered for long-term therapy. Which of the following medications has been shown to be effective in lowering blood pressure in such patients?", "options": {"A": "Minoxidil", "B": "Prazosin", "C": "Zidovudine", "D": "Furosemide"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Minoxidil is an orally effective vasodilator that has been shown to be successful in lowering blood pressure in patients with refractory hypertension and renal disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0034_5054", "title": "Long-term minoxidil therapy in patients with refractory hypertension and renal disease", "span_text": "Minoxidil, an orally effective vasodilator, was successful in lowering blood pressure in 22 patients, followed up for up to 3 yrs, with hypertension refractory to medical management, including both antihypertensive drug combinations and ultrafiltration."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0056_790", "pubmed23n0014_10418", "pubmed23n0039_6486", "pubmed23n0014_500", "pubmed23n0012_5291", "pubmed23n0050_20132", "pubmed23n0014_8318", "pubmed23n0045_6614", "pubmed23n0051_1059", "pubmed23n0056_13656", "pubmed23n0012_4654", "pubmed23n0052_508", "pubmed23n0015_697", "pubmed23n0050_12565", "pubmed23n0034_5054", "pubmed23n0063_7177", "pubmed23n0060_9697", "pubmed23n0045_13186", "pubmed23n0037_592", "pubmed23n0022_2866", "pubmed23n0046_20928", "pubmed23n0049_8519"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0045_6614", "pubmed23n0051_1059", "pubmed23n0056_13656", "pubmed23n0012_4654", "pubmed23n0052_508", "pubmed23n0015_697", "pubmed23n0050_12565", "pubmed23n0034_5054", "pubmed23n0063_7177", "pubmed23n0060_9697", "pubmed23n0045_13186", "pubmed23n0037_592", "pubmed23n0022_2866", "pubmed23n0056_790", "pubmed23n0014_10418", "pubmed23n0039_6486", "pubmed23n0014_500", "pubmed23n0012_5291", "pubmed23n0050_20132", "p