{"topic": "High blood pressure", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the primary role of beta blocking drugs such as propranolol in the treatment of high blood pressure according to a proposed system?", "options": {"A": "To increase blood pressure in patients with low renin levels", "B": "To diminish or normalize blood pressure in many patients with high and normal renin levels", "C": "To treat patients with congestive heart failure, bradycardia, or a history of asthma", "D": "To provide symptomatic relief for patients with atopic dermatitis"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The proposed system for treating high blood pressure suggests that beta blocking drugs such as propranolol play a primary role in diminishing or normalizing blood pressure in many patients with high and normal renin levels.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0001_5479", "title": "Modern system for treating high blood pressure based on renin profiling and vasoconstriction-volume analysis: a primary role for beta blocking drugs such as propranolol", "span_text": "In the new system, all patients, except the elderly and those with congestive heart failure, bradycardia or a history of asthma, are treated first with propranolol alone, a procedure which will diminish or normalize blood pressure in many patients with high and noraml renin levels."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_17944", "pubmed23n0047_9561", "pubmed23n0001_5479", "pubmed23n0062_14665", "pubmed23n0011_12972", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5731", "InternalMed_Harrison_22444", "InternalMed_Harrison_18596", "pubmed23n0017_5640"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0001_5479", "pubmed23n0062_14665", "pubmed23n0011_12972", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5731", "InternalMed_Harrison_22444", "InternalMed_Harrison_18596", "pubmed23n0017_5640", "pubmed23n0054_17944", "pubmed23n0047_9561"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "ga