{"topic": "Sepsis", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A neonate with jaundice is being treated for sepsis with sulfonamide antibiotics. What is a potential risk of using this medication in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Kernicterus due to displacement of bilirubin from albumin", "B": "Respiratory depression due to increased free drug concentration", "C": "Cardiac arrhythmias due to altered drug metabolism", "D": "Nephrotoxicity due to increased drug excretion"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Sulfonamide antibiotics can displace bilirubin from albumin, leading to increased levels of free bilirubin, which can cross the blood-brain barrier and cause kernicterus, particularly in neonates with jaundice.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_6588", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "This was in fact observed when sulfonamide antibiotics were given to preterm neonates as prophylaxis against sepsis. Conversely, as the serum bilirubin rises for physiologic reasons or because of a blood group incompatibility, bilirubin can displace a drug from albumin and substantially raise the free drug concentration."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"search_terms": "sepsis, pharmacology, neonate, jaundice", "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_6588"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_6588"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"expert_review": "yes", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Sepsis Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 4882.96033302322, "llm_ms": 948.3064169762656, "verification_ms": 743.2447079918347, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"at