{"topic": "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the primary treatment modality for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease related to extensive cigarette smoking?", "options": {"A": "Smoking cessation, inhaled anticholinergic therapy, and oxygen supplementation", "B": "Beta agonists, mucolytics, and antibiotics", "C": "Steroids and theophylline", "D": "Cromolyn and cromolyn sodium"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease related to extensive cigarette smoking is a leading cause of morbidity and mortality among patients age 55 and older. The primary treatment modalities include smoking cessation, inhaled anticholinergic therapy, and oxygen supplementation.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0048_9447", "title": "COPD: primary care management with drug and oxygen therapies.", "span_text": "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease related in most cases to extensive cigarette smoking is a leading cause of morbidity and mortality among patients age 55 and older. Smoking cessation, inhaled anticholinergic therapy, and oxygen supplementation (when indicated) are primary treatment modalities."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_2200", "First_Aid_Step2_1063", "pubmed23n0048_9447", "pubmed23n0059_20077", "pubmed23n0014_2698", "Gynecology_Novak_3795", "pubmed23n0061_12104", "pubmed23n0060_3302", "Gynecology_Novak_3798", "pubmed23n0061_8767", "pubmed23n0058_459", "pubmed23n0045_10934", "pubmed23n0045_1660", "pubmed23n0060_3301", "pubmed23n0060_13879", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3094", "InternalMed_Harrison_25237", "pubmed23n0001_10283", "pubmed23n0057_15176", "pubmed23n0022_2751", "pubmed23n0027_11294", "pubmed23n0055_17212", "pubmed23n0057_17794", "pubmed23n0045_6108", "pubmed23n0054_7490", "InternalMed_Harrison_23161", "pubmed23n0013_7751", "pubmed23n0056_7311", "pubmed23n0046_2320", "pubmed23n0027_4029", "pubmed23n0026_1356", "pub