{"topic": "Peptic ulcer disease", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the primary benefit of using Helicobacter pylori serology as a screening strategy for peptic ulcer disease in patients with dyspepsia?", "options": {"A": "Reduced endoscopy workload", "B": "Increased sensitivity for detection of peptic ulcer", "C": "Improved patient outcomes", "D": "Decreased cost of treatment"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary benefit of using Helicobacter pylori serology as a screening strategy for peptic ulcer disease in patients with dyspepsia is the reduction of endoscopy workload, as it can help identify patients who are less likely to have peptic ulcer disease and therefore do not require endoscopy.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0056_1912", "title": "Screening dyspepsia by serology to Helicobacter pylori", "span_text": "Overall, the screening strategy would have reduced endoscopy workload by 23.3% (95% confidence interval 20.9-25.8%) and would have had a sensitivity for detection of peptic ulcer of 97.4% (94.5-99.1%)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0056_1912", "pubmed23n0057_6081", "pubmed23n0063_20496", "pubmed23n0044_24565", "pubmed23n0059_1765", "InternalMed_Harrison_315", "pubmed23n0021_8317", "InternalMed_Harrison_5976", "InternalMed_Harrison_5978", "pubmed23n0058_3064", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "pubmed23n0053_11610", "pubmed23n0028_12412", "pubmed23n0045_19421", "pubmed23n0002_12168", "pubmed23n0033_9269", "pubmed23n0041_8966", "pubmed23n0053_19927", "InternalMed_Harrison_5983", "pubmed23n0053_5136", "InternalMed_Harrison_308", "InternalMed_Harrison_294", "pubmed23n0055_19783", "pubmed23n0028_2115", "pubmed23n0047_4508", "pubmed23n0062_19189", "pubmed23n0018_7002", "pubmed23n0044_11098", "InternalMed_Harrison_6708", "Gynecology_Novak_713", "pubmed23n0059_18931", "pubmed23n0058_693", "pubmed23n0059_13871", "pubmed23n0051_12721", "pubmed23n0043_3127", "InternalMed_Harris