{"topic": "Influenza", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is a key characteristic of influenza viruses that contributes to their ability to cause yearly epidemics?", "options": {"A": "They have a stable antigenic character", "B": "They change antigenic character at irregular intervals", "C": "They only infect individuals of a specific age group", "D": "They do not produce constitutional symptoms"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Influenza viruses have the ability to change their antigenic character, which allows them to evade the host's immune system and cause yearly epidemics.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0062_5865", "title": "Pathogenesis of respiratory infections due to influenza virus: implications for developing countries", "span_text": "The influenza viruses have an important and distinctive place among respiratory viruses: they change antigenic character at irregular intervals, infect individuals of all ages, cause illnesses characterized by constitutional symptoms and tracheobronchitis, produce yearly epidemics associated frequently with excess morbidity and mortality, and predispose the host to bacterial superinfections."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_21345", "pubmed23n0062_5865"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_21345", "pubmed23n0062_5865"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Influenza Etiology etiology cause risk factors pathogenesis mechanism underlying cause genetic factors environmental factors predisposing factors associated conditions epidemiology incidence", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6023.209708975628, "llm_ms": 809.3306659720838, "verification_ms": 749.3990000220947, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rera