{"topic": "Hypothyroidism", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "A 35-year-old woman presents with symptoms of hearing loss, and laboratory tests reveal she has hypothyroidism. What is the most likely cause of her hearing loss?", "options": {"A": "Conductive hearing loss due to middle ear changes", "B": "Sensorineural hearing loss due to cochlear damage", "C": "Mixed hearing loss due to both middle and inner ear abnormalities", "D": "Hearing loss is not related to hypothyroidism"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The patient's hearing loss is most likely due to sensorineural hearing loss caused by cochlear damage, as hypothyroidism can affect the cochlea and cause inner ear abnormalities.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0017_945", "title": "Hypothyroidism and the ear: electrophysiological, morphological, and chemical considerations", "span_text": "The morphological, biochemical, and electrophysiological findings in this study support the hypothesis that the cochlea is a site of lesion for sensorineural hearing loss in hypothyroidism."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_6132", "pubmed23n0046_16572", "InternalMed_Harrison_21109", "pubmed23n0020_3791", "pubmed23n0023_8630", "pubmed23n0060_9051", "pubmed23n0017_945", "pubmed23n0024_3235"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0046_16572", "InternalMed_Harrison_21109", "pubmed23n0020_3791", "pubmed23n0023_8630", "pubmed23n0060_9051", "pubmed23n0017_945", "pubmed23n0024_3235", "pubmed23n0049_6132"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hypothyroidism Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retri