{"topic": "Colorectal cancer", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is the recommended age to start fecal occult blood testing for colorectal cancer screening in average-risk adults?", "options": {"A": "40 years", "B": "50 years", "C": "60 years", "D": "70 years"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Fecal occult blood testing is recommended only for colorectal cancer screening and may be used beginning at age 50 in average-risk adults.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_3221", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Fecal occult blood testing is recommended only for colorectal cancer screening and may be used beginning at age 50 in average-risk adults and beginning at age 40 in adults with a first-degree relative with colorectal neoplasm at \u226560 years or two second-degree relatives with colorectal cancer."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "textbook", "id": "InternalMed_Harrison_3221", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_20199", "pubmed23n0054_1438", "pubmed23n0018_4903", "pubmed23n0036_7308", "pubmed23n0055_4142", "InternalMed_Harrison_28583", "Gynecology_Novak_3379", "pubmed23n0036_8039", "pubmed23n0041_8955", "InternalMed_Harrison_3221", "pubmed23n0057_24720", "pubmed23n0014_13380", "pubmed23n0060_6543", "pubmed23n0025_5999", "pubmed23n0063_11624", "pubmed23n0052_15320", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "pubmed23n0014_9733", "pubmed23n0010_8494", "pubmed23n0056_17878", "pubmed23n0017_5390", "Surgery_Schwartz_11662", "pubmed23n0016_5680", "InternalMed_Harrison_4503", "pubmed23n0011_2498", "pubmed23n0051_4306", "pubmed23n0020_4315", "pubmed23n0046_13933", "pubmed23n0006_663", "pubmed23n0057_9730", "pubmed23n0049_12473", "pubmed23n0048_5291"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_20199", "pubmed23n0054_1438", "pubmed23n0018_4903", "pubmed23n0036_7308", "pubmed23n0055_4142", "InternalMed_Harrison_28583", "Gynecology_Novak_3379", "pubmed23n0036_8039", "pubmed23n0041_8955", "InternalMed_Harrison_3221", "pubmed23n0057_2