{"topic": "Acne", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the first-line endocrine treatment for hirsutism and acne in women?", "options": {"A": "Combination estrogen-progestin therapy", "B": "Retinoic acid therapy", "C": "Tetracycline regimen", "D": "Keratolytic therapy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Combination estrogen-progestin therapy is usually the first-line endocrine treatment for hirsutism and acne, after cosmetic and dermatologic management.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_3884", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Combination estrogen-progestin therapy in the form of an oral contraceptive is usually the first-line endocrine treatment for hirsutism and acne, after cosmetic and dermatologic management."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 10, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_3884", "pubmed23n0005_8457", "pubmed23n0005_6210", "pubmed23n0006_244", "pubmed23n0061_4401", "pubmed23n0061_6834", "First_Aid_Step2_1008"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_3884", "pubmed23n0005_8457", "pubmed23n0005_6210", "pubmed23n0006_244", "pubmed23n0061_4401", "pubmed23n0061_6834", "First_Aid_Step2_1008"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 5, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Acne Treatment treatment therapy management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7140.219875029288, "llm_ms": 886.2374580348842, "verification_ms": 811.0763750155456, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": [