{"topic": "Atrial fibrillation", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is a recommended screening examination for WPW syndrome, particularly in active sportsmen and junior subjects?", "options": {"A": "Transoesophageal stimulation of the atria combined with bicycle ergometry", "B": "Electrocardiogram", "C": "Echocardiogram", "D": "Holter monitoring"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Transoesophageal stimulation of the atria combined with bicycle ergometry provides a satisfactory reproducibility of basic electrophysiological parameters and is recommended as a screening examination in WPW syndrome, especially in active sportsmen and junior subjects.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0053_8658", "title": "Esophageal stimulation in WPW syndrome", "span_text": "Due to the good sensitivity and low specificity this test can be recommended in WPW syndrome as a screening examination in particular in active sportsmen and junior subjects."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_8658"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_8658"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Atrial fibrillation Screening screening early detection risk assessment screening test sensitivity specificity guideline population screening high-risk preventive care follow-up diagnostic threshold", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6075.661666982342, "llm_ms": 903.0628339969553, "verification_ms": 705.9672500472516, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0053_8658"], "evi