{"topic": "Osteoarthritis", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the primary challenge in defining and classifying early osteoarthritis in both clinical and epidemiological settings?", "options": {"A": "Lack of radiographic evidence", "B": "Limited data on reproducibility of clinical methods", "C": "Insufficient patient population for studies", "D": "Inadequate understanding of the disease's progression"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The definition and classification of early clinically apparent osteoarthritis remains a problem due to limited data on the between-observer reproducibility of simple clinical methods of detecting hand and knee osteoarthritis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0062_16813", "title": "Clinical signs of early osteoarthritis: reproducibility and relation to x ray changes in 541 women in the general population", "span_text": "The definition and classification of early clinically apparent osteoarthritis both in clinical situations and in epidemiological surveys remains a problem. Few data exist on the between-observer reproducibility of simple clinical methods of detecting hand and knee osteoarthritis in the population and their sensitivity and specificity as compared with radiography."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_16813"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_16813"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteoarthritis Screening screening early detection risk assessment screening test sensitivity specificity guideline population screening high-risk preventive care follow-up diagnostic threshold", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 5101.915542036295, "llm_ms": 842.9463329957798, "verification_ms": 887.7847500261851, "extra_instructi