{"topic": "Pregnancy", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the preferred disease-modifying antirheumatic drug for treating rheumatic diseases in non-pregnant patients, but is contraindicated in pregnancy?", "options": {"A": "Methotrexate", "B": "Aspirin", "C": "NSAIDs", "D": "COX-2 inhibitors"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Methotrexate is the preferred disease-modifying antirheumatic drug, but it is contraindicated in pregnancy due to its potential harmful effects on the fetus.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Obstentrics_Williams_8258", "title": "Obstentrics_Williams", "span_text": "According to Shah and St. Clair (2015), methotrexate has become the preferred disease-modiying antirheumatic drug (DMARD)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_8258", "Obstentrics_Williams_8126", "pubmed23n0061_4958", "pubmed23n0011_7474", "Gynecology_Novak_3308", "pubmed23n0058_11572", "pubmed23n0044_2037", "pubmed23n0047_2992", "pubmed23n0060_15744", "pubmed23n0051_6710", "Obstentrics_Williams_6870", "Gynecology_Novak_3218", "Gynecology_Novak_5980", "pubmed23n0050_1508", "Gynecology_Novak_3217", "InternalMed_Harrison_7897", "Obstentrics_Williams_2587", "pubmed23n0046_11610", "pubmed23n0029_6825", "pubmed23n0037_6367", "pubmed23n0048_2187"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_8258", "Obstentrics_Williams_8126", "pubmed23n0061_4958", "pubmed23n0011_7474", "Gynecology_Novak_3308", "pubmed23n0058_11572", "pubmed23n0044_2037", "pubmed23n0047_2992", "pubmed23n0060_15744", "pubmed23n0051_6710", "Obstentrics_Williams_6870", "Gynecology_Novak_3218", "Gynecology_Novak_5980", "pubmed23n0050_1508", "Gynecology_Novak_3217", "InternalMed_Harrison_7897", "Obstentrics_Williams_2587", "pubmed23n0046_11610", "pubmed23n0029_6825", "pubmed23n0037_6367"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reas