{"topic": "Immunization", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What are the key diagnostic criteria for Guillain-Barr\u00e9 syndrome?", "options": {"A": "Absence of identified alternative diagnosis and monophasic illness pattern", "B": "Presence of limb weakness and abnormal nerve conduction studies", "C": "Interval between onset and nadir of weakness between 1-7 days", "D": "Polyphasic illness pattern and subsequent clinical deterioration"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The diagnostic criteria for Guillain-Barr\u00e9 syndrome include the absence of identified alternative diagnosis, monophasic illness pattern, and interval between onset and nadir of weakness between 12 h and 28 days.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_31262", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Absence of identified alternative diagnosis Level 3 of diagnostic certainty Absence of limb weakness Monophasic illness pattern and interval between onset and nadir of weakness between 12 h and 28 days and subsequent clinical plateau"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database query", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_31262"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_31262"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Immunization Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 5039.933542022482, "llm_ms": 865.4840000090189, "verification_ms": 1173.546957958024, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "