{"topic": "Schizophrenia", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary neurotransmitter system implicated in the pathogenesis of schizophrenia?", "options": {"A": "Dopaminergic", "B": "Serotonergic", "C": "GABAergic", "D": "Glutamatergic"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The dopaminergic system has been consistently implicated in the pathogenesis of schizophrenia, with dopamine-blocking drugs leading to an improvement in symptom control.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0053_3695", "title": "Schizophrenia and neurodevelopment", "span_text": "The use of dopamine-blocking drugs has led to an improvement in symptom control, and diminished the need for prolonged hospital stays."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_3695", "pubmed23n0006_6522", "pubmed23n0025_1481", "pubmed23n0055_1707", "pubmed23n0058_9757", "pubmed23n0056_4937", "pubmed23n0055_9470", "pubmed23n0002_5127", "pubmed23n0045_7842", "Neurology_Adams_12295", "pubmed23n0043_15362", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2177", "pubmed23n0049_20125", "pubmed23n0045_3573", "pubmed23n0063_21076", "pubmed23n0048_3373", "pubmed23n0002_6086", "pubmed23n0052_6839", "pubmed23n0052_9857", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3104", "pubmed23n0044_13461", "pubmed23n0053_19240", "pubmed23n0008_631", "pubmed23n0024_5294", "pubmed23n0002_6536"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_3695", "pubmed23n0006_6522", "pubmed23n0025_1481", "pubmed23n0055_1707", "pubmed23n0058_9757", "pubmed23n0056_4937", "pubmed23n0055_9470", "pubmed23n0002_5127", "pubmed23n0045_7842", "Neurology_Adams_12295", "pubmed23n0043_15362", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2177", "pubmed23n0049_20125", "pubmed23n0045_3573", "pubmed23n0063_21076", "pubmed23n0048_3373", "pubmed23n0002_6086", "pubmed23n0052_6839", "pubmed23n0052_9857", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3104"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"atte