{"topic": "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the most important factor in predicting survival for patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease?", "options": {"A": "Age of the patient", "B": "Percent predicted forced expiratory volume in 1 sec after administration of bronchodilator", "C": "Presence of cor pulmonale", "D": "History of congestive heart failure"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The percent predicted forced expiratory volume in 1 sec after administration of bronchodilator is the best indicator of prognosis for patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0015_10735", "title": "Predictors of mortality in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. A 15-year follow-up study.", "span_text": "After controlling for age, the per cent predicted forced expiratory volume in 1 sec after administration of bronchodilator was the best indicator of prognosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_17698", "pubmed23n0015_10735", "pubmed23n0052_19707", "pubmed23n0038_728", "InternalMed_Harrison_32", "pubmed23n0048_18301", "InternalMed_Harrison_20366", "pubmed23n0060_1027", "Obstentrics_Williams_7330", "pubmed23n0057_21938", "pubmed23n0017_11173", "pubmed23n0015_6226", "pubmed23n0053_10585", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3447", "pubmed23n0050_20923", "pubmed23n0057_22094", "pubmed23n0022_11030", "Surgery_Schwartz_9248", "pubmed23n0049_1918", "pubmed23n0058_1190", "pubmed23n0050_2620", "pubmed23n0057_21171", "pubmed23n0026_5364", "InternalMed_Harrison_25426", "pubmed23n0050_14509", "pubmed23n0061_3896", "pubmed23n0049_12951", "Obstentrics_Williams_2355", "pubmed23n0054_7544", "pubmed23n0062_12627", "pubmed23n0061_9530", "pubmed23n0003_12412", "pubmed23n0021_6096", "InternalMed_Harrison_25429", "pubmed23n0053_7061", "pubmed23n0016_13225", "InternalMed_Harrison_8603", "pubmed23n0051_10905", "pubmed23n0053_11668", "pubmed23n