{"topic": "Anxiety disorder", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is a common characteristic of the course of anxiety disorders?", "options": {"A": "They frequently begin between age 20-30 and can be triggered by life events", "B": "They typically resolve on their own without treatment", "C": "They are only complicated by depression in older adults", "D": "They are not associated with residual symptoms or mild impairment in social roles"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Anxiety disorders frequently begin between age 20-30 and can be triggered by life events, and the course is often characterized by a certain chronicity that manifests itself in residual symptoms and mild impairment in social roles even after many years.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0059_9396", "title": "The natural history of anxiety disorders", "span_text": "Anxiety disorders frequently begin between age 20-30 and can be triggered by life events. The course is often characterized by a certain chronicity that manifests itself in residual symptoms and mild impairment in social roles even after many years and is frequently complicated with depression."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0051_10905", "pubmed23n0029_12037", "pubmed23n0047_9563", "pubmed23n0059_5492", "pubmed23n0053_6834", "pubmed23n0044_402", "InternalMed_Harrison_12160", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3447", "pubmed23n0044_24354", "pubmed23n0059_9396", "Obstentrics_Williams_8496", "pubmed23n0031_4728", "pubmed23n0051_18118", "pubmed23n0047_20879", "pubmed23n0051_21851", "pubmed23n0042_15111", "Obstentrics_Williams_8540", "pubmed23n0024_6118", "pubmed23n0063_9128", "pubmed23n0054_21135", "pubmed23n0001_10085"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0051_10905", "pubmed23n0029_12037", "pubmed23n0047_9563", "pubmed23n0059_5492", "pubmed23n0053_6834", "pubmed23n0044_402", "InternalMed_Harrison_12160", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3447", "pubmed23n0044_24354", "pubmed23n0059_9396", "Obstentric