{"topic": "Schizophrenia", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is a common adverse effect of clozapine, an atypical neuroleptic agent used in the treatment of refractory schizophrenia?", "options": {"A": "Agranulocytosis", "B": "Acute dystonia", "C": "Parkinsonian symptoms", "D": "Tardive dyskinesia"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Clozapine is known to cause a number of adverse effects, including agranulocytosis, which is a potentially life-threatening decrease in white blood cells.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0047_13941", "title": "Clozapine in the treatment of refractory schizophrenia: Canadian policies and clinical guidelines.", "span_text": "Although it causes few extra-pyramidal symptoms, the drug has a number of other adverse effects including a risk of agranulocytosis in one to two percent of all patients."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 10, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_3223", "pubmed23n0047_13941", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3221", "pubmed23n0056_6604"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_3223", "pubmed23n0047_13941", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3221", "pubmed23n0056_6604"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 5, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Schizophrenia Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 4880.344917008188, "llm_ms": 1067.2750000376254, "verification_ms": 881.7669579875655, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["P