{"topic": "Hepatitis C", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism by which hepatitis C virus causes liver damage?", "options": {"A": "Direct cytopathic effect of the virus on hepatocytes", "B": "Immune-mediated response to infected cells", "C": "Oxidative stress and lipid peroxidation", "D": "Genetic mutation and oncogenesis"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The pathogenesis of hepatitis C is complex and involves both direct and indirect mechanisms. However, the immune-mediated response to infected cells is thought to play a key role in the development of liver damage and disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0003_9861", "title": "Cellular and humoral immunity in viral hepatitis", "span_text": "Cellular and humoral immunity combine to determine the outcome following exposure to hepatitis virus and are implicated in the proposed pathogenetic mechanism for acute and chronic hepatitis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Physiology_Levy_2885", "pubmed23n0027_160", "pubmed23n0049_15263", "pubmed23n0044_8510", "Pathology_Robbins_3866", "pubmed23n0003_9861", "pubmed23n0058_17560", "pubmed23n0002_8762", "pubmed23n0037_2179", "pubmed23n0041_3305", "pubmed23n0046_10502", "pubmed23n0060_11259", "pubmed23n0044_11637", "pubmed23n0053_10281"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Physiology_Levy_2885", "pubmed23n0027_160", "pubmed23n0049_15263", "pubmed23n0044_8510", "Pathology_Robbins_3866", "pubmed23n0003_9861", "pubmed23n0058_17560", "pubmed23n0002_8762", "pubmed23n0037_2179", "pubmed23n0041_3305", "pubmed23n0046_10502", "pubmed23n0060_11259", "pubmed23n0044_11637", "pubmed23n0053_10281"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hepatitis C Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodyn