{"topic": "Acute kidney injury", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a potential consequence of acute kidney injury in patients, according to large epidemiologic studies?", "options": {"A": "Adverse short- and long-term outcomes, including onset or progression of CKD", "B": "Only mild forms of acute kidney injury are associated with adverse outcomes", "C": "Acute kidney injury has no association with chronic inflammation or vascular rarefaction", "D": "Recurrent specific tubular injury leads to a pattern very typical of acute kidney disease in humans"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Large epidemiologic studies have shown that even mild forms of acute kidney injury are associated with adverse short- and long-term outcomes, including onset or progression of CKD and more rapid progression to end-stage kidney disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_21487", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "It has become increasingly recognized as a result of large epidemiologic studies that even mild forms of acute kidney injury are associated with adverse shortand long-term outcomes including onset or progression of CKD and more rapid progression to end-stage kidney disease."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_17698", "pubmed23n0061_16963", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1934", "Pathology_Robbins_1082", "pubmed23n0047_5691", "pubmed23n0048_7202", "InternalMed_Harrison_21641", "pubmed23n0052_9476", "pubmed23n0030_8211", "pubmed23n0028_9430", "InternalMed_Harrison_21487", "pubmed23n0016_1630", "pubmed23n0063_622", "pubmed23n0047_7719", "InternalMed_Harrison_8755", "InternalMed_Harrison_21649", "pubmed23n0062_3110", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6415", "Surgery_Schwartz_13389", "pubmed23n0062_6784", "pubmed23n0047_9618", "pubmed23n0049_19365", "pubmed23n0012_7416", "pubmed23n0051_11328", "pubmed23n0014_6129", "pubmed23n0030_11307", "pubmed23n0058_12689", "pubmed23n0047_3304", "Obstentrics_Willi