{"topic": "Allergic rhinitis", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the most accurate method for diagnosing allergic rhinitis, especially in terms of identifying the specific allergen responsible?", "options": {"A": "Nasal provocation test", "B": "Skin prick test", "C": "Radioallergosorbent test (RAST)", "D": "Total IgE measurement"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The nasal provocation test is considered the most accurate method for diagnosing allergic rhinitis, especially in terms of identifying the specific allergen responsible, as it is performed directly on the shock organ and gives the most accurate picture of clinically dominant allergens and the intensity and character of the rhinitis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0022_9210", "title": "Series on clinical testing. 1. The diagnostic usefulness of specific IgE antibody measurements", "span_text": "In vitro measurements of specific IgE antibodies are useful in the evaluation of patients with diseases characterized by clinical signs of immediate hypersensitivity."}, {"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0010_3899", "title": "Diagnostic procedures in chronic rhinitis", "span_text": "Among the procedures which aim at detecting specific allergens, i.e. skin testing, RAST, and nasal provocation tests, the last mentioned, as they are performed directly on the shock organ, have so far been found to give the most accurate picture of clinically dominant allergens and of the intensity and character of the rhinitis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0046_22758", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1753", "pubmed23n0011_9360", "pubmed23n0043_5967", "pubmed23n0022_2139", "pubmed23n0034_3594", "pubmed23n0050_11428", "pubmed23n0022_9210", "pubmed23n0010_3899", "pubmed23n0055_21505", "InternalMed_Harrison_24976", "pubmed23n0053_9427", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2245", "pubmed23n0005_9497", "pubmed23n0054_17200", "pubmed23n0059_16726", "p