{"topic": "Postpartum hemorrhage", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is a potential cause of postpartum hemorrhage?", "options": {"A": "Placental abruption", "B": "Uterine dysfunction during labor", "C": "Postpartum atony", "D": "All of the above"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "Postpartum hemorrhage can be caused by several factors, including placental abruption, uterine dysfunction during labor, and postpartum atony.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Obstentrics_Williams_1482", "title": "Obstentrics_Williams", "span_text": "Maternal complications associated with hydramnios include placental abruption, uterine dysfunction during labor, and postpartum hemorrhage. Placental abruption is fortunately infrequent. It may result from the rapid decompression of an overdistended uterus that follows fetal-membrane rupture or therapeutic amnioreduction. With prematurely ruptured membranes, a placental abruption occasionally occurs days or weeks after amniorrhexis. Uterine dysfunction consequent to overdistention may lead to postpartum atony and, in turn, postpartum hemorrhage."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "textbook", "id": "Obstentrics_Williams_1482", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_6812", "pubmed23n0055_23642", "pubmed23n0011_9091", "Surgery_Schwartz_923", "Obstentrics_Williams_5148", "pubmed23n0053_619", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3259", "Pathology_Robbins_691", "Obstentrics_Williams_1482", "pubmed23n0036_962", "pubmed23n0063_1598", "pubmed23n0063_5766", "pubmed23n0033_2386", "pubmed23n0051_7411", "pubmed23n0026_275", "pubmed23n0033_3272", "pubmed23n0035_1003", "pubmed23n0011_1543", "pubmed23n0016_5345", "pubmed23n0033_10796", "pubmed23n0011_8284", "pubmed23n0013_10808"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_6812", "pubmed23n0055_23642", "pubmed23n0011_9091", "Surgery_Schwartz_923", "Obstentrics_Williams_5148", "pubmed23n0053_619", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3259", "Pathology_Robbins_691", "Obstentrics_Williams_1482", "pubmed23n0036_