{"topic": "HIV", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 29-year-old heterosexual female presents with symptoms and signs similar to those indicating infectious mononucleosis and influenza. What is the most likely diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "Primary HIV infection", "B": "Infectious mononucleosis", "C": "Influenza", "D": "Tuberculosis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms and signs are similar to those of infectious mononucleosis and influenza, but the diagnosis turned out to be a primary HIV infection. This emphasizes the importance of considering HIV infection in the differential diagnosis of patients with sero-negative mononucleosis or influenza-like symptoms.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0054_13242", "title": "Primary HIV-infection. A differential diagnosis of mononucleosis/influenza-like symptoms", "span_text": "We describe the history of a 29 year-old heterosexual female who presented symptoms and signs similar to those indicating infectious mononucleosis and influenza. However, the diagnosis turned out to be a primary HIV infection."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_13242", "InternalMed_Harrison_12697", "pubmed23n0060_19660", "pubmed23n0043_7746", "pubmed23n0051_14694", "InternalMed_Harrison_15186", "pubmed23n0052_9428", "pubmed23n0060_19656", "pubmed23n0050_2242", "pubmed23n0043_6044"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_13242", "InternalMed_Harrison_12697", "pubmed23n0060_19660", "pubmed23n0043_7746", "pubmed23n0051_14694", "InternalMed_Harrison_15186", "pubmed23n0052_9428", "pubmed23n0060_19656", "pubmed23n0050_2242", "pubmed23n0043_6044"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "HIV Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup eva