{"topic": "Anxiety disorder", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the pathophysiology of panic disorder?", "options": {"A": "Involves alterations in dopamine neurotransmission, opioids, and second-messenger systems", "B": "Involves a growing body of neuroanatomical and neurochemical data", "C": "Involves endothelial cell dysfunction", "D": "Involves a complex inheritance pattern, with one or more major genes, multiple loci, low penetrance, and environmental influences"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Panic disorder is an anxiety disorder with a characteristic clinical presentation. A growing body of neuroanatomical and neurochemical data is beginning to elucidate its pathophysiology.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0059_5409", "title": "Panic disorder: clinical features, neurobiology, and pharmacotherapy", "span_text": "Panic disorder is an anxiety disorder with a characteristic clinical presentation. A growing body of neuroanatomical and neurochemical data is beginning to elucidate its pathophysiology."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_4256", "pubmed23n0052_6086", "pubmed23n0007_6635", "pubmed23n0046_16572", "pubmed23n0012_9799", "pubmed23n0060_15742", "pubmed23n0054_7022", "pubmed23n0055_15359", "InternalMed_Harrison_30441", "pubmed23n0060_6812", "pubmed23n0023_7239", "pubmed23n0059_5409", "pubmed23n0054_10712", "pubmed23n0057_20685", "pubmed23n0054_21134", "pubmed23n0052_16924", "pubmed23n0014_775", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1564", "pubmed23n0058_19913", "pubmed23n0047_20544", "pubmed23n0028_5573", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2177", "pubmed23n0026_4077", "pubmed23n0053_16157", "pubmed23n0048_1403", "Immunology_Janeway_3573", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3230", "pubmed23n0026_7181", "pubmed23n0045_5325", "pubmed23n0054_8259", "Neurology_Adams_9116", "pubmed23n0050_15172", "pubmed23n0047_15063", "pubmed23n0029_4967", "First_Aid_Step1_659", "pubmed23n0047_3688", "pubmed23n0029_1008", "Pharmacolog