{"topic": "Acute kidney injury", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is a characteristic laboratory finding in patients with renovascular hypertension?", "options": {"A": "Hyperkalemia", "B": "Hyperreninemia", "C": "Hypocalcemia", "D": "Hyperphosphatemia"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Hyperreninemia is a characteristic finding in patients with renovascular hypertension, as it is often associated with activation of the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0064_316", "title": "The role of laboratory testing in the diagnosis of renovascular hypertension", "span_text": "Hyperreninemia is a characteristic finding, and acute blockade of the renin system forms the basis of diagnostic tests such as the oral captopril test and captopril renography."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0064_316", "pubmed23n0015_13614", "pubmed23n0048_3420", "InternalMed_Harrison_23270", "pubmed23n0014_4992", "pubmed23n0051_13043", "InternalMed_Harrison_19243", "pubmed23n0023_5526", "pubmed23n0050_16244", "InternalMed_Harrison_24368", "pubmed23n0051_16909", "pubmed23n0042_7109", "pubmed23n0058_3477", "pubmed23n0058_17937", "pubmed23n0046_16252", "pubmed23n0011_1488", "pubmed23n0016_11213", "pubmed23n0013_5590", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "pubmed23n0054_9203", "pubmed23n0054_4832", "pubmed23n0014_12612", "InternalMed_Harrison_17680", "pubmed23n0051_6910", "pubmed23n0040_1766", "pubmed23n0056_12592", "pubmed23n0043_4665", "pubmed23n0037_7331", "pubmed23n0058_19650", "pubmed23n0019_1756", "pubmed23n0050_5713", "pubmed23n0059_19452", "pubmed23n0059_13027", "pubmed23n0014_2665", "pubmed23n0054_535", "pubmed23n0012_1376", "pubmed23n0006_3938", "pubmed23n0048_12294"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0064_316", "pubmed23n0015_13614", "pubmed23n0048_3420", "InternalMed_Harrison_23270", "pubmed23n0014_4992", "pubmed23n0051_13043", "InternalMed_Harrison_19243", "pubmed23n0023_5526", "pubmed23n0