{"topic": "GERD", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "A patient with gastroesophageal reflux disease is found to have a genetic predisposition to the condition. What type of study would be most relevant to understanding the genetic factors contributing to this patient's condition?", "options": {"A": "Genetic association study", "B": "Case-control study", "C": "Cohort study", "D": "Randomized controlled trial"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Genetic association studies are designed to identify genetic variants that are associated with an increased risk of developing a particular disease, such as gastroesophageal reflux disease. These studies can help researchers understand the genetic factors that contribute to the development of the disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41513492", "title": "The role of gene polymorphisms in the occurrence of gastroesophageal reflux disease: A systematic review and meta-analysis of genetic association studies", "span_text": "A systematic review of PubMed, Cochrane, ScienceDirect, Scopus, DisGENET, GWASCatalog, and HuGE Phenopedia databases (2012-2024) was conducted to identify GAS for GERD."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578529", "pubmed_web_41577482", "pubmed_web_41551831", "pubmed_web_41551533", "pubmed_web_41549496", "pubmed_web_41543102", "pubmed_web_41530072", "pubmed_web_41527695", "pubmed_web_41515225", "pubmed_web_41513492", "pubmed_web_41510928", "pubmed_web_41499733", "pubmed_web_41493925", "pubmed_web_41493429", "pubmed_web_41491019", "pubmed_web_41490510", "pubmed_web_41486904", "pubmed_web_41479934", "pubmed_web_41473181", "pubmed_web_41459837"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41551533", "pubmed_web_41549496", "pubmed_web_41543102", "pubmed_web_41530072", "pubmed_web_41527695", "pubmed_web_41515225", "pubmed_web_41513492", "pubmed_web_41510928", "pubmed_web_41499733", "pubmed_web_41493925", "pubmed_web_41493429", "pubmed_web_4149101