{"topic": "Hepatitis C", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the first-line therapy for hepatitis C\u2013associated cryoglobulinemic vasculitis?", "options": {"A": "Antiviral therapy", "B": "Glucocorticoids", "C": "Cyclophosphamide", "D": "Rheumatoid factor reduction"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Antiviral therapy is the first-line treatment for hepatitis C\u2013associated cryoglobulinemic vasculitis, as it can lead to clinical improvement and reduction in circulating cryoglobulins, IgM, and rheumatoid factor.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_25692", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "In such patients, treatment with antiviral therapy (Chap. 360) can prove beneficial and should be considered first-line therapy for hepatitis C\u2013associated cryoglobulinemic vasculitis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0043_1179", "pubmed23n0055_17212", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6103", "InternalMed_Harrison_25692", "pubmed23n0010_483", "InternalMed_Harrison_13598", "pubmed23n0060_15744"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0043_1179", "pubmed23n0055_17212", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6103", "InternalMed_Harrison_25692", "pubmed23n0010_483", "InternalMed_Harrison_13598", "pubmed23n0060_15744"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hepatitis C Therapy therapy treatment management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7650.351083022542, "llm_ms": 924.3424580199644, "verification_ms": 906.0133339953609, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK"