{"topic": "Myocardial infarction", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 55-year-old man presents with chest pain and electrocardiographic signs of myocardial infarction, but with patent coronary arteries. What diagnostic method may be helpful in this case?", "options": {"A": "Endomyocardial biopsy", "B": "Echocardiography", "C": "Technetium scanning", "D": "Thallium-201 myocardial imaging"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's clinical presentation and electrocardiographic signs suggest myocardial infarction, but the presence of patent coronary arteries makes the diagnosis uncertain. Endomyocardial biopsy can provide a definitive diagnosis by demonstrating changes consistent with myocardial infarction or other conditions such as cardiomyopathy.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0019_8817", "title": "Myocardial biopsy in diagnosis of endomyocardiopathy in patient with electro- and vectorcardiographic signs of myocardial infarction", "span_text": "Endomyocardial biopsy disclosed changes consistent with 'congestive cardiomyopathy'. Thus, the study shows that the Q wave pattern on the electrocardiogram provides insufficient evidence for the diagnosis of myocardial infarction, and may be misleading in patients with cardiomyopathy."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0013_4500", "pubmed23n0033_2730", "pubmed23n0019_8817", "pubmed23n0022_9045", "pubmed23n0042_7044", "pubmed23n0010_8536", "pubmed23n0061_10229", "pubmed23n0018_7002", "pubmed23n0027_15051", "pubmed23n0051_6443", "pubmed23n0012_1368", "pubmed23n0030_5874", "pubmed23n0021_3296", "pubmed23n0054_1390", "pubmed23n0041_8242", "pubmed23n0022_2454", "pubmed23n0052_1449", "pubmed23n0053_17740", "pubmed23n0049_445", "pubmed23n0051_2004", "pubmed23n0011_9221", "pubmed23n0018_7385", "pubmed23n0016_10805", "pubmed23n0038_9584", "pubmed23n0050_6697", "pubmed23n0011_10517", "pubmed23n0052_15583", "pubmed23n0049_12884", "pubmed23n0048_17267", "Surg