{"topic": "Cervical cancer", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the recommended screening interval for cervical cancer in women aged 25-60 using cervical cytology?", "options": {"A": "Every 2 years", "B": "Every 3 years", "C": "Every 5 years", "D": "Every 10 years"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The recommended screening interval for cervical cancer in women aged 25-60 using cervical cytology is every 3 years, as organized screening programs are essential to ensure a high proportion of women are screened and that the tests are of high quality with adequate quality control.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0057_5223", "title": "Epidemiological approaches to primary and secondary prevention of cancer", "span_text": "Epidemiology has shown that secondary prevention of cancer is applicable by screening for breast cancer with mammography with or without physical examination in women age 50-69, and screening for cervix cancer in women age 25-60 with cervical cytology. Organised screening programmes are essential to ensure that a high proportion of women are screened, and that the tests are high quality with adequate quality control. Under these circumstances screening every 2 years for breast cancer and every 3 years for cervix cancer is cost-effective."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_12794", "pubmed23n0049_13659", "pubmed23n0057_5223", "pubmed23n0053_8349", "pubmed23n0058_3524", "Gynecology_Novak_728", "pubmed23n0059_21445", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "pubmed23n0049_13658", "First_Aid_Step2_237", "pubmed23n0058_10943", "pubmed23n0048_17336", "pubmed23n0057_20451", "pubmed23n0061_8033", "pubmed23n0058_1366", "pubmed23n0058_15950", "pubmed23n0047_4505", "pubmed23n0063_12708", "pubmed23n0012_7606", "pubmed23n0062_1607", "pubmed23n0047_5386", "pubmed23n0050_20552", "pubmed23n0045_15534", "pubmed23n0062_20210", "InternalMed_Harrison_5956", "Surgery_Schwartz_2339", "Surgery_Schwartz_11