{"topic": "Dengue", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a potential complication of dengue fever, particularly in children and individuals with certain chronic diseases?", "options": {"A": "Dengue hemorrhagic fever and dengue shock syndrome", "B": "Japanese encephalitis", "C": "Sickle cell crisis", "D": "Asthma exacerbation"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Dengue fever can lead to severe complications, including dengue hemorrhagic fever and dengue shock syndrome, which are associated with a high mortality rate, especially in children and those with chronic diseases like asthma, sickle cell anemia, and diabetes mellitus.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0060_20230", "title": "Dengue. A review", "span_text": "This clinical syndrome being benign or severe like the Dengue hemorrhagic fever and dengue shock syndrome (DHF/DSS), has been associated with a very high mortality rate specifically in children with different ages and those under 1 year of age from mothers having antibodies to dengue virus."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_20230", "pubmed23n0006_12372"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_20230", "pubmed23n0006_12372"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Dengue Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 12953.783042030409, "llm_ms": 879.1021250071935, "verification_ms": 865.5618330230936, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAIL