{"topic": "Hypertension", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a significant risk factor for postoperative mortality in patients undergoing noncardiac surgery?", "options": {"A": "History of hypertension", "B": "Severely limited activity level", "C": "Reduced renal function", "D": "All of the above"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "A history of hypertension, severely limited activity level, and reduced renal function are all independently associated with an increased risk of postoperative mortality.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0053_17697", "title": "In-hospital and long-term mortality in male veterans following noncardiac surgery", "span_text": "Multivariable analysis disclosed that a history of hypertension (odds ratio [OR] = 3.8; 95% confidence interval [CI], 1.1 to 13), a severely limited activity level (OR = 9.7; 95% CI, 2.5 to 37), and a creatinine clearance of less than 0.83 mL/s (OR = 6.8; 95% CI, 2.8 to 16) were all independently associated with an increased risk of postoperative mortality."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_1027", "pubmed23n0053_17697", "pubmed23n0050_211", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1934", "pubmed23n0048_7202", "pubmed23n0047_5691", "pubmed23n0057_9433", "pubmed23n0043_106", "pubmed23n0049_6412", "pubmed23n0046_18247", "pubmed23n0038_3078", "pubmed23n0028_11795", "pubmed23n0051_18406", "pubmed23n0046_17991", "pubmed23n0047_6071", "InternalMed_Harrison_21649", "pubmed23n0057_14423", "pubmed23n0063_5297", "Obstentrics_Williams_6904", "pubmed23n0056_16013", "pubmed23n0058_9972", "Obstentrics_Williams_6591", "pubmed23n0042_15220", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6415", "Pathology_Robbins_4649", "pubmed23n0057_16827", "Obstentrics_Williams_6905", "pubmed23n0061_6503", "pubmed23n0022_1473", "pubmed23n0052_15590", "Obstentrics_Williams_6922", "pubmed23n0054_19712", "InternalMed_Harrison_19132", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1179", "pubmed23n0052_1066", "pubmed23n0063_20280", "pubmed23n