{"topic": "Urinary tract infection", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A patient with Crohn's disease presents with urinary tract symptoms. What is the most important consideration in diagnosing the cause of these symptoms?", "options": {"A": "The patient's symptoms are likely due to a primary infection of the lower urinary tract.", "B": "The patient's symptoms may be due to secondary involvement of the urinary bladder in Crohn's disease.", "C": "The patient's symptoms are likely due to a kidney stone.", "D": "The patient's symptoms are likely due to a urinary tract infection caused by a rare bacterium."}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms may be due to secondary involvement of the urinary bladder in Crohn's disease, and a diagnosis of primary infection of the lower urinary tract may be erroneous.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0006_15386", "title": "Roentgenologic abnormalities of the urinary bladder secondary to Crohn's disease.", "span_text": "Urinary tract symptoms and signs may result from secondary involvement of the urinary bladder in patients with Crohn's disease."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0006_15386", "pubmed23n0024_5555", "pubmed23n0045_19884", "InternalMed_Harrison_10692", "pubmed23n0030_10600", "pubmed23n0060_4405", "pubmed23n0055_8652", "pubmed23n0017_4960", "pubmed23n0040_7035", "pubmed23n0026_7093", "pubmed23n0005_9019", "pubmed23n0052_17360", "pubmed23n0054_1415", "pubmed23n0026_10937", "pubmed23n0026_11171", "pubmed23n0053_15759", "pubmed23n0026_8702", "pubmed23n0055_3950", "InternalMed_Harrison_12697", "Surgery_Schwartz_12846", "InternalMed_Harrison_16360", "pubmed23n0026_2200", "pubmed23n0059_19723", "pubmed23n0014_8377", "pubmed23n0024_1862", "pubmed23n0061_2909", "InternalMed_Harrison_10178", "pubmed23n0049_19653", "pubmed23n0028_3871", "pubmed23n0046_3360", "pubmed23n0054_14472", "pubmed23n0058_4750", "InternalMed_Harrison_11781", "pubmed23n00