{"topic": "Pneumonia", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a significant risk factor for respiratory complications, including pneumonia, in critically ill patients with acute upper gastrointestinal bleeding?", "options": {"A": "Advanced liver disease", "B": "Age less than 50 years", "C": "Low APACHE II score", "D": "Esophageal site of bleeding without advanced liver disease"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Advanced liver disease is identified as a risk factor for respiratory complications, including pneumonia, in critically ill patients with acute upper gastrointestinal bleeding.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_622", "title": "Respiratory complications in critically ill medical patients with acute upper gastrointestinal bleeding", "span_text": "Esophageal sites of bleeding (esophagitis, esophageal ulcers and esophageal varices), advanced liver disease, age greater than 70 yrs, and an Acute Physiology and Chronic Health Evaluation (APACHE) II score greater than 13 appeared to be risk factors."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_622", "pubmed23n0058_7804", "pubmed23n0016_1630", "Surgery_Schwartz_13389", "Obstentrics_Williams_7738", "pubmed23n0048_7046", "pubmed23n0047_9521", "pubmed23n0043_16464", "pubmed23n0047_8853", "pubmed23n0053_18034", "pubmed23n0043_21576", "InternalMed_Harrison_10197", "pubmed23n0036_5158", "Obstentrics_Williams_7116", "pubmed23n0052_792", "pubmed23n0054_12703", "InternalMed_Harrison_10135", "pubmed23n0058_11701", "First_Aid_Step2_436", "pubmed23n0052_18326", "pubmed23n0063_9643", "pubmed23n0026_5768", "pubmed23n0049_4462", "Surgery_Schwartz_2737", "pubmed23n0027_4713", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3345", "pubmed23n0055_13945", "pubmed23n0040_8379", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2165", "pubmed23n0048_416", "Surgery_Schwartz_1703"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_622", "pubmed23n0058_7804", "pubmed23n0016_1630", "Surgery_Schwartz_13389", "Obstentrics_Wil