{"topic": "Diarrhea", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism by which cholera enterotoxin causes diarrhea?", "options": {"A": "Induction of an augmented synthesis of cAMP in the mucosa cell", "B": "Leakage of the tight junctions between mucosal cells", "C": "Increased motility of the intestinal tract", "D": "Decreased absorption of electrolytes and water"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Cholera enterotoxin causes diarrhea by inducing an augmented synthesis of cAMP in the mucosa cell, leading to secretion of electrolytes and water into the intestinal lumen.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0011_7439", "title": "[Current concepts in the pathophysiology of the diarrhea (author's transl)]", "span_text": "Cholera enterotoxin and other bacterial toxins as well as VIP (vasoactive intestinal peptide) cause diarrhea by this mechanism."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0004_9746", "pubmed23n0008_1385", "InternalMed_Harrison_3067", "pubmed23n0013_10808", "pubmed23n0011_7439", "pubmed23n0047_13143"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0004_9746", "pubmed23n0008_1385", "InternalMed_Harrison_3067", "pubmed23n0013_10808", "pubmed23n0011_7439", "pubmed23n0047_13143"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Diarrhea Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6988.805875007529, "llm_ms": 866.6064580320381, "verification_ms": 794.0166249754839, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0