{"topic": "Epilepsy", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the role of magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) in the investigation of patients with late-onset epilepsy?", "options": {"A": "MRI is useful in investigation of patients with late-onset epilepsy with focal features.", "B": "MRI is not useful in investigation of patients with late-onset epilepsy.", "C": "MRI is only used to rule out other conditions.", "D": "MRI is only used in patients with a normal CT scan."}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "MRI is useful in investigation of patients with late-onset epilepsy with focal features, as it can help clarify the diagnosis and detect the cause of seizures.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_15199", "title": "Magnetic resonance imaging and late-onset epilepsy.", "span_text": "MRI was diagnostic in 32% of the patients with partial seizures and/or focal EEG findings, as compared with 0% of patients without focal features (p less than 0.01)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_443", "pubmed23n0063_15199", "pubmed23n0017_6049", "pubmed23n0062_6490", "pubmed23n0027_8231"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_443", "pubmed23n0063_15199", "pubmed23n0017_6049", "pubmed23n0062_6490", "pubmed23n0027_8231"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Epilepsy Investigation investigation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging workup evaluation differential diagnosis clinical criteria biomarkers screening confirmatory test diagnostic accuracy", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 12327.098624955397, "llm_ms": 1092.6510840072297, "verification_ms": 774.651832995005, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs"