{"topic": "Appendicitis", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "A patient with suspected appendicitis is being managed expectantly, what should be included in their management?", "options": {"A": "NPO status, NG tube placement, IV fluids, placement of a Foley catheter, and vital sign monitoring", "B": "Immediate surgical intervention, CT scan, and ultrasound", "C": "Electrolytes, LFTs, amylase, lipase, and a CBC with differential", "D": "CXR for suspected perforation and AXR for obstruction"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Expectant management for a patient with suspected appendicitis includes NPO status, NG tube placement, IV fluids, placement of a Foley catheter to monitor urine output and fluid status, and vital sign monitoring with serial abdominal exams and serial labs.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "First_Aid_Step2_1185", "title": "First_Aid_Step2", "span_text": "In stable patients, expectant management may include NPO status, NG tube placement, IV \ufb02uids, placement of a Foley catheter (to monitor urine output and \ufb02uid status), and vital sign monitoring with serial abdominal exams and serial labs."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2021-01-01", "doc_ids": ["First_Aid_Step2_1185"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["First_Aid_Step2_1185"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": "2021-01-01", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Appendicitis Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 14882.59824999841, "llm_ms": 1139.910499972757, "verification_ms": 843.5615000198595, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_