{"topic": "Dermatitis", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What role do neuropeptides play in the regulation of contact dermatitis?", "options": {"A": "They decrease allergic and irritant inflammation", "B": "They have no effect on allergic and irritant inflammation", "C": "They increase allergic and irritant inflammation", "D": "They only affect irritant inflammation"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "Neuropeptides, such as substance P, calcitonin gene-related peptide, and somatostatin, have been shown to increase allergic and irritant inflammation in contact dermatitis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0057_4504", "title": "Neuropeptides enhance irritant and allergic contact dermatitis", "span_text": "All three neuropeptides were equally able to increase allergic and irritant inflammation. Even minor irritant stimuli were enhanced."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 10, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_20635", "pubmed23n0050_6689", "pubmed23n0057_4504", "InternalMed_Harrison_22826", "pubmed23n0008_15299", "pubmed23n0044_8548", "pubmed23n0061_10985", "pubmed23n0042_14476", "pubmed23n0040_21", "Pediatrics_Nelson_4030"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_20635", "pubmed23n0050_6689", "pubmed23n0057_4504", "InternalMed_Harrison_22826", "pubmed23n0008_15299", "pubmed23n0044_8548", "pubmed23n0061_10985", "pubmed23n0042_14476", "pubmed23n0040_21", "Pediatrics_Nelson_4030"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 5, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Dermatitis Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 20061.03533296846, "llm_ms": 944.4762920029461, "verification_ms": 822.3012500093319, "extra_instruc