{"topic": "Migraine", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism of action of sumatriptan in the treatment of migraine?", "options": {"A": "Selective vasoconstriction within the cranial vasculature", "B": "Blockade of \u03b21 and \u03b22 adrenergic receptors", "C": "Inhibition of carbonic anhydrase isoenzymes", "D": "Agonism of dopamine receptors"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Sumatriptan is a serotonin agonist that works by mediating selective vasoconstriction within the cranial vasculature and preventing the release of inflammatory mediators from trigeminal nerve terminals.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0044_4959", "title": "Sumatriptan: a selective 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor agonist for the acute treatment of migraine", "span_text": "Sumatriptan is a serotonin agonist that has been studied for the acute treatment of migraine and cluster headache. The drug appears to work via specific serotonin receptors to mediate selective vasoconstriction within the cranial vasculature and to prevent the release of inflammatory mediators from trigeminal nerve terminals."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "pubmed", "query": "sumatriptan mechanism of action", "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_1752", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2940", "Pharmacology_Katzung_995", "pubmed23n0044_18009", "pubmed23n0022_816", "pubmed23n0044_4959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1718", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1719", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1742", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2560"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_1752", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2940", "Pharmacology_Katzung_995", "pubmed23n0044_18009", "pubmed23n0022_816", "pubmed23n0044_4959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1718", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1719", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1742", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2560"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Migraine Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7244.832958036568, "llm_ms": 1442.6074579823762, "verification_ms": 1068.9622089848854, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_1752", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2940", "Pharmacology_Katzung_995", "pubmed23n0044_18009", "pubmed23n0022_816", "pubmed23n0044_4959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1718", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1719", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1742", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2560"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 100.0, "verification": 200.0, "llm": 1442.6074579823762}}}
{"topic": "Hyperlipidemia", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A 70-year-old female with advanced, ROS1 fusion-positive lung adenocarcinoma develops severe hyperlipidemia during treatment with crizotinib. What strategy may be effective in managing this adverse effect?", "options": {"A": "Combined strategy of crizotinib dose reduction and concomitant lipid-lowering therapy", "B": "Discontinuation of crizotinib and initiation of alternative therapy", "C": "Increase in crizotinib dosage to enhance its therapeutic effects", "D": "Monitoring of lipid levels without any changes to the treatment regimen"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The case report presents a patient who developed severe hyperlipidemia during crizotinib therapy, and a combined strategy of crizotinib dose reduction and concomitant lipid-lowering therapy was effective in managing this adverse effect.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41578599", "title": "Crizotinib-induced hyperlipidemia in advanced lung adenocarcinoma: A case report and literature review", "span_text": "A combined strategy of crizotinib dose reduction and concomitant lipid-lowering therapy was initiated to address the hyperlipidemia, aiming to maintain control of the primary malignancy while managing the adverse effect."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "pubmed_web", "query": "crizotinib-induced hyperlipidemia", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41580008", "pubmed_web_41578599", "pubmed_web_41578026", "pubmed_web_41572716", "pubmed_web_41556761", "pubmed_web_41548057", "pubmed_web_41545567", "pubmed_web_41544465", "pubmed_web_41542742", "pubmed_web_41542285", "pubmed_web_41540694", "pubmed_web_41536652", "pubmed_web_41517767", "pubmed_web_41508511", "pubmed_web_41508489", "pubmed_web_41508247", "pubmed_web_41508208", "pubmed_web_41506518", "pubmed_web_41504494", "pubmed_web_41495336"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41580008", "pubmed_web_41578599", "pubmed_web_41578026", "pubmed_web_41572716", "pubmed_web_41556761", "pubmed_web_41548057", "pubmed_web_41545567", "pubmed_web_41544465", "pubmed_web_41542742", "pubmed_web_41542285", "pubmed_web_41540694", "pubmed_web_41536652", "pubmed_web_41517767", "pubmed_web_41508511", "pubmed_web_41508489", "pubmed_web_41508247", "pubmed_web_41508208", "pubmed_web_41506518", "pubmed_web_41504494", "pubmed_web_41495336"], "retrieval_mode": "pubmed_web"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "pubmed_web_fallback", "query": "Hyperlipidemia Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 15230.267876002472, "llm_ms": 1049.7717920225114, "verification_ms": 920.3798749949783, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "pubmed_web", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": true, "docs": 20, "runtime_ms": 9353.510417044163}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed_web_41580008", "pubmed_web_41578599", "pubmed_web_41578026", "pubmed_web_41572716", "pubmed_web_41556761", "pubmed_web_41548057", "pubmed_web_41545567", "pubmed_web_41544465", "pubmed_web_41542742", "pubmed_web_41542285", "pubmed_web_41540694", "pubmed_web_41536652", "pubmed_web_41517767", "pubmed_web_41508511", "pubmed_web_41508489", "pubmed_web_41508247", "pubmed_web_41508208", "pubmed_web_41506518", "pubmed_web_41504494", "pubmed_web_41495336"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 100.0, "verification": 200.0, "llm": 1049.7717920225114}}}
{"topic": "GERD", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is a potential consequence of eliminating H. pylori colonization on a population basis in terms of GERD complications?", "options": {"A": "Reduced risk of esophageal adenocarcinoma", "B": "Increased risk of esophageal adenocarcinoma", "C": "No effect on esophageal adenocarcinoma risk", "D": "Elimination of GERD symptoms"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Lifelong absence of H. pylori is a risk factor for GERD complications, including esophageal adenocarcinoma.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_12603", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "For example, lifelong absence of H. pylori is a risk factor for GERD complications, including esophageal adenocarcinoma."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_12603"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_12603"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "GERD Prevention prevention prophylaxis risk reduction screening vaccination primary prevention secondary prevention lifestyle modification counseling public health early detection follow-up", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6419.774750014767, "llm_ms": 796.062792011071, "verification_ms": 916.5827090037055, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["InternalMed_Harrison_12603"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 100.0, "verification": 200.0, "llm": 796.062792011071}}}
{"topic": "Typhoid fever", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is a common adverse effect of nifurtimox, a standard drug for Chagas disease?", "options": {"A": "Hypersensitivity reactions", "B": "Nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, fever, rash, headache, restlessness, insomnia, neuropathies, and seizures", "C": "Anemia or neutropenia", "D": "Pancytopenia"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Nifurtimox is a nitrofuran used in the treatment of Chagas disease and African trypanosomiasis. Common adverse effects include nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, fever, rash, headache, restlessness, insomnia, neuropathies, and seizures.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_5775", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Nifurtimox, a nitrofuran, is a standard drug for Chagas disease. Nifurtimox is also used in the treatment of African trypanosomiasis in combination with eflornithine. Nifurtimox is well absorbed after oral administration and eliminated with a plasma half-life of about 3 hours. The drug is administered at a dosage of 8\u201310 mg/kg/d in three divided doses with meals for 60\u201390 days. Toxicity related to nifurtimox is common. Adverse effects include nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, fever, rash, headache, restlessness, insomnia, neuropathies, and seizures."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_5841", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5770", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5229", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1397", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5775", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5752", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5771", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1043", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5068", "pubmed23n0045_14808", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6173", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6459", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4057", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5765", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4274", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5191", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5245", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6954", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1403", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6210", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1079", "p