{"topic": "Neonatal sepsis", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the recommended approach to treat neonatal sepsis, considering the difficulty in accurate diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "Initiate treatment with piperacillin plus cefotaxime as soon as sepsis is suspected", "B": "Wait for blood culture results before starting antibiotic therapy", "C": "Use antiendotoxin monoclonal antibodies as the primary treatment", "D": "Withhold treatment until definitive diagnostic test results are available"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Early recognition and treatment of neonatal sepsis are crucial to improve outcomes. Given the low sensitivity of diagnostic tests, including blood cultures, initiating treatment with broad-spectrum antibiotics like piperacillin plus cefotaxime as soon as sepsis is suspected can help reduce mortality rates.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_4311", "title": "Neonatal sepsis in an intensive care unit and results of treatment", "span_text": "Early diagnosis and treatment with piperacillin plus cefotaxime reduced the mortality rate of sepsis to 2%. Sepsis never developed under treatment with piperacillin plus cefotaxime."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_17702", "pubmed23n0054_18227", "pubmed23n0055_7387", "pubmed23n0053_20250", "Surgery_Schwartz_1241", "pubmed23n0012_2210", "pubmed23n0047_2992", "pubmed23n0061_12068", "pubmed23n0063_4311", "pubmed23n0047_12115", "pubmed23n0051_19522", "pubmed23n0030_11212", "pubmed23n0047_20084", "pubmed23n0059_15754", "pubmed23n0047_20077", "pubmed23n0038_11689", "pubmed23n0053_7095", "pubmed23n0014_9513", "pubmed23n0006_4262", "pubmed23n0037_4049"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_17702", "pubmed23n0054_18227", "pubmed23n0055_7387", "pubmed23n0053_20250", "Surgery_Schwartz_1241", "pubmed23n0012_2210", "pubmed23n0047_2992", "pubmed23n0061_12068", "pubmed23n0063_4311", "pubmed23n0047_12115", "pubme