{"topic": "Systemic lupus erythematosus", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is a common initial laboratory abnormality in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus?", "options": {"A": "Lymphopenia", "B": "Thrombocytopenia", "C": "Leukocytosis", "D": "Eosinophilia"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Lymphopenia is a common initial laboratory abnormality in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus, occurring in 75% of patients with active, untreated SLE.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0022_3155", "title": "Lymphopenia in systemic lupus erythematosus. Clinical, diagnostic, and prognostic significance.", "span_text": "Lymphopenia was present in 75%, and another 18% of those patients developed lymphopenia subsequent to disease reactivation."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0003_5576", "pubmed23n0052_12309", "InternalMed_Harrison_26171", "pubmed23n0022_2872", "pubmed23n0062_17682", "pubmed23n0043_8241", "pubmed23n0022_3155", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2154", "pubmed23n0023_3147", "pubmed23n0058_20356", "pubmed23n0022_8731", "pubmed23n0060_19660", "pubmed23n0017_11402", "pubmed23n0017_11669", "pubmed23n0010_8749", "pubmed23n0052_17360", "pubmed23n0022_1398", "pubmed23n0063_12359", "pubmed23n0033_2730", "pubmed23n0016_9935", "pubmed23n0031_5063", "pubmed23n0026_1167", "pubmed23n0054_1961", "pubmed23n0037_4606", "pubmed23n0015_11007", "pubmed23n0043_13643", "pubmed23n0063_6425", "pubmed23n0034_2145", "pubmed23n0063_15805", "pubmed23n0012_40", "pubmed23n0013_4543", "pubmed23n0011_5968", "InternalMed_Harrison_23904", "pubmed23n0037_11035", "pubmed23n0011_4286", "pubmed23n0011_8474", "pubmed23n0003_5022", "pubmed23n0013_197", "pubmed23n0009_93", "pubmed23n0045_8466", "pubmed23n0059_5665", "pubmed23n0059_15831", "pubmed23n0044_2815", "pubmed23n0033_9452", "pubmed23n0036_4294", "pubmed23n0043_12760", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1970", "InternalMed_Harrison_26020", "pubmed23n0004_9830", "pubmed23n0036_