{"topic": "Hepatitis C", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What percentage of patients with chronic hepatitis C may develop cirrhosis within 10-20 years of acute illness?", "options": {"A": "Up to 20%", "B": "Up to 50%", "C": "Up to 80%", "D": "Up to 90%"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Chronic hepatitis C may lead to cirrhosis in a significant proportion of patients, with the risk increasing over time.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_23555", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Although many patients with chronic hepatitis C have no symptoms, cirrhosis may develop in as many as 20% within 10\u201320 years of acute illness; in some series of cases reported by referral centers, cirrhosis has been reported in as many as 50% of patients with chronic hepatitis C."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23783", "pubmed23n0059_757", "pubmed23n0052_16488", "Pathology_Robbins_3910", "InternalMed_Harrison_23555", "pubmed23n0052_12953", "pubmed23n0045_10019", "pubmed23n0061_5869", "Obstentrics_Williams_7600", "InternalMed_Harrison_23825", "InternalMed_Harrison_23780", "Gynecology_Novak_3845", "pubmed23n0061_16962", "InternalMed_Harrison_23784", "InternalMed_Harrison_9900", "InternalMed_Harrison_23774", "InternalMed_Harrison_23934", "pubmed23n0039_4516", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7125", "Surgery_Schwartz_9022", "Gynecology_Novak_3844"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23783", "pubmed23n0059_757", "pubmed23n0052_16488", "Pathology_Robbins_3910", "InternalMed_Harrison_23555", "pubmed23n0052_12953", "pubmed23n0045_10019", "pubmed23n0061_5869", "Obstentrics_Williams_7600", "InternalMed_Harrison_23825", "InternalMed_Harrison_23780", "Gynecology_Novak_3845", "pubmed23n0061_16962", "InternalMed_Harrison_23784", "InternalMed_Harrison_9900", "InternalMed_Harrison_23774", "InternalMed_Harrison_23934", "pubmed23n0039_4516", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7125", "Surgery_Schwartz_902