{"topic": "Systemic lupus erythematosus", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is a significant risk factor for mortality in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus?", "options": {"A": "Systolic blood pressure", "B": "Diastolic blood pressure", "C": "Serum creatinine level", "D": "Anticardiolipin antibody status"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Hypertension is a significant risk factor for mortality in SLE, with each millimeter unit increase in systolic blood pressure corresponding to a 2% increase in mortality risk.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0058_11470", "title": "Variables associated with decreased survival in systemic lupus erythematosus", "span_text": "Fifty-one deaths occurred among 310 patients with systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) observed for 1,234 patient-years. Twenty-one of 97 entry variables at first clinic visit were associated with an increased risk of mortality. When corrected for multiple comparisons, the only risk factor that retained statistical significance was systolic blood pressure."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0058_14994", "pubmed23n0043_1775", "pubmed23n0059_2533", "pubmed23n0058_11470", "pubmed23n0058_12470", "pubmed23n0043_12759", "pubmed23n0047_11192", "pubmed23n0052_12309", "pubmed23n0041_10807", "pubmed23n0047_11191", "pubmed23n0043_1776", "pubmed23n0058_14992", "pubmed23n0032_4554", "pubmed23n0022_1088", "pubmed23n0028_1569", "pubmed23n0037_4788", "pubmed23n0025_1752", "pubmed23n0015_13441", "pubmed23n0016_10698", "pubmed23n0064_212", "pubmed23n0058_9184", "pubmed23n0022_5079", "pubmed23n0013_811", "pubmed23n0054_1941", "pubmed23n0029_1562", "pubmed23n0028_10804", "pubmed23n0015_728", "pubmed23n0060_1866", "Obstentrics_Williams_8343", "pubmed23n0051_21157", "pubmed23n0058_12469", "pubmed23n0048_18235", "pubmed23n0054_13105", "pubmed23n0003_10582", "pubmed23n0054_13257", "Obstentrics_Williams_7333", "pubmed23n0002_7034", "pubmed23n0059_5665", "pu