{"topic": "Asthma", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the importance of monitoring peak expiratory flow in patients with asthma?", "options": {"A": "It helps to assess the severity of asthma", "B": "It is used to diagnose asthma", "C": "It is used to monitor the side effects of medications", "D": "It is not necessary for asthma management"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Monitoring peak expiratory flow is important for evaluating the activity of bronchial asthma and for self-management in case of clinically latent deterioration and during maintenance treatment.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0048_16072", "title": "[Self-treatment and self-monitoring in patients with bronchial asthma]", "span_text": "Regular assessment of the peak expiratory flow (PEF), which after proper instruction, the patient can do himself is important for evaluation of the activity of bronchial asthma."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_4490", "pubmed23n0048_4629", "Pediatrics_Nelson_936", "pubmed23n0062_17609", "pubmed23n0048_16072", "pubmed23n0061_15437", "pubmed23n0050_11261", "Obstentrics_Williams_6996", "pubmed23n0052_18959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2081"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_4490", "pubmed23n0048_4629", "Pediatrics_Nelson_936", "pubmed23n0062_17609", "pubmed23n0048_16072", "pubmed23n0061_15437", "pubmed23n0050_11261", "Obstentrics_Williams_6996", "pubmed23n0052_18959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2081"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Asthma Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9499.45237499196, "llm_ms": 911.31