{"topic": "Sepsis", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a major cause of morbidity and mortality in patients with SJS/TEN?", "options": {"A": "Sepsis", "B": "Respiratory failure", "C": "Cardiac arrest", "D": "Renal failure"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Sepsis is the major cause of morbidity and mortality in patients with SJS/TEN, making meticulous wound care crucial.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pediatrics_Nelson_4100", "title": "Pediatrics_Nelson", "span_text": "SJS/TEN is a serious illness with a mortality rate as high as35% for severe cases of TEN. Prompt discontinuation of theoffending agent is key. No controlled clinical trials regardingmedical therapy exist, though early initiation of intravenous immunoglobulin has been proposed. Supportive care is anotheressential component of therapy, and a multidisciplinary careteam is often necessary. Sepsis is the major cause of morbidityand mortality, so meticulous wound care is crucial, with stringent surveillance for cutaneous infections and use of antibiotics as warranted."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_17697", "InternalMed_Harrison_11709", "Obstentrics_Williams_5951", "pubmed23n0014_6129", "pubmed23n0052_1066", "pubmed23n0053_14192", "pubmed23n0052_8663", "pubmed23n0047_6071", "Pediatrics_Nelson_4100", "Surgery_Schwartz_13390", "Obstentrics_Williams_7067", "pubmed23n0054_5962", "Gynecology_Novak_3843", "pubmed23n0045_6812", "pubmed23n0027_952", "pubmed23n0047_9618", "pubmed23n0048_164", "pubmed23n0060_8677", "pubmed23n0049_4462", "InternalMed_Harrison_23086", "Pediatrics_Nelson_741", "pubmed23n0049_14995", "pubmed23n0044_22800", "Pediatrics_Nelson_889", "pubmed23n0053_1183", "pubmed23n0042_6102", "Surgery_Schwartz_2607", "pubmed23n0061_15739", "pubmed23n0058_21152", "Obstentrics_Williams_5624", "pubmed23n0016_10698", "pubmed23n0062_15331", "pubmed23n0056_7057", "pubmed23n0026_8097", "pubmed23n0061_15536", "pubmed23n0057_24635"