{"topic": "Colorectal cancer", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the primary goal of monitoring patients after primary large bowel surgery for malignancy?", "options": {"A": "To assess the clinical potential of serial serum CA125 measurements", "B": "To detect recurrence and provide salvage treatment for cure", "C": "To investigate the individual and combined value of CA 15-3 and carcinoembryonic antigen", "D": "To establish the clinical significance of the CA-195 tandem immunoradiometric assay"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Monitoring patients after primary large bowel surgery for malignancy is predicated on the concept that early detection of recurrence may provide salvage treatment for cure.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0050_12566", "title": "Colorectal cancer. Principles of postoperative follow-up", "span_text": "Monitoring patients after primary large bowel surgery for malignancy is predicated on the concept that early detection of recurrence may provide salvage treatment for cure."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_7551", "pubmed23n0059_10567", "pubmed23n0051_1037", "pubmed23n0050_12566", "pubmed23n0063_4534", "pubmed23n0024_3931", "pubmed23n0062_9630", "pubmed23n0043_19064", "pubmed23n0049_19970", "pubmed23n0004_8620", "pubmed23n0044_22496", "pubmed23n0050_9885", "pubmed23n0045_513", "pubmed23n0033_8947", "pubmed23n0044_1723", "pubmed23n0057_21035", "pubmed23n0047_20362", "pubmed23n0050_4265", "pubmed23n0047_20358", "pubmed23n0046_1088", "InternalMed_Harrison_32562", "pubmed23n0003_10673", "pubmed23n0033_5816", "pubmed23n0056_19706", "pubmed23n0057_19565", "pubmed23n0020_4993", "pubmed23n0060_13607", "pubmed23n0004_1198", "pubmed23n0057_19681", "pubmed23n0047_11310", "pubmed23n0051_15459", "pubmed23n0060_14212", "pubmed23n0047_5553", "pubmed23n0056_13696", "pubmed23n0046_2718", "pubmed23n0012_1598"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_7551", "pubmed23n0059_10567", "p