{"topic": "Diarrhea", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "A 62-year-old patient with metastatic triple-negative breast cancer develops progressive dyspnea, dry cough, and diarrhea after receiving sacituzumab govitecan. What is the most likely cause of the patient's diarrhea?", "options": {"A": "Sacituzumab govitecan-induced interstitial pneumonitis", "B": "Infectious gastroenteritis", "C": "Irritable bowel syndrome", "D": "Celiac disease"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms of diarrhea, dyspnea, and dry cough, in combination with the chest computed tomography findings, suggest sacituzumab govitecan-induced interstitial pneumonitis as the most likely cause of the patient's diarrhea.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41578359", "title": "Interstitial pneumonitis related to sacituzumab govitecan in a patient with metastatic triple-negative breast cancer: a case report", "span_text": "After the second cycle, she developed progressive dyspnea, dry cough, and diarrhea. Chest computed tomography revealed diffuse ground grass opacity of the bilateral lungs with multiple foci of black area (reverse hall sign) and thickening of the interlobular septa."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578995", "pubmed_web_41578550", "pubmed_web_41578359", "pubmed_web_41577348", "pubmed_web_41576297", "pubmed_web_41575898", "pubmed_web_41575649", "pubmed_web_41573536", "pubmed_web_41573353", "pubmed_web_41571393", "pubmed_web_41570843", "pubmed_web_41570841", "pubmed_web_41570767", "pubmed_web_41568384", "pubmed_web_41567626", "pubmed_web_41566926", "pubmed_web_41566660", "pubmed_web_41566186", "pubmed_web_41563654", "pubmed_web_41562803"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578550", "pubmed_web_41578359", "pubmed_web_41577348", "pubmed_web_41576297", "pubmed_web_41575898", "pubmed_web_41575649", "pubmed_web_41573536", "pubmed_web_41573353", "pubmed_web_41571393", "pubmed_web_41570843", "pubmed_