{"topic": "Stroke", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is the most common medical complication in patients with preoperative risks undergoing carotid endarterectomy?", "options": {"A": "Myocardial infarction", "B": "Hypoxia", "C": "Carotid occlusion/thrombus", "D": "Intraoperative glucose administration"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The most common medical complication in patients with preoperative risks undergoing carotid endarterectomy is myocardial infarction, which had the highest incidence in Groups 3 and 4.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0054_778", "title": "Preoperative risks predict neurological outcome of carotid endarterectomy related stroke", "span_text": "The most common medical complication was myocardial infarction, which had the highest incidence in Groups 3 and 4 (6.1 and 5%, respectively)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0018_6422", "pubmed23n0054_778", "pubmed23n0050_211", "pubmed23n0052_19808", "pubmed23n0057_14423", "pubmed23n0049_12951", "Obstentrics_Williams_6591", "pubmed23n0028_4922", "pubmed23n0023_9957", "pubmed23n0054_12486", "Biochemistry_Lippincott_1201", "pubmed23n0060_228", "pubmed23n0050_1238", "First_Aid_Step2_600", "pubmed23n0044_9135", "pubmed23n0063_20280", "pubmed23n0050_13944", "pubmed23n0057_19174", "pubmed23n0063_2773", "Obstentrics_Williams_6905", "pubmed23n0049_16234", "pubmed23n0018_238", "pubmed23n0054_19638", "pubmed23n0052_15590", "pubmed23n0048_4150", "pubmed23n0017_7606", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3692", "Neurology_Adams_6916", "InternalMed_Harrison_19132", "pubmed23n0057_19175", "pubmed23n0005_966", "InternalMed_Harrison_30676", "pubmed23n0061_18584", "Biochemistry_Lippincott_1849", "InternalMed_Harrison_19633", "pubmed23n0048_6215", "pubmed23n0062_585", "pubmed23n0063_9562", "pubmed23n0058_15142", "pubmed23n0036_4718", "pubmed23n0056_4133", "Surgery_Schwartz_13398", "Surgery_Schwartz_13787", "pubmed23n0004_1360", "Pathology_Robbins_4