{"topic": "Appendicitis", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the potential benefit of using shortened postoperative antibiotic regimens in children with perforated appendicitis?", "options": {"A": "Reduced risk of intra-abdominal abscess", "B": "Increased risk of readmission", "C": "Shorter length of hospital stay", "D": "Higher risk of treatment-related complications"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "Shortened postoperative antibiotic regimens may offer the advantage of reduced hospital stay in children with perforated appendicitis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41443239", "title": "Effectiveness and Safety of Shortened Postoperative Antibiotic Regimens in Children with Perforated Appendicitis: A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis", "span_text": "This systematic review shows neither non-inferiority nor an increased risk of intra-abdominal abscess with a shortened postoperative antibiotic regimen. There may be no difference regarding readmission rates and treatment-related complications. Shorter regimens probably offer the advantage of reduced hospital stay."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41558042", "pubmed_web_41541914", "pubmed_web_41451717", "pubmed_web_41443239", "pubmed_web_41416556", "pubmed_web_41372491", "pubmed_web_41361410", "pubmed_web_41345705", "pubmed_web_41345613", "pubmed_web_41337977", "pubmed_web_41337808", "pubmed_web_41307592", "pubmed_web_41288210", "pubmed_web_41278158", "pubmed_web_41270771", "pubmed_web_41270586", "pubmed_web_41265933", "pubmed_web_41249563", "pubmed_web_41225369", "pubmed_web_41214563"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41558042", "pubmed_web_41541914", "pubmed_web_41451717", "pubmed_web_41443239", "pubmed_web_41416556", "pubmed_web_41372491", "pubmed_web_41361410", "pubmed_web_41345705", "pubmed_web_41345613", "pubmed_web_41337977", "pubmed_web_41337808", "pubmed_web_41307592", "pubmed_web_41288210", "pubmed_web_41278158", "pub