{"topic": "Epilepsy", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the long-term prognosis for juvenile head-injured patients who experience early epileptic seizures?", "options": {"A": "Favourable, with late epilepsy occurring in 15.3% of cases", "B": "Unfavourable, with late epilepsy occurring in 50% of cases", "C": "Variable, depending on the severity of the head injury", "D": "Unknown, due to limited follow-up data"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The long-term prognosis for juvenile head-injured patients who experience early epileptic seizures is favourable, with late epilepsy occurring in 15.3% of cases, and responding favourably to anticonvulsive therapy.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0004_13213", "title": "Long-term prognosis of early epilepsy in juvenile head-injured patients (preliminary results)", "span_text": "The authors present the results of a long-term follow up of 52 juvenile head-injured patients who showed early epileptic seizures. The purpose of this study is to stress the role of long-term prognosis in the early seizures and to determine in which cases a treatment preventing late seizures is eligible. They consider long-term prognosis as to be favourable. Late epilepsy occurred in 15.3% of the cases and responded favourably to anticonvulsive therapy."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0016_10801", "pubmed23n0004_13213", "pubmed23n0055_404", "pubmed23n0025_7340", "pubmed23n0053_250", "Surgery_Schwartz_12423"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0016_10801", "pubmed23n0004_13213", "pubmed23n0055_404", "pubmed23n0025_7340", "pubmed23n0053_250", "Surgery_Schwartz_12423"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Epilepsy Prognosis prognosis outcomes mortality survival complications disease course recurrence risk stratification severity long-term outcomes quality of life predictors", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9093.378625053447, "llm_ms": 916.1379159777425, "verification_ms": 735.6350000482053, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0016_10801", "pubmed23n0004_13213", "pubmed23n0055_404", "pubmed23n0025_7340", "pubmed23n0053_250", "Surgery_Schwartz_12423"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"total": 300.0, "retrieval": 9093.378625053447, "llm": 916.1379159777425, "verification": 735.6350000482053}}}
{"topic": "GERD", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the mechanism of action of a medication used to treat persistent GERD, and what are its effects on the gastrointestinal system?", "options": {"A": "D2 receptor antagonist that promotes gastric emptying and increases lower esophageal sphincter tone", "B": "\u03bc-opioid receptor agonist that slows gut motility", "C": "5-HT3 antagonist that stimulates vagal stimulation", "D": "H2 receptor antagonist that reduces acid production"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The correct answer is supported by the evidence, which states that the medication is a D2 receptor antagonist that promotes gastric emptying and increases lower esophageal sphincter tone, making it useful for treating persistent GERD.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "First_Aid_Step1_433", "title": "First_Aid_Step1", "span_text": "meCHanism D2 receptor antagonist. \u008f resting tone, contractility, LES tone, motility, promotes gastric emptying. Does not influence colon transport time. CliniCal Use Diabetic and postoperative gastroparesis, antiemetic, persistent GERD."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "exact match", "doc_ids": ["First_Aid_Step1_433"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["First_Aid_Step1_433"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "GERD Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 4814.20274998527, "llm_ms": 926.6845000092871, "verification_ms": 812.8056660061702, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 0, "INSUFFICIENT_E