{"topic": "Pancreatitis", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the primary goal of surgical management in patients with necrotizing pancreatitis?", "options": {"A": "To remove the entire pancreas", "B": "To carefully remove necrotic tissue and drain infected areas", "C": "To perform a cholecystectomy", "D": "To administer antibiotics"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The primary goal of surgical management in patients with necrotizing pancreatitis is to carefully remove necrotic tissue and drain infected areas, as this approach has been shown to be effective in reducing mortality and improving outcomes.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0062_1499", "title": "Surgery in acute pancreatitis", "span_text": "Carefully performed necrosectomy or debridement, in combination with continuous or repeatedly applied surgical evacuation techniques for necrotic tissue, bacteria, and biologically active compounds, has proved to be very effective in experienced treatment centers."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0011_3770", "Surgery_Schwartz_9958", "pubmed23n0062_1499", "pubmed23n0060_14369", "pubmed23n0001_7283", "pubmed23n0049_6845", "pubmed23n0053_6692", "InternalMed_Harrison_24381", "pubmed23n0054_963", "Surgery_Schwartz_9712", "pubmed23n0036_856", "Surgery_Schwartz_9708", "Surgery_Schwartz_9547", "pubmed23n0036_176", "pubmed23n0016_10164", "pubmed23n0033_9851", "pubmed23n0055_19653", "InternalMed_Harrison_10179", "pubmed23n0059_17817", "pubmed23n0059_17813", "pubmed23n0036_777", "pubmed23n0050_14687", "pubmed23n0011_7046", "pubmed23n0021_2092", "pubmed23n0047_5741"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0011_3770", "Surgery_Schwartz_9958", "pubmed23n0062_1499", "pubmed23n0060_14369", "pubmed23n0001_7283", "pubmed23n0049_6845", "pubmed23n0053_6692", "InternalMed_Harrison_24381", "pubmed23n0054_963", "Surgery_Schwartz_9712", "pubmed23n0036_856", "Surgery_Schwartz_9708", "Surgery_Schwartz_9547", "pubmed23n0036