{"topic": "Iron deficiency anemia", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is a useful screening method for detecting iron deficiency in blood donors?", "options": {"A": "Erythrocyte protoporphyrin measurement", "B": "Serum ferritin", "C": "Transferrin saturation", "D": "Mean corpuscular volume"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Erythrocyte protoporphyrin measurement is a simple and low-cost screening test that can detect early iron deficiency in blood donors.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0062_8871", "title": "[The value of erythrocytic protoporphyrin measurement for screening blood donors for iron deficiency: a decision analysis]", "span_text": "Erythrocyte protoporphyrin assay on an hematofluorometer is very easy and of a low cost. So we studied its diagnostic value on a sample of 285 blood donors (131 men and 154 women)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0002_11976", "pubmed23n0062_8871", "pubmed23n0059_1424", "pubmed23n0050_21391", "pubmed23n0043_18931", "pubmed23n0061_519", "InternalMed_Harrison_29042", "Pediatrics_Nelson_130", "pubmed23n0058_13451"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0002_11976", "pubmed23n0062_8871", "pubmed23n0059_1424", "pubmed23n0050_21391", "pubmed23n0043_18931", "pubmed23n0061_519", "InternalMed_Harrison_29042", "Pediatrics_Nelson_130", "pubmed23n0058_13451"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Iron deficiency anemia Screening screening early detection risk assessment screening test sensitivity specificity guideline population screening high-risk preventive care follow-up diagnostic threshold", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 10326.440000033472, "llm_ms": 906.7129580071196, "verification_ms": 783.5455419844948, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rera