{"topic": "Hepatitis C", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the primary method for screening for hepatitis C virus infection?", "options": {"A": "Liver biopsy", "B": "Testing for the presence of antibodies to HCV in serum", "C": "Measuring alanine aminotransferase levels", "D": "Assessing patient history and physical findings"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The primary method for screening for hepatitis C virus infection is to test for the presence of antibodies to HCV in serum, as this generally indicates either a current infection or a previous infection that the patient\u2019s immune system has successfully cleared.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_32561", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "A common approach is to test first for the presence of antibodies to HCV in serum. A positive result generally indicates either a current infection or a previous infection that the patient\u2019s immune system has successfully cleared."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23270", "pubmed23n0042_11887", "pubmed23n0044_8840", "pubmed23n0044_7855", "pubmed23n0056_18913", "pubmed23n0027_1630", "InternalMed_Harrison_32561", "pubmed23n0055_7729", "pubmed23n0002_8348", "pubmed23n0006_5951", "pubmed23n0044_8646", "pubmed23n0044_13968", "pubmed23n0003_10892", "pubmed23n0003_37"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23270", "pubmed23n0042_11887", "pubmed23n0044_8840", "pubmed23n0044_7855", "pubmed23n0056_18913", "pubmed23n0027_1630", "InternalMed_Harrison_32561", "pubmed23n0055_7729", "pubmed23n0002_8348", "pubmed23n0006_5951", "pubmed23n0044_8646", "pubmed23n0044_13968", "pubmed23n0003_10892", "pubmed23n0003_37"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hepatitis C Investigation inves