{"topic": "Chronic pain", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the primary goal of community-based screening programs for chronic health conditions?", "options": {"A": "To provide medical treatment for individuals with chronic diseases", "B": "To identify asymptomatic individuals who have the disease or are at risk for developing it", "C": "To promote health education and risk-reduction programs", "D": "To develop effective screening programs for biochemical markers"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The primary goal of community-based screening programs for chronic health conditions is to identify asymptomatic individuals who have the disease or are at risk for developing it, allowing for early intervention and prevention.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_20496", "title": "Guidelines for community-based screening for chronic health conditions", "span_text": "Preventive measures for many chronic diseases depend upon identification of asymptomatic individuals who have the disease or who may be at risk for developing it."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_20496", "pubmed23n0043_3127", "pubmed23n0049_16517", "pubmed23n0021_6096", "InternalMed_Harrison_19039"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_20496", "pubmed23n0043_3127", "pubmed23n0049_16517", "pubmed23n0021_6096", "InternalMed_Harrison_19039"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Chronic pain Screening screening early detection risk assessment screening test sensitivity specificity guideline population screening high-risk preventive care follow-up diagnostic threshold", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 10408.620083006099, "llm_ms": 983.9160000556149, "verification_ms": 886.1545830150135, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "