{"topic": "GERD", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is the primary method for establishing a diagnosis of reflux esophagitis and excluding other esophageal diseases?", "options": {"A": "Endoscopy", "B": "Fluoroscopy", "C": "Ambulatory 24-hour esophageal pH-monitoring", "D": "The Bernstein test"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Endoscopy is necessary for diagnosing reflux esophagitis and ruling out other esophageal conditions.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0052_17375", "title": "Diagnostic assessment of gastroesophageal reflux disease: what is possible vs. what is practical?", "span_text": "Endoscopy is mandatory to establish a diagnosis of reflux esophagitis, to exclude other esophageal disease and to permit directed biopsy if columnar metaplasia, dysplasia or carcinoma is suspected."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "exact_match", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_17375"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_17375"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert_review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "GERD Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 10070.981791999657, "llm_ms": 905.2409160067327, "verification_ms": 728.9684169809334, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 0, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 1}, "failed_checks": ["reviewer_mismatch"], "failed_checks_all": ["reviewer_mismatch"], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0052_17375"], "evidence_reused": false}, {"attempt": 2, "reason": "v5_reviewer", "query": "GERD Diagnosis diagnosis differential d