{"topic": "Osteoarthritis", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism by which oxaprozin, a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug, decreases pain and inflammatory responses in osteoarthritis?", "options": {"A": "Inhibiting cyclo-oxygenase and decreasing prostaglandin biosynthesis", "B": "Increasing the formation of prostaglandin precursors from arachidonic acid", "C": "Enhancing the elimination of the drug by urinary excretion", "D": "Reducing the absorption of the drug after oral administration"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Oxaprozin works by inhibiting cyclo-oxygenase, which decreases the formation of prostaglandin precursors from arachidonic acid, resulting in decreased prostaglandin biosynthesis and reduced pain and inflammatory responses.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0054_3142", "title": "Oxaprozin: a once-daily nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug", "span_text": "By inhibiting cyclo-oxygenase, oxaprozin decreases the formation of prostaglandin (PG) precursors from arachidonic acid, resulting in decreased PG biosynthesis and reduced pain and inflammatory responses."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "pubmed", "query": "oxaprozin mechanism of action", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_3142", "pubmed23n0057_5403"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_3142", "pubmed23n0057_5403"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteoarthritis Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6203.467042010743, "llm_ms": 915.8339160494506, "verification_ms": 800.905124982819, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_reran