{"topic": "Myocardial infarction", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the recommended dosage of clopidogrel for patients with non-ST-elevation acute myocardial infarction (NSTEMI) in combination with aspirin?", "options": {"A": "300-mg loading dose orally followed by 75 mg daily of clopidogrel, with a daily aspirin dosage of 75\u2013325 mg", "B": "75 mg daily of clopidogrel orally, in association with aspirin as above", "C": "150 mg three times a day, but up to 1 g/d has been used", "D": "A 300-mg loading dose orally followed by 150 mg daily of clopidogrel, with a daily aspirin dosage of 75\u2013325 mg"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The correct dosage of clopidogrel for patients with NSTEMI in combination with aspirin is a 300-mg loading dose orally followed by 75 mg daily of clopidogrel, with a daily aspirin dosage of 75\u2013325 mg.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_3818", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Clopidogrel is approved for patients with unstable angina or non-ST-elevation acute myocardial infarction (NSTEMI) in combination with aspirin; for patients with ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI); or recent myocardial infarction, stroke, or established peripheral arterial disease. For NSTEMI, the dosage is a 300-mg loading dose orally followed by 75 mg daily of clopidogrel, with a daily aspirin dosage of 75\u2013325 mg."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_6141", "pubmed23n0013_9855", "pubmed23n0057_16532", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1206", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1405", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3019", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3807", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4715", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3818", "Pharmacology_Katzung_987"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_6141", "pubmed23n0013_9855", "pubmed23n0057_16532", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1206", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1405", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3019", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3807", "Pharmacology_Katzung