{"topic": "Osteoarthritis", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What are the biochemical changes that occur in the cartilage of osteoarthritic joints?", "options": {"A": "Decrease in glycosaminoglycan content and increase in the rate of glycosaminoglycan synthesis", "B": "Increase in glycosaminoglycan content and decrease in the rate of glycosaminoglycan synthesis", "C": "No change in glycosaminoglycan content and rate of glycosaminoglycan synthesis", "D": "Increase in glycosaminoglycan content and no change in the rate of glycosaminoglycan synthesis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The biochemical changes that occur in the cartilage of osteoarthritic joints include a decrease in the content of glycosaminoglycan and an increase in the rate of glycosaminoglycan synthesis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0017_9722", "title": "An experimental study on the pathogenesis of osteoarthritis--histological and biochemical changes of proteoglycan in the osteoarthritic cartilage of rabbit in the early stage-- (author's transl)", "span_text": "Biochemical analysis of the cartilage from experimental osteoarthritic model demonstrated a decrease in the content of glycosaminoglycan and increase in the rate of the synthesis of glycosaminoglycan as compared to the normals."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2022-01-01 12:00:00", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0017_9722", "pubmed23n0058_16371", "pubmed23n0053_6016", "pubmed23n0062_8959", "pubmed23n0025_9583"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0017_9722", "pubmed23n0058_16371", "pubmed23n0053_6016", "pubmed23n0062_8959", "pubmed23n0025_9583"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": "2022-01-01 12:05:00", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteoarthritis Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physi