{"topic": "Diarrhea", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the primary goal of supportive therapy in the management of diarrhea?", "options": {"A": "To treat the underlying cause of diarrhea", "B": "To improve the consistency of the stool and reduce the frequency of bowel movements", "C": "To replace lost fluids and electrolytes", "D": "To block the cellular mechanisms of fluid and electrolyte loss"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "Supportive therapy in the management of diarrhea focuses on replacing lost fluids and electrolytes to prevent dehydration and maintain proper bodily functions.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0004_9746", "title": "Drug therapy reviews: pharmacotherapy of diarrhea", "span_text": "The management of diarrhea can be divided into three categories: (1) supportive therapy (fluid and electrolyte replacement);"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0004_9746", "pubmed23n0048_1407", "pubmed23n0060_17565", "pubmed23n0060_17563", "pubmed23n0010_6814", "pubmed23n0047_13138", "pubmed23n0008_7040"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0004_9746", "pubmed23n0048_1407", "pubmed23n0060_17565", "pubmed23n0060_17563", "pubmed23n0010_6814", "pubmed23n0047_13138", "pubmed23n0008_7040"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Diarrhea Treatment treatment therapy management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7001.697999949101, "llm_ms": 890.999999945052, "verification_ms": 1105.5700419819914, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_