{"topic": "Cirrhosis", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is the most sensitive test for diagnosing alcoholic cirrhosis?", "options": {"A": "Gamma-GT test", "B": "Laparoscopy and puncture biopsy", "C": "Endoscopy", "D": "Per-rectal portal scintigraphy with technetium-99m pertechnetate"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The gamma-GT test is the most sensitive in alcoholic cirrhosis, but may be more an expression of the degree of alcoholism than of the hepatic lesion per se.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0002_2921", "title": "Liver cirrhosis. Clinical and biological aspects", "span_text": "The gamma-GT test is the most sensitive in alcoholic cirrhosis, but may be more an expression of the degree of alcoholism than of the hepatic lesion per se."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23994", "pubmed23n0029_3344", "pubmed23n0053_4666", "pubmed23n0055_21421", "pubmed23n0012_40", "pubmed23n0007_7379", "pubmed23n0058_19908", "pubmed23n0042_12216", "pubmed23n0002_2921", "pubmed23n0044_8663", "pubmed23n0002_9291"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23994", "pubmed23n0029_3344", "pubmed23n0053_4666", "pubmed23n0055_21421", "pubmed23n0012_40", "pubmed23n0007_7379", "pubmed23n0058_19908", "pubmed23n0042_12216", "pubmed23n0002_2921", "pubmed23n0044_8663", "pubmed23n0002_9291"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Cirrhosis Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 8822.684374987148, "llm_ms": 1019.376625015866, "verification_ms": 821.4679160155356, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode