{"topic": "Allergic rhinitis", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the primary use of antihistamines in the treatment of allergic rhinitis?", "options": {"A": "To reduce inflammation", "B": "To block peripheral histamine receptors", "C": "To treat cardiac arrhythmias", "D": "To prevent infection"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Antihistamines are valuable drugs for treating allergic rhinitis by blocking peripheral histamine receptors.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0001_5978", "title": "Pharmacology and therapeutic use of antihistamines", "span_text": "It is concluded that antihistamines are valuable drugs for treating a number of conditions and diseases (e.g. allergic rhinitis, motion sickness and parkinsonism), but proof of efficacy has not been established for the treatment of cardiac arrhythmias, peptic ulcers, insomnia and headaches."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0001_5978", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1670", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1549", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5325", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6457", "pubmed23n0054_3142", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4732", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6212", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5941", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7143", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5326", "pubmed23n0008_11737", "pubmed23n0046_4884", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6210", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6779", "pubmed23n0062_2927", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2145", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5834", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4575"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0001_5978", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1670", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1549", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5325", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6457", "pubmed23n0054_3142", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4732", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6212", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5941", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7143", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5326", "pubmed23n0008_11737", "pubmed23n0046_4884", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6210", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6779", "pubmed23n0062_2927", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2145", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5834", "Pharmacology