{"topic": "Hepatitis C", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What laboratory test is required for the diagnosis of hepatitis C?", "options": {"A": "Quantitative HCV RNA testing", "B": "Hepatitis B serologies", "C": "Liver biopsy", "D": "Complete blood count"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Quantitative HCV RNA testing is necessary for the diagnosis of hepatitis C, as it measures the amount of viral RNA in the blood.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_23994", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Diagnosis requires a thorough laboratory evaluation, including quantitative HCV RNA testing and analysis for HCV genotype, or hepatitis B serologies to include HBsAg, anti-HBs, HBeAg (hepatitis B e antigen), anti-HBe, and quantitative HBV DNA levels."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23994", "InternalMed_Harrison_23270", "InternalMed_Harrison_12697", "pubmed23n0045_2021", "InternalMed_Harrison_23900", "pubmed23n0055_7729", "pubmed23n0027_1630", "pubmed23n0056_18913", "pubmed23n0059_12611", "pubmed23n0002_8348", "pubmed23n0039_10215", "pubmed23n0016_5491", "InternalMed_Harrison_23904", "pubmed23n0053_4666", "pubmed23n0003_37"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23994", "InternalMed_Harrison_23270", "InternalMed_Harrison_12697", "pubmed23n0045_2021", "InternalMed_Harrison_23900", "pubmed23n0055_7729", "pubmed23n0027_1630", "pubmed23n0056_18913", "pubmed23n0059_12611", "pubmed23n0002_8348", "pubmed23n0039_10215", "pubmed23n0016_5491", "InternalMed_Harrison_23904", "pubmed23n0053_4666", "pubmed23n0003_37"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hepatitis C Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory f