{"topic": "Acne", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "A 25-year-old woman presents with moderate to severe acne and is considering treatment options. What is the potential benefit of using a topical antioxidant serum containing vitamin C, vitamin E, and ferulic acid after ablative fractional CO2 laser treatment for her atrophic acne scars?", "options": {"A": "Enhanced wound healing and reduced erythema", "B": "Increased risk of post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation", "C": "Decreased skin hydration and increased trans-epidermal water loss", "D": "No significant improvement in acne scar appearance"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The use of a topical antioxidant serum containing vitamin C, vitamin E, and ferulic acid after ablative fractional CO2 laser treatment has been shown to enhance wound healing, reduce erythema and melanin levels, and improve skin hydration in patients with atrophic acne scars.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41521693", "title": "Reparative Effects of a Topical Antioxidant Serum Containing Vitamin C, Vitamin E, and Ferulic Acid After Ablative Fractional CO", "span_text": "This study found that CE Ferulic led to enhanced wound healing, reduced erythema and melanin levels, and improved skin hydration following laser treatment, suggesting its beneficial application in combination with laser treatment to accelerate skin recovery."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41580621", "pubmed_web_41552868", "pubmed_web_41543972", "pubmed_web_41539852", "pubmed_web_41521693", "pubmed_web_41499938", "pubmed_web_41492791", "pubmed_web_41487026", "pubmed_web_41482092", "pubmed_web_41476262", "pubmed_web_41471115", "pubmed_web_41467245", "pubmed_web_41466591", "pubmed_web_41465543", "pubmed_web_41457483", "pubmed_web_41447583", "pubmed_web_41439563", "pubmed_web_41428599", "pubmed_web_41421802", "pubmed_web_41416232"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41552868", "pubmed_web_41543972