{"topic": "Immunization", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is a major risk factor for liver cancer that can be prevented through immunization?", "options": {"A": "Hepatitis B infection", "B": "Hepatitis A infection", "C": "Influenza infection", "D": "Human papillomavirus infection"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Hepatitis B immunization in children has been shown to reduce the incidence of liver cancer, indicating that hepatitis B infection is a major risk factor for liver cancer that can be prevented through immunization.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Surgery_Schwartz_2072", "title": "Surgery_Schwartz", "span_text": "Worldwide, the major risk factors for liver cancer are infection with hepatitis B and C viruses and consumption of foods contaminated with aflatoxin. Hepatitis B immunization in children has recently been shown to reduce the incidence of liver cancer."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["Surgery_Schwartz_2072", "pubmed23n0029_3293"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Surgery_Schwartz_2072", "pubmed23n0029_3293"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Immunization Etiology etiology cause risk factors pathogenesis mechanism underlying cause genetic factors environmental factors predisposing factors associated conditions epidemiology incidence", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6943.382834026124, "llm_ms": 945.4173750127666, "verification_ms": 763.0159999825992, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Surgery_Schwartz_2072", "pubmed23n0029_32