{"topic": "Peptic ulcer disease", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the general trend in survival for patients with peptic ulcer disease, particularly in the first year or two after diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "The excess of deaths is significant and persists throughout the patient's life.", "B": "The excess of deaths is small and is present only in the first year or two after the diagnosis.", "C": "The survival rate is significantly different for men and women.", "D": "The prognosis is more serious in duodenal ulcer than in gastric ulcer."}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The prognosis in peptic ulcer disease tends to have a small excess of deaths, primarily within the first year or two after diagnosis, with the difference between gastric and duodenal ulcers not being significant.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0024_4559", "title": "Survival in peptic ulcer", "span_text": "The two methods of analysis both showed that peptic ulcer does influence the survival, but the excess of deaths was small and, in the case of solitary peptic ulcer, was present only in the first year or two after the diagnosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_17698", "pubmed23n0024_4559", "pubmed23n0060_1027", "pubmed23n0057_22094", "pubmed23n0063_20179", "pubmed23n0022_11030", "Surgery_Schwartz_7669", "pubmed23n0050_3346", "pubmed23n0048_18301", "pubmed23n0034_1116", "pubmed23n0062_5690", "pubmed23n0056_2351", "pubmed23n0045_2592", "pubmed23n0063_19435", "pubmed23n0045_3995", "pubmed23n0062_981", "pubmed23n0011_10604", "Surgery_Schwartz_9248", "Obstentrics_Williams_7330", "pubmed23n0017_11173", "pubmed23n0014_9879", "pubmed23n0053_7061", "pubmed23n0049_12951", "pubmed23n0013_6783", "pubmed23n0003_12412", "pubmed23n0054_7544", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3447", "pubmed23n0038_728", "pubmed23n0060_1847", "pubmed23n0063_10697", "pubmed23n0032_7390", "pubmed23n0021_11297", "pubmed23n0045_31