{"topic": "Hepatitis B", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the primary goal of antiviral therapy in patients with chronic hepatitis B?", "options": {"A": "To reduce aminotransferase levels and HBV DNA levels", "B": "To increase inflammation and fibrosis", "C": "To promote the development of ascites and edema", "D": "To exacerbate encephalopathy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Antiviral therapy is effective at viral suppression, as evidenced by reducing aminotransferase levels and HBV DNA levels, and improving histology by reducing inflammation and fibrosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_23995", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "In patients with chronic hepatitis B, numerous studies have shown beneficial effects of antiviral therapy, which is effective at viral suppression, as evidenced by reducing aminotransferase levels and HBV DNA levels, and improving histology by reducing inflammation and fibrosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2023-02-20", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0055_17212", "pubmed23n0043_1179", "InternalMed_Harrison_13598", "InternalMed_Harrison_23295", "pubmed23n0010_483", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6103", "InternalMed_Harrison_23995", "pubmed23n0020_8204"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0055_17212", "pubmed23n0043_1179", "InternalMed_Harrison_13598", "InternalMed_Harrison_23295", "pubmed23n0010_483", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6103", "InternalMed_Harrison_23995", "pubmed23n0020_8204"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": "2023-02-20", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hepatitis B Therapy therapy treatment management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 8584.892291983124, "llm_ms": 951.1516249622218, "