{"topic": "Pneumonia", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the characteristic feature of rheumatoid pneumonia in the lungs?", "options": {"A": "Necrotic vasculitis, fibrinoid necrosis or thrombovasculitis of the pulmonary and bronchial arterioles", "B": "Interstitial pneumonia with rheumatoid nodule formation", "C": "Obliterative bronchiolitis with amyloidosis", "D": "Lipoid pneumonia caused by mineral oil"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Rheumatoid pneumonia is characterized by necrotic vasculitis, fibrinoid necrosis or thrombovasculitis of the pulmonary and bronchial arterioles, and of small arteries, leading to diminished blood supply and inflammatory foci.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0059_18382", "title": "Changes of the lung in rheumatoid arthritis--rheumatoid pneumonia. A clinicopathological study.", "span_text": "The rheumatoid pneumonia is a disseminating inflammatory lobular-sublobular process, not described previously. The frequency of rheumatoid pneumonia was 4%. The rheumatoid pneumonia is characterized by the necrotic vasculitis, fibrinoid necrosis or thrombovasculitis of the pulmonary and bronchial arterioles, and of small arteries."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0005_7701", "pubmed23n0059_17398", "pubmed23n0059_18382", "pubmed23n0004_1032", "pubmed23n0058_11527"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0005_7701", "pubmed23n0059_17398", "pubmed23n0059_18382", "pubmed23n0004_1032", "pubmed23n0058_11527"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Pneumonia Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index