{"topic": "Hypertension", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the primary benefit of using ambulatory blood pressure monitoring in the management of antihypertensive therapy?", "options": {"A": "To provide a more accurate diagnosis of hypertension", "B": "To monitor the effectiveness of antihypertensive medication", "C": "To identify patients with white coat hypertension", "D": "To predict the risk of cardiovascular disease"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Ambulatory blood pressure monitoring allows for the continuous measurement of blood pressure over a 24-hour period, providing a more accurate assessment of blood pressure patterns and the effectiveness of antihypertensive therapy.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0043_93", "title": "Use of ambulatory blood pressure monitoring in the management of antihypertensive therapy", "span_text": "The application of ABP differs according to which of these 2 applications is being considered. In therapeutic trials, a placebo control is required. The large quantity of precise data acquired with ABP monitoring allows the study of a limited number of patients; it also allows individual study of patients with a 'white coat' response (i.e. elevated blood pressure in response to examination by the clinician)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_6959", "pubmed23n0054_3416", "pubmed23n0043_93", "pubmed23n0059_6801", "Obstentrics_Williams_6445", "pubmed23n0049_3318", "pubmed23n0062_3510", "pubmed23n0055_1864", "InternalMed_Harrison_19565", "pubmed23n0063_7177", "pubmed23n0056_3533", "pubmed23n0060_3043", "pubmed23n0060_1040", "pubmed23n0059_20080", "pubmed23n0063_11792", "pubmed23n0043_17568", "pubmed23n0056_11748", "pubmed23n0054_18051", "pubmed23n0054_11561", "pubmed23n0063_7178", "pubmed23n0063_7173", "pubmed23n0037_11105", "InternalMed_Harrison_22965", "pubmed23n0060_1026", "pubmed23n0063_7176", "pubmed23n0017_3637", "pubmed23n0050_13123", "p