{"topic": "Heart failure", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the primary goal of risk assessment in the prevention of heart disease?", "options": {"A": "To identify patients who require immediate medical attention", "B": "To determine the best course of treatment for patients with heart disease", "C": "To guide detection and interpretation of symptoms that could reflect an STD", "D": "To assess the risk of heart disease and guide preventive measures"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "Risk assessment is a crucial step in the prevention of heart disease, as it helps identify individuals who are at high risk of developing the condition and guides preventive measures.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "InternalMed_Harrison STD care and management begin with risk assessment and proceed to clinical assessment, diagnostic testing or screening, treatment, and prevention. Indeed, the routine care of any patient begins with risk assessment (e.g., for risk of heart disease, cancer)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "pubmed23n0063_11753", "Surgery_Schwartz_5388", "pubmed23n0063_3886", "pubmed23n0054_4200", "InternalMed_Harrison_17264", "pubmed23n0024_1190", "pubmed23n0061_8532", "pubmed23n0007_6598", "InternalMed_Harrison_11663", "pubmed23n0043_573", "pubmed23n0052_13402", "pubmed23n0063_21353", "pubmed23n0038_9414", "pubmed23n0061_8802", "pubmed23n0060_14011", "pubmed23n0054_2264", "InternalMed_Harrison_29933", "pubmed23n0043_1659", "pubmed23n0058_12921", "pubmed23n0022_5378", "pubmed23n0025_10436", "InternalMed_Harrison_10524", "pubmed23n0060_225", "pubmed23n0043_101"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "pubmed23n0063_11753", "Surgery_Schwartz_5388", "pubmed23n0063_3886", "pubmed23n0054_4200", "InternalMed_Harrison_17264", "pubmed23n0024_1190", "pubmed23n0061_8532", "pubmed23n0007_6598", "Inte