{"topic": "Acne", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the expected outcome of using clindamycin phosphate 1.2%/adapalene 0.15%/benzoyl peroxide 3.1% gel for the long-term treatment of acne vulgaris?", "options": {"A": "Significant reduction in inflammatory and noninflammatory lesions", "B": "No improvement in acne severity", "C": "Increased risk of scarring and dyspigmentation", "D": "Only temporary relief from acne symptoms"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The treatment is expected to significantly reduce inflammatory and noninflammatory lesions, making it an effective topical option for the long-term treatment of acne vulgaris.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41552868", "title": "Long-term efficacy and tolerability of clindamycin phosphate 1.2%/adapalene 0.15%/benzoyl peroxide 3.1% gel for acne: pooled results from two 6-month studies", "span_text": "At week 24, 67% of participants achieved treatment success, and significant reductions from baseline in inflammatory (88%) and noninflammatory (68%) lesions were observed"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41562471", "pubmed_web_41552868", "pubmed_web_41546576", "pubmed_web_41537698", "pubmed_web_41538670", "pubmed_web_41521693", "pubmed_web_41492791", "pubmed_web_41487026", "pubmed_web_41457483", "pubmed_web_41428599", "pubmed_web_41412995", "pubmed_web_41412986", "pubmed_web_41405932", "pubmed_web_41353672", "pubmed_web_41347526", "pubmed_web_41341579", "pubmed_web_41329150", "pubmed_web_41329145", "pubmed_web_41307186", "pubmed_web_41298831"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41562471", "pubmed_web_41552868", "pubmed_web_41546576", "pubmed_web_41537698", "pubmed_web_41538670", "pubmed_web_41521693", "pubmed_web_41492791", "pubmed_web_41487026", "pubmed_web_41457483", "pubmed_web_41428599", "pubmed_web_41412995", "pubmed_web_41412986", "pubmed_web_41405932", "pubmed_web_41353672", "pubmed_web_41347526", "pubmed_web_41341579", "pu