{"topic": "Pancreatitis", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 35-year-old man presents with severe abdominal pain radiating to the back, nausea, and vomiting. What is the most appropriate initial diagnostic step to confirm acute pancreatitis?", "options": {"A": "Measure serum lipase and/or amylase levels", "B": "Perform an abdominal ultrasound", "C": "Conduct endoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography (ERCP)", "D": "Order a computed tomography (CT) scan"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The diagnosis of acute pancreatitis is typically established by a combination of clinical presentation and laboratory tests, including serum lipase and/or amylase levels. While imaging studies such as ultrasound, CT, or ERCP may be useful in certain cases, they are not the initial diagnostic step.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0047_21213", "title": "Pancreatitis heralding Kawasaki disease", "span_text": "A 5 1/2 year-old boy was hospitalized with clinical and laboratory evidence of pancreatitis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0023_5526", "pubmed23n0047_21213", "pubmed23n0013_3149", "InternalMed_Harrison_24368", "pubmed23n0062_1500", "pubmed23n0004_1792", "pubmed23n0062_5886", "InternalMed_Harrison_24307", "pubmed23n0056_18914", "InternalMed_Harrison_24367", "pubmed23n0020_6557", "pubmed23n0034_4853", "Surgery_Schwartz_9644", "Surgery_Schwartz_9662", "InternalMed_Harrison_24327", "pubmed23n0045_14443", "pubmed23n0051_2481", "pubmed23n0012_1885", "pubmed23n0030_8799", "pubmed23n0049_12899", "pubmed23n0024_278", "pubmed23n0016_856", "pubmed23n0026_1400"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0023_5526", "pubmed23n0047_21213", "pubmed23n0013_3149", "InternalMed_Harrison_24368", "pubmed23n0062_1500", "pubmed23n0004_1792", "pubmed23n0062_5886", "InternalMed_Harrison_24307", "pubmed23n0056_18914", "InternalMed_Harrison_24367", "pubmed23n0020_6557", "pubmed23n0034_4853", "Surgery_Schwartz_9644", "Surgery_Schwartz_96