{"topic": "Dehydration", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is crucial to monitor during the correction of hypernatremic dehydration to minimize the risk of cerebral edema?", "options": {"A": "Serum sodium concentration", "B": "Fluid intake", "C": "Urine output", "D": "Blood pressure"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Monitoring the serum sodium concentration is essential to avoid a rapid decrease, which can lead to cerebral edema. The serum sodium concentration should not decrease more than 12 mEq/L every 24 hours.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pediatrics_Nelson_731", "title": "Pediatrics_Nelson", "span_text": "To minimize the risk of cerebral edema during correctionof hypernatremic dehydration, the serum sodium concentration should not decrease more than 12 mEq/L every 24 hours"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0017_3996", "Pediatrics_Nelson_731"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0017_3996", "Pediatrics_Nelson_731"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Dehydration Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 8210.331208014395, "llm_ms": 805.3114580106921, "verification_ms": 1946.9881249824539, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0017_3996", "Pediatrics_Nelson_731"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 100.0, "verification": 2