{"topic": "Malaria", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the primary goal of the Kilombero Malaria Project in Tanzania?", "options": {"A": "To define operationally useful indicators of levels of transmission and disease", "B": "To develop a new antimalarial drug", "C": "To conduct a double-blind randomized comparative study of mefloquine", "D": "To monitor the emergence of multidrug-resistant Plasmodium falciparum"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The Kilombero Malaria Project aims to define operationally useful indicators of levels of transmission and disease, as well as health system relevant monitoring indicators, to evaluate the impact of disease control at the community or health facility level.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0045_139", "title": "Household-based malaria control in a highly endemic area of Africa (Tanzania): determinants of transmission and disease and indicators for monitoring--Kilombero Malaria Project", "span_text": "The Kilombero Malaria Project (KMP) attempts to define operationally useful indicators of levels of transmission and disease and health system relevant monitoring indicators to evaluate the impact of disease control at the community or health facility level."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "Kilombero Malaria Project", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0045_139", "pubmed23n0062_4436", "pubmed23n0054_16850", "pubmed23n0045_166"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0045_139", "pubmed23n0062_4436", "pubmed23n0054_16850", "pubmed23n0045_166"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Malaria Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index"