{"topic": "Depression", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the effect of cognitive therapy on the relapse rate of patients with depression?", "options": {"A": "Cognitive therapy reduces the relapse rate of patients with depression.", "B": "Cognitive therapy has no effect on the relapse rate of patients with depression.", "C": "Cognitive therapy increases the relapse rate of patients with depression.", "D": "The effect of cognitive therapy on the relapse rate of patients with depression is unknown."}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Cognitive therapy has been shown to reduce the relapse rate of patients with depression. This is because cognitive therapy helps patients to identify and change negative thought patterns and behaviors that contribute to their depression.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0047_9565", "title": "Differential relapse following cognitive therapy and pharmacotherapy for depression.", "span_text": "Patients treated with cognitive therapy (either alone or in combination with medication) evidenced less than half the rate of relapse shown by patients in the medication--no continuation condition, and their rate did not differ from that of patients provided with continuation medication."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_2200", "pubmed23n0047_9565", "pubmed23n0056_2610", "pubmed23n0062_10204", "pubmed23n0047_9561", "pubmed23n0056_4757", "pubmed23n0053_6874", "pubmed23n0062_112", "pubmed23n0052_13251", "pubmed23n0057_17817", "pubmed23n0051_18119", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1218", "pubmed23n0057_21089", "pubmed23n0063_14292", "Gynecology_Novak_7625", "pubmed23n0001_13261", "pubmed23n0014_10259", "pubmed23n0059_6938", "pubmed23n0053_19325", "pubmed23n0002_2987", "pubmed23n0060_12863"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_2200", "pubmed23n0047_9565", "pubmed23n0056_2610", "pubmed23n0062_10204", "pubmed23n0047_9561", "pubmed23n0056_4757", "pubmed23n0053_6874", "pubme