{"topic": "Dermatitis", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "A patient with eczematous dermatitis is prescribed a topical corticosteroid. Which of the following formulations may be used for the management of this condition?", "options": {"A": "0.1 percent amcinonide cream", "B": "0.05 percent betamethasone valerate ointment", "C": "2 percent hydrocortisone lotion", "D": "1 percent triamcinolone acetonide gel"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient may be prescribed 0.1 percent amcinonide cream for the management of eczematous dermatitis, as it has been shown to be safe and effective in a double-blind, parallel study.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0013_9304", "title": "Management of eczematous dermatitis with amcinonide or betamethasone valerate", "span_text": "A new topical corticosteroid formulation, 0.1 percent amcinonide cream, was compared with 0.1 percent betamethasone valerate cream in a double-blind, parallel study of the management of eczematous dermatitis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_4043", "InternalMed_Harrison_16952", "pubmed23n0042_14476", "pubmed23n0013_9304", "pubmed23n0051_20999", "pubmed23n0012_7561", "pubmed23n0062_14665"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_16952", "pubmed23n0042_14476", "pubmed23n0013_9304", "pubmed23n0051_20999", "pubmed23n0012_7561", "pubmed23n0062_14665", "Pediatrics_Nelson_4043"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Dermatitis Treatment treatment therapy management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6991.061125008855, "llm_ms": 1206.357792019844, "verification_ms": 973.521834006533, "extra_instructions": "", 