{"topic": "Prostate cancer", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the primary role of serum prostate specific antigen in the early detection of prostate cancer?", "options": {"A": "To confirm the diagnosis of prostate cancer", "B": "To screen for prostate cancer and identify individuals at high risk", "C": "To monitor the progression of prostate cancer", "D": "To determine the stage of prostate cancer"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Serum prostate specific antigen is used as a screening test to identify individuals at high risk of prostate cancer, allowing for early detection and potential curative treatment.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0045_19421", "title": "Serum prostate specific antigen as pre-screening test for prostate cancer", "span_text": "Prostate cancer has become the most common cancer and the second cause of death due to cancer in men in North America. Since curative therapies are limited to early stages of the disease, the availability of an efficient, easy to perform, widely acceptable and cost-effective method of early detection of prostate cancer is particularly important."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_20199", "pubmed23n0045_19421", "Surgery_Schwartz_3920", "pubmed23n0015_6391", "pubmed23n0014_13380", "pubmed23n0014_9733", "pubmed23n0057_15721", "pubmed23n0041_8955", "pubmed23n0056_16753", "pubmed23n0020_9012", "pubmed23n0046_6458", "pubmed23n0013_8315", "pubmed23n0063_11624", "pubmed23n0046_2312", "pubmed23n0049_3106", "pubmed23n0033_12207", "Surgery_Schwartz_11662", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "pubmed23n0051_6910", "pubmed23n0041_5855", "pubmed23n0030_11306", "pubmed23n0002_9792", "pubmed23n0059_1427", "pubmed23n0036_10638", "pubmed23n0036_7308", "pubmed23n0052_7446", "pubmed23n0025_7560", "pubmed23n0040_10104", "pubmed23n0051_1842", "pubmed23n0056_17878", "Gynecology_Novak_3318", "InternalMed_Harrison_24327", "Pathology_Robbins_4120", "pubmed23n0036_803