{"topic": "Breast cancer", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the primary use of CA 15-3 and carcinoembryonic antigen in breast cancer management?", "options": {"A": "Detection of early breast cancer", "B": "Monitoring therapeutic response", "C": "Diagnosis of metastatic disease", "D": "Prediction of disease recurrence"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "CA 15-3 and carcinoembryonic antigen are not reliable for the detection of early breast cancer, but they are helpful in monitoring therapeutic response since antigen levels correlate closely with disease status.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0059_10567", "title": "CA 15-3 and carcinoembryonic antigen in the clinical evaluation of breast cancer", "span_text": "Tumor marker elevations predominated in patients with advanced disease indicating that CA 15-3 and CEA are not reliable for the detection of early breast cancer. Both markers were helpful in monitoring therapeutic response since antigen levels correlated closely with disease status."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_10567", "pubmed23n0051_1037", "pubmed23n0052_7551", "pubmed23n0052_1034", "pubmed23n0014_13284", "pubmed23n0049_19970", "pubmed23n0049_16474", "pubmed23n0045_513", "pubmed23n0043_19064", "pubmed23n0004_8620", "pubmed23n0063_22287", "pubmed23n0033_8947", "pubmed23n0050_9885", "pubmed23n0037_9174", "pubmed23n0003_10673", "pubmed23n0062_2076", "pubmed23n0043_11914", "pubmed23n0012_3180", "pubmed23n0047_11086", "pubmed23n0050_4265", "InternalMed_Harrison_32562", "pubmed23n0060_2319", "pubmed23n0046_1088", "pubmed23n0061_2567", "pubmed23n0053_4445", "pubmed23n0057_19565", "pubmed23n0053_2370", "pubmed23n0056_19706", "pubmed23n0047_20358", "Surgery_Schwartz_2245", "pubmed23n0060_13607", "pubmed23n0004_1198", "pubmed23n0020_4993", "pubmed23n0055_1982", "pubmed23n0047_5553", "pubmed23n0051_15459", "pubmed23n0055_20973", "pubmed23n0056_13696", "pubmed23n0033_8284", "pubmed