{"topic": "Pulmonary embolism", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A patient presents with symptoms suggestive of pulmonary embolism, but the clinical presentation is atypical. What should be included in the differential diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "Primary pulmonary artery sarcoma and pulmonary carcinosarcoma", "B": "Fat embolism syndrome and pneumonia", "C": "Pulmonary edema and cardiac arrhythmias", "D": "Aortic dissection and myocardial infarction"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's atypical clinical presentation suggests that the diagnosis may not be straightforward. Including primary pulmonary artery sarcoma and pulmonary carcinosarcoma in the differential diagnosis is important, as these rare conditions can mimic acute pulmonary embolism.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0041_7284", "title": "Primary and secondary pulmonary artery neoplasia mimicking acute pulmonary embolism", "span_text": "Two cases of rare pulmonary neoplastic lesions (primary pulmonary artery sarcoma and pulmonary carcinosarcoma) directly involving the pulmonary artery and presenting with findings mimicking acute pulmonary embolism are discussed."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0041_7284", "pubmed23n0031_10852", "pubmed23n0062_8891", "pubmed23n0058_15056", "pubmed23n0046_18097", "pubmed23n0053_5112", "pubmed23n0028_5127", "pubmed23n0058_15060", "pubmed23n0029_360", "pubmed23n0051_3380", "pubmed23n0009_278", "pubmed23n0038_8478", "InternalMed_Harrison_10178", "pubmed23n0062_4194", "pubmed23n0055_22109", "pubmed23n0025_2323", "pubmed23n0043_15626", "pubmed23n0050_20923", "pubmed23n0003_10860", "pubmed23n0048_3420", "pubmed23n0051_19322", "pubmed23n0054_5365", "pubmed23n0061_17821", "pubmed23n0041_9897", "InternalMed_Harrison_19673", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3292", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2992", "pubmed23n0031_1734", "pubmed23n0030_1621", "pubmed23n0024_10212", "pubmed23n0048_20527", "pubmed23n0062_5858", "pubmed23n0