{"topic": "Appendicitis", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the recommended treatment approach for pediatric patients with uncomplicated acute appendicitis, considering the effectiveness of patient choice in nonoperative versus surgical management?", "options": {"A": "Nonoperative management with antibiotics", "B": "Surgical appendectomy", "C": "Hospitalization for observation", "D": "Outpatient management with pain relief"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The effectiveness of patient choice in nonoperative versus surgical management of pediatric uncomplicated acute appendicitis suggests that nonoperative management with antibiotics can be a viable treatment approach, especially when considering patient choice and preferences.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Surgery_Schwartz_8874", "title": "Surgery_Schwartz", "span_text": "Minneci PC, Mahida JB, Lodwick DL, et al. Effectiveness of patient choice in nonoperative vs surgical management of pediatric uncomplicated acute appendicitis. JAMA Surg. 2016;151(5):408-415."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["Surgery_Schwartz_8874", "Surgery_Schwartz_8863", "InternalMed_Harrison_10845", "Surgery_Schwartz_8875", "pubmed23n0004_9769", "pubmed23n0045_13592", "pubmed23n0046_12726", "pubmed23n0022_4752"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Surgery_Schwartz_8874", "Surgery_Schwartz_8863", "InternalMed_Harrison_10845", "Surgery_Schwartz_8875", "pubmed23n0004_9769", "pubmed23n0045_13592", "pubmed23n0046_12726", "pubmed23n0022_4752"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Appendicitis Therapy therapy treatment management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1