{"topic": "Pregnancy", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is a known risk factor for the development of pityriasis versicolor?", "options": {"A": "Pregnancy", "B": "Genetic mutation", "C": "Vitamin deficiency", "D": "Hypertension"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Pityriasis versicolor is a superficial chronic fungal infection, and its onset and course are influenced by various factors, including pregnancy.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0049_1606", "title": "Pityriasis versicolor--modern views on etiology, pathogenesis and therapy", "span_text": "The onset and course of the disease are under the influence of genetic factors, age, sex, climate, local environmental factors, malnutrition, pregnancy, oral contraceptives, corticosteroid and immunosuppressive treatment."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "pubmed", "query": "pityriasis versicolor etiology", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_1606", "pubmed23n0052_6086", "InternalMed_Harrison_21456", "Obstentrics_Williams_8022", "pubmed23n0014_5370", "pubmed23n0044_23005", "pubmed23n0048_20338", "pubmed23n0047_10564", "pubmed23n0059_6422", "InternalMed_Harrison_2212", "pubmed23n0033_6501", "pubmed23n0055_556", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_2482", "pubmed23n0062_10502", "pubmed23n0057_24483", "pubmed23n0022_2416", "pubmed23n0060_17352", "InternalMed_Harrison_7574", "Gynecology_Novak_3134"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_1606", "pubmed23n0052_6086", "InternalMed_Harrison_21456", "Obstentrics_Williams_8022", "pubmed23n0014_5370", "pubmed23n0044_23005", "pubmed23n0048_20338", "pubmed23n0047_10564", "pubmed23n0059_6422", "InternalMed_Harrison_2212", "pubmed23n0033_6501", "pubmed23n0055_556", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_2482", "pubmed23n0062_10502", "pubmed23n0057_24483", "pubmed23n0022_2416", "pubmed23n0060_17352", "InternalMed_Harrison_7574", "Gynecology_Novak_3134"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": [