{"topic": "Psoriasis", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the typical course of generalized pustular psoriasis over time?", "options": {"A": "A consistent and predictable pattern", "B": "A fluctuating pattern, varying with time and from patient to patient", "C": "A steady improvement with treatment", "D": "A rapid progression to a life-threatening state"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The course of generalized pustular psoriasis is difficult to assess due to its fluctuating pattern, which varies with time and from patient to patient.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0002_12057", "title": "Generalized pustular psoriasis. A report on thirteen patients.", "span_text": "Generalized pustular psoriasis shows a fluctuating pattern, its course varying with time and from patient to patient."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0002_12057"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0002_12057"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Psoriasis Prognosis prognosis outcomes mortality survival complications disease course recurrence risk stratification severity long-term outcomes quality of life predictors", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 8265.315917029511, "llm_ms": 868.7087500002235, "verification_ms": 800.9068749961443, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0002_12057"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 100.0, "verification": 200.0, "llm": 868.7087500002235}}}
{"topic": "Osteoporosis", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is a crucial aspect of diagnostic testing in osteoporosis?", "options": {"A": "Identifying candidates for treatment", "B": "Monitoring the response to therapy or progression of disease", "C": "Characterizing the bone and mineral metabolism of the individual patient", "D": "All of the above"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "Diagnostic testing in osteoporosis should not only identify candidates for treatment but also permit monitoring of the response to therapy or progression of disease, and characterize the bone and mineral metabolism of the individual patient.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0043_9564", "title": "The future of osteoporosis diagnosis and therapy", "span_text": "Diagnostic testing must become more effective at characterizing the bone and mineral metabolism of the individual patient. Testing must do far more than identify candidates for treatment; it must permit monitoring of the response to therapy or progression of disease."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0043_9564", "First_Aid_Step1_472", "pubmed23n0061_3671", "Gynecology_Novak_2724", "pubmed23n0049_8872"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0043_9564", "First_Aid_Step1_472", "pubmed23n0061_3671", "Gynecology_Novak_2724", "pubmed23n0049_8872"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteoporosis Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6961.367500014603, "llm_ms": 882.4626249843277, "verification_ms": 862.054375000298, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {