{"topic": "Hyperthyroidism", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "A 46-year-old male is incidentally diagnosed with hyperthyroidism during an annual physical examination. What is the most likely cause of his condition, given that he has elevated TSH and free T4 consistent with central hyperthyroidism?", "options": {"A": "Graves' disease", "B": "TSH-secreting pituitary adenoma", "C": "Toxic multinodular goiter", "D": "Thyroiditis"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The patient's elevated TSH and free T4 levels are consistent with central hyperthyroidism, which is often caused by a TSH-secreting pituitary adenoma. This condition is characterized by the excessive production of TSH, leading to hyperthyroidism.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41573500", "title": "Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone (TSH)-Secreting Pituitary Macroadenoma Presenting as Biochemical Hyperthyroidism Without Clinical Symptoms: A Case Report", "span_text": "Thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH)-secreting pituitary adenomas (TSH-omas) are a rare cause of hyperthyroidism. We present a case of a 46-year-old male who was incidentally diagnosed with hyperthyroidism during an annual physical examination, with elevated TSH and free T4 consistent with central hyperthyroidism."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41573500", "pubmed_web_41571841", "pubmed_web_41557149", "pubmed_web_41551367", "pubmed_web_41549983", "pubmed_web_41536459", "pubmed_web_41531741", "pubmed_web_41522638", "pubmed_web_41520457", "pubmed_web_41510005", "pubmed_web_41506167", "pubmed_web_41502204", "pubmed_web_41498932", "pubmed_web_41497295", "pubmed_web_41496136", "pubmed_web_41488723", "pubmed_web_41488629", "pubmed_web_41488172", "pubmed_web_41485171"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41573500", "pubmed_web_41571841", "pubmed_web_41557149", "pubmed_web_41551367", "pubmed_web_41549983", "pubmed_web_41536459", "pubmed_web_41531741", "pubmed_web_41522638", "pubmed_we