{"topic": "Neonatal sepsis", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the primary method for preventing early-onset group B streptococcal disease in newborns?", "options": {"A": "Intrapartum antibiotic prophylaxis", "B": "Neonatal vaccination", "C": "Maternal vaccination before pregnancy", "D": "Avoiding close contact with infected individuals"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Intrapartum antibiotic prophylaxis is the primary method for preventing early-onset group B streptococcal disease in newborns, as it significantly reduces the risk of transmission from mother to fetus during delivery.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0062_1366", "title": "Intrapartum chemoprophylaxis of early-onset group B streptococcal disease", "span_text": "A randomized study in 121 pregnant women carrier of group B streptococci is undertaken in order to assess the administration of 500 mg of intrapartum ampicillin intravenously to interrupt mother-to-fetus group B streptococcal transmission."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_16032", "pubmed23n0041_11473", "pubmed23n0043_11737", "Obstentrics_Williams_8845", "pubmed23n0062_1366", "pubmed23n0049_18694", "pubmed23n0052_12053"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_16032", "pubmed23n0041_11473", "pubmed23n0043_11737", "Obstentrics_Williams_8845", "pubmed23n0062_1366", "pubmed23n0049_18694", "pubmed23n0052_12053"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Neonatal sepsis Prevention prevention prophylaxis risk reduction screening vaccination primary prevention secondary prevention lifestyle modification counseling public health early detection follow-up", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 8985.280458990019, "llm_ms": 2931.4261249965057, "verificat