{"topic": "Hepatitis C", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the long-term prognosis for the majority of patients with chronic hepatitis C?", "options": {"A": "Relatively benign", "B": "Poor due to high risk of liver failure", "C": "Variable depending on the presence of other liver diseases", "D": "Always results in liver transplantation"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The long-term prognosis for chronic hepatitis C in a majority of patients is relatively benign, with mortality over 10\u221220 years among patients with transfusion-associated chronic hepatitis C not differing from mortality in a matched population of transfused patients in whom hepatitis C did not develop.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_23783", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Despite this substantial rate of progression of chronic hepatitis C, and despite the fact that liver failure can result from end-stage chronic hepatitis C, the long-term prognosis for chronic hepatitis C in a majority of patients is relatively benign."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23783", "pubmed23n0036_1940", "InternalMed_Harrison_23934", "InternalMed_Harrison_24121", "pubmed23n0059_9002", "pubmed23n0052_10452", "pubmed23n0049_2731", "Obstentrics_Williams_7600", "pubmed23n0021_10046", "pubmed23n0058_18602", "Surgery_Schwartz_9022", "InternalMed_Harrison_23987"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23783", "pubmed23n0036_1940", "InternalMed_Harrison_23934", "InternalMed_Harrison_24121", "pubmed23n0059_9002", "pubmed23n0052_10452", "pubmed23n0049_2731", "Obstentrics_Williams_7600", "pubmed23n0021_10046", "pubmed23n0058_18602", "Surgery_Schwartz_9022", "InternalMed_Harrison_23987"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hepatitis C Prognosis prognos