{"topic": "Breast cancer", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 45-year-old woman presents with a palpable mass in her right breast. What is the most appropriate initial imaging modality to differentiate a cystic from a solid mass?", "options": {"A": "Mammography", "B": "Breast sonography", "C": "MRI", "D": "CT scan"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Breast sonography is the most appropriate initial imaging modality to differentiate a cystic from a solid mass, as it can accurately diagnose simple cysts and has a high diagnostic accuracy for this purpose.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_11624", "title": "Breast sonography", "span_text": "Breast sonography is not useful for screening for breast cancer in any age group. Its main use is for the differentiation of cystic vs solid palpable and mammographically visible masses."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_18841", "pubmed23n0054_20199", "pubmed23n0017_1983", "pubmed23n0014_9733", "pubmed23n0036_7308", "pubmed23n0054_1438", "Gynecology_Novak_3379", "pubmed23n0063_11624", "pubmed23n0018_4903", "pubmed23n0041_8955", "InternalMed_Harrison_28583", "pubmed23n0030_1016", "pubmed23n0053_4263", "pubmed23n0016_5680", "pubmed23n0036_8039", "Gynecology_Novak_3318", "pubmed23n0024_3840", "pubmed23n0059_8918", "Surgery_Schwartz_4074", "pubmed23n0034_218", "pubmed23n0046_13933", "pubmed23n0020_4315", "pubmed23n0047_2770", "pubmed23n0052_9196", "pubmed23n0008_8750", "pubmed23n0051_392", "pubmed23n0014_13380", "pubmed23n0006_7486", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "pubmed23n0050_10466", "pubmed23n0023_10159", "pubmed23n0007_1772", "pubmed23n0056_17878", "pubmed23n0060_6543", "pubmed23n0043_8258", "pubmed23n0052_15320", "Surgery_Schwartz_3924", "pubmed23n0051_4745", "pubmed23n0018_1257", "pubmed23n0040_10104", "pubmed23n0051_12048", "pubmed23n0017_5390", "pubmed23n0039_3047", "Surgery_Schwartz_11662", "pubmed23n0051_4306", "InternalMed_Harrison_4503", "pubmed23n0