{"topic": "Immunization", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary role of mast cells in the pathophysiology of intestinal disorders?", "options": {"A": "Releasing potent mediators and cytokines that induce pathophysiology", "B": "Producing antibodies against intestinal antigens", "C": "Regulating the immune response to food allergies", "D": "Maintaining the integrity of the epithelial barrier"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Mast cells play a significant role in the pathophysiology of intestinal disorders, including food allergy and inflammatory bowel disease, by releasing potent mediators and cytokines that induce pathophysiology.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0050_6969", "title": "Functional abnormalities in the intestine associated with mucosal mast cell activation", "span_text": "When activated, mast cells release a host of potent mediators and cytokines which are capable of inducing pathophysiology."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0050_6969", "pubmed23n0061_22290", "pubmed23n0031_8318"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0050_6969", "pubmed23n0061_22290", "pubmed23n0031_8318"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Immunization Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7941.182042006403, "llm_ms": 943.4857920277864, "verification_ms": 740.9313750104047, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_check