{"topic": "Chronic kidney disease", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the primary purpose of screening tests in the diagnosis of chronic kidney disease?", "options": {"A": "To confirm the presence of disease", "B": "To identify all individuals who have the disease, even if some healthy individuals are misidentified", "C": "To provide a definitive diagnosis", "D": "To rule out other potential causes of symptoms"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Screening tests are designed to identify all individuals who have the disease of interest, even if some healthy individuals are misidentified as possibly having the disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_32560", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Screening tests are generally less expensive and more widely available than are confirmatory tests, which often require more specialized equipment or personnel. As a general principle, screening tests are designed to identify all individuals who have the disease of interest, even if, in the process, some healthy individuals are misidentified as possibly having the disease."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0026_2112", "pubmed23n0054_20199", "InternalMed_Harrison_32560", "pubmed23n0015_9331", "pubmed23n0010_4736", "InternalMed_Harrison_22254", "pubmed23n0015_6391", "pubmed23n0020_9012", "pubmed23n0051_16909", "pubmed23n0018_7002", "pubmed23n0014_4992", "pubmed23n0012_40", "pubmed23n0048_14554", "pubmed23n0062_18963", "pubmed23n0015_8551", "pubmed23n0007_4725", "pubmed23n0055_19211", "pubmed23n0045_2542", "pubmed23n0026_5748", "pubmed23n0026_2893", "InternalMed_Harrison_24327", "pubmed23n0057_20630", "pubmed23n0039_7416", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3004", "pubmed23n0047_20303", "pubmed23n0011_1488", "pubmed23n0043_15638", "pubmed23n0016_11213", "pubmed23n0052_20664", "pubmed23n0061_8494", "pubmed23n0023_3386", "pubmed23n0032_12239", "InternalMed_Harrison_17680", "pubmed23n0040_1766"