{"topic": "Postpartum hemorrhage", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism of action of ergonovine in the treatment of postpartum bleeding?", "options": {"A": "Mixed partial agonist effects at 5-HT2 and \u03b1 adrenoceptors", "B": "Selective inhibition of plasminogen activator", "C": "Central nervous system 5-HT2 and dopamine agonist", "D": "Uteroselective \u03b1-agonist vasoconstriction"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Ergonovine works by causing marked smooth muscle contraction, which helps to control postpartum bleeding, but it also blocks \u03b1-agonist vasoconstriction.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_1752", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "ErgonovineMixed partial agonist effects at 5-HT2 and \u03b1 adrenoceptors Sameasergotamine\u2022someselectivity for uterine smooth muscle Postpartum bleeding \u2022migraineheadacheOral,parenteral(methylergonovine)\u2022duration2\u20134h\u2022Toxicity: Same as ergotamine"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_1752", "Pharmacology_Katzung_276", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3843", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1744", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5453", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3761", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3817"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_1752", "Pharmacology_Katzung_276", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3843", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1744", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5453", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3761", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3817"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Postpartum hemorrhage Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7152.4164589936845