{"topic": "Pancreatitis", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is crucial in the management of patients with hemorrhagic pancreatitis to avoid shock and renal and pulmonary failure?", "options": {"A": "Careful monitoring of fluid and electrolytes and blood gases", "B": "Early surgical intervention", "C": "Administration of antibiotics", "D": "Use of glucocorticoids"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Careful monitoring of fluid and electrolytes and blood gases is required to avoid shock and renal and pulmonary failure in patients with hemorrhagic pancreatitis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0015_10620", "title": "Hemorrhagic pancreatitis", "span_text": "Adequate initial resuscitation and intensive follow-up are probably the most important elements in the management of patients with hemorrhagic pancreatitis. Careful monitoring of fluid and electrolytes and blood gases is required to avoid shock and renal and pulmonary failure."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_10620", "pubmed23n0047_10691", "pubmed23n0046_2361", "InternalMed_Harrison_24423", "InternalMed_Harrison_24386", "pubmed23n0051_2023"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_10620", "pubmed23n0047_10691", "pubmed23n0046_2361", "InternalMed_Harrison_24423", "InternalMed_Harrison_24386", "pubmed23n0051_2023"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Pancreatitis Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9569.043958035763, "llm_ms": 951.1752499965951, "verification_ms": 849.1646670154296, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attem