{"topic": "Anemia", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary pathophysiological mechanism underlying the development of anemia in patients with chronic disease?", "options": {"A": "Inadequate erythropoietin response", "B": "Impaired iron absorption", "C": "Vitamin B12 deficiency", "D": "Bone marrow failure"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary pathophysiological mechanism underlying the development of anemia in patients with chronic disease is inadequate erythropoietin response. Normally, as anemia develops, the erythropoietin level increases to stimulate red blood cell production. However, in chronic disease, this response is blunted, leading to anemia.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0054_1282", "title": "Changing patterns of care in the management of anemia", "span_text": "One of the components in the pathophysiology of ACD is inadequate erythropoietin response. Normally, as anemia develops, the erythropoietin level does not begin to increase until the hematocrit level decreases below 35%. However, the increase in the erythropoietin level is blunted in ACD."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_15742", "pubmed23n0012_9799", "Pathology_Robbins_3004", "pubmed23n0046_985", "pubmed23n0030_749", "pubmed23n0014_775", "pubmed23n0054_1282", "pubmed23n0052_18495", "InternalMed_Harrison_22826", "pubmed23n0052_16605", "pubmed23n0031_9441", "InternalMed_Harrison_7953", "pubmed23n0058_18453", "pubmed23n0028_1519", "pubmed23n0056_94", "pubmed23n0057_12805", "pubmed23n0045_1472", "pubmed23n0054_20182", "Obstentrics_Williams_3112"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_15742", "pubmed23n0012_9799", "Pathology_Robbins_3004", "pubmed23n0046_985", "pubmed23n0030_749", "pubmed23n0014_775", "pubmed23n0054_1282", "pubmed23n0052_18495", "InternalMed_Harrison_22826", "pubmed23n0052_16605", "pubmed23n0031_9441", "InternalMed_Harrison_7953", "pubmed23n0058_18453", "pubmed23n0028_1519", "pu