{"topic": "Malaria", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the main drawback in preventing transfusion-associated malaria in endemic areas?", "options": {"A": "Lack of effective antimalarial medications", "B": "Inadequate routine blood donor screening techniques", "C": "Insufficient funding for malaria research", "D": "Limited access to healthcare facilities"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The main drawback in preventing transfusion-associated malaria is that routine blood donor screening techniques are not very satisfactory, which can lead to the transmission of malaria through blood transfusions.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0060_20036", "title": "Donor screening for malaria by antibody and antigen detection in endemic area", "span_text": "The main drawback in preventing this menace is that routine blood donor screening techniques are not very satisfactory."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_20036"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_20036"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Malaria Screening screening early detection risk assessment screening test sensitivity specificity guideline population screening high-risk preventive care follow-up diagnostic threshold", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7291.014041984454, "llm_ms": 879.4247499899939, "verification_ms": 737.6295829890296, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0060_20036"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 100.0, "verific