{"topic": "Psoriasis", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism underlying the development of psoriasis?", "options": {"A": "Autoimmune response with T cell-mediated inflammation", "B": "Genetic mutation in the HLA gene", "C": "Environmental factors such as trauma or infection", "D": "Imbalance of cytokines and growth factors"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Psoriasis is a T cell-mediated inflammatory disease, presumed to be autoimmune in origin, with both genetic and environmental factors contributing to the risk.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pathology_Robbins_5226", "title": "Pathology_Robbins", "span_text": "Psoriasis is a T cell-mediated inflammatory disease, presumed to be autoimmune in origin, although the antigens are not well described."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "textbook", "query": "psoriasis etiology", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_22850", "pubmed23n0050_6955", "Pathology_Robbins_5226"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_22850", "pubmed23n0050_6955", "Pathology_Robbins_5226"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Psoriasis Etiology etiology cause risk factors pathogenesis mechanism underlying cause genetic factors environmental factors predisposing factors associated conditions epidemiology incidence", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7664.675957988948, "llm_ms": 1146.3312080013566, "verification_ms": 818.579500017222, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["InternalMed_Harrison_22850", "pubmed23n0050_6955", "Pathology_R