{"topic": "Rheumatoid arthritis", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the recommended method for screening protein-energy malnutrition in patients with juvenile rheumatoid arthritis?", "options": {"A": "Arm circumference less than or equal to 10th percentile for age and sex matched norms", "B": "Slit lamp biomicroscopy", "C": "Upper body anthropometric measurements", "D": "Biochemical measurements"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The arm circumference less than or equal to 10th percentile for age and sex matched norms is selected as the screening test for protein-energy malnutrition in patients with juvenile rheumatoid arthritis due to its excellent measurement characteristics and ease of measurement.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0047_555", "title": "A nutritional screening test for use in children and adolescents with juvenile rheumatoid arthritis", "span_text": "Arm circumference less than or equal to 10th percentile for age and sex matched norms was selected as the screening test for PEM in patients with JRA due to a combination of excellent measurement characteristics (sensitivity 0.80, specificity 0.86, positive predictive value 0.90, negative predictive value 0.73, index of validity 0.88) and ease of measurement."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0047_555", "pubmed23n0051_1581"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0047_555", "pubmed23n0051_1581"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Rheumatoid arthritis Screening screening early detection risk assessment screening test sensitivity specificity guideline population screening high-risk preventive care follow-up diagnostic threshold", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6889.215625007637, "llm_ms": 839.86108400