{"topic": "Psoriasis", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What histopathological features are characteristic of psoriasis vulgaris of the scalp?", "options": {"A": "Moderate condensed hyperkeratosis with alternating parakeratosis, PAS-reactive serum inclusions and Munro abscesses within the horny layer", "B": "Irregular acanthosis with relatively thin condensed orthoor parakeratotic horny layer, spongiosis and spongiotic vesicles", "C": "Strong spongiform pustles and neutrophilic leukocytes within the dermis", "D": "Lack of any hard criteria for psoriasis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The histopathological features characteristic of psoriasis vulgaris of the scalp include moderate condensed hyperkeratosis with alternating parakeratosis, PAS-reactive serum inclusions and Munro abscesses within the horny layer, spongiform pustles and neutrophilic leukocytes within the epidermis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0006_3747", "title": "[Histological differential diagnosis of psoriasis vulgaris and seborrheic eczema of the scalp]", "span_text": "Strong criteria favouring psoriasis are: moderate condensed hyperkeratosis with alternating parakeratosis, PAS-reactive serum inclusions and Munro abscesses within the horny layer, spongiform pustles and neutrophilic leukocytes within the epidermis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0006_3667", "InternalMed_Harrison_25557", "pubmed23n0006_3747"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0006_3667", "InternalMed_Harrison_25557", "pubmed23n0006_3747"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Psoriasis Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_t