{"topic": "Chronic pain", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is a key feature that distinguishes polymyalgia rheumatica from other conditions?", "options": {"A": "Bilateral shoulder pain or stiffness", "B": "Unilateral hip pain", "C": "Acute onset of illness", "D": "Normal ESR"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The correct answer is supported by the evidence, which states that bilateral shoulder pain or stiffness is one of the most valuable criteria for differentiating polymyalgia rheumatica from other conditions.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0017_12050", "title": "An evaluation of criteria for polymyalgia rheumatica", "span_text": "The 7 most valuable criteria for differentiation were bilateral shoulder pain or stiffness, onset of illness of less than 2 weeks' duration, initial ESR greater than 40 mm/h, duration of morning stiffness exceeding 1 hour, age 65 years or more, depression and/or weight loss, and bilateral tenderness in the upper arms."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_13614", "InternalMed_Harrison_23994", "pubmed23n0059_19498", "InternalMed_Harrison_26171", "pubmed23n0060_18841", "pubmed23n0020_1117", "pubmed23n0017_12050", "InternalMed_Harrison_26020", "pubmed23n0005_9019", "InternalMed_Harrison_26086", "pubmed23n0061_1975", "InternalMed_Harrison_2580", "pubmed23n0062_11087", "Gynecology_Novak_3379", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1599", "pubmed23n0028_13079", "pubmed23n0049_6708", "InternalMed_Harrison_24368", "Gynecology_Novak_5476", "InternalMed_Harrison_1386", "pubmed23n0051_16909", "pubmed23n0061_4359", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1924", "pubmed23n0052_17360", "pubmed23n0062_1477", "pubmed23n0051_13043", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3292", "pubmed23n0047_12996", "InternalMed_Harrison_23036", "Gynecology_Novak_4607", "pubmed23n0002_6409", "pubmed23n0051_6910", "pubmed23n0017_4519", "pubmed23n0010_90", "pubmed23n0047_14401", "pubmed23n0050_6697", "pubmed23n0059_8127", "pubmed23n0027_1630", "pubmed