{"topic": "Cirrhosis", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the most sensitive test for detecting alcoholic cirrhosis?", "options": {"A": "Gamma-GT test", "B": "Liver biopsy", "C": "Aminophenazone breath test", "D": "Ultrasonographic liver examination"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The gamma-GT test is the most sensitive in alcoholic cirrhosis, but may be more an expression of the degree of alcoholism than of the hepatic lesion per se.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0002_2921", "title": "Liver cirrhosis. Clinical and biological aspects", "span_text": "The gamma-GT test is the most sensitive in alcoholic cirrhosis, but may be more an expression of the degree of alcoholism than of the hepatic lesion per se."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0055_21421", "pubmed23n0012_40", "pubmed23n0060_12480", "pubmed23n0055_13126", "pubmed23n0044_8663", "pubmed23n0025_2009", "pubmed23n0002_2921"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0055_21421", "pubmed23n0012_40", "pubmed23n0060_12480", "pubmed23n0055_13126", "pubmed23n0044_8663", "pubmed23n0025_2009", "pubmed23n0002_2921"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Cirrhosis Investigation investigation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging workup evaluation differential diagnosis clinical criteria biomarkers screening confirmatory test diagnostic accuracy", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6958.064917009324, "llm_ms": 836.9223750196397, "verification_ms": 2061.2675420125015, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["