{"topic": "Urinary tract infection", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the long-term prognosis for patients with post-infectious renal scarring after pyelonephritis in childhood?", "options": {"A": "The prognosis is generally good, with no long-term complications.", "B": "The prognosis is poor, with a high risk of serious long-term complications, including hypertension and renal failure.", "C": "The prognosis is variable, depending on the extent of renal scarring and the presence of other underlying conditions.", "D": "The prognosis is not well established, due to a lack of long-term follow-up studies."}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "The long-term prognosis for patients with post-infectious renal scarring after pyelonephritis in childhood is variable, depending on the extent of renal scarring and the presence of other underlying conditions. Studies have shown that patients with unilateral scarring are at risk of serious long-term complications, including hypertension and renal failure.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0051_9953", "title": "Long-term prognosis of post-infectious renal scarring in relation to radiological findings in childhood--a 27-year follow-up", "span_text": "A radiological progression of scarring from childhood to adulthood was seen in one-third of the kidneys. The 7 patients with bilateral scarring in childhood had a smaller renal area, lower glomerular filtration rate and higher plasma vasopressin at follow-up than 13 healthy controls."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_9530", "pubmed23n0036_8618", "pubmed23n0062_12627", "pubmed23n0049_19658", "pubmed23n0051_9953", "pubmed23n0016_10524", "Surgery_Schwartz_11808", "pubmed23n0052_6631", "InternalMed_Harrison_12013", "pubmed23n0053_19769", "pubmed23n0012_4954", "pubmed23n0052_10115", "pubmed23n0052_8663", "Obstentrics_Williams_7064", "Obstentrics_Williams_8828", "pubmed23n0051_15183", "Surgery_Schwartz_4430", "p