{"topic": "Urinary tract infection", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is a cost-effective method for preventing urinary tract infections in renal transplant recipients?", "options": {"A": "Prophylaxis with low-dose trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole", "B": "Prophylaxis with high-dose ciprofloxacin", "C": "Increased fluid intake", "D": "Avoiding sexual activity"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Prophylaxis with low-dose trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole has been shown to be cost-effective in preventing urinary tract infections in renal transplant recipients.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0045_78", "title": "Trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole compared with ciprofloxacin for the prevention of urinary tract infection in renal transplant recipients", "span_text": "Prophylaxis with low-dose trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole has been shown to be cost-effective in the prevention of urinary tract infections, pyelonephritis, urosepsis, and pneumocystis pneumonia in renal transplant recipients."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_20690", "pubmed23n0055_13775", "First_Aid_Step2_237", "pubmed23n0053_8313", "InternalMed_Harrison_25306", "pubmed23n0051_768", "pubmed23n0045_78", "pubmed23n0048_7714", "pubmed23n0054_21402", "pubmed23n0034_1255", "pubmed23n0061_3727", "pubmed23n0049_9825", "pubmed23n0043_7574", "Gynecology_Novak_249", "pubmed23n0055_13757", "pubmed23n0063_12968", "InternalMed_Harrison_11663", "pubmed23n0055_13772", "Obstentrics_Williams_9092", "pubmed23n0049_19658", "pubmed23n0062_2547", "InternalMed_Harrison_12251", "pubmed23n0049_18694", "pubmed23n0062_3058", "pubmed23n0025_11486", "InternalMed_Harrison_17080", "pubmed23n0055_13764", "pubmed23n0050_8981", "InternalMed_Harrison_10885", "InternalMed_Harrison_22316", "pubmed23n0061_8590", "pubmed23n0036_5974", "Surgery_Schwartz_1269", "pubmed23n0059_19131", "pubmed23n0059_5692", "pubmed23n0047_2137", "pubmed23n0036_3694", "Pediatrics_N