{"topic": "Sepsis", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is a challenge in diagnosing neonatal sepsis?", "options": {"A": "There is a definitive diagnostic test available", "B": "Blood cultures have high sensitivity", "C": "There is no definitive diagnostic test and blood cultures have low sensitivity", "D": "Historical and clinical data are not useful in diagnosis"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "Diagnosing neonatal sepsis is difficult due to the lack of a definitive diagnostic test and the low sensitivity of blood cultures.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0062_17702", "title": "Clinicopathologic approach to the diagnosis of neonatal sepsis", "span_text": "Accurate diagnosis is difficult because there is no definitive diagnostic test; even blood cultures have an unacceptably low sensitivity."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 10, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_17702", "pubmed23n0062_20157", "pubmed23n0022_8342", "pubmed23n0056_12592", "pubmed23n0037_1777", "pubmed23n0052_12052"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_17702", "pubmed23n0062_20157", "pubmed23n0022_8342", "pubmed23n0056_12592", "pubmed23n0037_1777", "pubmed23n0052_12052"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 5, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Sepsis Investigation investigation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging workup evaluation differential diagnosis clinical criteria biomarkers screening confirmatory test diagnostic accuracy", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 21158.076166990213, "llm_ms": 906.0627910075709, "verification_ms": 837.421957985498, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_check