{"topic": "Typhoid fever", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the primary diagnostic test used in Sri Lanka for typhoid fever, and what are its limitations?", "options": {"A": "Standard Agglutination Test (SAT), which has high sensitivity and specificity", "B": "Widal test, which has low sensitivity and specificity", "C": "Standard Agglutination Test (SAT), which has low sensitivity and specificity", "D": "Limulus test, which is highly specific for typhoid fever"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "The Standard Agglutination Test (SAT) is the primary diagnostic test used in Sri Lanka for typhoid fever. However, it has limitations, including low sensitivity and specificity, particularly at titres other than 1/120.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0047_14460", "title": "An evaluation of the SAT in the diagnosis of typhoid", "span_text": "Although the SAT continues to be used in Sri Lanka as the main diagnostic test in typhoid, the sensitivity and specificity of this test fall below the requirements of a useful diagnostic test."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0047_14460", "pubmed23n0032_10993", "pubmed23n0023_6855", "pubmed23n0050_1196", "pubmed23n0014_4025", "InternalMed_Harrison_1724", "pubmed23n0049_10977", "pubmed23n0050_14531", "InternalMed_Harrison_1707", "pubmed23n0014_10523", "InternalMed_Harrison_12697", "pubmed23n0049_10442", "pubmed23n0058_8709", "InternalMed_Harrison_24368", "pubmed23n0028_8407", "InternalMed_Harrison_16947", "pubmed23n0029_5015", "InternalMed_Harrison_1698", "pubmed23n0046_18848", "pubmed23n0058_3477", "pubmed23n0045_2497", "pubmed23n0061_15456", "pubmed23n0009_3610", "InternalMed_Harrison_13929", "pubmed23n0043_14688", "pubmed23n0005_8108", "pubmed23n0058_547", "InternalMed_Harrison_15807", "pubmed23n0050_11124", "pubmed23n0019_1756", "pubmed23n0045_14916", "pubmed23n0020_9619", "InternalMed_Harrison_1672", "pubmed23n0056_4955"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubme