{"topic": "Back pain", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A patient presents with intractable low back pain, and the diagnosis can only be made by a high degree of suspicion and repeated X-rays. What is the most likely cause of this patient's symptoms?", "options": {"A": "Disc space infections", "B": "Ankylosing spondylitis", "C": "Polymyalgia rheumatica", "D": "Fuchs' heterochromic cyclitis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms of intractable low back pain, particularly in a child, are often due to disc space infections. The diagnosis can only be made by a high degree of suspicion and repeated X-rays, as symptoms often occur well before radiographic findings are evident.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0005_9019", "title": "Disc space infections in children", "span_text": "Intractable low back pain in children is often due to disc space infections. The clinical presentation, diagnostic workup, and treatment of four cases are presented. Symptoms often occur well before radiographic findings are evident."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_1975", "InternalMed_Harrison_24368", "pubmed23n0015_13614", "InternalMed_Harrison_26171", "pubmed23n0005_9019", "pubmed23n0005_8739", "pubmed23n0060_18841", "InternalMed_Harrison_23994", "pubmed23n0005_1145", "pubmed23n0059_19498", "pubmed23n0057_23468", "pubmed23n0061_12582", "pubmed23n0016_3243", "pubmed23n0061_4359", "pubmed23n0017_12050", "InternalMed_Harrison_1481", "pubmed23n0005_5171", "pubmed23n0005_10264", "pubmed23n0017_11402", "pubmed23n0007_8253", "pubmed23n0020_1117", "InternalMed_Harrison_1520", "pubmed23n0006_2703", "Gynecology_Novak_3379", "pubmed23n0051_13043", "InternalMed_Harrison_2580", "InternalMed_Harrison_1386", "pubmed23n0005_3601", "pubmed23n0061_3851", "InternalMed_Harrison_23036", "InternalMed_Harrison_26086", "pubmed23n0051_8455", "pubmed23n0002_6409", "InternalMed_Harrison_10692", "pubmed23n0051_7125", "pubmed