{"topic": "Acne", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the recommended frequency for monitoring the clinical effectiveness and safety of testosterone replacement therapy in patients with acne?", "options": {"A": "Every 3 to 6 months after initiating therapy and annually thereafter", "B": "Every 6 to 12 months after initiating therapy and biannually thereafter", "C": "Every 1 to 2 months after initiating therapy and quarterly thereafter", "D": "Only at the discretion of the physician"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The clinical effectiveness and safety of testosterone replacement therapy should be assessed regularly to minimize potential adverse effects, including acne.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_27450", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "The clinical effectiveness and safety of testosterone replacement therapy should be assessed 3 to 6 months after initiating testosterone therapy and annually thereafter (Table 411-5)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "database", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_27450", "pubmed23n0061_7555", "Pediatrics_Nelson_4027"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_27450", "pubmed23n0061_7555", "Pediatrics_Nelson_4027"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Acne Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 15679.491416027304, "llm_ms": 886.2585420138203, "verification_ms": 997.1684169722721, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0