{"topic": "Chronic kidney disease", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the significance of monitoring kidney graft function at 1 day, 1 week, or 1 month after transplantation in predicting long-term graft survival?", "options": {"A": "It has no correlation with long-term graft survival", "B": "It is significantly correlated with long-term graft survival", "C": "It is only correlated with short-term graft survival", "D": "It is not a reliable indicator of graft survival"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Monitoring kidney graft function at 1 day, 1 week, or 1 month after transplantation is significantly correlated with long-term graft survival, as it can help identify potential issues early on and allow for timely interventions.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0012_3584", "title": "Prediction of long-term kidney transplant survival rates by monitoring early graft function and clinical grades", "span_text": "Statistically significant correlations were found between kidney graft function at 1 day, 1 week, or 1 month and long-term graft survival."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0012_3584", "Obstentrics_Williams_6959", "pubmed23n0049_5754", "pubmed23n0044_6373", "pubmed23n0052_4583", "pubmed23n0047_7602", "pubmed23n0058_4011", "pubmed23n0052_7551", "pubmed23n0050_6798", "pubmed23n0062_3510", "InternalMed_Harrison_337", "pubmed23n0059_575", "pubmed23n0052_21566", "pubmed23n0032_5167", "pubmed23n0026_3378", "pubmed23n0053_14029", "InternalMed_Harrison_13413", "pubmed23n0058_18326", "InternalMed_Harrison_19680", "Obstentrics_Williams_6440", "pubmed23n0043_4462", "InternalMed_Harrison_11428", "pubmed23n0058_6601", "pubmed23n0063_11348", "InternalMed_Harrison_576", "InternalMed_Harrison_27058", "pubmed23n0043_8994", "pubmed23n0003_6323", "pubmed23n0004_10454", "pubmed23n0049_20973", "pubmed23n0045_6170", "pubmed23n0043_18199", "pubmed23n0048_4237", "pubmed23n0054_3069", "pubmed23n0036_11166", "