{"topic": "Osteoporosis", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a potential complication of long-term heparin therapy in pregnant women?", "options": {"A": "Increased risk of osteoporosis", "B": "Decreased risk of osteoporosis", "C": "No effect on osteoporosis risk", "D": "Reversal of osteoporosis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Long-term heparin administration can lead to substantial decreases in bone mass, increasing the risk of osteoporosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0044_8581", "title": "[Risk of osteoporosis in long-term heparin therapy of thromboembolic diseases in pregnancy: attempted prevention with ossein-hydroxyapatite].", "span_text": "More frequently, long-term heparin administration to treat deep thrombosis in the legs or pelvis may lead to substantial decreases in bone mass and consequently increased risk of osteoporosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_25237", "Histology_Ross_1152", "Gynecology_Novak_4331", "InternalMed_Harrison_29254", "pubmed23n0044_8581", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1978", "pubmed23n0060_12607", "pubmed23n0052_4189", "pubmed23n0057_5408"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_25237", "Histology_Ross_1152", "Gynecology_Novak_4331", "InternalMed_Harrison_29254", "pubmed23n0044_8581", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1978", "pubmed23n0060_12607", "pubmed23n0052_4189", "pubmed23n0057_5408"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteoporosis Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 31359.864666999783, "llm_ms": 1437.4282500357367, "verification_ms": 3453.2589580048807, "extra_ins