{"topic": "Malaria", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is believed to be the pathophysiology of coma in cerebral malaria?", "options": {"A": "Brain anoxia from ischemia due to sequestration of erythrocytes containing mature parasites in cerebral capillaries and venules", "B": "Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC) caused by low parasitemia", "C": "Auto-immune process involving TNF production", "D": "Mechanical obstruction of cerebral blood vessels by parasitized red blood cells"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The pathophysiology of coma in cerebral malaria is believed to be brain anoxia from ischemia due to sequestration of erythrocytes containing mature parasites in cerebral capillaries and venules.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0045_14801", "title": "Overview: pathophysiology and management of cerebral malaria", "span_text": "The pathophysiology of coma is believed to be brain anoxia from ischemia due to sequestration of erythrocytes containing mature parasites in cerebral capillaries and venules."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_11867", "pubmed23n0045_14801", "Pathology_Robbins_3003", "InternalMed_Harrison_10066", "pubmed23n0012_1332", "pubmed23n0044_11866", "pubmed23n0049_7025"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_11867", "pubmed23n0045_14801", "Pathology_Robbins_3003", "InternalMed_Harrison_10066", "pubmed23n0012_1332", "pubmed23n0044_11866", "pubmed23n0049_7025"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Malaria Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 20070.885583001655, "llm_ms": 1244.28254098