{"topic": "Acne", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What factor can increase the risk of acne, particularly in young people and males?", "options": {"A": "Non-optimal apparent temperatures", "B": "Genetic predisposition", "C": "Poor diet", "D": "Lack of sleep"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Non-optimal apparent temperatures, including both cold and hot temperatures, have been shown to increase the risk of acne, particularly in young people and males.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41553558", "title": "Non-optimal apparent temperatures can increase the risk of acne: a multi-center time-series study", "span_text": "Results showed that both cold and hot AT were significantly associated with acne. The significant single-lag effects of cold AT lasted from lag0 to lag3, and cumulative-lag effects lasted from lag00 to lag07, with the highest relative risk of 1.09 (95%CI: 1.03-1.17) on lag0, and 1.34 (95%CI: 1.17-1.53) on lag07, respectively."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41580305", "pubmed_web_41570025", "pubmed_web_41563775", "pubmed_web_41553558", "pubmed_web_41552868", "pubmed_web_41526511", "pubmed_web_41521693", "pubmed_web_41486969", "pubmed_web_41465805", "pubmed_web_41462936", "pubmed_web_41412980", "pubmed_web_41403042", "pubmed_web_41366990", "pubmed_web_41357617", "pubmed_web_41348470", "pubmed_web_41341360", "pubmed_web_41317036", "pubmed_web_41313649", "pubmed_web_41307186"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41580305", "pubmed_web_41570025", "pubmed_web_41563775", "pubmed_web_41553558", "pubmed_web_41552868", "pubmed_web_41526511", "pubmed_web_41521693", "pubmed_web_41486969", "pubmed_web_41465805", "pubmed_web_41462936", "pubmed_web_41412980", "pubmed_web_41403042", "pubmed_web_41366990", "pubmed_web_41357617", "pubmed_web_41348470", "pubmed_web_41341360", "pubmed_web_41317036", "pubmed_web_41313649", "pubmed_web_41307186"], "retrieval_mode": "pubmed_web"}, "verification