{"topic": "Migraine", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a potential long-term consequence of alternating hemiplegic migraine?", "options": {"A": "Cognitive and neurological deterioration", "B": "Increased risk of stroke", "C": "Transient focal neurologic symptoms", "D": "Regression of atheroma in coronary arteries"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Alternating hemiplegic migraine can lead to long-term deterioration in cognitive and neurological function.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0061_11977", "title": "Alternating hemiplegic migraine in childhood", "span_text": "Alternating hemiplegic migraine results immediately in an incapacitated state and can lead to long-term deterioration in cognitive and neurological function."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "pubmed", "query": "alternating hemiplegic migraine", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_11977", "Obstentrics_Williams_8463", "pubmed23n0044_13659", "pubmed23n0059_20980"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_11977", "Obstentrics_Williams_8463", "pubmed23n0044_13659", "pubmed23n0059_20980"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Migraine Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 14909.243167028762, "llm_ms": 2521.083958039526, "verification_ms": 2810.496541962493, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0061_11977", "Obstentrics_Wil