{"topic": "Hepatitis B", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the primary method for detecting hepatitis B infection?", "options": {"A": "Liver biopsy", "B": "Detection of Australia antigen", "C": "Serum immunoglobulin determinations", "D": "Antinuclear antibody test"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The detection of Australia antigen is considered an indication for the presence of hepatitis B, and it has considerable diagnostic and prognostic importance.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0039_10215", "title": "[Clinical evaluation of Australia-antigen detection (author's transl)]", "span_text": "The detection of Australia antigen is considered as indication for the presence of a hepatitis with a long incubation period (hepatitis B)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23270", "pubmed23n0039_10215", "pubmed23n0042_11887", "pubmed23n0006_5951", "pubmed23n0020_6706", "pubmed23n0056_18913", "pubmed23n0002_8348", "pubmed23n0012_5731", "pubmed23n0014_13401", "pubmed23n0027_1630", "pubmed23n0037_1144", "pubmed23n0044_8840", "pubmed23n0055_7729", "pubmed23n0044_13968", "pubmed23n0003_4956", "pubmed23n0031_1767"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_23270", "pubmed23n0039_10215", "pubmed23n0042_11887", "pubmed23n0006_5951", "pubmed23n0020_6706", "pubmed23n0056_18913", "pubmed23n0002_8348", "pubmed23n0012_5731", "pubmed23n0014_13401", "pubmed23n0027_1630", "pubmed23n0037_1144", "pubmed23n0044_8840", "pubmed23n0055_7729", "pubmed23n0044_13968", "pubmed23n0003_4956", "pubmed23n0031_1767"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hepatitis B Investigation investigation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging workup evaluation differential diagnosis clinical criteria biomarkers screening confirmatory te