{"topic": "Peptic ulcer disease", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the primary goal of maintenance therapy in patients with peptic ulcer disease?", "options": {"A": "To reduce the risk of ulcer recurrence and complications", "B": "To relieve symptoms and heal the acute ulcer", "C": "To decrease the economic impact of the disease", "D": "To improve the patient's quality of life"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Maintenance therapy is recommended for patients with previous bleeding or other complications, severe symptoms, and frequent recurrences, as it reduces the complication rate and prevents ulcer recurrence.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0045_3995", "title": "Short- and long-term management of peptic ulcer disease: current role of H2-antagonists", "span_text": "Maintenance therapy is recommended for the patient with previous bleeding or other complication, the patient with severe symptoms, and the patient with frequent recurrences. Maintenance therapy appears to reduce the complication rate in the patient with previous bleeding and possibly in the patient with uncomplicated disease, although the incidence of complications in this group is quite low."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0045_3995", "pubmed23n0045_7038", "pubmed23n0051_5799", "InternalMed_Harrison_2200", "pubmed23n0059_20077", "pubmed23n0045_2592", "pubmed23n0056_2351", "Gynecology_Novak_3795", "pubmed23n0026_8616", "InternalMed_Harrison_12562", "pubmed23n0046_10785", "pubmed23n0021_3527", "pubmed23n0057_17794", "pubmed23n0014_2698", "pubmed23n0045_14340", "pubmed23n0057_15176", "pubmed23n0001_9054", "pubmed23n0001_7283", "pubmed23n0046_15758", "pubmed23n0044_23705", "pubmed23n0034_4261", "pubmed23n0053_11836", "pubmed23n0045_10934", "pubmed23n0063_3639", "pubmed23n0062_981", "pubmed23n0058_459", "pubmed23n0051_9527", "pubmed23n0001_5919", "pubmed23n0051_12056", "pubmed23n0052_17374", "pubmed23n0055_7387", "pubmed23n0