{"topic": "Rheumatoid arthritis", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the value of laboratory investigation in the diagnosis of rheumatoid arthritis?", "options": {"A": "It can improve diagnostic sensitivity and specificity in relatively early rheumatoid arthritis", "B": "It is not useful in the diagnosis of rheumatoid arthritis", "C": "It can only be used to diagnose late-stage rheumatoid arthritis", "D": "It is only useful in conjunction with clinical evaluation"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Laboratory investigation, including histopathology and immunofluorescence, can help narrow the differential diagnosis and improve diagnostic sensitivity and specificity in relatively early rheumatoid arthritis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0026_2893", "title": "Laboratory diagnosis of rheumatoid arthritis", "span_text": "Because early diagnosis of rheumatoid arthritis is difficult increasingly important, we have assessed the value of laboratory investigation in 85 patients with knee effusions studied from presentation and followed for sufficiently long periods to allow a definite diagnosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0026_2893", "pubmed23n0052_20664", "pubmed23n0021_10808", "InternalMed_Harrison_26171", "pubmed23n0062_16486", "pubmed23n0010_6856", "pubmed23n0037_3340", "pubmed23n0054_83", "pubmed23n0032_4076", "pubmed23n0022_1398", "pubmed23n0047_17905", "pubmed23n0026_6079", "pubmed23n0035_1853", "InternalMed_Harrison_23904", "pubmed23n0026_7554", "InternalMed_Harrison_25528", "pubmed23n0014_538", "pubmed23n0052_6440", "pubmed23n0013_197", "pubmed23n0056_4517", "pubmed23n0036_4991", "pubmed23n0011_8474", "pubmed23n0057_6136", "pubmed23n0048_16841", "pubmed23n0013_6771", "pubmed23n0040_10735", "pubmed23n0036_1338", "pubmed23n0013_2829", "pubmed23n0037_5977", "pubmed23n0016_6286", "pubmed23n0030_2347", "pubmed23n0060_19655", "pubmed23n0045_15313", "pubmed23n0033_6712", "pubmed23n00