{"topic": "GERD", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "A patient with symptoms of gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) is being evaluated for potential complications. What is the significance of identifying a correlation between sleep disorder and GERD in this patient?", "options": {"A": "It may indicate a need for simultaneous treatment of both conditions", "B": "It is not relevant to the patient's GERD treatment plan", "C": "It suggests that the patient's sleep disorder is the primary cause of their GERD symptoms", "D": "It implies that the patient is at higher risk for developing Barrett's esophagus"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The correlation between sleep disorder and GERD suggests that treating one condition may have an impact on the other. Therefore, identifying this correlation is significant in developing an effective treatment plan for the patient.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41577822", "title": "Association between Gastroesophageal Reflux and Sleep Disorder: A Systematic Review and Meta-analysis", "span_text": "Our findings indicate a statistically significant unidirectional association between GERD and sleep disorder (RR = 2.02, 95% CI 1.71 to 2.37)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578529", "pubmed_web_41577822", "pubmed_web_41577482", "pubmed_web_41553747", "pubmed_web_41551831", "pubmed_web_41551533", "pubmed_web_41550049", "pubmed_web_41549496", "pubmed_web_41548508", "pubmed_web_41545289", "pubmed_web_41543102", "pubmed_web_41542834", "pubmed_web_41537290", "pubmed_web_41536225", "pubmed_web_41534397", "pubmed_web_41530072", "pubmed_web_41530069", "pubmed_web_41530067", "pubmed_web_41525274", "pubmed_web_41510928"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41577822", "pubmed_web_41577482", "pubmed_web_41553747", "pubmed_web_41551831", "pubmed_web_41551533", "pubmed_web_41550049", "pubmed_web_41549496", "pubmed_web_41548508", "pubmed_web_41545289", "pubmed_web_415431