{"topic": "Acute kidney injury", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the significance of monitoring blood cyclosporin concentrations in heart and heart-lung transplant recipients?", "options": {"A": "To assess the risk of acute rejection", "B": "To monitor the effectiveness of immunosuppression", "C": "To predict changes in renal function", "D": "To evaluate the risk of cardiac failure"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "Monitoring blood cyclosporin concentrations is essential to predict changes in renal function and manage acute nephrotoxicity in heart and heart-lung transplant recipients.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0050_18624", "title": "Blood cyclosporin concentrations but not doses correlate with acute changes in renal function following heart and heart-lung transplantation", "span_text": "The blood CyA concentration, however, correlated significantly with the reciprocal creatinine concentration measured in the same 5-day period and was also predictive of changes in creatinine measured in the subsequent 5-day period."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0012_3584", "pubmed23n0050_6798", "pubmed23n0051_18475", "pubmed23n0050_18624", "pubmed23n0058_6601", "pubmed23n0035_451", "Surgery_Schwartz_3093", "pubmed23n0053_5099", "pubmed23n0043_8994", "pubmed23n0046_23335", "InternalMed_Harrison_18253", "InternalMed_Harrison_21188", "pubmed23n0018_1877", "pubmed23n0022_8740", "InternalMed_Harrison_21189", "pubmed23n0036_11166", "pubmed23n0013_9550", "InternalMed_Harrison_19680", "Surgery_Schwartz_670", "pubmed23n0043_18199", "pubmed23n0031_12889", "pubmed23n0029_4090", "pubmed23n0017_3635", "pubmed23n0036_7298", "pubmed23n0046_12052", "pubmed23n0046_23818", "pubmed23n0048_16066", "pubmed23n0054_15969", "pubmed23n0010_4784", "pubmed23n0054_1955", "pubmed23n0057_19792", "pubmed23n0036_10290", "pubmed23n0057_12160", "InternalMed_Harrison_24140", "pubmed23n0060_2370", "pubmed23n0059_15944", "pubm