{"topic": "Osteoporosis", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the primary goal of osteoporosis prevention in adolescents and young adults?", "options": {"A": "To reduce the risk of fractures in older adults", "B": "To help each person achieve as high a peak skeletal mass and bone density as genetically possible prior to skeletal maturity", "C": "To promote a healthy and stable population of working women", "D": "To reduce the incidence of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The primary goal of osteoporosis prevention in adolescents and young adults is to help each person achieve as high a peak skeletal mass and bone density as genetically possible prior to skeletal maturity, as this is a critical factor in determining the risk of osteoporosis later in life.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0044_23228", "title": "Reduction of risk factors for osteoporosis among adolescents and young adults", "span_text": "The most promising approach in the primary prevention of osteoporosis is to help each person achieve as high a peak skeletal mass and bone density as genetically possible prior to skeletal maturity."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2022-01-01", "method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0051_809", "pubmed23n0046_15676", "pubmed23n0044_23228", "pubmed23n0048_3940", "pubmed23n0049_864", "pubmed23n0063_12708", "pubmed23n0048_4152", "pubmed23n0054_770", "pubmed23n0059_20799", "InternalMed_Harrison_25239", "Gynecology_Novak_6543", "pubmed23n0060_8553", "InternalMed_Harrison_28778", "pubmed23n0049_16375"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0051_809", "pubmed23n0046_15676", "pubmed23n0044_23228", "pubmed23n0048_3940", "pubmed23n0049_864", "pubmed23n0063_12708", "pubmed23n0048_4152", "pubmed23n0054_770", "pubmed23n0059_20799", "InternalMed_Harrison_25239", "Gynecology_Novak_6543", "pubmed23n0060_8553", "InternalMed_Harrison_28778", "pubmed23n0049_16375"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid