{"topic": "Anxiety disorder", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What role do genetic factors play in the etiology of generalized anxiety disorder?", "options": {"A": "Genetic factors play a major role in the etiology of generalized anxiety disorder", "B": "Genetic factors play a modest role in the etiology of generalized anxiety disorder", "C": "Genetic factors play no role in the etiology of generalized anxiety disorder", "D": "The role of genetic factors in the etiology of generalized anxiety disorder is unknown"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Genetic factors are estimated to contribute around 30% to the liability of generalized anxiety disorder, with the remainder resulting from environmental factors not shared by adult twins.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0052_3650", "title": "Generalized anxiety disorder in women. A population-based twin study.", "span_text": "Our results suggest the following: (1) GAD is a moderately familial disorder; (2) the tendency for GAD to run in families seems to be due largely or entirely to genetic factors shared between relatives rather than to the effects of the familial environment; (3) the heritability of GAD, estimated at around 30%, is modest, with the remainder of the variance in liability resulting from environmental factors not shared by adult twins;"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_3650", "pubmed23n0050_15176", "pubmed23n0048_17127", "Pediatrics_Nelson_357", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_2683", "pubmed23n0033_4056", "pubmed23n0052_6086", "pubmed23n0062_16590", "pubmed23n0047_4526", "pubmed23n0053_4805", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1143", "pubmed23n0054_5898", "pubmed23n0054_7177", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1040", "Pediatrics_Nelson_358", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1039", "pubmed23n0061_13917", "pubmed23n0045_5504", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1216", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_2138", "InternalMed_Harrison_5005", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_2634", "pubmed23n0035_826", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_989", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_2