{"topic": "Acne", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism by which Propionibacterium acnes contributes to the development of inflammatory acne lesions?", "options": {"A": "By activating the complement cascade", "B": "By stimulating sebaceous gland secretion", "C": "By promoting abnormal follicular hyperkeratosis", "D": "By inducing cellular immune mechanisms"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Propionibacterium acnes plays a key role in the genesis of the comedo and of inflammatory acne efflorescences, and its presence can lead to the activation of the complement cascade, which contributes to inflammation.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0006_3001", "title": "Activation of complement-a mechanism for the inflammation in acne", "span_text": "The mechanism of complement activation remains uncertain."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0006_3001", "pubmed23n0061_8584", "pubmed23n0061_5616", "pubmed23n0005_3041", "pubmed23n0005_13066", "pubmed23n0061_3214", "pubmed23n0006_244", "pubmed23n0005_7944", "pubmed23n0005_10827", "pubmed23n0048_19307"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0006_3001", "pubmed23n0061_8584", "pubmed23n0061_5616", "pubmed23n0005_3041", "pubmed23n0005_13066", "pubmed23n0061_3214", "pubmed23n0006_244", "pubmed23n0005_7944", "pubmed23n0005_10827", "pubmed23n0048_19307"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Acne Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7575.4127919790335, "llm_ms": 1232.1564580197446, "verification_ms": 1259.4632089603692, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid