{"topic": "Urinary tract infection", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism of action of methenamine in treating urinary tract infections?", "options": {"A": "It achieves therapeutic blood concentrations to combat infection", "B": "It is converted to formaldehyde in the urine, which has antibacterial activity", "C": "It prevents bacterial cell wall synthesis", "D": "It promotes the excretion of urinary tract pathogens"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Methenamine works by being converted into formaldehyde in the urine, which then acts to kill bacteria, making it effective against a broad spectrum of urinary tract pathogens.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0013_9123", "title": "Drug therapy reviews: methenamine mandelate and methenamine hippurate", "span_text": "The antimicrobial activity of methenamine depends on its conversion in the urine to formaldehyde. Formaldehyde's spectrum of antibacterial activity encompasses all urinary tract pathogens."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0013_422", "pubmed23n0013_9123", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5172", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4047", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5038", "pubmed23n0054_10758", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4080", "pubmed23n0055_16874", "pubmed23n0048_2651", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5625", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5068", "pubmed23n0044_10624", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5453", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2995", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5559", "pubmed23n0054_3142", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5758", "InternalMed_Harrison_338", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6467", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5325", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6811", "Pharmacology_Katzung_770", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1054", "pubmed23n0013_11508", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4063", "pubmed23n0011_6609", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2527", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5278", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5754", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1403", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5768"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0013_422", "pub