{"topic": "Immunization", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the primary method of preventing liver cancer through immunization?", "options": {"A": "Hepatitis A virus vaccine", "B": "Hepatitis B virus vaccine", "C": "Hepatitis C virus vaccine", "D": "Human papillomavirus vaccine"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Hepatitis B virus vaccine is the primary method of preventing liver cancer through immunization, as it provides durable immunity against hepatitis B virus infection, which is a major risk factor for liver cancer.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0055_9924", "title": "A worldwide perspective on the epidemiology and primary prevention of liver cancer", "span_text": "Primary prevention involves conducting mass immunization for hepatitis B virus in endemic countries along with education programs to improve food hygiene, decreasing alcohol intake, using sterile implements for immunizations and injections, smoking cessation, avoiding unnecessary blood transfusions and screening of blood for transfusions."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["First_Aid_Step2_237", "pubmed23n0023_10306", "pubmed23n0051_768", "pubmed23n0003_7908", "pubmed23n0055_9924", "pubmed23n0053_7099", "InternalMed_Harrison_12603", "InternalMed_Harrison_17080", "pubmed23n0044_19424", "pubmed23n0044_1828", "Surgery_Schwartz_1283", "InternalMed_Harrison_10885", "pubmed23n0052_14692", "Obstentrics_Williams_8908", "pubmed23n0061_9105", "pubmed23n0002_7294"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["First_Aid_Step2_237", "pubmed23n0023_10306", "pubmed23n0051_768", "pubmed23n0003_7908", "pubmed23n0055_9924", "pubmed23n0053_7099", "InternalMed_Harrison_12603", "InternalMed_Harrison_17080", "pubmed23n0044_19424", "pubmed23n0044_1828", "Surgery_Schwartz_1283", "InternalMed_Harrison_10885", "pubmed23n0052_14692", "Obstentrics_Williams_8908", "pubmed23n0061_9105", "pubmed23n0002_7294"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate"