{"topic": "Colorectal cancer", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the main dose-limiting toxicity of TAS-102 in the treatment of colorectal cancer?", "options": {"A": "Myelosuppression", "B": "Nausea and vomiting", "C": "Diarrhea", "D": "Fatigue"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "TAS-102 is an oral fluoropyrimidine that has clinical activity in 5-FU resistant tumors and displays similar clinical activity in the setting of wild-type and mutant RAS colorectal cancer. The main dose-limiting toxicity is myelosuppression, with neutropenia more commonly observed than anemia and thrombocytopenia.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_5928", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "The main dose-limiting toxicity is myelosuppression, with neutropenia more commonly observed than anemia and thrombocytopenia."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0051_6937", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5928", "Pharmacology_Katzung_108", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2398", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5914", "pubmed23n0054_5472", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3499", "pubmed23n0008_957", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5891", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5941", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5945", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7085", "Pharmacology_Katzung_422", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7144", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3997"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0051_6937", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5928", "Pharmacology_Katzung_108", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2398", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5914", "pubmed23n0054_5472", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3499", "pubmed23n0008_957", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5891", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5941", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5945", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7085", "Pharmacology_Katzung_422", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7144", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3997"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason"