{"topic": "Malaria", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a significant complication of severe malaria that requires increased awareness and widely available diagnostic and treatment facilities?", "options": {"A": "Hypoglycaemia", "B": "Hyperglycaemia", "C": "Dehydration", "D": "Hypertension"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Severe malaria can lead to several complications, including hypoglycaemia, which is a significant concern and requires prompt diagnosis and treatment.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0044_23398", "title": "Malaria in children in Papua New Guinea", "span_text": "Awareness of the complications of severe malaria, particularly hypoglycaemia, needs to be increased. Methods for the diagnosis and facilities for treatment of hypoglycaemia should be widely available."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_23398", "InternalMed_Harrison_9900", "pubmed23n0053_4218", "pubmed23n0044_23944", "pubmed23n0026_2683"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_23398", "InternalMed_Harrison_9900", "pubmed23n0053_4218", "pubmed23n0044_23944", "pubmed23n0026_2683"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Malaria Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6773.170541040599, "llm_ms": 1177.570666943211, "verification_ms": 917.3816660186276, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evide