{"topic": "Influenza", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What was a main objective of monitoring influenza in Israel during the 1976/77 season?", "options": {"A": "To define the prevalent virus involved in influenza activity", "B": "To determine the effectiveness of the influenza vaccine", "C": "To evaluate the economic impact of influenza on the healthcare system", "D": "To assess the role of influenza in cardiovascular disease"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The main objectives of the monitoring were to define the prevalent virus involved in influenza activity, determine the time of its occurrence, and evaluate its extent and impact.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0020_8409", "title": "Monitoring of influenza in Israel 1976/77", "span_text": "The main objectives of the monitoring were: (1) to define the prevalent virus involved in influenza activity: (2) to determine the time of its occurrence; and (3) to evaluate its extent and impact."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0020_8409", "pubmed23n0058_18485"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0020_8409", "pubmed23n0058_18485"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Influenza Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9452.395541011356, "llm_ms": 1068.9111250103451, "verification_ms": 1017.8990000276826, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all