{"topic": "Anemia", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is the primary step in diagnosing anemia in a patient?", "options": {"A": "Ordering a series of laboratory tests, including a complete blood count and peripheral blood smear", "B": "Conducting a physical examination to look for signs of anemia", "C": "Asking the patient about their medical history and symptoms", "D": "Prescribing iron supplements without further testing"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "A systematic approach to laboratory testing is essential for diagnosing anemia, and a complete blood count and peripheral blood smear are typically the first steps in this process.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0015_9331", "title": "Anemia in the orthopedic patient: a diagnostic approach", "span_text": "The diagnostic work-up is relatively simple if a systematic routine for ordering laboratory test is employed."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_9331", "pubmed23n0015_4995", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1924", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "Surgery_Schwartz_10044", "pubmed23n0010_6579", "pubmed23n0058_17636", "InternalMed_Harrison_8213", "pubmed23n0020_5155", "pubmed23n0062_17803"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_9331", "pubmed23n0015_4995", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1924", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "Surgery_Schwartz_10044", "pubmed23n0010_6579", "pubmed23n0058_17636", "InternalMed_Harrison_8213", "pubmed23n0020_5155", "pubmed23n0062_17803"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Anemia Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 5974.917749990709, "llm_ms": 1300.7019579526968, "ver