{"topic": "Colorectal cancer", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism of action of oxaliplatin in the treatment of colorectal cancer?", "options": {"A": "Inhibition of topoisomerase I", "B": "Inhibition of dihydrofolate reductase", "C": "Inhibition of thymidylate synthase", "D": "Formation of platinum-DNA adducts"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "Oxaliplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug that works by forming platinum-DNA adducts, which interfere with DNA replication and transcription, ultimately leading to cell death.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_5908", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Oxaliplatin is a third-generation diaminocyclohexane platinum analog. Its mechanism of action and clinical pharmacology are identical to those of cisplatin and carboplatin."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "textbook", "query": "oxaliplatin mechanism of action", "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_5954", "pubmed23n0049_1490", "pubmed23n0035_5", "pubmed23n0045_20584", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5908", "pubmed23n0046_2320", "Gynecology_Novak_7505", "Surgery_Schwartz_8778", "Obstentrics_Williams_8749", "pubmed23n0048_2733", "pubmed23n0056_3208", "pubmed23n0046_19458", "pubmed23n0022_3535", "pubmed23n0060_5654", "pubmed23n0057_9751", "pubmed23n0051_386", "pubmed23n0061_2569", "pubmed23n0061_19896", "pubmed23n0063_15166", "pubmed23n0054_17944", "pubmed23n0050_3505", "pubmed23n0014_1234", "pubmed23n0003_3940", "pubmed23n0057_6886", "pubmed23n0063_22274", "pubmed23n0062_10201", "pubmed23n0059_8920", "pubmed23n0046_11650", "pubmed23n0057_17763", "pubmed23n0036_4452", "pubmed23n0051_15077", "pubmed23n0057_12535", "pubmed23n0048_2729", "pubmed23n0059_21327", "pubmed23n0062_10726", "pubmed23n0037_592", "Gynecology_Novak_7625", "pubmed23n0018_5923", "pubmed23n0014_3696", "pubmed23n0010_1239", "pubmed23n0032_8070", "pubmed23n0024_3932", "pubmed23n0063_22383", "pubmed23n0057_22148", "pubmed23n