{"topic": "Dehydration", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A patient presents with sudden onset of profuse, watery diarrhea, vomiting, and rapid dehydration. What is the most likely diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "Cholera", "B": "Diabetes insipidus", "C": "Compulsive polydipsia", "D": "Gastroenteritis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms, such as sudden onset of profuse, watery diarrhea, vomiting, and rapid dehydration, are consistent with cholera, a diarrheal disease caused by the Vibrio cholerae organism.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0049_1302", "title": "The diagnosis and treatment of cholera", "span_text": "Cholera is a diarrheal disease that results from colonization of the small intestine by the Vibrio cholerae organism. The disease is spread primarily by means of fecal contamination of drinking water and may begin with the sudden onset of profuse, watery diarrhea."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "pubmed", "query": "cholera diagnosis", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0028_13951", "pubmed23n0049_1302"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0028_13951", "pubmed23n0049_1302"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Dehydration Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7205.520791991148, "llm_ms": 1452.5582080241293, "verification_ms": 1021.823792019859, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used":