{"topic": "HIV", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is the term for the paradoxical clinical deterioration that occurs in some patients with advanced HIV disease who are given anti-retroviral therapy during the period of recovery of the immune system?", "options": {"A": "Immune reconstitution inflammatory syndrome", "B": "Antiretroviral therapy syndrome", "C": "HIV-associated immune dysfunction", "D": "AIDS-related morbidity"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The immune reconstitution inflammatory syndrome is a complication of anti-retroviral therapy in patients with advanced HIV disease, characterized by a paradoxical clinical deterioration during the period of recovery of the immune system.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pathology_Robbins_1082", "title": "Pathology_Robbins", "span_text": "This disorder, called the immune reconstitution inflammatory syndrome, is not understood but is postulated to be a poorly regulated host response to the high antigenic burden of persistent microbes."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pathology_Robbins_1082", "pubmed23n0044_24349", "Pathology_Robbins_3910", "pubmed23n0046_13162", "pubmed23n0045_10855", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2636", "pubmed23n0053_1837", "pubmed23n0047_3072", "InternalMed_Harrison_4259", "pubmed23n0063_19914", "Obstentrics_Williams_7116", "InternalMed_Harrison_25535", "pubmed23n0060_4164", "InternalMed_Harrison_11709", "pubmed23n0053_1183", "Obstentrics_Williams_7793", "pubmed23n0043_6196", "Obstentrics_Williams_4882", "Obstentrics_Williams_6506"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pathology_Robbins_1082", "pubmed23n0044_24349", "Pathology_Robbins_3910", "pubmed23n0046_13162", "pubmed23n0045_10855", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2636", "pubmed23n0053_1837", "pubmed23n0047_3072", "InternalMed_Harrison_4259", "pubmed23n0063_19914", "Obstentrics_Williams_7116", "InternalMed_Harrison_25535", "pubmed23n0060_4164", "InternalMed_Harrison_11709", "pubmed23n0053_1183", "Obstentrics_Will