{"topic": "Preeclampsia", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is a key revision to the diagnostic criteria for preeclampsia made by The American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists in 2013?", "options": {"A": "Proteinuria is now an absolute requirement for making the diagnosis", "B": "Proteinuria is no longer an absolute requirement for making the diagnosis", "C": "Fetal growth restriction is now a defining criterion for severe preeclampsia", "D": "The terms mild and severe preeclampsia have been retained"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists issued a report in 2013 that included several revisions to the diagnostic criteria for preeclampsia, including the removal of proteinuria as an absolute requirement for diagnosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_552", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "proteinuria is no longer an absolute requirement for making the diagnosis; the terms mild and severe preeclampsia have been replaced, and the disease is now termed preeclampsia either with or without severe features; removal of fetal growth restriction as a defining criterion for severe preeclampsia."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "database", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_552", "pubmed23n0043_10754"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_552", "pubmed23n0043_10754"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Preeclampsia Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 22293.74179104343, "llm_ms": 1156.8523329915479, "verification_ms": 2896.837709005922, "extra_i