{"topic": "Prostate cancer", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the primary benefit of using serum prostate-specific antigen as a pre-screening test for prostate cancer?", "options": {"A": "It can detect prostate cancer at an early stage, reducing the risk of death from the disease.", "B": "It can distinguish between benign and malignant prostate tumors.", "C": "It can predict the aggressiveness of prostate cancer.", "D": "It can replace digital rectal examination and transrectal ultrasonography as a screening tool."}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary benefit of using serum prostate-specific antigen as a pre-screening test for prostate cancer is that it can detect the disease at an early stage, reducing the risk of death from prostate cancer.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0045_19421", "title": "Serum prostate specific antigen as pre-screening test for prostate cancer.", "span_text": "Prostate cancer has become the most common cancer and the second cause of death due to cancer in men in North America. Since curative therapies are limited to early stages of the disease, the availability of an efficient, easy to perform, widely acceptable and cost-effective method of early detection of prostate cancer is particularly important."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0045_19421", "pubmed23n0056_22895", "pubmed23n0052_12794", "pubmed23n0057_1843", "InternalMed_Harrison_7411", "InternalMed_Harrison_315", "pubmed23n0028_3223", "InternalMed_Harrison_6013", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "InternalMed_Harrison_312", "Surgery_Schwartz_11735", "InternalMed_Harrison_7413", "Gynecology_Novak_7457", "InternalMed_Harrison_7533", "Surgery_Schwartz_2375", "Surgery_Schwartz_2212", "pubmed23n0050_13753", "pubmed23n0024_423", "Surgery_Schwartz_11795", "Surgery_Schwartz_2210", "pubmed23n0046_3838", "pubmed23n0021_8317", "Gynecology_Novak_7456", "Surgery_Schwartz_2204", "pubmed23n0056_19772", "InternalM