{"topic": "Depression", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the recommended screening instrument for detecting depressive disorders in drug-dependent populations?", "options": {"A": "Beck Depression Inventory", "B": "Hamilton Depression Scale", "C": "Raskin Depression Scale", "D": "Symptom Checklist 90 Overall"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The Beck Depression Inventory is a 13-item patient self-report that has been shown to be the most sensitive and specific for screening drug-dependent populations for depression.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0006_4151", "title": "Detecting depressive disorders in drug abusers: a comparison of screening instruments", "span_text": "The results showed that: (1) although the sensitivity of the symptom scales was applicable, ranging from 65--94%, the specificity was less impressive, ranging from 39--61%, and (2) the Beck Depression Inventory, a 13-item patient self report was the most sensitive and specific and is recommended for screening drug-dependent populations for depression."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_10615", "pubmed23n0055_17232", "pubmed23n0006_4151", "InternalMed_Harrison_32015", "pubmed23n0047_9195", "Surgery_Schwartz_5393"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0054_10615", "pubmed23n0055_17232", "pubmed23n0006_4151", "InternalMed_Harrison_32015", "pubmed23n0047_9195", "Surgery_Schwartz_5393"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Depression Screening screening early detection risk assessment screening test sensitivity specificity guideline population screening high-risk preventive care follow-up diagnostic threshold", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 8392.316374985967, "llm_ms": 1427.6222500484437, "verification_ms": 919.7200000053272, 