{"topic": "Neonatal sepsis", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a significant risk factor for neonatal sepsis in newborns?", "options": {"A": "Low birth weight", "B": "Gestational age less than 37 weeks", "C": "Birth asphyxia", "D": "Neonatal hypoglycemia"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Newborns with weights < 5th percentile had a higher risk of low 5-minute Apgar score, respiratory distress, necrotizing enterocolitis, and neonatal sepsis than appropriate-weight neonates.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Obstentrics_Williams_5951", "title": "Obstentrics_Williams", "span_text": "In another analysis of more than 91,000 uncomplicated pregnancies, newborns with weights < 5th percentile had a higher risk of low 5-minute Apgar score, respiratory distress, necrotizing enterocolitis, and neonatal sepsis than appropriate-weight neonates."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_9297", "pubmed23n0053_17697", "pubmed23n0054_5962", "pubmed23n0047_21103", "Obstentrics_Williams_5951", "pubmed23n0024_12109", "pubmed23n0016_5043", "pubmed23n0043_1775", "Pathology_Robbins_1684", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1175", "Obstentrics_Williams_2354", "Obstentrics_Williams_5624", "pubmed23n0042_12454", "pubmed23n0014_6129", "pubmed23n0048_19624", "pubmed23n0015_6402", "pubmed23n0054_12552", "pubmed23n0052_1066", "pubmed23n0027_952", "pubmed23n0060_10639", "Obstentrics_Williams_7545", "pubmed23n0053_14192", "pubmed23n0047_6071", "InternalMed_Harrison_11709", "pubmed23n0038_8905", "pubmed23n0053_14517", "Surgery_Schwartz_13390", "Obstentrics_Williams_7067", "Obstentrics_Williams_3002", "Obstentrics_Williams_3189", "pubmed23n0059_164", "pubmed23n0048_164", "Pediatrics_Nelson_4100", "pubmed23n0052_8663", "Obstentrics_Williams_5623", "pubmed23n0018_2121", "pubmed23n0045_6812", "Gynecology_Novak_3843", "Obstentrics_Williams_6672", "pubmed23n0049_14995", "Pediatrics_Nelson_741", "pubmed23n0016_1976", "Obstentrics_Williams_5304", "Ob