{"topic": "Smoking cessation", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the recommended age range for initiating a discussion about lung cancer screening with apparently healthy patients who have at least a 30 pack-year smoking history?", "options": {"A": "55-74 years", "B": "45-64 years", "C": "65-80 years", "D": "35-54 years"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The U.S. Preventive Services Task Force recommends annual screening for lung cancer with low-dose computed tomography in high-risk patients, including those aged 55-74 years with a 30 pack-year smoking history.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Surgery_Schwartz_2209", "title": "Surgery_Schwartz", "span_text": "Surgery_Schwartz and treatment centers should initiate a discussion about lung cancer screening with apparently healthy patients age 55\u201374 y who have at least a 30 pack-y smoking history, and who currently smoke or have quit within the past 15 y."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Surgery_Schwartz_2209", "pubmed23n0058_693", "InternalMed_Harrison_6718", "pubmed23n0047_4026", "InternalMed_Harrison_5986", "Surgery_Schwartz_4496", "pubmed23n0061_8771", "pubmed23n0049_2332", "InternalMed_Harrison_6708", "pubmed23n0058_10126", "InternalMed_Harrison_5997", "InternalMed_Harrison_6719", "pubmed23n0050_12717", "pubmed23n0023_6984", "pubmed23n0022_1429"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Surgery_Schwartz_2209", "pubmed23n0058_693", "InternalMed_Harrison_6718", "pubmed23n0047_4026", "InternalMed_Harrison_5986", "Surgery_Schwartz_4496", "pubmed23n0061_8771", "pubmed23n0049_2332", "InternalMed_Harrison_6708", "pubmed23n0058_10126", "InternalMed_Harrison_5997", "InternalMed_Harrison_6719", "pubmed23n0050_12717", "pubmed23n0023_6984", "pubmed23n0022_1429"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Smoking cessation Screenin