{"topic": "Cirrhosis", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a potential complication of long-term parenteral nutrition?", "options": {"A": "Cirrhosis", "B": "Nephrotic syndrome", "C": "Hemolytic anemia", "D": "Myasthenia gravis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Cholestatic liver disease, which can lead to cirrhosis and liver failure, is a potential complication of long-term parenteral nutrition.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pediatrics_Nelson_741", "title": "Pediatrics_Nelson", "span_text": "The most concerning complication of long-term PN is cholestatic liver disease, which can lead to cirrhosis and liver failure."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0048_17874", "InternalMed_Harrison_23244", "Obstentrics_Williams_7600", "pubmed23n0058_1190", "Pediatrics_Nelson_741", "InternalMed_Harrison_23974", "Gynecology_Novak_3843", "InternalMed_Harrison_23532", "pubmed23n0037_12152", "InternalMed_Harrison_23916", "pubmed23n0048_16715"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0048_17874", "InternalMed_Harrison_23244", "Obstentrics_Williams_7600", "pubmed23n0058_1190", "Pediatrics_Nelson_741", "InternalMed_Harrison_23974", "Gynecology_Novak_3843", "InternalMed_Harrison_23532", "pubmed23n0037_12152", "InternalMed_Harrison_23916", "pubmed23n0048_16715"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Cirrhosis Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 12830.002542003058, "llm_ms": 1495.5499999923632, "verification_ms": 1312.9587910370901, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime