{"topic": "Stroke", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is crucial to avoid in patients with stroke or head trauma to prevent secondary brain injury?", "options": {"A": "Hypotension and hypoxia", "B": "Fever and hyperglycemia", "C": "Hypertension and hypoglycemia", "D": "Tachycardia and tachypnea"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Avoiding hypotension and hypoxia is critical in patients with stroke or head trauma as these conditions can lead to secondary brain injury.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_21189", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Thus, close monitoring of vital signs is important, as is early intervention to prevent secondary ischemia. Avoiding hypotension and hypoxia is critical, as significant hypotensive events (systolic blood pressure <90 mmHg) as short as 10 min in duration have been shown to adversely influence outcome after traumatic brain injury."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0005_7856", "InternalMed_Harrison_21189", "InternalMed_Harrison_21188", "First_Aid_Step1_476", "InternalMed_Harrison_18060", "pubmed23n0046_15578", "pubmed23n0056_6232", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3817"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0005_7856", "InternalMed_Harrison_21189", "InternalMed_Harrison_21188", "First_Aid_Step1_476", "InternalMed_Harrison_18060", "pubmed23n0046_15578", "pubmed23n0056_6232", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3817"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Stroke Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9352.58933401201, "llm_ms": 1141.3272499921732, "verification_ms": 1150.7867079926655, "ex