{"topic": "Preeclampsia", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the primary focus in preeclampsia research to understand the pathogenesis of the condition?", "options": {"A": "Understanding the coordinated interactions between the maternal vasculature and circulating pathogenic factors released from the placenta", "B": "Investigating the role of extracellular vesicles in placental-maternal vascular communication", "C": "Correlating BAFF levels in pregnancy with pregnancy outcomes among women with rheumatic disease", "D": "Analyzing the immunohistochemical expression of placental Netrin-1, Netrin-4, and UNC5B"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Preeclampsia research focuses on understanding the pathogenesis of the condition, which involves the coordinated interactions between the maternal vasculature and circulating pathogenic factors released from the placenta.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41575287", "title": "Exploring Placental Dysfunction: Models of Extracellular Vesicle Action in Preeclampsia", "span_text": "Understanding the coordinated interactions between the maternal vasculature and circulating pathogenic factors released from the placenta is a key focus in preeclampsia research."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41575287", "pubmed_web_41572585", "pubmed_web_41570703", "pubmed_web_41570402", "pubmed_web_41558071", "pubmed_web_41556143", "pubmed_web_41553376", "pubmed_web_41547325", "pubmed_web_41546192", "pubmed_web_41536443", "pubmed_web_41532530", "pubmed_web_41527979", "pubmed_web_41525794", "pubmed_web_41525064", "pubmed_web_41523416", "pubmed_web_41521060", "pubmed_web_41505823", "pubmed_web_41505741", "pubmed_web_41498149", "pubmed_web_41493740"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41575287", "pubmed_web_41572585", "pubmed_web_41570703", "pubmed_web_41570402", "pubmed_web_41558071", "pubmed_web_41556143", "pubmed_web_41553376", "pubmed_web_41547325", "pubmed_web_41