{"topic": "Pulmonary embolism", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the pathophysiological hallmark of massive pulmonary embolism?", "options": {"A": "Dyspnea, syncope, hypotension, and cyanosis", "B": "Tachypnea, tachycardia, and decreased oxygen saturation", "C": "Chest pain, cough, and hemoptysis", "D": "Fever, chills, and leukocytosis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Massive pulmonary embolism is characterized by extensive thrombosis affecting at least half of the pulmonary vasculature, leading to dyspnea, syncope, hypotension, and cyanosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_19658", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Massive PE accounts for 5\u201310% of cases, and is characterized by extensive thrombosis affecting at least half of the pulmonary vasculature. Dyspnea, syncope, hypotension, and cyanosis are hallmarks of massive PE."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_18253", "Surgery_Schwartz_923", "First_Aid_Step1_845", "InternalMed_Harrison_19658", "pubmed23n0030_628", "InternalMed_Harrison_20978", "pubmed23n0047_20701", "pubmed23n0016_5489", "InternalMed_Harrison_20982", "pubmed23n0044_5458", "pubmed23n0049_18840", "InternalMed_Harrison_32381", "pubmed23n0033_10796", "pubmed23n0038_5897", "pubmed23n0037_1320", "pubmed23n0051_15642", "pubmed23n0062_8891", "pubmed23n0032_3475", "pubmed23n0054_3031", "pubmed23n0028_7380", "pubmed23n0058_9975", "pubmed23n0034_1758", "InternalMed_Harrison_17616", "pubmed23n0012_7542", "pubmed23n0036_3024", "InternalMed_Harrison_1743", "pubmed23n0044_20770", "Neurology_Adams_6131", "InternalMed_Harrison_19926", "pubmed23n0046_3715", "InternalMed_Harrison_1371", "pubmed23n0060_13975", "pubmed23n0039_12237", "Physiology_Levy_2804", "pubmed23n0055_294", "InternalMed_Harrison_20981", "pubmed23n0049_19054", "pubmed23n0020_4299", "pubmed23n0041_6292", "pubmed23n0053_18573", "pubmed23n0049_14622", "InternalMed_Harrison_17