{"topic": "Hypothyroidism", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the recommended initial screening test for detecting primary hypothyroidism in neonates, considering the need to avoid a high recall rate and false-positive incidence?", "options": {"A": "Cord T.S.H.", "B": "Dried capillary-blood thyroxine (T4)", "C": "Serum T4 and thyroid-stimulating hormone (T.S.H.) assays from cord blood", "D": "Triiodothyronine resin uptake (T3U) measurements"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Cord T.S.H. is recommended as the initial screening test for primary hypothyroidism in neonates due to its higher specificity and sensitivity compared to other methods, which helps avoid a high recall rate and false-positive incidence.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0002_11976", "title": "Evaluation of three thyroid-function screening tests for detecting neonatal hypothyroidism", "span_text": "In marked contrast, cord T.S.H. as an initial screening test had a higher specificity and sensitivity for the diagnosis of primary hypothyroidism with the two affected cases, having values greater than 70 muU/ml (with only 0-24% of the screened population having values greater than 50 muU/ml)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0002_11976", "pubmed23n0016_13058", "pubmed23n0047_9261", "pubmed23n0018_452", "pubmed23n0015_2388", "pubmed23n0023_9529"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0002_11976", "pubmed23n0016_13058", "pubmed23n0047_9261", "pubmed23n0018_452", "pubmed23n0015_2388", "pubmed23n0023_9529"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hypothyroidism Screening screening early detection risk assessment screening test sensitivity specificity guideline population screening high-risk preventive care follow-up diagnostic threshold", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "sel