{"topic": "Pancreatitis", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What are the most common causes of acute pancreatitis?", "options": {"A": "Gallstones and alcohol", "B": "Smoking and obesity", "C": "Hypertriglyceridemia and autoimmune disorders", "D": "Genetic mutations and idiopathic factors"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The most common causes of acute pancreatitis are gallstones and alcohol, accounting for up to 80% of cases.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Surgery_Schwartz_9526", "title": "Surgery_Schwartz", "span_text": "The most common causes are gallstones and alcohol (Table 33-4), accounting for up to 80% of cases, but it is not uncommon to diagnose acute pancreatitis in the absence of these etiological factors (\u201cidiopathic acute pancreatitis\u201d), and it is important that a systematic approach is taken to the identification of other, less common and potentially modifiable factors."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Surgery_Schwartz_9526", "Surgery_Schwartz_9525", "pubmed23n0037_2404", "Surgery_Schwartz_9601", "pubmed23n0027_37", "pubmed23n0047_6931", "Surgery_Schwartz_9605", "InternalMed_Harrison_7143", "pubmed23n0020_6423", "pubmed23n0028_12232", "InternalMed_Harrison_28178", "pubmed23n0059_8949", "pubmed23n0036_6071"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Surgery_Schwartz_9526", "Surgery_Schwartz_9525", "pubmed23n0037_2404", "Surgery_Schwartz_9601", "pubmed23n0027_37", "pubmed23n0047_6931", "Surgery_Schwartz_9605", "InternalMed_Harrison_7143", "pubmed23n0020_6423", "pubmed23n0028_12232", "InternalMed_Harrison_28178", "pubmed23n0059_8949", "pubmed23n0036_6071"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Pancreatitis Etiology etiology cause risk factors pathogenesis mechanism underlying cause genetic factors environmental factors predisposing factors associated condi