{"topic": "Preeclampsia", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the recommended approach for monitoring women with severe preeclampsia, according to the Task Force?", "options": {"A": "Routine invasive monitoring", "B": "Invasive monitoring reserved for severely preeclamptic women with accompanying cardiac disease, renal disease, or both or with refractory hypertension, oliguria, and pulmonary edema", "C": "Daily outpatient monitoring of the mother and her fetus", "D": "No monitoring"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The Task Force recommends against routine invasive monitoring, reserving it for specific cases.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Obstentrics_Williams_5075", "title": "Obstentrics_Williams", "span_text": "The Task Force (2013) recommends against routine invasive monitoring. Such monitoring is best reserved for severely preeclamptic women with accompanying cardiac disease, renal disease, or both or with refractory hypertension, oliguria, and pulmonary edema."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "textbook", "doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_6959", "Obstentrics_Williams_5075", "Obstentrics_Williams_2298", "Obstentrics_Williams_5009", "pubmed23n0062_10388", "pubmed23n0051_14892"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_6959", "Obstentrics_Williams_5075", "Obstentrics_Williams_2298", "Obstentrics_Williams_5009", "pubmed23n0062_10388", "pubmed23n0051_14892"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Preeclampsia Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 39583.381166972686, "llm_ms": 1300.0567500130273, "verification_ms": 1367.772833968047, 