{"topic": "Pneumonia", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is a major risk factor for the development of pneumonia in children?", "options": {"A": "Malnutrition", "B": "Vaccination", "C": "Genetic predisposition", "D": "Family history of cancer"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Malnutrition is a major risk factor for the development of pneumonia in children, as it can impair the immune system and increase the risk of infection.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0062_17765", "title": "Case-control study on pathogenesis of pneumonia in children aged 0-2 years", "span_text": "Single factor analysis showed 29 factors were responsible for the increasing incidence of pneumonia. 13 of 29 factors were major pneumonia risk factors by the standard of means greater than 15 and OR greater than 3. They were malnutrition, anemia, riskets, pneumonia history, repeated colds, chronic diarrhoea, congenital malformation, asphyxia neonatorum, amniotic fluid aspiration, artificial feeding, too much clothing, family member with acute respiratory illness (ARI) and contact with ARI patients."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_17765", "pubmed23n0062_11179", "pubmed23n0063_21345", "pubmed23n0052_11440", "pubmed23n0058_14108", "pubmed23n0053_4478", "pubmed23n0052_1411", "pubmed23n0015_10739", "pubmed23n0062_5861", "pubmed23n0057_24111", "InternalMed_Harrison_10171", "pubmed23n0040_8379", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3017", "pubmed23n0049_8803", "InternalMed_Harrison_10904", "pubmed23n0007_1527"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_17765", "pubmed23n0062_11179", "pubmed23n0063_21345", "pubmed23n0052_11440", "pubmed23n0058_14108", "pubmed23n0053_4478", "pubmed23n0052_1411", "pubmed23n0015_10739", "pubmed23n0062_5861", "pubmed23n0057_24111", "InternalMed_Harrison_10171", "pubmed23n0040_8379", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3017", "pubmed23n0049_8803", "InternalMed_Harrison_10904", "pubmed23n0007_1527"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, 