{"topic": "Hepatitis C", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is a potential adverse effect of methyldopa?", "options": {"A": "Hepatitis", "B": "Nephritis", "C": "Arthritis", "D": "Pneumonia"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Methyldopa can cause hepatitis as a potential adverse effect.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_1043", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Other important adverse effects of methyldopa are development of a positive Coombs test (occurring in 10\u201320% of patients undergoing therapy for longer than 12 months), which sometimes makes cross-matching blood for transfusion difficult and rarely is associated with hemolytic anemia, as well as hepatitis and drug fever."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_1397", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1043", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5308", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6954", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1403", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4007", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2547", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5395", "Pharmacology_Katzung_453"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_1397", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1043", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5308", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6954", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1403", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4007", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2547", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5395", "Pharmacology_Katzung_453"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hepatitis C Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 10083.6506250198, "llm_ms": 1183.9136250200681, "verification_ms": 984.5959169906564, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted":