{"topic": "Rheumatoid arthritis", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 45-year-old woman presents with chronic widespread pain and morning stiffness. What is the most appropriate initial step in diagnosing rheumatoid arthritis?", "options": {"A": "Order a rheumatoid factor test", "B": "Perform a synovial membrane biopsy", "C": "Use the 1987 American College of Rheumatology criteria for classification of rheumatoid arthritis", "D": "Assess for the most common entities in the differential diagnosis"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms suggest a differential diagnosis that includes rheumatoid arthritis. Assessing for the most common entities in the differential diagnosis is the most appropriate initial step.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0010_6856", "title": "Differential diagnosis of rheumatic disease in the elderly", "span_text": "In each case the correct diagnosis should have been suspected from the history and physical examination alone, with the laboratory and x-ray findings providing supportive evidence."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_26171", "pubmed23n0010_6856", "pubmed23n0026_2893", "pubmed23n0037_5977", "pubmed23n0062_16486", "pubmed23n0054_83", "pubmed23n0037_3340", "InternalMed_Harrison_24082", "pubmed23n0022_1398", "pubmed23n0062_20034", "pubmed23n0025_3326", "pubmed23n0021_10808", "pubmed23n0037_10635", "InternalMed_Harrison_25959", "pubmed23n0060_19655", "InternalMed_Harrison_23904", "pubmed23n0053_14298", "pubmed23n0013_197", "pubmed23n0063_2568", "pubmed23n0007_7707", "pubmed23n0056_4517", "pubmed23n0010_7094", "pubmed23n0016_6286", "InternalMed_Harrison_25528", "pubmed23n0026_7554", "pubmed23n0011_8474", "pubmed23n0001_13700", "pubmed23n0003_768", "Neurology_Adams_7345", "pubmed23n0047_17905", "pubmed23n0010_8665", "InternalMed_Harrison_25217", "pubmed23n0052_6440", "pubmed23n0033_6712", "pubmed23n0051_16707", "pubmed23n0048_4595", "InternalMe