{"topic": "Hyperthyroidism", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is a known risk factor for autoimmune hepatitis in individuals with hyperthyroidism?", "options": {"A": "Hypothyroidism", "B": "Thyrotoxicosis with diffuse goiter", "C": "Malignant neoplasm of the thyroid gland", "D": "Goiter"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The odds ratio of thyrotoxicosis with diffuse goiter on AIH was 1.27, indicating an elevated risk.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41578488", "title": "Association between thyroid diseases and autoimmune hepatitis: A bidirectional Mendelian randomization study", "span_text": "The MR analysis showed that the odds ratio (OR) of hypothyroidism or myxedema on AIH was 1.23 (95% confidence intervals [CI] = 1.10 to 1.38, P = .0004), the OR of thyrotoxicosis with diffuse goiter on AIH was 1.27 (95% CI = 1.13-1.44, P = .0001), and the OR of Hashimoto thyroiditis on AIH was 1.41 (95% CI = 1.10-1.80, P = .0062) with inverse variance weighted method."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578488", "pubmed_web_41570039", "pubmed_web_41543742", "pubmed_web_41533941", "pubmed_web_41523860", "pubmed_web_41517795", "pubmed_web_41509944", "pubmed_web_41503929", "pubmed_web_41502204", "pubmed_web_41498932", "pubmed_web_41496136", "pubmed_web_41488629", "pubmed_web_41485171", "pubmed_web_41480813", "pubmed_web_41475880", "pubmed_web_41472742", "pubmed_web_41467267", "pubmed_web_41465251", "pubmed_web_41462485", "pubmed_web_41450582"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578488", "pubmed_web_41570039", "pubmed_web_41543742", "pubmed_web_41533941", "pubmed_web_41523860", "pubmed_web_41517795", "pubmed_web_41509944", "pubmed_web_41503929", "pubmed_web_41502204", "pubmed_web_41498932", "pubmed_web_41496136", "pubmed_web_41488629", "pubmed_web_41485171", "pubmed_web_41480813", "pubmed_web_41475880", "pubmed_web_41472742", "pubmed_web_41467267", "pubmed_web_41465251", "pubmed_web_41462485", "pu