{"topic": "Depression", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is a key consideration when diagnosing depression in patients with other medical conditions?", "options": {"A": "The presence of manic or hypomanic episodes", "B": "The absence of symptoms or signs of disease", "C": "The presence of clear-cut manifestations of other disorders", "D": "The exclusion of depression that is plausibly connected to personal distress or grieving due to a loss"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "Depression can be a comorbid condition with other medical conditions, and it is essential to consider the potential causes of depressive symptoms when making a diagnosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Neurology_Adams_12140", "title": "Neurology_Adams", "span_text": "Several formalized diagnostic criteria have been devised for both screening and diagnosis of major depression (Table 48-2). These codify the clinical features discussed in previous paragraphs but separate major depression from bipolar disorder by requiring the absence of elements that suggest a manic or hypomanic episode and further exclude depression that is plausibly connected to personal distress or grieving due to a loss, or the effects of a drug or toxic substance."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0017_12050", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1599", "InternalMed_Harrison_28583", "Neurology_Adams_12140", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1501", "pubmed23n0051_13441", "pubmed23n0017_6049", "pubmed23n0022_8534", "pubmed23n0034_1216", "pubmed23n0018_694", "pubmed23n0014_13165", "pubmed23n0037_8435"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0017_12050", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1599", "InternalMed_Harrison_28583", "Neurology_Adams_12140", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1501", "pubmed23n0051_13441", "pubmed23n0017_6049", "pubmed23n0022_8534", "pubmed23n0034_1216", "pubmed23n0018_694", "pubmed23n0014_13165", "pubmed23n0037_8435"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, 