{"topic": "Anemia", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "A 10-year-old patient presents with symptoms of anemia. What is the best initial screening test to identify the cause of anemia in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Complete Blood Count (CBC) with differential and review of the peripheral blood smear", "B": "Erythrocyte Sedimentation Rate (ESR) test", "C": "Liver function tests", "D": "Thyroid function tests"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "A CBC with differential and review of the peripheral blood smear is the best initial screening test to identify the cause of anemia in pediatric patients, as it can help identify various conditions such as leukemia, iron deficiency anemia, and other hematologic disorders.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "title": "Pediatrics_Nelson", "span_text": "A CBC with differential and review of the peripheral blood smear is the best screening test for many pediatric malignancies."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_9331", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "pubmed23n0015_4995", "pubmed23n0052_3067", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1924", "Pediatrics_Nelson_457", "pubmed23n0058_17636", "pubmed23n0019_1756", "InternalMed_Harrison_1835", "Surgery_Schwartz_8167"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_9331", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3308", "pubmed23n0015_4995", "pubmed23n0052_3067", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1924", "Pediatrics_Nelson_457", "pubmed23n0058_17636", "pubmed23n0019_1756", "InternalMed_Harrison_1835", "Surgery_Schwartz_8167"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Anemia Investigation investigation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging workup evaluation differential diagnosis clinical criteria biomarkers screening confirmatory test diagnostic accuracy", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index":