{"topic": "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the primary treatment modality for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) related to extensive cigarette smoking?", "options": {"A": "Smoking cessation, inhaled anticholinergic therapy, and oxygen supplementation", "B": "Beta agonists, mucolytics, and antibiotics", "C": "Steroids and theophylline", "D": "Corticosteroids and cromolyn"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary treatment modalities for COPD include smoking cessation, inhaled anticholinergic therapy, and oxygen supplementation, as these address the underlying causes and symptoms of the disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0048_9447", "title": "COPD: primary care management with drug and oxygen therapies", "span_text": "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease related in most cases to extensive cigarette smoking is a leading cause of morbidity and mortality among patients age 55 and older. Smoking cessation, inhaled anticholinergic therapy, and oxygen supplementation (when indicated) are primary treatment modalities."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_2200", "pubmed23n0014_2698", "pubmed23n0059_20077", "pubmed23n0048_9447", "Gynecology_Novak_3795", "First_Aid_Step2_1063", "pubmed23n0061_12104", "InternalMed_Harrison_25237", "pubmed23n0060_3302", "pubmed23n0061_8767", "pubmed23n0058_459", "pubmed23n0001_10283", "pubmed23n0045_10934", "pubmed23n0046_2320", "pubmed23n0045_1660", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3094", "pubmed23n0057_15176", "Gynecology_Novak_3798", "pubmed23n0013_7751", "pubmed23n0057_17794", "pubmed23n0022_2751", "pubmed23n0060_13879", "pubmed23n0026_1356", "pubmed23n0027_11294", "pubmed23n0054_7490", "pubmed23n0004_9746", "InternalMed_Harrison_16076", "pubmed23n0056_4757", "pubmed23n0042_9725", "Neurology_Adams_12315", "pubmed23n0044_15835", "pubmed23n0050_3505", "pubmed23n0014_10562", "pubmed23n0060_10873", "pubmed2