{"topic": "Preeclampsia", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is a key event in the development of preeclampsia?", "options": {"A": "Incomplete trophoblastic invasion of the maternal spiral arteries", "B": "Excessive placental production of vascular epithelial growth factor", "C": "Impaired vasodepressor function due to endothelial cell injury", "D": "Increased uterine artery vascular impedance"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Incomplete trophoblastic invasion of the maternal spiral arteries is a key event in the development of preeclampsia, leading to poor trophoblastic perfusion and endothelial cell injury.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0059_950", "title": "Pathophysiology of preeclampsia", "span_text": "Pathogenetically important events in the development of preeclampsia include incomplete trophoblastic invasion of the maternal spiral arteries, poor trophoblastic perfusion, elaboration of a putative endothelial cell toxin, and endothelial cell injury with resulting activation of coagulation, impairment of vasodepressor function, and altered endothelial permeability."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_4970", "Obstentrics_Williams_5190", "pubmed23n0059_950", "pubmed23n0059_958", "pubmed23n0030_4827", "Obstentrics_Williams_5167", "InternalMed_Harrison_550", "pubmed23n0051_9602", "pubmed23n0009_485", "Obstentrics_Williams_4900", "pubmed23n0052_18674", "Obstentrics_Williams_5148", "pubmed23n0043_3551", "Obstentrics_Williams_4903", "Obstentrics_Williams_6961", "Obstentrics_Williams_6444", "pubmed23n0062_11880", "Obstentrics_Williams_4893"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_4970", "Obstentrics_Williams_5190", "pubmed23n0059_950", "pubmed23n0059_958", "pubmed23n0030_4827", "Obstentrics_Williams_5167", "InternalMed_Harrison_550", "pubmed23n0051_9602", "pubmed23n0009_485", "Obstentrics_Williams_4900", "pubmed23n0052_18674", "Obstentrics_Williams_5148", "pubmed23n0043_