{"topic": "Migraine", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What was the outcome of migraine activity in patients who received biofeedback treatment, as measured at follow-up?", "options": {"A": "Migraine activity was significantly less at follow-up than at pretreatment", "B": "Migraine activity remained the same at follow-up as at pretreatment", "C": "Migraine activity increased at follow-up compared to pretreatment", "D": "Migraine activity could not be measured due to lack of follow-up data"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The study found that migraine activity was significantly less at follow-up than at pretreatment, although the long-term benefits could not be solely attributed to biofeedback due to the use of medication.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0059_7672", "title": "Long-term effects of biofeedback on migraine headache: a prospective follow-up study", "span_text": "Overall, results showed that migraine activity was significantly less at follow-up than at pretreatment."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "pubmed", "query": "migraine biofeedback treatment", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_7672", "pubmed23n0055_8121"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_7672", "pubmed23n0055_8121"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Migraine Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9070.78495901078, "llm_ms": 1406.9165409891866, "verification_ms": 1457.6004589907825, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 