{"topic": "Diabetes mellitus", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "A 30-year-old woman with a family history of diabetes is planning to become pregnant. What is the most appropriate approach to screening for gestational diabetes mellitus in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Screening should be performed only if she has symptoms of diabetes", "B": "Universal screening should be performed at least once during pregnancy", "C": "Screening should be based on the presence of historical risk factors and biophysical attributes", "D": "No screening is necessary due to her age and family history"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Universal screening for gestational diabetes mellitus is recommended for all pregnant women, regardless of risk factors, to reduce morbidity and improve outcomes.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_19621", "title": "Screening recommendations for gestational diabetes mellitus", "span_text": "Universal screening for gestational diabetes mellitus is justified by morbidity reduction, cost, and protocol simplicity and ease."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0058_693", "pubmed23n0050_7407", "pubmed23n0048_928", "pubmed23n0063_19621", "pubmed23n0002_4932", "pubmed23n0021_6096", "pubmed23n0037_2893", "pubmed23n0022_10344", "pubmed23n0053_3691", "pubmed23n0051_17081", "pubmed23n0063_21874", "pubmed23n0017_8616", "Obstentrics_Williams_7943", "pubmed23n0050_1929", "pubmed23n0057_2140", "pubmed23n0063_13878", "pubmed23n0055_22226", "pubmed23n0018_7972", "pubmed23n0061_13423", "pubmed23n0050_2715", "pubmed23n0049_11701", "pubmed23n0043_6323", "pubmed23n0047_15523", "pubmed23n0063_4728", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4655", "pubmed23n0053_4083", "Obstentrics_Williams_7945", "InternalMed_Harrison_896", "pubmed23n0048_17499"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0050_7407", "pubmed23n0048_928", "pubmed23n0063_19621", "pubmed23n0002_4932", "pubmed23n0021_6096", "pubmed23n0037_2893", "pubmed23n0022_10344", "p