{"topic": "Hyperlipidemia", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a significant predictor of angiographic coronary artery disease severity in members of high-risk pedigrees?", "options": {"A": "Increasing low-density lipoprotein cholesterol", "B": "Decreasing high-density lipoprotein cholesterol", "C": "Family history of hypertension", "D": "Age of onset of hyperlipidemia"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Clinical CHD, increasing low-density lipoprotein cholesterol, and decreasing high-density lipoprotein cholesterol are significant predictors of angiographic CAD severity.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0058_2094", "title": "Coronary risk factors and the severity of angiographic coronary artery disease in members of high-risk pedigrees", "span_text": "Clinical CHD (p less than 0.0001), increasing low-density lipoprotein cholesterol (LDL-C) (p = 0.0107), and decreasing HDL-C (p = 0.0068) were significant predictors of angiographic CAD severity."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0010_7082", "pubmed23n0042_15220", "pubmed23n0062_12872", "pubmed23n0058_2094", "InternalMed_Harrison_24161", "pubmed23n0050_3192", "pubmed23n0053_7125", "pubmed23n0047_1371", "Pathology_Robbins_2247", "Gynecology_Novak_6504"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0010_7082", "pubmed23n0042_15220", "pubmed23n0062_12872", "pubmed23n0058_2094", "InternalMed_Harrison_24161", "pubmed23n0050_3192", "pubmed23n0053_7125", "pubmed23n0047_1371", "Pathology_Robbins_2247", "Gynecology_Novak_6504"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hyperlipidemia Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "s