{"topic": "Hyperthyroidism", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is the most useful single screening test for hyperthyroidism?", "options": {"A": "Measurement of serum TSH", "B": "Measurement of free T4", "C": "Measurement of radioactive iodine uptake", "D": "Measurement of serum T3"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The measurement of serum TSH is the most useful single screening test for hyperthyroidism because TSH levels are decreased even at the earliest stages, when the disease may still be subclinical.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pathology_Robbins_4497", "title": "Pathology_Robbins", "span_text": "The measurement of serum TSH is the most useful single screening test for hyperthyroidism, because TSH levels are decreased even at the earliest stages, when the disease may still be subclinical."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_1599", "pubmed23n0053_16157", "pubmed23n0060_8987", "Pathology_Robbins_4497", "pubmed23n0017_8164", "InternalMed_Harrison_26785", "pubmed23n0037_11998", "pubmed23n0024_2010"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_1599", "pubmed23n0053_16157", "pubmed23n0060_8987", "Pathology_Robbins_4497", "pubmed23n0017_8164", "InternalMed_Harrison_26785", "pubmed23n0037_11998", "pubmed23n0024_2010"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hyperthyroidism Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 38683.18587500835, "llm_ms": 1388.4266249951907, "verification_ms": 2042.4409999977797, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "