{"topic": "Back pain", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the recommended approach for managing low back pain?", "options": {"A": "Ninety percent of all low back pain can be managed successfully by the skillful and appropriate use of the major analgesic drugs, NSAIDs, and the opioids.", "B": "Low back pain should be managed with surgery as the first line of treatment.", "C": "Low back pain can only be managed with alternative therapies such as acupuncture and massage.", "D": "Low back pain should be left untreated as it will resolve on its own."}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The management of low back pain involves the use of major analgesic drugs, NSAIDs, and opioids. Adjunctive drugs, such as skeletal muscle relaxants and antidepressants, may also be used as temporary aids to the major analgesics.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0061_4936", "title": "Management of low back pain by analgesics and adjuvant drugs", "span_text": "Ninety percent of all low back pain can be managed successfully by the skillful and appropriate use of the major analgesic drugs, NSAIDs, and the opioids."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_2200", "pubmed23n0045_20584", "pubmed23n0061_4936", "pubmed23n0050_17341", "pubmed23n0050_17342", "pubmed23n0045_6108", "pubmed23n0031_4281", "pubmed23n0060_260", "Gynecology_Novak_2502", "Surgery_Schwartz_13529", "pubmed23n0049_3730", "InternalMed_Harrison_1268", "Gynecology_Novak_2536", "pubmed23n0051_7898", "Obstentrics_Williams_8258", "pubmed23n0057_12535", "pubmed23n0057_17763", "pubmed23n0052_18176", "pubmed23n0050_14130", "pubmed23n0056_3208", "pubmed23n0047_12993", "pubmed23n0050_10339", "pubmed23n0063_22274", "pubmed23n0050_16161", "pubmed23n0009_1678", "InternalMed_Harrison_21302", "pubmed23n0002_13348", "pubmed23n0056_7129", "pubmed23n0052_20712", "pubmed23n0021_7295", "pubmed23n0016_3392", "pubmed23n0059_14951", "pubmed23n0011_3770", "Neurology_Adams_