{"topic": "Myocardial infarction", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the effect of beta-blockers on mortality in patients with myocardial infarction?", "options": {"A": "Beta-blockers decrease mortality by 15% at 1 week and 30% at 1 year", "B": "Beta-blockers have no effect on mortality in patients with myocardial infarction", "C": "Beta-blockers increase mortality in patients with myocardial infarction", "D": "Beta-blockers decrease mortality only in patients with hypertension"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Beta-blockers have been shown to decrease mortality in patients with myocardial infarction. Early intervention with intravenous beta-blockers results in a 15% reduction in cardiovascular mortality at 1 week, while later intervention with oral non-ISA beta-blockers results in a 30% reduction in mortality after 1 year.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0043_573", "title": "Beta-blockers: primary and secondary prevention", "span_text": "Early intervention (within 12 h) of chest pain with intravenous beta-blockers results in a 15% reduction in cardiovascular mortality at 1 week. Later intervention (3-28 days) with oral non-ISA beta-blockers results in a 30% reduction in mortality after 1 year;"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0043_573", "pubmed23n0057_19176", "pubmed23n0062_12527", "pubmed23n0054_8446", "pubmed23n0055_21461", "pubmed23n0043_14318", "InternalMed_Harrison_27562", "pubmed23n0058_12921", "pubmed23n0043_4744", "pubmed23n0063_12520", "InternalMed_Harrison_19052", "pubmed23n0045_3362", "pubmed23n0053_8595", "pubmed23n0010_5455", "pubmed23n0057_19797", "pubmed23n0023_5433", "pubmed23n0046_4582", "pubmed23n0055_16040", "pubmed23n0050_18826", "pubmed23n0053_18358", "pubmed23n0029_3715", "pubmed23n0045_13732", "pubmed23n0043_1659", "pubmed23n0022_1876", "pubmed23n0045_8140", "InternalMed_Harrison_29933", "pubmed23n0030_7401", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3815", "pubmed23n0026_6996", 