{"topic": "Hyperthyroidism", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the primary method of controlling hyperthyroidism in young patients with small glands and mild disease?", "options": {"A": "Antithyroid drug therapy", "B": "Destruction of the gland with radioactive iodine", "C": "Surgical thyroidectomy", "D": "Hormone replacement therapy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Antithyroid drug therapy is most useful in young patients with small glands and mild disease, as it allows for the possibility of spontaneous remission and does not permanently affect thyroid function.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_4295", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Drug therapy is most useful in young patients with small glands and mild disease. Methimazole (preferred) or propylthiouracil is administered until the disease undergoes spontaneous remission."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0057_17794", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4295", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4327", "pubmed23n0056_11432", "pubmed23n0057_11749", "pubmed23n0056_11930", "pubmed23n0053_20469", "Gynecology_Novak_3695", "pubmed23n0056_7324"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0057_17794", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4295", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4327", "pubmed23n0056_11432", "pubmed23n0057_11749", "pubmed23n0056_11930", "pubmed23n0053_20469", "Gynecology_Novak_3695", "pubmed23n0056_7324"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hyperthyroidism Therapy therapy treatment management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 5772.298375028186, "llm_ms": 882.219624996651, "verification_ms": 793.5493750264868, "ext