{"topic": "Acne", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is the pathogenesis of acne vulgaris?", "options": {"A": "A chronic inflammatory disorder with multifactorial causes", "B": "A bacterial infection caused by Propionibacterium acnes", "C": "A viral infection caused by a skin virus", "D": "A fungal infection caused by a skin fungus"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Acne vulgaris is a chronic inflammatory disorder that affects areas with the greatest concentration of sebaceous glands, such as the face, chest, and back. The pathogenesis of acne is multifactorial.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pediatrics_Nelson_4021", "title": "Pediatrics_Nelson", "span_text": "Pediatrics_Nelson Acne vulgaris (or acne) is a chronic inflammatory disorderthat affects areas with the greatest concentration of sebaceous glands, such as the face, chest, and back. The pathogenesis of acne is multifactorial."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 10, "doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_4021", "pubmed23n0061_5616"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_4021", "pubmed23n0061_5616"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 5, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Acne Etiology etiology cause risk factors pathogenesis mechanism underlying cause genetic factors environmental factors predisposing factors associated conditions epidemiology incidence", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 4994.3280830048025, "llm_ms": 836.093541001901, "verification_ms": 0.5007500294595957, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 0, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 1}, "failed_checks": ["evidence_span_mismatch"], "failed_checks_all": ["evidence_span_mismatch"], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_