{"topic": "Asthma", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism of action of albuterol in the treatment of asthma?", "options": {"A": "Selective \u03b22 agonist", "B": "Nonselective \u03b2-adrenoceptor antagonist", "C": "Phosphodiesterase inhibition", "D": "Adenosine receptor antagonist"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Albuterol is a selective \u03b22 agonist, which means it primarily acts on \u03b22 receptors in the lungs to cause bronchodilation, making it an effective treatment for asthma.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_2160", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Albuterol Prompt, efficacious bronchodilation Selective \u03b22 agonist"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_2160", "Pharmacology_Katzung_278", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2162", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1231", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2081", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2161", "pubmed23n0050_11261", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2086", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2119", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3051", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4408"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_2160", "Pharmacology_Katzung_278", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2162", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1231", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2081", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2161", "pubmed23n0050_11261", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2086", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2119", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3051", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4408"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Asthma Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6919.714333023876, "llm_ms": 886.108582955