{"topic": "Hypertension", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the primary goal of preventive practices for hypertension?", "options": {"A": "To reduce blood pressure in individuals with established hypertension", "B": "To prevent the development of hypertension in high-risk individuals", "C": "To manage symptoms of hypertension", "D": "To reduce the risk of cardiovascular disease in individuals with hypertension"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The primary goal of preventive practices for hypertension is to prevent the development of hypertension in high-risk individuals, as stated in the evidence from [E3] and [E6].", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0037_11153", "title": "A protocol for hypertension screening and referral", "span_text": "The current nationwide attack on hypertension, with its emphasis on early detection and prevention, has served to reinforce optometry's commitment to vision-related health screening and referral."}, {"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Gynecology_Novak_839", "title": "Gynecology_Novak", "span_text": "The Joint National Committee on Prevention, Detection, Evaluation, and Treatment of High Blood Pressure (JNC 7) released their seventh report in 2003. The purpose was to provide an evidence-based approach to the prevention and management of hypertension."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_13659", "pubmed23n0053_19289", "pubmed23n0037_11153", "pubmed23n0043_6323", "pubmed23n0052_82", "Gynecology_Novak_839", "Surgery_Schwartz_5388", "InternalMed_Harrison_322", "pubmed23n0007_6598", "InternalMed_Harrison_17264", "pubmed23n0063_12708", "Gynecology_Novak_836", "pubmed23n0043_573", "pubmed23n0063_6707", "Neurology_Adams_6348", "pubmed23n0054_2264", "pubmed23n0049_16234", "pubmed23n0057_3845", "InternalMed_Harrison_19570", "InternalMed_Harrison_24032", "pubmed23n0052_2656", "pubmed23n0050_3812", "pubmed23n0022_1876", "pubmed23n0046_10063"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["