{"topic": "Appendicitis", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 25-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with a 2-day history of abdominal pain, initially diffuse and now localized to the right lower quadrant. What is the most important part of the diagnosis in suspected appendicitis?", "options": {"A": "Laboratory tests", "B": "Imaging studies", "C": "Clinical examination", "D": "Surgical consultation"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "Clinical examination remains the most important part of the diagnosis in suspected appendicitis, as it allows for the evaluation of signs and symptoms, such as migration of pain to the right iliac fossa, guarding, and rigidity, which support the diagnosis of appendicitis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0061_3824", "title": "[Clinical examination remains the most important part of the diagnosis in suspected appendicitis]", "span_text": "This paper reports why the rate of unnecessary appendectomies can not be reduced exclusively by selected diagnostic laparoscopy. 75 women and 94 men greater than or equal to 16 years of age which had undergone appendectomy and/or diagnostic laparoscopy were analyzed for 19 clinical criteria in a retrospective study."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_13611", "pubmed23n0059_8127", "pubmed23n0063_8551", "pubmed23n0060_12036", "pubmed23n0061_3824", "pubmed23n0063_4437", "pubmed23n0041_11346", "pubmed23n0058_19650", "pubmed23n0046_16252", "pubmed23n0012_856", "pubmed23n0040_3708", "pubmed23n0044_25120", "pubmed23n0063_345", "Obstentrics_Williams_7483", "pubmed23n0034_446", "pubmed23n0046_12653"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_13611", "pubmed23n0059_8127", "pubmed23n0063_8551", "pubmed23n0060_12036", "pubmed23n0061_3824", "pubmed23n0063_4437", "pubmed23n0041_11346", "pubmed23n0058_19650", "pubmed23n0046_16252", "pubmed23n0012_856", "pubmed23n0040_3708", "pubmed23n0044_25120", "pubmed23n0063_345", "Obstentrics_Wil