{"topic": "Anxiety disorder", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is a common comorbidity found in patients with eating disorders, such as bulimia nervosa?", "options": {"A": "Generalized anxiety disorder", "B": "Schizophrenia", "C": "Personality disorder", "D": "Substance abuse"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "A striking proportion of eating disorder subjects were comorbid for one or more anxiety disorders, the most frequent diagnoses being generalized anxiety disorder and social phobia.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0047_19745", "title": "Comparison of bulimics, obese binge eaters, social phobics, and individuals with panic disorder on comorbidity across DSM-III-R anxiety disorders.", "span_text": "A striking proportion of eating disorder subjects were comorbid for one or more anxiety disorders, the most frequent diagnoses being generalized anxiety disorder and social phobia."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_22254", "pubmed23n0047_19745", "Pediatrics_Nelson_443", "pubmed23n0050_16725", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_2608", "pubmed23n0044_23435", "pubmed23n0043_1229", "pubmed23n0002_2983", "pubmed23n0003_2374", "pubmed23n0045_2497", "pubmed23n0030_8411", "pubmed23n0060_4894", "pubmed23n0046_3360", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1415", "pubmed23n0018_2369", "pubmed23n0062_15586", "pubmed23n0058_1106", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1044", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1175", "pubmed23n0043_15656", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1187", "pubmed23n0056_6564", "pubmed23n0054_12961", "pubmed23n0034_1216", "pubmed23n0060_4940", "pubmed23n0041_11325", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1107", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1275"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_22254", "pubmed23n0047_19745", "Pediatrics_Nelson_443", "pubmed23n0050_16725", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_2608", "pubmed23n0044_23435", "pubmed23n0043_1229", "pubmed23n0002_2983", "pubmed23n0003_2374", "pubmed23n0045_2497", "pubmed23n0030_8411", "pubmed23n0060_4894", "pubmed23n0046_3360", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_141