{"topic": "Pancreatitis", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What role do stellate cells play in the development of chronic pancreatitis?", "options": {"A": "They produce digestive enzymes that contribute to pancreatic damage", "B": "They activate cytokine expression and produce extracellular matrix proteins, leading to inflammation and fibrosis", "C": "They regulate the secretion of hormones that stimulate pancreatic growth", "D": "They are involved in the absorption of nutrients from the pancreatic duct"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Stellate cells play a key role in the development of chronic pancreatitis by activating cytokine expression and producing extracellular matrix proteins, which leads to inflammation and fibrosis in the pancreas.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_24406", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Irrespective of the mechanism of injury, it is becoming apparent that stellate cell activation that results in cytokine expression and production of extracellular matrix proteins cause acute and chronic inflammation and collagen deposition in the pancreas."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_10514", "Surgery_Schwartz_9916", "InternalMed_Harrison_24406", "Surgery_Schwartz_9544", "Pathology_Robbins_691", "Surgery_Schwartz_9915", "pubmed23n0032_7385", "pubmed23n0003_3608", "InternalMed_Harrison_21516", "pubmed23n0060_3158", "pubmed23n0013_10808", "pubmed23n0039_1501", "pubmed23n0057_17284", "pubmed23n0036_9907", "pubmed23n0043_14548", "pubmed23n0042_13508", "pubmed23n0026_2295", "Pathology_Robbins_4094", "pubmed23n0048_18663", "pubmed23n0025_5052", "pubmed23n0051_20326", "pubmed23n0060_2237", "pubmed23n0014_6129"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Surgery_Schwartz_9916", "InternalMed_Harrison_24406", "Surgery_Schwartz_9544", "Pathology_Robbins_691", "Surgery_Schwartz_9915", "pubmed23n0032_7385", "pubmed23n0003_3608", "InternalMed_Harrison_21516", "pubmed23n00