{"topic": "Appendicitis", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is believed to be an important step in the development of appendicitis?", "options": {"A": "Obstruction of the appendiceal lumen", "B": "Inflammation of the ileocecal region", "C": "Vascular thrombosis", "D": "Ischemic necrosis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Obstruction of the appendiceal lumen is believed to be an important step in the development of appendicitis, as it can lead to bacterial overgrowth and luminal distension, resulting in increased intraluminal pressure and potentially causing vascular thrombosis and ischemic necrosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_23202", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Although not proven, obstruction of the appendiceal lumen is believed to be an important step in the development of appendicitis. In some cases, obstruction leads to bacterial overgrowth and luminal distension, with an increase in intraluminal pressure that can inhibit the flow of lymph and blood in some cases."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2022-01-01 12:00:00", "doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_2861", "InternalMed_Harrison_23202", "Surgery_Schwartz_8859", "pubmed23n0024_8310", "pubmed23n0031_2492", "pubmed23n0052_822", "pubmed23n0016_13617"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_2861", "InternalMed_Harrison_23202", "Surgery_Schwartz_8859", "pubmed23n0024_8310", "pubmed23n0031_2492", "pubmed23n0052_822", "pubmed23n0016_13617"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": "2022-01-01 12:05:00", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Appendicitis Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 8532.28