{"topic": "Breast cancer", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism by which breast cancer cells metastasize to bone?", "options": {"A": "Through the stepwise process of metastasis development", "B": "By direct invasion of breast tissue into bone", "C": "Through the bloodstream, targeting areas of high metabolic activity", "D": "By lymphatic spread, bypassing the bloodstream"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Breast cancer cells undergo a stepwise process for metastases development, similar to other tumor types, to metastasize to bone.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0048_12140", "title": "Bone metastasis in breast cancer", "span_text": "It is presumed that breast cancer cells undergo the same stepwise process for metastases development as demonstrated in other tumor types."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_4473", "Surgery_Schwartz_3891", "pubmed23n0048_12140", "pubmed23n0053_18083", "Surgery_Schwartz_3918", "pubmed23n0049_16863", "pubmed23n0049_11909", "pubmed23n0057_1716", "pubmed23n0052_14395", "pubmed23n0049_16862", "pubmed23n0062_16314", "pubmed23n0062_13846", "InternalMed_Harrison_7947", "pubmed23n0063_22312", "Surgery_Schwartz_3901", "pubmed23n0062_1706", "pubmed23n0049_239", "Cell_Biology_Alberts_5732", "Surgery_Schwartz_3916", "pubmed23n0003_586", "pubmed23n0050_6566", "Surgery_Schwartz_2373", "pubmed23n0060_9051", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4622", "Gynecology_Novak_3459", "Pathology_Robbins_4988", "Gynecology_Novak_7920", "Gynecology_Novak_560", "pubmed23n0049_4467", "Pathology_Robbins_4910", "pubmed23n0040_3898", "Surgery_Schwartz_2102", "Surgery_Schwartz_2374", "pubmed23n0051_141", "pubmed23n0007_11863", "pubmed23n0050_19064", "pubmed23n0014_986", "InternalMed_Harrison_27371", "pubmed23n0010_1080", "pubmed23n0045_9605", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7182", "Surgery_Schwartz_4153", "pubmed23n0050_3863"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_4473", "Surgery_Schwart