{"topic": "Diarrhea", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "A patient develops diarrhea after treatment with antimicrobial drugs. What is the most appropriate method for diagnosing the cause of diarrhea?", "options": {"A": "Monitoring of the degree of inflammation of the bowel mucosa, the intensity and severity of diarrhea, the duration of illness, changes in stool form, and the eradication of C. difficile or its toxins from stool", "B": "Assessing the patient's temperature and blood pressure", "C": "Checking the patient's white blood cell count", "D": "Performing a liver function test"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Diagnosing the cause of diarrhea after treatment with antimicrobial drugs requires a comprehensive approach, including monitoring of the degree of inflammation of the bowel mucosa, the intensity and severity of diarrhea, the duration of illness, changes in stool form, and the eradication of C. difficile or its toxins from stool.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0049_9822", "title": "Evaluation of new anti-infective drugs for the treatment of antibiotic-associated colitis", "span_text": "Outcome should be assessed by monitoring of the degree of inflammation of the bowel mucosa, the intensity and severity of diarrhea, the duration of illness, changes in stool form, and the eradication of C. difficile or its toxins from stool."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_9822", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4045", "pubmed23n0053_17129", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6141"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_9822", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4045", "pubmed23n0053_17129", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6141"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Diarrhea Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease con