{"topic": "Urinary tract infection", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is a possible virulence factor of Escherichia coli that contributes to its ability to cause pyelonephritis?", "options": {"A": "The ability to adhere and colonize the urinary tract", "B": "The ability to produce toxins that damage the kidney", "C": "The ability to invade the bloodstream", "D": "The ability to form biofilms"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Escherichia coli's ability to adhere and colonize the urinary tract is a key factor in its ability to cause pyelonephritis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0055_22124", "title": "Etiology and pathophysiology of pyelonephritis", "span_text": "Escherichia coli is the most frequent cause of pyelonephritis. Its possible virulence factors include the ability to adhere and colonize the urinary tract, an important initiating factor in all urinary tract infections (UTIs)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0025_3893", "InternalMed_Harrison_3815", "pubmed23n0055_22124", "pubmed23n0060_1503", "Physiology_Levy_3277", "pubmed23n0052_16850", "pubmed23n0063_8555", "pubmed23n0049_10514", "pubmed23n0019_10662", "pubmed23n0051_201", "InternalMed_Harrison_14832", "InternalMed_Harrison_9290", "pubmed23n0062_1152", "InternalMed_Harrison_21379", "pubmed23n0050_7242", "pubmed23n0055_23642", "pubmed23n0057_23722", "pubmed23n0050_6969", "pubmed23n0019_4659", "pubmed23n0007_15296", "pubmed23n0062_3480", "pubmed23n0019_7839", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3436", "pubmed23n0056_1604", "pubmed23n0008_15129", "pubmed23n0058_9823", "pubmed23n0008_5019", "pubmed23n0006_15386", "pubmed23n0060_10410", "pubmed23n0053_18402", "pubmed23n0027_15447", "pubmed23n0037_1001", "pubmed23n0049_8701", "InternalMed_Harrison_10685", "pubmed23n0012_4998", "pubmed23n0015_7052", "pubmed23n0026_4222", "pubmed23n0032_9420", "pubmed23n0027_4551", "pubmed23n0047_5576", "pubmed23n0002_9449", "InternalMed_Harrison_7475", "pubme