{"topic": "COVID-19", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "A patient with COVID-19 infection develops ascending symmetrical limb weakness and progressive loss of reflexes, accompanied by arterial blood pressure fluctuations and other signs of autonomic dysfunction. What is the likely diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "Guillain-Barre Syndrome (GBS) with dysautonomia", "B": "Myalgic encephalomyelitis/chronic fatigue syndrome", "C": "Post-infection irritable bowel syndrome (PI-IBS)", "D": "Cutaneous leukocytoclastic vasculitis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms, including ascending symmetrical limb weakness and progressive loss of reflexes, accompanied by arterial blood pressure fluctuations and other signs of autonomic dysfunction, are indicative of Guillain-Barre Syndrome (GBS) with dysautonomia.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41579008", "title": "Dysautonomia after COVID-19 infection: A case report", "span_text": "Clinical manifestations, neurophysiological findings, and laboratory results were indicative of Guillain-Barre Syndrome (GBS), leading to a conclusive diagnosis of GBS with dysautonomia triggered by a COVID-19 infection."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41580870", "pubmed_web_41580869", "pubmed_web_41580219", "pubmed_web_41579008", "pubmed_web_41578455", "pubmed_web_41577611", "pubmed_web_41576966", "pubmed_web_41576058", "pubmed_web_41576003", "pubmed_web_41574613", "pubmed_web_41574293", "pubmed_web_41574291", "pubmed_web_41573986", "pubmed_web_41573794", "pubmed_web_41573583", "pubmed_web_41573439", "pubmed_web_41573202", "pubmed_web_41572466", "pubmed_web_41572075", "pubmed_web_41571780"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41580869", "pubmed_web_41580219", "pubmed_web_41579008", "pubmed_web_41578455", "pubmed_web_41577611", "pubmed_web_41576966", "pubmed_web_41576058", "pubmed_web_41576003", "pubmed_web_41574613", "pubmed_web_41574293", "pubmed_web_415