{"topic": "Sepsis", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What role do toll-like receptors play in the pathophysiology of sepsis?", "options": {"A": "They recognize pathogen-associated molecular patterns and trigger proinflammatory responses.", "B": "They inhibit the production of cytokines and reduce inflammation.", "C": "They have no role in the recognition of microbial cell wall constituents.", "D": "They only recognize damage-associated molecular patterns."}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Toll-like receptors recognize pathogen-associated molecular patterns and trigger proinflammatory responses, which is a key factor in the pathophysiology of sepsis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pathology_Robbins_694", "title": "Pathology_Robbins", "span_text": "Likely initiators of inflammation in sepsis are signaling pathways that lie downstream of Toll-like receptors (TLRs) (Chapter 5), which recognize a host of microbe-derived substances containing so-called \u201cpathogen-associated molecular patterns\u201d (PAMPs)"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_16789", "Pathology_Robbins_694", "InternalMed_Harrison_21505", "pubmed23n0060_3157", "pubmed23n0062_2056", "InternalMed_Harrison_9290", "Surgery_Schwartz_923", "pubmed23n0047_14615", "pubmed23n0051_11348", "Surgery_Schwartz_276", "pubmed23n0050_18868", "pubmed23n0035_253", "pubmed23n0053_15022", "pubmed23n0059_14752", "pubmed23n0045_19477", "Pathology_Robbins_716", "pubmed23n0055_6038", "pubmed23n0050_21085"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pathology_Robbins_694", "InternalMed_Harrison_21505", "pubmed23n0060_3157", "pubmed23n0062_2056", "InternalMed_Harrison_9290", "Surgery_Schwartz_923", "pubmed23n0047_14615", "pubmed23n0051_11348", "Surgery_Schwartz_276", "pubmed23n0050_18868", "pubmed23n0035_253", "pubmed23n0053_15022", "pubmed23n0059_14752", "pubmed23n0045_19477", "Pathology_Robbins_716", "pubmed23n0055_6038", "pubmed23n0050_21085", "pubmed23n0061_16789"], "r