{"topic": "Back pain", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the primary approach for managing low back pain?", "options": {"A": "Surgical intervention", "B": "Skillful and appropriate use of major analgesic drugs", "C": "Alternative therapies such as acupuncture", "D": "Lifestyle modifications only"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The management of low back pain primarily involves the skillful and appropriate use of major analgesic drugs, including NSAIDs and opioids, along with adjunctive drugs like skeletal muscle relaxants and antidepressants.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0061_4936", "title": "Management of low back pain by analgesics and adjuvant drugs", "span_text": "Ninety percent of all low back pain can be managed successfully by the skillful and appropriate use of the major analgesic drugs, NSAIDs, and the opioids."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_2200", "pubmed23n0045_20584", "pubmed23n0061_4936", "pubmed23n0050_17341", "pubmed23n0050_17342", "pubmed23n0045_6108", "pubmed23n0031_4281", "pubmed23n0060_260", "Gynecology_Novak_2502", "Surgery_Schwartz_13529", "pubmed23n0049_3730", "InternalMed_Harrison_1268", "Gynecology_Novak_2536", "pubmed23n0051_7898", "Obstentrics_Williams_8258", "pubmed23n0057_12535", "pubmed23n0057_17763", "pubmed23n0052_18176", "pubmed23n0050_14130", "pubmed23n0056_3208", "pubmed23n0047_12993", "pubmed23n0050_10339", "pubmed23n0063_22274", "pubmed23n0050_16161", "pubmed23n0009_1678", "InternalMed_Harrison_21302", "pubmed23n0002_13348", "pubmed23n0056_7129", "pubmed23n0052_20712", "pubmed23n0021_7295", "pubmed23n0016_3392", "pubmed23n0059_14951", "pubmed23n0011_3770", "Neurology_Adams_1117", "pubmed23n0060_14369", "pubmed23n0051_15077", "pubmed23n0043_2187", "Gynecology_Novak_2856", "pubmed23n0048_15419", "pubmed23n0018_5923", "pubmed23n0059_17142", "pubmed23n0026_6441", "pubmed23n0028_12066", "Neurology_Adams_162