{"topic": "Rheumatoid arthritis", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the primary goal of management in rheumatoid arthritis?", "options": {"A": "To suppress symptoms and signs of rheumatoid disease", "B": "To decrease disease activity and lessen permanent joint damage", "C": "To increase or maintain function and produce few side effects", "D": "To keep the cost to a minimum"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Management should help relieve symptoms, increase or maintain function, produce few side effects and keep the cost to a minimum. However, only gold compounds, penicillamine and cytotoxic therapy have been shown to decrease disease activity and lessen permanent joint damage.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0022_10689", "title": "Rheumatoid arthritis", "span_text": "Management should help relieve symptoms, increase or maintain function, produce few side effects and keep the cost to a minimum. Aspirin remains the first-line drug; other nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs may be useful when aspirin cannot be tolerated. Symptoms and signs of rheumatoid disease may be suppressed by corticosteroids, but only gold compounds, penicillamine and cytotoxic therapy have been shown to decrease disease activity and lessen permanent joint damage."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0022_10689", "pubmed23n0043_7755", "pubmed23n0043_10192", "pubmed23n0059_2531", "pubmed23n0032_10468", "pubmed23n0002_13348", "pubmed23n0026_6441", "pubmed23n0022_2751", "pubmed23n0009_4538", "pubmed23n0045_3078", "pubmed23n0036_4633", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6103", "pubmed23n0032_7276", "pubmed23n0051_18174", "pubmed23n0059_2530", "pubmed23n0017_11264", "pubmed23n0051_9936", "pubmed23n0043_13274", "Obstentrics_Williams_8302", "pubmed23n0054_180", "pubmed23n0052_15883", "pubmed23n0010_1218", "pubmed23n0056_16156", "pubmed23n0046_1892", "pubmed23n0045_4449", "pubmed23n0049_8621", "pubmed23n0028_12066", "pubmed23n0024_5960", "pu