{"topic": "Osteoporosis", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is a potential consequence of long-term heparin therapy in patients?", "options": {"A": "Osteoporosis and spontaneous fractures", "B": "Increased bone density", "C": "Improved renal function", "D": "Enhanced lipoprotein lipase activity"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Long-term heparin therapy is associated with osteoporosis and spontaneous fractures due to its effects on bone mineral homeostasis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_3761", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Long-term heparin therapy is associated with osteoporosis and spontaneous fractures. Heparin accelerates the clearing of postprandial lipemia by causing the release of lipoprotein lipase from tissues, and long-term use is associated with mineralocorticoid deficiency."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 10, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_385", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4839", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3761", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4404", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4842", "Pharmacology_Katzung_244"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_385", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4839", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3761", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4404", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4842", "Pharmacology_Katzung_244"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 5, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteoporosis Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6895.949749974534, "llm_ms": 945.5710829934105, "verification_ms": 962.9202919895761, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"