{"topic": "Hypertension", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the current approach to the management of hypertension, replacing the traditional stepped care method?", "options": {"A": "Tailored therapy", "B": "Stepped care", "C": "Combination therapy", "D": "Monotherapy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The current approach to the management of hypertension has evolved from stepped care to tailored therapy, which involves selecting the first-line drug therapy based on an assessment of the patient's overall cardiovascular risk profile.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0059_20077", "title": "From stepped care to tailored therapy", "span_text": "Stepped care has been replaced by 'tailored therapy'. That is, based on an assessment of the patient's overall cardiovascular risk profile, the choice of first-line drug therapy has been broadened beyond diuretics and beta-blockers to include ACE inhibitors, calcium antagonists and selective alpha 1-blockers."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_20077", "pubmed23n0042_12959", "pubmed23n0022_11986", "InternalMed_Harrison_25125", "InternalMed_Harrison_22127", "InternalMed_Harrison_21652", "pubmed23n0045_14165", "pubmed23n0039_410", "pubmed23n0061_1343", "pubmed23n0061_19780", "pubmed23n0049_16234", "pubmed23n0062_12872", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1218", "pubmed23n0045_6481", "pubmed23n0056_4389", "InternalMed_Harrison_18590", "pubmed23n0044_2037", "pubmed23n0057_21089", "pubmed23n0045_4850", "pubmed23n0056_790", "Obstentrics_Williams_8126", "pubmed23n0014_10259", "pubmed23n0001_4834", "InternalMed_Harrison_19619", "pubmed23n0045_13186", "pubmed23n0034_5054", "pubmed23n0017_2808", "pubmed23n0054_8923", "pubmed23n0054_20860", "pubmed23n0059_14790", "pubmed23n0015_4594", "pubmed23n0008_12884", "pubmed23n0049_12543"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_20077", "pubmed23n0042_12959", "pubmed23n0022_11986", "InternalMed_Harrison_25125", "InternalMed_Harrison_22