{"topic": "Hypothyroidism", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the outcome of pregnancy in women with overt hypothyroidism who receive appropriate replacement therapy?", "options": {"A": "Rates of adverse effects are not increased in most reports", "B": "Rates of preterm birth are higher", "C": "Risks for some pregnancy complications are greater", "D": "Infant mortality is increased"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "With appropriate replacement therapy, rates of adverse effects are not increased in most reports, although some studies suggest that risks for some pregnancy complications may be greater even with replacement therapy.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Obstentrics_Williams_8071", "title": "Obstentrics_Williams", "span_text": "With appropriate replacement therapy, however, rates of adverse efects are not increased in most reports (Bryant, 2015; Matalon, 2006; Tan, 2006)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_8071", "pubmed23n0059_5119", "Obstentrics_Williams_8091"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_8071", "pubmed23n0059_5119", "Obstentrics_Williams_8091"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hypothyroidism Prognosis prognosis outcomes mortality survival complications disease course recurrence risk stratification severity long-term outcomes quality of life predictors", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 10484.424084017519, "llm_ms": 879.0996659663506, "verification_ms": 959.1010420117527, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Obstent