{"topic": "Dermatitis", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is a potential treatment for atopic dermatitis that selectively inhibits T-cell proliferation by inhibiting calcineurin and subsequent interleukin 2 production?", "options": {"A": "Topical calcineurin inhibitors", "B": "Cyclosporin A", "C": "Levamisole therapy", "D": "High-dose UVA1 therapy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Topical calcineurin inhibitors, such as topical tacrolimus and pimecrolimus, are used to treat atopic dermatitis by selectively inhibiting T-cell proliferation.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pediatrics_Nelson_4043", "title": "Pediatrics_Nelson", "span_text": "Topical calcineurin inhibitors (also referred to as topicalimmune modulators) such as topical tacrolimus and pimecrolimus may be part of the treatment regimen for atopic dermatitis.These agents selectively inhibit T-cell proliferation by inhibitingcalcineurin and subsequent interleukin 2 production."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 10, "doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_4043", "pubmed23n0042_14476", "pubmed23n0012_7561", "pubmed23n0051_20999", "pubmed23n0062_14665"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_4043", "pubmed23n0042_14476", "pubmed23n0012_7561", "pubmed23n0051_20999", "pubmed23n0062_14665"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 5, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Dermatitis Therapy therapy treatment management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 14933.228374982718, "llm_ms": 909.1821250040084, "verification_ms": 0.6494589615613222, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 0, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDE