{"topic": "Hypertension", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the primary factor that influences the long-term prognosis of patients with hypertension and type I diabetes?", "options": {"A": "Quality of life", "B": "Presence of proteinuric type I diabetic patients", "C": "Genetic predisposition to hypertension", "D": "Sodium/lithium countertransport activity"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The presence of proteinuric type I diabetic patients has a significant influence on the long-term prognosis of patients with hypertension and type I diabetes, as it increases the risk of complications such as diabetic nephropathy, renal dysfunction, and mortality.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0049_6412", "title": "Comments on the clinical impact of hypertension in type I diabetes", "span_text": "Cumulative evidence has shown that proteinuric type I diabetic patients are easily susceptible to hypertension and its accompanying sequelae."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_1027", "pubmed23n0049_6412", "pubmed23n0005_12236", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1934", "pubmed23n0036_3361", "Obstentrics_Williams_8283", "pubmed23n0039_7037", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3447", "pubmed23n0008_13969", "InternalMed_Harrison_18570", "pubmed23n0045_726", "pubmed23n0038_11069", "pubmed23n0063_12841", "pubmed23n0057_21938", "InternalMed_Harrison_25129", "pubmed23n0062_5695", "pubmed23n0031_2267", "pubmed23n0042_6504", "pubmed23n0015_715", "pubmed23n0047_14284", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6415", "InternalMed_Harrison_19741", "Obstentrics_Williams_1010", "Obstentrics_Williams_6904", "pubmed23n0049_6776", "pubmed23n0061_10992", "pubmed23n0051_18406", "Surgery_Schwartz_5057", "pubmed23n0049_16234", "InternalMed_Harrison_21649", "InternalMed_Harrison_19906", "pubmed23n0049_16207"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_1027", "pubmed23n0049_6412", "pubmed23n0005_12236", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1934", "pubmed23n0036_3361", "Obstentrics_Williams_8283", 