{"topic": "Anemia", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is a potential consequence of not detecting heterozygous carriers of thalassemias in a population with a high prevalence of these conditions?", "options": {"A": "Inappropriate work-up or treatment for iron deficiency", "B": "Increased risk of developing a different type of anemia", "C": "Reduced risk of severe anemia in children", "D": "No significant impact on public health"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Heterozygous carriers for either type of thalassemia mimic iron deficiency, which may lead to inappropriate work-up or treatment if not detected.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0059_1424", "title": "Hereditary anemias in Hawaii", "span_text": "Heterozygous carriers for either type mimic iron deficiency, which may lead to inappropriate work-up or treatment."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_1424"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_1424"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Anemia Prevention prevention prophylaxis risk reduction screening vaccination primary prevention secondary prevention lifestyle modification counseling public health early detection follow-up", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 8832.481624966022, "llm_ms": 1216.972458991222, "verification_ms": 762.6232079928741, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0059_1424"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 100.0, "verification": 200.0, "llm": 1216.972458991222}}}
{"topic": "Acute kidney injury", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is a potential therapeutic strategy for acute kidney injury that involves targeting damaged renal tubular epithelial cells and mitigating oxidative stress?", "options": {"A": "Renal replacement therapy", "B": "Cascade-targeted core-shell nanotherapeutic agent", "C": "Hemodialysis", "D": "Plasma exchange"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The correct answer is B, as it describes a therapeutic strategy that involves targeting damaged renal tubular epithelial cells and mitigating oxidative stress, which is a key aspect of acute kidney injury treatment.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41580683", "title": "Renal-tubular-mitochondrial sequentially targeted nanoagent breaks the vicious cycle of oxidative stress and mtDNA-driven inflammation in acute kidney injury therapy", "span_text": "The present study developed a cascade-targeted core-shell nanotherapeutic agent STMB with L-serine shell that enables precise kidney injury molecule 1-mediated delivery to damaged RTECs, while tannic acid core facilitates mitochondrial localization."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41580843", "pubmed_web_41580683", "pubmed_web_41580574", "pubmed_web_41580347", "pubmed_web_41579307", "pubmed_web_41578941", "pubmed_web_41578542", "pubmed_web_41578395", "pubmed_web_41578027", "pubmed_web_41578009", "pubmed_web_41576499", "pubmed_web_41575963", "pubmed_web_41575788", "pubmed_web_41575776", "pubmed_web_41575591", "pubmed_web_41575219", "pubmed_web_41574613", "pubmed_web_41573814", "pubmed_web_41573720", "pubmed_web_41573632"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41580843", "pubmed_web_41580683", "pubmed_web_41580574", "pubmed_web_41580347", "pubmed_web_41579307", "pubmed_web_41578941", "pubmed_web_41578542", "pubmed_web_41578395", "pubmed_web_41578027", "pubmed_web_41578009", "pubmed_web_41576499", "pubmed_web_41575963", "pubmed_web_41575788", "pu