{"topic": "Osteoporosis", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 45-year-old woman presents with hip pain and limping. What is the most likely diagnosis if conventional radiography shows patchy osteoporosis of the proximal femur?", "options": {"A": "Transient osteoporosis of the hip", "B": "Osteonecrosis", "C": "Senile osteoporosis", "D": "Reflex sympathetic dystrophy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The clinical presentation and radiographic findings are consistent with transient osteoporosis of the hip, a condition characterized by pain, limping, and patchy osteoporosis of the proximal femur.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0049_3158", "title": "Transient osteoporosis of the hip: clinical and imaging features", "span_text": "Transient osteoporosis of the hip is a form of reflex sympathetic dystrophy characterized by pain, limping, limitation of hip joint motion, and delayed radiographic patchy osteoporosis of the proximal femur."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0029_10838", "pubmed23n0049_3158", "pubmed23n0048_2443", "pubmed23n0063_21226", "pubmed23n0016_1324", "pubmed23n0048_4241"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0029_10838", "pubmed23n0049_3158", "pubmed23n0048_2443", "pubmed23n0063_21226", "pubmed23n0016_1324", "pubmed23n0048_4241"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteoporosis Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 5761.53424999211, "llm_ms": 1007.7928339596838, "verification_ms": 758.5110000218265, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted