{"topic": "HIV", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the primary goal of HIV risk assessment in primary care settings?", "options": {"A": "To determine the need for mandatory HIV testing", "B": "To guide detection and interpretation of symptoms that could reflect an STD", "C": "To provide treatment for patients with known infections", "D": "To conduct routine demographic data collection"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "HIV risk assessment is important in primary care settings to guide detection and interpretation of symptoms that could reflect an STD, decisions on screening or prophylactic/preventive treatment, and risk reduction counseling and intervention.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "STD/HIV risk assessment guides detection and interpretation of symptoms that could reflect an STD; decisions on screening or prophylactic/preventive treatment; risk reduction counseling and intervention (e.g., hepatitis B vaccination); and treatment of partners of patients with known infections."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_11098", "First_Aid_Step2_800", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "Gynecology_Novak_713", "pubmed23n0045_9263", "pubmed23n0062_6531", "pubmed23n0059_1775", "InternalMed_Harrison_15079", "pubmed23n0056_4156", "InternalMed_Harrison_23590", "Gynecology_Novak_709", "pubmed23n0046_23613", "pubmed23n0055_22938", "pubmed23n0059_18696", "pubmed23n0058_19887", "First_Aid_Step2_852", "pubmed23n0047_7842", "pubmed23n0048_7714", "pubmed23n0044_11028", "pubmed23n0051_18245", "pubmed23n0060_9625", "pubmed23n0052_19218", "pubmed23n0054_12575"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_11098", "First_Aid_Step2_800", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "Gynecology_Novak_713", "pubmed23n0045_9263", "pubmed23n0062_6531", "pubmed23n0059_1775", "InternalMed_Harrison_15079", "pubmed23n0056_4156", "InternalMed_Harrison_23590", "Gynecology_Nov