{"topic": "Influenza", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the primary public health measure for preventing influenza?", "options": {"A": "Vaccination", "B": "Antiviral medication", "C": "Infection control", "D": "Improved management of diabetes"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The major public health measure for prevention of influenza is vaccination, which can provide 50-80% protection against influenza if the vaccine virus and the currently circulating viruses are closely related.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_14754", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "The major public health measure for prevention of influenza is vaccination. Both inactivated (killed) and live attenuated vaccines are available and are generated from isolates of influenza A and B viruses that circulated in the previous influenza seasons and are anticipated to circulate in the upcoming season."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_13659", "InternalMed_Harrison_11663", "pubmed23n0025_2073", "pubmed23n0013_73", "pubmed23n0044_3044", "Obstentrics_Williams_7084", "InternalMed_Harrison_14754", "InternalMed_Harrison_9865", "pubmed23n0002_7474", "pubmed23n0005_2948", "InternalMed_Harrison_11296", "Obstentrics_Williams_8908"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_13659", "InternalMed_Harrison_11663", "pubmed23n0025_2073", "pubmed23n0013_73", "pubmed23n0044_3044", "Obstentrics_Williams_7084", "InternalMed_Harrison_14754", "InternalMed_Harrison_9865", "pubmed23n0002_7474", "pubmed23n0005_2948", "InternalMed_Harrison_11296", "Obstentrics_Williams_8908"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Influenza Prevention prevention prophylaxis risk reduction screening vaccination primary prevention secondary prevention lifestyle modification counseling public h