{"topic": "Influenza", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a potential complication of influenza in individuals with underlying diseases?", "options": {"A": "Reversible deterioration of cardiovascular function", "B": "Irreversible deterioration of pulmonary function", "C": "Temporary improvement of renal function", "D": "Enhanced immune response"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Influenza outbreaks can lead to a gradual deterioration of underlying cardiovascular, pulmonary, or renal function in elderly and high-risk individuals, which can occasionally be irreversible and lead to death.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_14743", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "In addition to complications involving the specific organ systems described above, influenza outbreaks include cases in which elderly and other high-risk individuals develop influenza and subsequently experience a gradual deterioration of underlying cardiovascular, pulmonary, or renal function\u2014changes that occasionally are irreversible and lead to death."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_14743", "pubmed23n0024_8060", "InternalMed_Harrison_14719", "InternalMed_Harrison_14692", "pubmed23n0053_18352", "pubmed23n0019_11981", "pubmed23n0050_11350", "pubmed23n0062_5865", "pubmed23n0060_227", "pubmed23n0019_12527"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_14743", "pubmed23n0024_8060", "InternalMed_Harrison_14719", "InternalMed_Harrison_14692", "pubmed23n0053_18352", "pubmed23n0019_11981", "pubmed23n0050_11350", "pubmed23n0062_5865", "pubmed23n0060_227", "pubmed23n0019_12527"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Influenza Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity h