{"topic": "Appendicitis", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the diagnostic value of serial total leucocyte counts in acute appendicitis?", "options": {"A": "The sensitivity and specificity of serial leucocyte counts in acute appendicitis were 92 and 100 per cent", "B": "The sensitivity and specificity of serial leucocyte counts in acute appendicitis were 50 and 75 per cent", "C": "The sensitivity and specificity of serial leucocyte counts in acute appendicitis were 25 and 50 per cent", "D": "The sensitivity and specificity of serial leucocyte counts in acute appendicitis were 10 and 25 per cent"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The diagnostic value of serial total leucocyte counts in acute appendicitis is high, with sensitivity and specificity of 92 and 100 per cent, respectively.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0046_16252", "title": "Role of sequential leucocyte counts and C-reactive protein measurements in acute appendicitis", "span_text": "The sensitivity and specificity of serial leucocyte counts in acute appendicitis were 92 and 100 per cent, and for CRP concentrations 69 and 75 per cent, respectively."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_13611", "pubmed23n0061_3824", "pubmed23n0046_16252", "pubmed23n0048_16667", "pubmed23n0043_7671", "pubmed23n0058_19650", "pubmed23n0062_3408", "pubmed23n0063_8551", "pubmed23n0014_910", "Obstentrics_Williams_7483", "pubmed23n0041_11346", "pubmed23n0045_3383", "pubmed23n0060_12036", "pubmed23n0012_856", "Obstentrics_Williams_7482", "pubmed23n0048_15620", "pubmed23n0017_6765", "pubmed23n0052_3140", "pubmed23n0006_13072", "pubmed23n0039_11079", "pubmed23n0059_4198"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_13611", "pubmed23n0061_3824", "pubmed23n0046_16252", "pubmed23n0048_16667", "pubmed23n0043_7671", "pubmed23n0058_19650", "pubmed23n0062_3408", "pubmed23n0063_8551", "pubmed23n0014_910", "Obstentrics_Williams_7483", "pubmed23n0041_11346", "pubmed