{"topic": "Typhoid fever", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the importance of monitoring serum iron and zinc concentrations during typhoid fever?", "options": {"A": "To assess the effectiveness of chloramphenicol therapy", "B": "To diagnose the disease", "C": "To monitor the patient's nutritional status", "D": "To predict the risk of complications"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Monitoring serum iron and zinc concentrations is important to assess the effectiveness of chloramphenicol therapy, as the therapy can increase serum iron concentrations, while the increase in serum zinc concentrations is a disease-related phenomenon.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0036_6052", "title": "Serum zinc, iron, and copper concentrations during typhoid fever in man: effect of chloramphenicol therapy", "span_text": "In volunteers experimentally infected with Salmonella typhi, serum iron and zinc concentrations became significantly depressed and there was a concomitant rise in serum copper before the onset of overt clinical illness. However, after several days of fever and the initiation of chloramphenicol therapy, serum iron and zinc concentrations significantly increased."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0036_6052", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5618", "InternalMed_Harrison_21189", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3329", "pubmed23n0049_9816", "pubmed23n0048_4943", "pubmed23n0062_4436", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2224", "pubmed23n0011_7454", "pubmed23n0048_12280", "pubmed23n0041_3763", "pubmed23n0061_15653"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0036_6052", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5618", "InternalMed_Harrison_21189", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3329", "pubmed23n0049_9816", "pubmed23n0048_4943", "pubmed23n0062_4436", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2224", "pubmed23n0011_7454", "pubmed23n0048_12280", "pubmed23n0041_3763", "pubmed23n0061_15653"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [],