{"topic": "Cervical cancer", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the primary goal of monitoring CA 125 levels in patients with epithelial ovarian cancer?", "options": {"A": "To assess the clinical potential of serial serum CA 125 measurements", "B": "To determine the efficacy of pharmacokinetic monitoring and dose modification of etanidazole", "C": "To investigate the individual and combined value of CA 15-3 and carcinoembryonic antigen as breast cancer tumor markers", "D": "To study the incidence of and time to a complete response for patients receiving etanidazole and radiation therapy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary goal of monitoring CA 125 levels in patients with epithelial ovarian cancer is to assess the clinical potential of serial serum CA 125 measurements in the follow-up of patients with histologically confirmed ovarian carcinoma.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0052_7551", "title": "CA125-response assessment in epithelial ovarian cancer", "span_text": "To assess the clinical potential of serial serum CA125 measurements in the follow-up of patients with epithelial ovarian cancer, 74 consecutive unselected patients with histologically confirmed ovarian carcinoma were studied prospectively."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_7551", "pubmed23n0051_1037", "pubmed23n0059_10567", "pubmed23n0004_8620", "pubmed23n0050_9885", "pubmed23n0043_19064", "pubmed23n0033_8947", "pubmed23n0049_19970", "pubmed23n0046_23335", "pubmed23n0045_513", "pubmed23n0003_10673", "InternalMed_Harrison_32562", "pubmed23n0050_4265", "pubmed23n0046_1088", "pubmed23n0033_8254", "pubmed23n0011_5118", "pubmed23n0057_19565", "pubmed23n0047_5553", "pubmed23n0056_19706", "pubmed23n0060_13607", "pubmed23n0044_10834", "pubmed23n0020_4993", "pubmed23n0050_8496", "pubmed23n0004_1198", "pubmed23n0056_13696", "pubmed23n0051_15459", "pubmed23n0046_2718", "pubmed23n0012_1598", "InternalMed_Harrison_26718",