{"topic": "Obesity", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is a limitation of using ultrasound to examine the pancreas?", "options": {"A": "The patient's age", "B": "The patient's gender", "C": "Bowel gas and obesity", "D": "The patient's blood pressure"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "Bowel gas and obesity are limitations of using ultrasound to examine the pancreas because they can interfere with the ultrasound waves and reduce the quality of the images.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0024_278", "title": "Ultrasonic evaluation of the pancreas", "span_text": "Bowel gas and obesity remain serious limitations to adequate examination, and in these patients computed tomography offers a complementary modality."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0064_321", "pubmed23n0024_278", "pubmed23n0052_13273", "pubmed23n0039_5412", "pubmed23n0050_6556"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0064_321", "pubmed23n0024_278", "pubmed23n0052_13273", "pubmed23n0039_5412", "pubmed23n0050_6556"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Obesity Investigation investigation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging workup evaluation differential diagnosis clinical criteria biomarkers screening confirmatory test diagnostic accuracy", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 25619.441959017422, "llm_ms": 1238.0396659718826, "verification_ms": 884.802957996726, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0064_321", "pubmed23n0024_278", "pubmed23n0052_13273", "pubme