{"topic": "Rheumatoid arthritis", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism of action of oxaprozin in the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis?", "options": {"A": "Inhibition of cyclo-oxygenase, resulting in decreased prostaglandin biosynthesis", "B": "Stimulation of osteoblastic activity", "C": "Inhibition of fibroblast proliferation", "D": "Induction of apoptosis in malignant lymphoma cells"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Oxaprozin is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) that works by inhibiting cyclo-oxygenase, which decreases the formation of prostaglandin precursors from arachidonic acid, resulting in decreased prostaglandin biosynthesis and reduced pain and inflammatory responses.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0054_3142", "title": "Oxaprozin: a once-daily nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug.", "span_text": "By inhibiting cyclo-oxygenase, oxaprozin decreases the formation of prostaglandin (PG) precursors from arachidonic acid, resulting in decreased PG biosynthesis and reduced pain and inflammatory responses."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "pubmed", "query": "oxaprozin mechanism of action", "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_7183", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4090", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7188", "pubmed23n0054_3142", "pubmed23n0043_16914", "First_Aid_Step1_537", "pubmed23n0062_21124", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6173", "pubmed23n0026_8770", "pubmed23n0051_20067", "pubmed23n0045_4449", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6229", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7187", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7085", "pubmed23n0050_6015", "pubmed23n0010_3863", "pubmed23n0003_8453", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7184", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3994", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3944", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4063", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6667", "pubmed23n0035_4885", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4001", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6967", "pubmed23n0051_9936", "pubmed23n0033_5934", "pubmed23n0012_254"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_7183", "Pharmacology_Katzun