{"topic": "Anemia", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is a recommended screening test for children?", "options": {"A": "Anemia and lead screening", "B": "Lipid disorders screening", "C": "Tuberculosis testing", "D": "Hearing and vision evaluation only"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Children usually are quite healthy and only the following screening tests are recommended: newborn metabolic screening with hemoglobin electrophoresis, hearing and vision evaluation, anemia and lead screening, and tuberculosis testing.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pediatrics_Nelson_130", "title": "Pediatrics_Nelson", "span_text": "Children usually are quite healthy and only the following screening tests are recommended: newborn metabolic screening with hemoglobin electrophoresis, hearing and vision evaluation, anemia and lead screening, and tuberculosis testing."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "database", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0043_18931", "Pediatrics_Nelson_130", "pubmed23n0059_1424"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0043_18931", "Pediatrics_Nelson_130", "pubmed23n0059_1424"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Anemia Screening screening early detection risk assessment screening test sensitivity specificity guideline population screening high-risk preventive care follow-up diagnostic threshold", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 13283.560583018698, "llm_ms": 1005.0292919622734, "verification_ms": 1104.1022909921594, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0043_18931", "Pediatrics_Nel