{"topic": "Deep vein thrombosis", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A patient is diagnosed with deep-vein thrombosis and is prescribed thalidomide. What is a common adverse effect of thalidomide that increases the risk of this condition?", "options": {"A": "Peripheral neuropathy", "B": "Increased risk of bleeding", "C": "Increased risk of deep-vein thrombosis", "D": "Hypothyroidism"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "Thalidomide has several adverse effects, including an increased risk of deep-vein thrombosis, particularly in patients with hematologic malignancies.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_6121", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "The adverse effect profile of thalidomide is extensive. The most important toxicity is teratogenesis. Because of this effect, thalidomide prescription and use is closely regulated by the manufacturer. Other adverse effects of thalidomide include peripheral neuropathy, constipation, rash, fatigue, hypothyroidism, and increased risk of deep-vein thrombosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["First_Aid_Step1_472", "InternalMed_Harrison_366", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3753", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6121", "pubmed23n0047_156", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3843", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3004", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2504", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3817"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_366", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3753", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6121", "pubmed23n0047_156", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3843", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3004", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2504", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3817", "First_Aid_Step1_472"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Deep vein thrombosis Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics moni