{"topic": "Deep vein thrombosis", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism by which deep vein thrombosis forms and flourishes?", "options": {"A": "In an environment of stasis, low oxygen tension, and upregulation of proinflammatory genes", "B": "In an environment of high blood flow, high oxygen tension, and downregulation of proinflammatory genes", "C": "In an environment of normal blood flow, normal oxygen tension, and normal regulation of proinflammatory genes", "D": "In an environment of low blood flow, high oxygen tension, and upregulation of proinflammatory genes"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Deep vein thrombosis forms and flourishes in an environment of stasis, low oxygen tension, and upregulation of proinflammatory genes.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_19653", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Venous thrombi form and flourish in an environment of stasis, low oxygen tension, and upregulation of proinflammatory genes."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_13507", "InternalMed_Harrison_19653", "pubmed23n0026_7298", "pubmed23n0063_1900", "InternalMed_Harrison_9290", "InternalMed_Harrison_19849", "pubmed23n0048_6008", "pubmed23n0046_3715", "pubmed23n0060_1744", "pubmed23n0038_8200", "Pathology_Robbins_717", "pubmed23n0029_6845", "Pathology_Robbins_2401", "pubmed23n0018_1347", "pubmed23n0050_7742", "pubmed23n0050_6562", "InternalMed_Harrison_19658", "InternalMed_Harrison_9296", "pubmed23n0048_19489", "pubmed23n0037_2479", "pubmed23n0017_3970", "pubmed23n0055_9827", "pubmed23n0056_22812", "pubmed23n0051_1768", "pubmed23n0036_3438", "pubmed23n0058_13213", "pubmed23n0058_18274", "pubmed23n0058_11857", "InternalMed_Harrison_19048", "Surgery_Schwartz_6756", "pubmed23n0016_12071", "pubmed23n0059_18076", "pubmed23n0015_1536", "pubmed23n0061_1163", "Obstentrics_Williams_7242", "pubmed23n0042_5550", "Surgery_Schwartz_6762", "InternalMed_Har