{"topic": "Peptic ulcer disease", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a significant risk factor for the development of gastrointestinal complications, including peptic ulcer disease, in renal transplant recipients?", "options": {"A": "HLA identical recipients not given maintenance steroids", "B": "HLA identical recipients treated with maintenance corticosteroids", "C": "Preexisting diverticular disease", "D": "Preexisting esophagitis"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The development of gastrointestinal complications, including peptic ulcer disease, is more common in HLA identical recipients treated with maintenance corticosteroids.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0013_6783", "title": "Alimentary tract complications after renal transplantation", "span_text": "Eleven of 32 HLA identical recipients treated with maintenance corticosteroids during stable kidney function developed gastrointestinal disease while only one of 13 HLA identical recipients not given maintenance steroids developed a problem, which strongly suggests a causal role for steroids in the development of late complications."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0013_6783", "pubmed23n0062_981", "pubmed23n0058_9235", "pubmed23n0053_17698", "pubmed23n0060_5709", "pubmed23n0050_3346", "pubmed23n0055_22850", "pubmed23n0026_2920", "pubmed23n0045_3995", "pubmed23n0055_21831", "pubmed23n0053_17697", "pubmed23n0033_6476", "pubmed23n0052_8305", "pubmed23n0046_15762", "pubmed23n0036_11146", "InternalMed_Harrison_25408", "pubmed23n0045_2471", "pubmed23n0045_2592", "pubmed23n0060_1027", "pubmed23n0052_9476", "Pathology_Robbins_1082", "pubmed23n0045_15009", "pubmed23n0059_757", "pubmed23n0045_6427", "pubmed23n0046_19601", "pubmed23n0062_5879", "pubmed23n0052_17377", "pubmed23n0018_6422", "pubmed23n0011_10604", "pubmed23n0043_106", "pubmed23n0053_10924", "pubmed23n0063_19435", "pubmed23n0059_12982", "pubmed23n0053_17538", "pubmed23n0045_31