{"topic": "Diabetes mellitus", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "A 35-year-old woman with a family history of diabetes is diagnosed with type 2 diabetes mellitus. What is the most likely combination of factors contributing to her condition?", "options": {"A": "Genetic susceptibility and environmental triggers", "B": "Only genetic factors", "C": "Only environmental factors", "D": "Infection and autoimmune response"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus is caused by a combination of inherited genetic susceptibility and various environmental triggers, such as obesity and physical inactivity.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_4891", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "The identification of genetic variations and environmental factors that either predispose to or protect against disease is essential for predicting disease risk, designing preventive strategies, and developing novel therapeutic approaches."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0011_8448", "Surgery_Schwartz_9785", "pubmed23n0047_10795", "pubmed23n0049_10699", "InternalMed_Harrison_4891", "pubmed23n0058_15904", "Pathology_Robbins_180", "pubmed23n0047_3573", "pubmed23n0052_10976", "InternalMed_Harrison_27738", "pubmed23n0011_12758", "pubmed23n0054_12259", "pubmed23n0020_2185", "pubmed23n0044_25131", "pubmed23n0045_3149", "pubmed23n0051_13190", "pubmed23n0063_2659", "pubmed23n0053_15762", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_2138", "InternalMed_Harrison_21456", "Obstentrics_Williams_8022", "InternalMed_Harrison_4995", "pubmed23n0051_2125", "pubmed23n0018_254", "pubmed23n0052_2656", "Gynecology_Novak_6504", "pubmed23n0049_16179", "pubmed23n0053_8966", "pubmed23n0061_13069", "pubmed23n0043_11188", "pubmed23n0050_7402", "pubmed23n0045_7510", "InternalMed_Harrison_18335", "InternalMed_Harrison_22850", "pubmed23n0047_3576", "pubmed23n0060_12434", "pubmed23n0049_10431", "Pathology_Robbins_4030", "InternalMed_Harrison_4890", 