{"topic": "Hyperthyroidism", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the primary goal of treating hyperthyroidism in patients with pancreatic diabetes?", "options": {"A": "To reduce thyroidal hyperactivity", "B": "To increase antidiabetic management", "C": "To perform surgical thyroidectomy", "D": "To administer antithyroid drug therapy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The treatment of surgical patients with pancreatic diabetes and hyperthyroidism should first aim at reducing thyroidal hyperactivity, as hyperthyroidism exacerbates the symptoms of diabetes.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0041_2367", "title": "[Hyperthyroidism and diabetes mellitus]", "span_text": "Since hyperthyroidism exacerbates the symptoms of diabetes, the treatment of surgical patients with pancreatic diabetes and hyperthyroidism should first aim at reducing thyroidal hyperactivity."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0057_17794", "pubmed23n0057_11749", "pubmed23n0041_2367", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4295", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4327", "pubmed23n0056_11930"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0057_17794", "pubmed23n0057_11749", "pubmed23n0041_2367", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4295", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4327", "pubmed23n0056_11930"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hyperthyroidism Treatment treatment therapy management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 15142.388041014783, "llm_ms": 815.844249969814, "verification_ms": 787.2542499681003, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENC