{"topic": "Allergic rhinitis", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary role of eosinophils in the pathophysiology of allergic rhinitis?", "options": {"A": "To mediate the immediate allergic reaction", "B": "To contribute to the late allergic reaction and airway injury", "C": "To regulate the function of mast cells", "D": "To produce anti-inflammatory cytokines"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Eosinophils play a significant role in the late-phase allergic reaction, contributing to airway injury and inflammation. They are attracted to the airway during the late-phase reaction and release granular proteins that cause airway damage.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0057_13963", "title": "The role of eosinophils in the pathophysiology of asthma", "span_text": "An increased presence of eosinophils suggests that they are an important contributor to the late allergic reaction and may be one of the major constituents in the development of bronchial inflammation."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0057_13963", "Immunology_Janeway_3573", "pubmed23n0051_18950", "pubmed23n0058_5394", "pubmed23n0044_2521", "Physiology_Levy_2802", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2163", "pubmed23n0046_22758", "InternalMed_Harrison_3951", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1831", "pubmed23n0021_10401", "pubmed23n0057_7922", "pubmed23n0057_16518", "pubmed23n0025_8566", "pubmed23n0056_20035", "pubmed23n0058_5836", "pubmed23n0026_7175", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1752", "pubmed23n0046_3830", "pubmed23n0055_19387", "pubmed23n0001_5220", "pubmed23n0048_20003", "pubmed23n0022_8121", "pubmed23n0057_1462", "pubmed23n0058_4812", "Physiology_Levy_2799", "pubmed23n0063_3406", "pubmed23n0046_396", "pubmed23n0057_4504", "pubmed23n0005_4961", "pubmed23n0051_1909", "pubmed23n0056_20344", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1811", "InternalMed_Harrison_24980", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1751", "pubmed23n0051_9471", "pubmed23n0052_2641", "pubmed23n0044_17723", "pubmed23n0048_19386",