{"topic": "Malnutrition", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is a potential risk factor for the development of pneumonia in children aged 0-2 years?", "options": {"A": "Malnutrition", "B": "High socioeconomic status", "C": "Good oral hygiene", "D": "Family history of pneumonia"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Malnutrition is a known risk factor for the development of pneumonia in children, as it can weaken the immune system and make them more susceptible to infections.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0062_17765", "title": "Case-control study on pathogenesis of pneumonia in children aged 0-2 years", "span_text": "Single factor analysis showed 29 factors were responsible for the increasing incidence of pneumonia. 13 of 29 factors were major pneumonia risk factors by the standard of means greater than 15 and OR greater than 3. They were malnutrition, anemia, riskets, pneumonia history, repeated colds, chronic diarrhoea, congenital malformation, asphyxia neonatorum, amniotic fluid aspiration, artificial feeding, too much clothing, family member with acute respiratory illness (ARI) and contact with ARI patients."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_5865", "Gynecology_Novak_799", "InternalMed_Harrison_1957", "pubmed23n0049_1606", "pubmed23n0062_17765", "pubmed23n0035_3358", "pubmed23n0051_757", "pubmed23n0049_7022", "pubmed23n0042_8217"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_5865", "Gynecology_Novak_799", "InternalMed_Harrison_1957", "pubmed23n0049_1606", "pubmed23n0062_17765", "pubmed23n0035_3358", "pubmed23n0051_757", "pubmed23n0049_7022", "pubmed23n0042_8217"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Malnutrition Etiology etiology cause risk factors pathogenesis mechanism underlying cause genetic factors environmental factors predisposing facto