{"topic": "Obesity", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is a key factor in the development of arterial hypertension in obese subjects?", "options": {"A": "Increased activity of the sympathetic nervous system", "B": "Decreased high-density lipoprotein levels", "C": "Hyperthyroidism", "D": "Low-grade chronic systemic inflammation"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The state of insulin resistance with hyperinsulinaemia, as well as increased activity of the sympathetic nervous system, are probably responsible for the development of arterial hypertension in obese subjects.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0053_15369", "title": "Pathophysiology and treatment of the obesity-related arterial hypertension.", "span_text": "Among several possible mechanisms, the state of insulin resistance with hyperinsulinaemia, as well as increased activity of the sympathetic nervous system, are probably responsible for the development of arterial hypertension in obese subjects."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_3815", "Surgery_Schwartz_7967", "pubmed23n0053_15369", "InternalMed_Harrison_27679", "Biochemistry_Lippincott_1234", "pubmed23n0023_8829", "InternalMed_Harrison_5232", "InternalMed_Harrison_27668", "pubmed23n0060_9051", "InternalMed_Harrison_27652", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1704"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_3815", "Surgery_Schwartz_7967", "pubmed23n0053_15369", "InternalMed_Harrison_27679", "Biochemistry_Lippincott_1234", "pubmed23n0023_8829", "InternalMed_Harrison_5232", "InternalMed_Harrison_27668", "pubmed23n0060_9051", "InternalMed_Harrison_27652", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1704"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Obesity Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation