{"topic": "Osteoarthritis", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What approach has been used to gain a broader understanding of the general course of osteoarthritis?", "options": {"A": "Careful radiographic monitoring of selected groups of patients", "B": "Biochemical analysis of blood samples", "C": "Genetic testing for mutations", "D": "Patient self-reporting of symptoms"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The use of careful radiographic monitoring of selected groups of patients has provided valuable insights into the progression of osteoarthritis, allowing for a better understanding of the condition.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_20618", "title": "Clinical features of osteoarthritis, diffuse idiopathic skeletal hyperostosis, and hypermobility syndromes", "span_text": "The work-up of classic data and the use of new information from epidemiologic surveys as well as careful radiographic monitoring of selected groups of patients have brought us broader views on the general course of the condition."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database query", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_20618"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_20618"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteoarthritis Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 40337.73500000825, "llm_ms": 929.4949999894015, "verification_ms": 943.9282909734175, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "