{"topic": "Diabetes mellitus", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a common chronic complication of diabetes mellitus that can lead to increased morbidity and mortality in diabetic patients?", "options": {"A": "Hypoglycemia", "B": "Nephropathy", "C": "Hyperthyroidism", "D": "Gout"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Nephropathy is a common chronic complication of diabetes mellitus that can lead to increased morbidity and mortality in diabetic patients. It is a well-established fact that diabetes is the leading cause of renal failure.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0047_5691", "title": "Diabetic complications with special anaesthetic risk", "span_text": "Chronic complications are neuropathies, nephropathy, retinopathy, peripheral arterial disease, cerebrovascular disease, coronary artery disease, cardiomyopathy, hypertension, infection, delayed wound healing and stiff joint disease."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_8305", "pubmed23n0047_5691", "pubmed23n0059_379", "pubmed23n0060_409", "pubmed23n0002_4932", "pubmed23n0062_12875", "pubmed23n0057_16827", "InternalMed_Harrison_27993", "pubmed23n0027_7422", "pubmed23n0056_16013", "Obstentrics_Williams_8008", "pubmed23n0042_12962", "pubmed23n0044_9135", "pubmed23n0049_10703", "InternalMed_Harrison_17394", "pubmed23n0061_16963", "pubmed23n0062_12872", "InternalMed_Harrison_30676", "Obstentrics_Williams_6591", "pubmed23n0056_19136", "pubmed23n0046_18247", "pubmed23n0045_8920", "pubmed23n0043_8772", "pubmed23n0033_10609", "pubmed23n0042_12960", "pubmed23n0014_302", "pubmed23n0048_16794", "pubmed23n0024_12109", "pubmed23n0049_19625", "Pathology_Robbins_4630", "pubmed23n0049_6412", "pubmed23n0026_2689", "pubmed23n0052_19808", "pubmed23n0062_3110", "pubmed23n0052_6708", "pubmed23n0018_254", "pubmed23n0017_8620", "Pathology_Robbins_4648", "Pathology_Robbins_4649", "pubmed23n0061_1492", "pubmed23n0048_12282", "pubmed23n0048_17501", "pubmed23n00