{"topic": "Preeclampsia", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the primary goal of managing severe preeclampsia at 28 to 32 weeks' gestation?", "options": {"A": "To deliver the fetus as soon as possible", "B": "To control blood pressure and prevent seizures", "C": "To hospitalize the patient and monitor their condition", "D": "To administer antihypertensive medication and bed rest"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The primary goal of managing severe preeclampsia at 28 to 32 weeks' gestation is to control blood pressure and prevent seizures, as stated in the evidence. This approach aims to improve maternal and fetal outcomes by reducing the risk of complications.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Obstentrics_Williams_5201", "title": "Obstentrics_Williams", "span_text": "Aggressive versus expectant management of severe preeclampsia at 28 to 32 weeks' gestation: a randomized controlled trial."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_5201", "pubmed23n0054_18227", "First_Aid_Step2_748", "Obstentrics_Williams_5200", "pubmed23n0044_2037", "pubmed23n0055_22197", "Obstentrics_Williams_5009", "InternalMed_Harrison_554", "pubmed23n0059_954", "Obstentrics_Williams_5128", "pubmed23n0026_5190", "pubmed23n0043_3551", "pubmed23n0050_6835", "Obstentrics_Williams_6973", "pubmed23n0062_11877"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_5201", "pubmed23n0054_18227", "First_Aid_Step2_748", "Obstentrics_Williams_5200", "pubmed23n0044_2037", "pubmed23n0055_22197", "Obstentrics_Williams_5009", "InternalMed_Harrison_554", "pubmed23n0059_954", "Obstentrics_Williams_5128", "pubmed23n0026_5190", "pubmed23n0043_3551", "pubmed23n0050_6835", "Obstentrics_Williams_6973", "pubmed23n0062_11877"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Preeclampsia Treatment treatment therapy ma