{"topic": "Acne", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism of action of isotretinoin in the treatment of severe cystic acne?", "options": {"A": "Inhibiting sebaceous gland size and function", "B": "Reducing the density, diameter, and rate of growth of facial hair", "C": "Providing antibacterial activity against Propionibacterium acnes", "D": "Acting as an androgen antagonist"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Isotretinoin is a synthetic retinoid that acts by inhibiting sebaceous gland size and function, making it an effective treatment for severe cystic acne.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_6750", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Isotretinoin is a synthetic retinoid currently restricted to the oral treatment of severe cystic acne that is recalcitrant to standard therapies. The precise mechanism of action of isotretinoin in cystic acne is not known, although it appears to act by inhibiting sebaceous gland size and function."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 10, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_4569", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6806", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6750", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4434", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6705"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_4569", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6806", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6750", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4434", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6705"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 5, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Acne Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 33763.850958959665, "llm_ms": 1018.9405000419356, "verification_ms": 905.8812499861233, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_re