{"topic": "Pneumonia", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "A 35-year-old HIV-positive patient presents with symptoms of interstitial pneumonia. What non-invasive procedure can be used to diagnose Pneumocystis carinii pneumonia in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Induced sputum test", "B": "Exercise test", "C": "Chest roentgenogram", "D": "Open lung biopsy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The induced sputum test is a non-invasive procedure that can be used to diagnose Pneumocystis carinii pneumonia in HIV-positive patients.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0062_6031", "title": "Diagnosis of Pneumocystis carinii pneumonia in HIV-positive patients. The diagnostic value of induced sputum and exercise test", "span_text": "The object of investigation is to illustrate the values of two noninvasive procedures: the induced sputum test and the exercise test in the diagnosis of Pneumocystis carinii pneumonia (PCP)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2023-02-20", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_2440", "pubmed23n0053_21069", "pubmed23n0059_14258", "pubmed23n0015_8114", "pubmed23n0062_6031"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_21069", "pubmed23n0059_14258", "pubmed23n0015_8114", "pubmed23n0062_6031", "pubmed23n0062_2440"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": "2023-02-20", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Pneumonia Investigation investigation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging workup evaluation differential diagnosis clinical criteria biomarkers screening confirmatory test diagnostic accuracy", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 5419.982832972892, "llm_ms": 972.8385420166887, "verification_ms": 903.3372919657268, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "IN