{"topic": "Urinary tract infection", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the significance of antibody-coated bacteria test in the diagnosis of urinary tract infections in children?", "options": {"A": "It can differentiate between upper and lower urinary tract infections", "B": "It is used to diagnose asymptomatic bacteriuria", "C": "It is a screening test for urinary tract infections in adults", "D": "It is used to diagnose kidney infections"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The antibody-coated bacteria test can help differentiate between upper and lower urinary tract infections in children.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0026_7093", "title": "Antibody-coated bacteria in the urine of children with urinary tract infections", "span_text": "The test for antibody-coated bacteria in urine for the diagnosis of the anatomical level of urinary tract infections was evaluated in children with UTI. The ability of the test to differentiate between an upper and lower infection is influenced by the antiglobulin preparation used, since too sensitive an antiglobulin probably detects nonspecifically bound antibodies."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "exact_match", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0003_4246", "pubmed23n0059_19723", "pubmed23n0024_5555", "pubmed23n0053_15759", "pubmed23n0058_9997", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2204", "pubmed23n0055_8652", "pubmed23n0026_7093", "pubmed23n0058_4750", "pubmed23n0050_18140", "pubmed23n0024_5704", "pubmed23n0042_1896", "pubmed23n0019_10662", "pubmed23n0057_15721", "pubmed23n0054_7205", "pubmed23n0060_4405", "pubmed23n0030_10600", "pubmed23n0054_14472", "pubmed23n0040_7035", "pubmed23n0038_11049", "pubmed23n0050_7247", "pubmed23n0023_3386", "InternalMed_Harrison_10178", "pubmed23n0026_11171", "pubmed23n0044_19893", "pubmed23n0019_1825", "pubmed23n0011_1488", "pubmed23n0063_20660", "pubmed23n0046_3360", "pubmed23n0026_2200", "pubmed23n0031_6818", "pubmed23n0025_10756", "pubmed23n0059_4310", "pubmed23n0