{"topic": "HIV", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is a key goal of antiretroviral treatment in HIV-1-infected patients?", "options": {"A": "A reduction in the viral load to below the level of detection", "B": "An increase in the CD4 leukocyte count", "C": "A decrease in the level of tumor markers", "D": "An increase in the plasma HIV-1 levels"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The key goal of antiretroviral treatment is to reduce the viral load to below the level of detection, which is typically in the range of 40\u201375 copies/mL.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_32564", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "According to current guidelines from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, a successful antiretroviral response is defined by a fall in plasma HIV-1 levels of 0.5 log10 copies/mL, and a key goal of treatment is a reduction in the viral load to below the level of detection, which is typically in the range of 40\u201375 copies/mL."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 10, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_15431", "InternalMed_Harrison_32564", "pubmed23n0046_18324", "pubmed23n0051_20298"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_15431", "InternalMed_Harrison_32564", "pubmed23n0046_18324", "pubmed23n0051_20298"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 5, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "HIV Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9334.458916971926, "llm_ms": 887.4381250352599, "verification_ms": 1443.5900829848833, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_