{"topic": "Smoking cessation", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is one of the factors that should be identified during the initial workup of a patient with hypertension?", "options": {"A": "Smoking", "B": "Family history", "C": "Age", "D": "Occupation"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The initial workup of a patient with hypertension aims to identify all definable and curable causes for the hypertension, as well as attendant risk factors.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0064_321", "title": "Clinical evaluation and differential diagnosis of the individual hypertensive patient", "span_text": "The initial workup aims to (a) establish that the hypertension is sustained and should be treated; (b) identify all definable and curable causes for the hypertension; (c) identify the presence and degree of attendant risk factors such as smoking, alcohol use, obesity, diabetes, and abnormal lipid metabolism;"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0064_321"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0064_321"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Smoking cessation Investigation investigation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging workup evaluation differential diagnosis clinical criteria biomarkers screening confirmatory test diagnostic accuracy", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 5666.814416006673, "llm_ms": 1100.3093749750406, "verification_ms": 0.41874998714774847, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 0, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 1}, "failed_checks": ["evidence_span_mismatch"], "failed_checks_all": ["evidence_span_mismatch"], "evidence_doc_id