{"topic": "Myocardial infarction", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the role of technetium-99m pyrophosphate scintigraphy in the detection of acute myocardial infarction?", "options": {"A": "It is a highly specific method for detecting acute myocardial infarction", "B": "It is a highly sensitive method for detecting acute myocardial infarction but not specific", "C": "It is not useful in the detection of acute myocardial infarction", "D": "It is only used for detecting transmural infarctions"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Technetium-99m pyrophosphate scintigraphy is a highly sensitive and specific method for detecting acute myocardial infarction, especially when using a modified classification that defines the 2+ diffuse pattern of tracer uptake as equivocal rather than positive.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0011_7609", "title": "New approach to interpretation of technetium-99m pyrophosphate scintigraphy in detection of acute myocardial infarction: clinical assessment of diagnostic accuracy", "span_text": "Thus the definitely positive scintigraphic pattern was relatively highly specific for acute myocardial infarction. If the 2+ pattern had been considered positive, the specificity of the technique would have been greatly decreased."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0011_7609", "pubmed23n0013_4500", "pubmed23n0051_6443", "pubmed23n0018_7002", "pubmed23n0027_15051", "InternalMed_Harrison_19227", "pubmed23n0010_8536", "InternalMed_Harrison_19243", "pubmed23n0007_1075", "InternalMed_Harrison_17715", "pubmed23n0022_9045", "pubmed23n0049_19500", "pubmed23n0015_329", "pubmed23n0037_4300", "pubmed23n0012_1368", "pubmed23n0062_538", "pubmed23n0058_6835", "pubmed23n0054_10198", "pubmed23n0051_2004", "pubmed23n0013_7765", "pubmed23n0025_1249", "pubmed23n0053_17740", "pubmed23n0022_2454", "pubmed23n0047_9523", "pubmed23n0017_10305", "pubmed23n0006_14046", "pubmed23n0029_7233", "pubmed2