{"topic": "Hypothyroidism", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the primary method for monitoring the effectiveness of L-thyroxine treatment in patients with hypothyroidism?", "options": {"A": "Determination of blood serum T3 and T4 concentrations", "B": "Monitoring of cardiac symptoms", "C": "Assessment of psychical reaction time", "D": "Evaluation of thyroid hormone concentrations in urine"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The determination of blood serum T3 and T4 concentrations is the primary method for monitoring the effectiveness of L-thyroxine treatment in patients with hypothyroidism, as it allows for the assessment of the normalization of thyroid hormone levels and the adjustment of the therapeutic dose.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0045_1270", "title": "Monitoring of treatment for hypothyroidism with L-thyroxine", "span_text": "The administration of L-thyroxine at a dose of 2 micrograms/kg/day effectively eradicated all symptoms of the disease and led to the normalization of blood serum T3 and T4 values in the majority of patients with autoimmune hypothyroidism."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0045_1270", "pubmed23n0045_10555", "pubmed23n0047_9261", "pubmed23n0048_8037", "pubmed23n0043_11799", "pubmed23n0002_10201"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0045_1270", "pubmed23n0045_10555", "pubmed23n0047_9261", "pubmed23n0048_8037", "pubmed23n0043_11799", "pubmed23n0002_10201"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hypothyroidism Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 24831.362