{"topic": "Iron deficiency anemia", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is a method for preventing iron deficiency anemia in Chinese preschool children?", "options": {"A": "Soft drink powder supplementation with iron, zinc, calcium, vitamin D, riboflavin, and ascorbic acid", "B": "Table salt supplementation with iron and zinc", "C": "Cow's milk supplementation with vitamins A and D", "D": "Multivitamin prophylaxis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Soft drink powder is a convenient vehicle for the supplementation of iron, zinc, calcium, vitamin D, riboflavin, and ascorbic acid, which can help prevent iron deficiency anemia in Chinese preschool children.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0049_20701", "title": "Studies on iron deficiency anemia, rickets and zinc deficiency and their prevention among Chinese preschool children", "span_text": "From our studies, it can be seen that a soft drink powder is a convenient vehicle for the supplementation of iron, zinc, calcium, vitamin D, riboflavin, and ascorbic acid. Table salt is also a good, low-cost carrier for iron and zinc, and cow's milk can only be used for the enrichment of vitamins A and D."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "exact match", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_1424", "pubmed23n0058_13495", "pubmed23n0043_15411", "pubmed23n0033_5206", "pubmed23n0049_20701", "pubmed23n0059_20933", "pubmed23n0050_8981", "pubmed23n0043_2285", "pubmed23n0006_5961"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_1424", "pubmed23n0058_13495", "pubmed23n0043_15411", "pubmed23n0033_5206", "pubmed23n0049_20701", "pubmed23n0059_20933", "pubmed23n0050_8981", "pubmed23n0043_2285", "pubmed23n0006_5961"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Iron deficiency anemia Prevention prevention prophylaxis risk reduction screening vaccination prima