{"topic": "Sepsis", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the recommended first-line agent for vasopressor therapy in patients with sepsis?", "options": {"A": "Norepinephrine", "B": "Vasopressin", "C": "Dopamine", "D": "Epinephrine"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Norepinephrine is the recommended first-line agent for vasopressor therapy in patients with sepsis, as it can help achieve a mean arterial pressure of at least 65 mmHg.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0053_20250", "title": "Gram-negative sepsis, the sepsis syndrome, and the role of antiendotoxin monoclonal antibodies", "span_text": "Proper management of gram-negative sepsis includes appropriate antimicrobial therapy, fluids and electrolytes, nutritional support, administration of vasopressors, and mechanical ventilation if necessary."}, {"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Surgery_Schwartz_1241", "title": "Surgery_Schwartz", "span_text": "In patients who require vasopressor therapy, the first-line agent should be norepinephrine."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0055_7387", "pubmed23n0053_20250", "Surgery_Schwartz_1241", "pubmed23n0061_12068", "pubmed23n0047_12115", "pubmed23n0047_20084", "pubmed23n0030_11212", "pubmed23n0053_7095", "pubmed23n0006_4262", "pubmed23n0038_11689", "pubmed23n0014_9513", "pubmed23n0047_20077", "pubmed23n0049_6845", "pubmed23n0037_4049"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0055_7387", "pubmed23n0053_20250", "Surgery_Schwartz_1241", "pubmed23n0061_12068", "pubmed23n0047_12115", "pubmed23n0047_20084", "pubmed23n0030_11212", "pubmed23n0053_7095", "pubmed23n0006_4262", "pubmed23n0038_11689", "pubmed23n0014_9513", "pubmed23n0047_20077", "pubmed23n0049_6845", "pubmed23n0037_4049"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Sepsis Therapy therapy treatment management drug 