{"topic": "Diabetes mellitus", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is the primary benefit of self-monitoring of blood glucose in patients with diabetes mellitus?", "options": {"A": "To detect poor diabetic control", "B": "To show how to improve diabetic control", "C": "To measure HbA1c levels", "D": "To diagnose gestational diabetes"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Self-monitoring of blood glucose provides an accurate pattern of blood-glucose changes in everyday life, which is the basis for treatment in insulin-dependent diabetes. It is especially useful in elucidating problems in diabetic control, preventing hypoglycaemia, and managing diabetic pregnancy.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0003_6323", "title": "Self-monitoring of blood-glucose. Improvement of diabetic control.", "span_text": "Self-monitoring was especially useful in elucidating problems in diabetic control, preventing hypoglycaemia, and managing diabetic pregnancy. Unlike the measurement of HbA1c which only detects poor diabetic control, self-monitoring also shows how to improve it."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0043_93", "pubmed23n0003_6323", "pubmed23n0047_21096", "Gynecology_Novak_904", "pubmed23n0024_12104", "pubmed23n0051_9237", "Obstentrics_Williams_8002", "pubmed23n0048_16592", "pubmed23n0061_13023", "pubmed23n0049_10516", "pubmed23n0050_7407", "pubmed23n0043_17806", "pubmed23n0058_6257", "pubmed23n0063_822", "pubmed23n0043_16858", "pubmed23n0060_4629", "pubmed23n0058_10353", "InternalMed_Harrison_26448", "pubmed23n0050_1939", "pubmed23n0042_12960", "pubmed23n0052_12467", "pubmed23n0062_11114", "pubmed23n0032_2515", "pubmed23n0052_2317", "InternalMed_Harrison_31767", "pubmed23n0013_10301", "pubmed23n0061_13030", "pubmed23n0049_19620", "pubmed23n0062_17838", "pubmed23n0061_13021", "pubmed23n0014_305", "pubmed23n0051_16507", "pubmed23n0016_5507", "pubmed23n0048_8060", "pubmed23n0053_6012", "InternalMed_Harrison_991