{"topic": "Heart failure", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "What is the cornerstone of pharmacotherapy for heart failure?", "options": {"A": "ACE inhibitors and beta blockers", "B": "Diuretics and vasodilators", "C": "Digoxin and inotropic therapy", "D": "Calcium antagonists and selective alpha 1-blockers"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "ACE inhibitors and beta blockers form the cornerstone of pharmacotherapy for heart failure, leading to attenuation of decline and improvement in cardiac structure and function with consequent reduction in symptoms, improvement in quality of life, decreased burden of hospitalizations, and a decline in mortality from both pump failure and arrhythmic deaths.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_18264", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "ACEIs and beta blockers form the cornerstone of pharmacotherapy and lead to attenuation of decline and improvement in cardiac structure and function with consequent reduction in symptoms, improvement in quality of life, decreased burden of hospitalizations, and a decline in mortality from both pump failure and arrhythmic deaths (Fig. 280-3)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0059_20077", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5246", "pubmed23n0014_2698", "InternalMed_Harrison_18276", "InternalMed_Harrison_18264", "pubmed23n0054_9515", "pubmed23n0054_9514", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1331", "pubmed23n0062_743", "InternalMed_Harrison_18263", "pubmed23n0019_13460", "InternalMed_Harrison_18234", "pubmed23n0054_9512", "InternalMed_Harrison_18590", "InternalMed_Harrison_18253", "pubmed23n0051_1059", "Obstentrics_Williams_6869", "pubmed23n0051_100", "pubmed23n0014_10562", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1303", "InternalMed_Harrison_874", "Gynecology_Novak_2502", "pubmed23n0056_10906", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1595", "pubmed23n0023_6700", "pubmed23n0046_17670", "pubmed23n0013_11386", "pubmed23n0026_5602", "pubmed23n0027_4029", "pubmed23n0017_2808", "Ph