{"topic": "Acute kidney injury", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is a key laboratory finding in the diagnosis of renovascular hypertension?", "options": {"A": "Hyperkalemia", "B": "Hyperreninemia", "C": "Hypophosphatemia", "D": "Hypocalcemia"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Hyperreninemia is a characteristic finding in renovascular hypertension, and acute blockade of the renin system forms the basis of diagnostic tests such as the oral captopril test and captopril renography.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0064_316", "title": "The role of laboratory testing in the diagnosis of renovascular hypertension", "span_text": "Hyperreninemia is a characteristic finding, and acute blockade of the renin system forms the basis of diagnostic tests such as the oral captopril test and captopril renography."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_13614", "pubmed23n0064_316", "InternalMed_Harrison_16947", "pubmed23n0059_19498", "InternalMed_Harrison_23270", "pubmed23n0063_10719", "pubmed23n0062_5116", "pubmed23n0045_2021", "InternalMed_Harrison_2580", "pubmed23n0059_13611", "pubmed23n0014_12612", "pubmed23n0023_5526", "pubmed23n0048_12294", "InternalMed_Harrison_21491", "pubmed23n0051_16909", "InternalMed_Harrison_23259", "pubmed23n0033_4013", "pubmed23n0030_8528", "pubmed23n0061_4359", "pubmed23n0051_13043", "InternalMed_Harrison_12697", "pubmed23n0059_5937", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1924", "pubmed23n0005_1387", "pubmed23n0042_8976", "pubmed23n0059_8127", "pubmed23n0042_12416", "pubmed23n0050_2691", "pubmed23n0016_11213", "InternalMed_Harrison_24082", "pubmed23n0008_12394", "pubmed23n0011_1488", "pubmed23n0050_6697", "pubmed23n0036_8877", "InternalMed_Harrison_16679", "InternalMed_Harrison_11027", "pubmed23n0022_1398", "InternalMed_Harrison_10065", "pubmed23n0012_6735", "pubmed23n0046_20593", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_522", "pubmed23n0049_5426", "pubmed23n0058_11451", "pubmed23n0048_10844", "pubmed23n0010_6056", "p