{"topic": "Prostate cancer", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary goal of chemoprevention trials in prostate cancer?", "options": {"A": "To reduce the incidence of prostate cancer", "B": "To increase the survival rate of patients with prostate cancer", "C": "To improve the quality of life of patients with prostate cancer", "D": "To develop new treatments for advanced prostate cancer"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary goal of chemoprevention trials in prostate cancer is to reduce the incidence of the disease, which can be achieved by identifying and targeting high-risk populations and using effective chemopreventive agents.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0043_4325", "title": "When is intervention warranted?", "span_text": "A chemoprevention trial in prostate cancer would be a formidable but potentially rewarding study. The current status of knowledge of drug interactions with, biomarkers of, and even the natural history of prostate cancer is insufficient to study all levels of men at risk."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0043_4325", "pubmed23n0049_4473", "pubmed23n0044_20761", "pubmed23n0055_20887", "pubmed23n0057_16261", "InternalMed_Harrison_534", "pubmed23n0057_1716", "pubmed23n0053_18083", "Pathology_Robbins_4253", "Histology_Ross_3674", "pubmed23n0049_11909", "pubmed23n0062_16314", "InternalMed_Harrison_7401", "pubmed23n0049_16863", "pubmed23n0043_4321", "pubmed23n0049_16862", "pubmed23n0062_1706", "pubmed23n0049_4467", "pubmed23n0050_6566", "Pathology_Robbins_4988", "InternalMed_Harrison_3816", "Surgery_Schwartz_3891", "Pathology_Robbins_4910", "pubmed23n0052_14395", "pubmed23n0050_19064", "Pathology_Robbins_4254", "InternalMed_Harrison_27371", "pubmed23n0007_11863", "pubmed23n0052_7450", "Surgery_Schwartz_2102", "Gynecology_Novak_560", "InternalMed_Harrison_536", "InternalMed_Harrison_7948", "pubmed23n0056_15306", "Pharmacology_Katzung_7182", "pubmed2