{"topic": "HIV", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is a characteristic of HIV-associated non-Hodgkin lymphoma?", "options": {"A": "High grade of malignancy, B cell origin, and extensive extranodal involvement", "B": "Low grade of malignancy, T cell origin, and limited extranodal involvement", "C": "Intermediate grade of malignancy, mixed cell origin, and moderate extranodal involvement", "D": "Variable grade of malignancy, unknown cell origin, and unpredictable extranodal involvement"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "HIV-associated non-Hodgkin lymphoma is characterized by a high grade of malignancy, B cell origin, and extensive extranodal involvement, particularly of the central nervous system.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0060_19248", "title": "Epidemiology of HIV associated non-Hodgkin lymphoma", "span_text": "Clinically, HIV associated NHL is characterized by histological evidence of a high grade of malignancy, B cell origin, extensive extranodal involvement (most notably of the CNS) and poor prognosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "database", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_19248", "InternalMed_Harrison_30799"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0060_19248", "InternalMed_Harrison_30799"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "HIV Etiology etiology cause risk factors pathogenesis mechanism underlying cause genetic factors environmental factors predisposing factors associated conditions epidemiology incidence", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7520.442250010092, "llm_ms": 1001.7658339929767, "verification_ms": 741.1218330380507, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE