{"topic": "Epilepsy", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is a key factor in the prevention of secondary neurotic and other mental disorders in patients with traumatic epilepsy?", "options": {"A": "Administration of nootropic and long-acting psychotropic drugs", "B": "Reduction of antiepileptic drug metabolism in liver diseases", "C": "Presence of seizure potentials in EEG", "D": "Teratogenic side effects of anticonvulsants"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The administration of nootropic and long-acting psychotropic drugs has been shown to reduce cerebral asthenic symptomatology and stabilize emotional disturbances, which promotes the prevention of secondary neurotic and other mental disorders in patients with traumatic epilepsy.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0055_17797", "title": "Prevention of secondary neurotic and other mental disorders in traumatic epilepsy", "span_text": "Administration of nootropic and long-acting drugs brought about a reduction of the cerebral asthenic symptomatology and stabilization of emotional disturbances which promoted prevention of secondary neurotic and other mental disorders in patients with traumatic epilepsy."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0055_17797", "pubmed23n0027_7896", "pubmed23n0042_4914", "pubmed23n0048_1400", "pubmed23n0053_250"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0055_17797", "pubmed23n0027_7896", "pubmed23n0042_4914", "pubmed23n0048_1400", "pubmed23n0053_250"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Epilepsy Prevention prevention prophylaxis risk reduction screening vaccination primary prevention secondary prevention lifestyle modification counseling public health early detection follow-up", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieva