{"topic": "Pregnancy", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the recommended management approach for asymptomatic bacteriuria in pregnancy?", "options": {"A": "Short-term administration of antimicrobials with surveillance for recurrent bacteriuria", "B": "Continuous therapy with antimicrobials for the remainder of gestation", "C": "Expectant management without antimicrobial therapy", "D": "Surgical intervention"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Short-term administration of antimicrobials, when combined with surveillance for recurrent bacteriuria, is effective for the management of the pregnant woman with asymptomatic bacteriuria.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0011_7474", "title": "Short-term versus continuous antimicrobial therapy for asymptomatic bacteriuria in pregnancy", "span_text": "Short-term administration of antimicrobials, when combined with surveillance for recurrent bacteriuria, is effective for the management of the pregnant woman with asymptomatic bacteriuria."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_4958", "pubmed23n0044_2037", "Obstentrics_Williams_8126", "pubmed23n0011_7474", "Obstentrics_Williams_8258", "Gynecology_Novak_3308", "Obstentrics_Williams_6870", "pubmed23n0050_9647", "pubmed23n0058_11572", "Gynecology_Novak_5980", "Gynecology_Novak_3217", "pubmed23n0051_6710", "Gynecology_Novak_3218", "InternalMed_Harrison_7897", "InternalMed_Harrison_3920", "pubmed23n0039_3461", "pubmed23n0048_2187", "pubmed23n0017_10672", "pubmed23n0046_11610", "pubmed23n0058_3920", "Obstentrics_Williams_8140", "pubmed23n0002_4839", "pubmed23n0037_6367", "pubmed23n0029_6825", "pubmed23n0057_8082"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_4958", "pubmed23n0044_2037", "Obstentrics_Williams_8126", "pubmed23n0011_7474", "Obstentrics_Williams_8258", "Gynecology_Novak_3308", "Obstentrics_Williams_6870", "pubmed23n0050_9647", "pubmed23n0058_11572", "Gynecology_Novak_5980", "Gynecology_Novak_3217", "pubme