{"topic": "Pregnancy", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "A 28-year-old woman presents with a history of two consecutive spontaneous abortions and is now pregnant again. What is the recommended approach for clinical investigation of pregnancy loss in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Initiate investigation after three or more spontaneous abortions", "B": "Initiate investigation after two consecutive spontaneous abortions, especially since the woman is older than 35 years of age", "C": "Perform a routine ultrasound examination to confirm the pregnancy", "D": "Order a series of blood tests to check for any underlying medical conditions"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Clinical investigation of pregnancy loss may be initiated after two consecutive spontaneous abortions, especially when the woman is older than 35 years of age, or when the couple has had difficulty conceiving.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Gynecology_Novak_6186", "title": "Gynecology_Novak", "span_text": "Clinical investigation of pregnancy loss, however, may be initiated after two consecutive spontaneous abortions, especially when fetal heart activity is identified before any of the pregnancy losses, when the women is older than 35 years of age, or when the couple has had difficulty conceiving (5)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "method": "database query", "doc_ids": ["Gynecology_Novak_3160", "Gynecology_Novak_6186", "pubmed23n0043_13800", "Gynecology_Novak_3318", "pubmed23n0039_7416", "pubmed23n0004_6282", "pubmed23n0013_8763", "Obstentrics_Williams_1849", "pubmed23n0056_22866", "pubmed23n0058_10364", "pubmed23n0058_10349", "pubmed23n0044_24509", "pubmed23n0039_5412", "pubmed23n0058_6846", "Gynecology_Novak_2406", "Gynecology_Novak_3293", "pubmed23n0030_10856"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Gynecology_Novak_3160", "Gynecology_Novak_6186", "pubmed23n0043_13800", "Gynecology_Novak_3318", "pubmed23n0039_7416", "pubmed23n0004_6282", "pubmed23n0013_8763", "Obst