{"topic": "Pancreatitis", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What is crucial for the management of patients with hemorrhagic pancreatitis?", "options": {"A": "Adequate initial resuscitation and intensive follow-up", "B": "Early surgical intervention", "C": "Administration of antibiotics", "D": "Monitoring of liver function"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Adequate initial resuscitation and intensive follow-up are crucial for the management of patients with hemorrhagic pancreatitis to avoid shock and renal and pulmonary failure.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0015_10620", "title": "Hemorrhagic pancreatitis", "span_text": "Adequate initial resuscitation and intensive follow-up are probably the most important elements in the management of patients with hemorrhagic pancreatitis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_10620", "pubmed23n0047_10691", "pubmed23n0046_2361", "InternalMed_Harrison_24423", "InternalMed_Harrison_24386", "pubmed23n0051_2023"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_10620", "pubmed23n0047_10691", "pubmed23n0046_2361", "InternalMed_Harrison_24423", "InternalMed_Harrison_24386", "pubmed23n0051_2023"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Pancreatitis Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 15895.25041700108, "llm_ms": 3125.5269999965094, "verification_ms": 0.5415829946286976, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 0, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION"