{"topic": "Migraine", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "What is the primary advantage of using a diagnostic headache diary in conjunction with a clinical interview for diagnosing migraine?", "options": {"A": "It provides a more precise diagnosis than a clinical interview alone", "B": "It is a more cost-effective method of diagnosis", "C": "It can only be used for patients with aura", "D": "It is not based on the operational diagnostic criteria of the International Headache Society"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The diagnostic headache diary provides a more precise diagnosis than a clinical interview alone by allowing patients to record their symptoms over time, which can help identify patterns and characteristics of their headaches that may not be apparent during a single clinical interview.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0049_6708", "title": "Presentation of a new instrument: the diagnostic headache diary", "span_text": "A combination of a clinical interview and the diagnostic headache diary gives a qualitatively and quantitatively more precise diagnosis than a clinical interview alone."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_6708", "pubmed23n0055_22801", "pubmed23n0018_11244", "InternalMed_Harrison_30124"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_6708", "pubmed23n0055_22801", "pubmed23n0018_11244", "InternalMed_Harrison_30124"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Migraine Investigation investigation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging workup evaluation differential diagnosis clinical criteria biomarkers screening confirmatory test diagnostic accuracy", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9817.381666973233, "llm_ms": 1412.751791998744, "verification_ms": 1