{"topic": "Cervical cancer", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the primary goal of screening for cervical cancer in high-risk populations?", "options": {"A": "To reduce the cost of healthcare", "B": "To detect cancer at an early stage and prevent mortality", "C": "To identify new cases of cancer", "D": "To provide treatment for existing cases of cancer"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The primary goal of screening for cervical cancer in high-risk populations is to detect cancer at an early stage and prevent mortality. This is because early detection and treatment can significantly improve survival rates and reduce the risk of complications.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0044_14923", "title": "Detection of human papillomavirus in cervical scrapes by the polymerase chain reaction in relation to cytology: possible implications for cervical cancer screening", "span_text": "A relationship was found between an increasing HPV prevalence rate and a higher degree of cervical dysplasia (up to 100% in cervical carcinoma)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_12794", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "pubmed23n0045_19421", "Surgery_Schwartz_2204", "pubmed23n0020_6113", "pubmed23n0028_3223", "Gynecology_Novak_7457", "InternalMed_Harrison_315", "pubmed23n0044_14923", "pubmed23n0033_9269", "Surgery_Schwartz_4106", "Surgery_Schwartz_2212", "InternalMed_Harrison_7533", "InternalMed_Harrison_300", "InternalMed_Harrison_5986", "Gynecology_Novak_7456", "pubmed23n0055_19783", "pubmed23n0021_8317", "pubmed23n0056_22895", "pubmed23n0050_13335", "Gynecology_Novak_3097", "Gynecology_Novak_713", "pubmed23n0014_9461", "pubmed23n0014_9775", "First_Aid_Step2_852", "InternalMed_Harrison_5978", "pubmed23n0024_423", "InternalMed_Harrison_312", "pubmed23n0042_9495", "pubmed23n0047_4508", "pubmed23n0048_17330", "pubmed23n0052_4065", "pubmed23n0046_16013", "Obstentrics_Williams_5683", "pubmed23n0049_2332", "Surgery_Sch