{"topic": "Typhoid fever", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is a common adverse effect of nifurtimox?", "options": {"A": "Hypersensitivity reactions", "B": "Nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, fever, rash, headache, restlessness, insomnia, neuropathies, and seizures", "C": "Anemia or neutropenia", "D": "Pancytopenia"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Nifurtimox is a nitrofuran used in the treatment of Chagas disease and African trypanosomiasis. Adverse effects include nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, fever, rash, headache, restlessness, insomnia, neuropathies, and seizures.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_5775", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Toxicity related to nifurtimox is common. Adverse effects include nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, fever, rash, headache, restlessness, insomnia, neuropathies, and seizures."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_5841", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5770", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5229", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1397", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5775", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5752", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5771", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1043", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5068", "pubmed23n0045_14808", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6173", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6459", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4057", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5765", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4274", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5191", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5245", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6954", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1403", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6210", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1079", "pubmed23n0062_4436", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5941", "pubmed23n0051_16146"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_5841", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5770", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5229", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1397", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5775", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5752", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5771", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1043", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5068", "pubmed23n0045_14808", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6173", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6459"