{"topic": "Iron deficiency anemia", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "A 32-year-old woman presents with fatigue, pallor, and menorrhagia. Laboratory studies confirm iron deficiency anemia. She is hemodynamically stable and asymptomatic from a cardiovascular standpoint. What is the most appropriate initial treatment?", "options": {"A": "Oral iron supplementation", "B": "Intravenous iron therapy", "C": "Red blood cell transfusion", "D": "High-dose estrogen therapy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "In asymptomatic patients with established iron deficiency anemia, oral iron therapy is the preferred initial treatment. Transfusion is reserved for those with severe symptoms or cardiovascular instability. Intravenous iron is typically used when oral iron is not tolerated or ineffective. Hormonal therapy may help control menorrhagia but does not correct the underlying iron deficiency acutely.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_7990", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "In the asymptomatic patient with established iron-deficiency anemia, treatment with oral iron is usually adequate. Multiple preparations are available, ranging from simple iron salts to complex iron compounds designed for sustained release throughout the small intestine (Table 126-5)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "treatment of iron deficiency anemia in asymptomatic patients", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_7990", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1562", "pubmed23n0060_3233", "Obstentrics_Williams_2104", "pubmed23n0056_13656", "pubmed23n0048_2729", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3726", "First_Aid_Step2_1240", "pubmed23n0060_15744", "pubmed23n0051_386", "InternalMed_Harrison_22449", "pubmed23n0029_1509", "pubmed23n0024_1746", "pubmed23n0058_3919", "pubmed23n0051_9191", "InternalMed_Harrison_7989", "pubmed23n0028_2423", "pubmed23n0052_18491", "pubmed23n0011_12107", "pubmed23n0063_9142", "pubmed23n0021_3538", "pubmed23n0050_1508", "pubmed23n0043_8419", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3195", "pubmed23n0028_3206", "pubmed23n0052_9089", "pubmed23n0059_21274", "Pediatrics_Nelson_694", "pubmed23n0047_16831", "pubmed23n0019_6546"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_7990", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1562", "pubmed23n0060_3233", "Obstentrics_Williams_2104", "pubmed23n0056_13656", "pubmed23n0048_2729", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3726", "First_Aid_Step2_1240", "pubmed23n0060_15744", "pubmed23n0051_386", "InternalMed_Harrison_22449", "pubmed23n0029_1509", "pubmed23n0024_1746", "pubmed23n0058_3919", "pubmed23n0051_9191", "InternalMed_Harrison_7989", "pubmed23n0028_2423", "pubmed23n0052_18491", "pubmed23n0011_12107", "pubmed23n0063_9142"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "evidence_match", "result": "confirmed", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Iron deficiency anemia Treatment treatment therapy management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 13670.895999995992, "llm_ms": 1699.371709022671, "verification_ms": 876.1660410091281, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["InternalMed_Harrison_7990", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1562", "pubmed23n0060_3233", "Obstentrics_Williams_2104", "pubmed23n0056_13656", "pubmed23n0048_2729", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3726", "First_Aid_Step2_1240", "pubmed23n0060_15744", "pubmed23n0051_386", "InternalMed_Harrison_22449", "pubmed23n0029_1509", "pubmed23n0024_1746", "pubmed23n0058_3919", "pubmed23n0051_9191", "InternalMed_Harrison_7989", "pubmed23n0028_2423", "pubmed23n0052_18491", "pubmed23n0011_12107", "pubmed23n