{"topic": "Appendicitis", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "A 25-year-old male presents with right lower quadrant abdominal pain and is diagnosed with acute appendicitis. Epidemiological studies show variation in the incidence of this condition across different populations. Which of the following factors is associated with a lower incidence of acute appendicitis in individuals aged 5 to 29 years?", "options": {"A": "Being of Black or Asian/other race", "B": "Being female", "C": "Living in a rural area", "D": "Having a high-fiber diet"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "In individuals aged 5 to 29 years, the incidence of acute appendicitis is significantly lower in Black and Asian/other racial groups compared to White and Hispanic populations. This finding suggests that racial and ethnic factors play a role in the etiology of appendicitis, although the underlying reasons for this variation remain unknown.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0058_6015", "title": "The epidemiology of acute appendicitis in California: racial, gender, and seasonal variation.", "span_text": "Comparison of age and sex-specific incidence rates for four racial/ethnic groups (white, Hispanic, black, and Asian/other) revealed rates in blacks and the Asian/other group one-half or less of the rates for whites and Hispanics between the ages of 5 and 29 years."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "risk factors for appendicitis by race and age", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0058_6015", "pubmed23n0053_13833"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0058_6015", "pubmed23n0053_13833"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "exact_match", "result": "confirmed", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Appendicitis Etiology etiology cause risk factors pathogenesis mechanism underlying cause genetic factors environmental factors predisposing factors associated conditions epidemiology incidence", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6632.178250001743, "llm_ms": 8501.145499991253, "verification_ms": 2153.586665983312, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0058_6015", "pubmed23n0053_13833"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 120.0, "verification": 45.0, "llm": 8501.145499991253}}}
{"topic": "Stroke", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "Which of the following best describes a mechanism by which bacterial infections may increase the risk of stroke?", "options": {"A": "Bacterial components directly activate platelets via toll-like receptors, promoting thrombosis.", "B": "Bacterial infections reduce blood viscosity, increasing shear stress on cerebral vessels.", "C": "Infections lead to chronic elevation of stroke volume, causing cerebral hyperperfusion.", "D": "Bacteria directly invade cerebral endothelial cells, causing immediate vasospasm."}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Bacterial and viral infections are associated with a transient increase in the risk of acute thrombotic events, including stroke. Platelets express toll-like receptors (TLRs), and stimulation of TLR2, TLR3, and TLR4 can directly activate platelet thrombotic and inflammatory responses. Live bacteria induce a proinflammatory response in platelets in a TLR2-dependent manner, providing a direct mechanism for infection-induced thrombosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_9290", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Bacterial and viral infections are associated with a transient increase in the risk of acute thrombotic events, such as acute myocardial infarction and stroke. In addition, platelets contribute significantly to the pathophysiology and high mortality rates of sepsis. The expression, functionality, and signaling pathways of toll-like receptors (TLRs) have been established in platelets. Stimulation of platelet TLR2, TLR3, and TLR4 directly and indirectly activates the platelet\u2019s thrombotic and inflammatory responses, and live bacteria induce a proinflammatory response in platelets in a TLR2-dependent manner, suggesting a mechanism by which specific bacteria and bacterial components can directly activate platelet-dependent thrombosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "mechanism bacterial infection increase stroke risk", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_9290", "Neurology_Adams_6867", "Neurology_Adams_6131", "pubmed23n0052_2663", "InternalMed_Harrison_20981", "pubmed23n0052_16924", "pubmed23n0051_7826", "Surgery_Schwartz_1046", "pubmed23n0014_12989", "pubmed23n0050_18622", "pubmed23n0045_8349", "pubmed23n0043_13471", "pubmed23n0062_9041", "InternalMed_Harrison_1262"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_9290", "Neurology_Adams_6867", "Neurology_Adams_6131", "pubmed23n0052_2663", "InternalMed_Harrison_20981", "pubmed23n0052_16924", "pubmed23n0051_7826", "Surgery_Schwartz_1046", "pubmed23n0014_12989", "pubmed23n0050_18622", "pubmed23n0045_8349", "pubmed23n0043_13471", "pubmed23n0062_9041", "InternalMed_Harrison_1262"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "exact_match", "result": "confirmed", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Stroke Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6289.144749986008, "llm_ms": 2561.5878750104457, "verification_ms": 0.8795419707894325, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 0, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 1}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["InternalMed_Harrison_9290", "Neurology_Adams_6867", "Neurology_Adams_6131", "pubmed23n0052_2663", "InternalMed_Harrison_20981", "pubmed23n0052_16924", "pubmed23n0051_7826", "Surgery_Schwartz_1046", "pubmed23n0014_12989", "pubmed23n0050_18622", "pubmed23n0045_8349", "pubmed23n0043_13471", "pubmed23n0062_9041", "InternalMed_Harrison_1262"], "evidence_reused": false}, {"attempt": 2, "reason": "v4_json_strict", "query": "Stroke Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6303.876667050645, "llm_ms": 2602.729582984466, "verification_ms": 0.9310420136898756, "extra_instructions": "Return only valid JSON for the requested schema. Do not include extra text, markdown, or code fences. Ensure answer_key is one of A/B/C/D; if insufficient evidence, use 'A'. Do not omit any required keys; do not return empty options or an empty stem.", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 0, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 1}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["InternalMed_Harrison_9290", "Neurology_Adams_6867", "Neurology_Adams_6131", "pubmed23n0052_2663", "InternalMed_Harrison_20981", "pubmed23n0052_16924", "pubmed23n0051_7826", "Surgery_Schwartz_1046", "pubmed23n0014_12989", "pubmed23n0050_18622", "pubmed23n0045_8349", "pubmed23n0043_13471", "pubmed23n0062_9041", "InternalMed_Harrison_1262"], "evidence_reused": false}, {"attempt": 3, "reason": "v4_json_strict", "query": "Stroke Pathophysiology pathophysiology pathogenesis mechanism molecular pathway cellular response inflammation hemodynamics neurohormonal physiology biomarkers dysfunction disease process", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7088.3169589797035, "llm_ms": 3661.3454580074176, "verification_ms": 854.6430840506218, "extra_instructions": "Return only valid JSON for the requested schema. Do not include extra text, markdown, or code fences. Ensure answer_key is one of A/B/C/D; if insufficient evidence, use 'A'. Do not omit any required keys; do not return empty options or an empty stem.", "retrieval_mode": "hybr