{"topic": "Pulmonary embolism", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "A 65-year-old man is scheduled for major abdominal surgery and is identified as being at high risk for venous thromboembolism. Which of the following is the most appropriate prophylactic measure to reduce his risk of postoperative pulmonary embolism?", "options": {"A": "Low-dose heparin alone", "B": "Graduated compression stockings alone", "C": "Low-molecular-weight heparin (LMWH)", "D": "Aspirin 325 mg daily"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "For patients at high risk of venous thromboembolism undergoing major surgery, low-molecular-weight heparin (LMWH) is recommended as a highly effective prophylactic modality. While low-dose heparin is well-documented for general use, it has limited efficacy in high-risk patients. Mechanical methods like graduated compression stockings are useful, particularly in low-risk patients or as adjuncts, but are insufficient alone in high-risk cases. Aspirin is not effective for venous thromboembolism prophylaxis in this setting.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0044_2780", "title": "[Prevention of pulmonary embolism].", "span_text": "The following anithrombotic regimens are recommended in these patients: adjusted - dose heparin; oral anticoagulants with low intensity of anticoagulation; dextran; heparin in combination with dihydroergotamine; low-molecular-weight heparin fractions (LMWH). It is likely that prevention with LMWH will become the most important prophylactic modality in the near future."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "prophylaxis for pulmonary embolism in high-risk surgical patients", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_2780", "pubmed23n0016_5510", "pubmed23n0059_8009", "pubmed23n0059_1335", "pubmed23n0059_5393", "pubmed23n0030_8826", "pubmed23n0034_2683", "pubmed23n0029_9420", "InternalMed_Harrison_29933", "pubmed23n0013_10878", "pubmed23n0059_1931", "pubmed23n0060_2333", "pubmed23n0055_16040", "InternalMed_Harrison_5930", "Surgery_Schwartz_6771", "pubmed23n0025_1442", "pubmed23n0062_15316", "pubmed23n0025_1433"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_2780", "pubmed23n0016_5510", "pubmed23n0059_8009", "pubmed23n0059_1335", "pubmed23n0059_5393", "pubmed23n0030_8826", "pubmed23n0034_2683", "pubmed23n0029_9420", "InternalMed_Harrison_29933", "pubmed23n0013_10878", "pubmed23n0059_1931", "pubmed23n0060_2333", "pubmed23n0055_16040", "InternalMed_Harrison_5930", "Surgery_Schwartz_6771", "pubmed23n0025_1442", "pubmed23n0062_15316", "pubmed23n0025_1433"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "evidence_match", "result": "confirmed", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Pulmonary embolism Prevention prevention prophylaxis risk reduction screening vaccination primary prevention secondary prevention lifestyle modification counseling public health early detection follow-up", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7602.5135410000075, "llm_ms": 1658.459917000016, "verification_ms": 927.0051250000506, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0044_2780", "pubmed23n0016_5510", "pubmed23n0059_8009", "pubmed23n0059_1335", "pubmed23n0059_5393", "pubmed23n0030_8826", "pubmed23n0034_2683", "pubmed23n0029_9420", "InternalMed_Harrison_29933", "pubmed23n0013_10878", "pubmed23n0059_1931", "pubmed23n0060_2333", "pubmed23n0055_16040", "InternalMed_Harrison_5930", "Surgery_Schwartz_6771", "pubmed23n0025_1442", "pubmed23n0062_15316", "pubmed23n0025_1433"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 120.0, "generation": 45.0, "verification": 60.0, "llm": 1658.459917000016}}}
{"topic": "Breast cancer", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "A 45-year-old woman is diagnosed with node-negative, estrogen receptor-positive breast cancer. She is concerned about her long-term prognosis and whether adjuvant chemotherapy will improve her survival. According to a decision-analysis model, what is the estimated lifetime benefit of chemotherapy in quality-adjusted months for women like her?", "options": {"A": "5.1 quality-months", "B": "10.5 quality-months", "C": "2.3 quality-months", "D": "7.8 quality-months"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The decision-analysis model found an average lifetime benefit from chemotherapy of 5.1 quality-months for a 45-year-old woman with node-negative breast cancer. This benefit is adjusted for quality of life and represents the base-line scenario assuming a 30 percent reduction in the relative risk of recurrence for five years after treatment.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_10697", "title": "Efficacy and cost effectiveness of adjuvant chemotherapy in women with node-negative breast cancer. A decision-analysis model.", "span_text": "For the 45-year-old woman, the base-line analysis found an average lifetime benefit from chemotherapy of 5.1 quality-months at a cost of $15,400 per quality-year."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "benefit of chemotherapy in node-negative breast cancer decision model", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_10697", "pubmed23n0015_666", "pubmed23n0062_13842", "pubmed23n0062_13837", "pubmed23n0049_4984", "pubmed23n0054_10173", "pubmed23n0044_23548", "pubmed23n0057_12404", "pubmed23n0050_1921", "Surgery_Schwartz_3921", "pubmed23n0057_20740", "pubmed23n0061_9002", "pubmed23n0054_13123", "Surgery_Schwartz_9248", "pubmed23n0054_17029", "pubmed23n0021_12033", "pubmed23n0056_7990", "pubmed23n0063_12841", "pubmed23n0045_3378", "pubmed23n0063_6431", "Surgery_Schwartz_3694", "pubmed23n0017_877", "pubmed23n0007_6125", "InternalMed_Harrison_31956", "Gynecology_Nov