{"topic": "Pneumonia", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "A 65-year-old man with a history of alcohol abuse and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease presents with fever, cough, and dyspnea. Blood cultures grow Streptococcus pneumoniae. Which of the following is most commonly associated with increased risk for this type of infection in adults?", "options": {"A": "Alcohol abuse and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease", "B": "Recent travel to a tropical region", "C": "Long-term use of inhaled corticosteroids alone", "D": "Previous vaccination with pneumococcal conjugate vaccine"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Alcohol abuse and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease are well-established underlying conditions that predispose adults to pneumococcal pneumonia. These comorbidities impair host defense mechanisms in the respiratory tract, increasing susceptibility to bacterial infection.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0052_11440", "title": "Pneumococcal bacteraemia during a recent decade.", "span_text": "The most common underlying factors were alcohol abuse, cardiovascular diseases and chronic obstructive pulmonary diseases."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "risk factors for pneumococcal pneumonia in adults", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_17765", "pubmed23n0062_11179", "pubmed23n0063_21345", "pubmed23n0052_11440", "pubmed23n0058_14108", "pubmed23n0053_4478", "pubmed23n0052_1411", "pubmed23n0015_10739", "pubmed23n0062_5861", "pubmed23n0057_24111", "InternalMed_Harrison_10171", "pubmed23n0040_8379", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3017", "pubmed23n0049_8803", "InternalMed_Harrison_10904", "pubmed23n0007_1527"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0062_17765", "pubmed23n0062_11179", "pubmed23n0063_21345", "pubmed23n0052_11440", "pubmed23n0058_14108", "pubmed23n0053_4478", "pubmed23n0052_1411", "pubmed23n0015_10739", "pubmed23n0062_5861", "pubmed23n0057_24111", "InternalMed_Harrison_10171", "pubmed23n0040_8379", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3017", "pubmed23n0