{"topic": "Pneumonia", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A patient with AIDS is being treated for Pneumocystis pneumonia with trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole. Which of the following is most likely to occur as a common adverse effect of this therapy?", "options": {"A": "Hyperkalemia and elevated hepatic aminotransferases", "B": "Hypokalemia and decreased serum creatinine", "C": "Megaloblastic anemia and thrombocytosis", "D": "Insomnia and headache"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Patients with AIDS and Pneumocystis pneumonia have a particularly high frequency of adverse reactions to trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole, including fever, rashes, leukopenia, diarrhea, elevated hepatic aminotransferases, hyperkalemia, and hyponatremia.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_5191", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Patients with AIDS and pneumocystis pneumonia have a particularly high frequency of untoward reactions to trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole, especially fever, rashes, leukopenia, diarrhea, elevations of hepatic aminotransferases, hyperkalemia, and hyponatremia."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "adverse effects of trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole in AIDS patients with pneumonia", "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_5457", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3004", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5191"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_5457", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3004", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5191"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "exact_match", "result": "confirmed", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Pneumonia Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 5942.663458000197, "llm_ms": 950.3107079999609, "verification_ms": 823.0389170000763, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_5457", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3004", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5191"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 120.0, "verification": 45.0, "llm": 950.3107079999609}}}
{"topic": "Asthma", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 35-year-old patient with a history of asthma presents with worsening cough and production of brownish mucus plugs. Despite standard asthma therapy, symptoms remain uncontrolled. Laboratory testing reveals elevated total serum IgE and peripheral eosinophilia. Which of the following findings on chest imaging would most support a diagnosis of allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis (ABPA) in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Central bronchiectasis", "B": "Pleural effusion", "C": "Interstitial fibrosis", "D": "Pneumothorax"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Central bronchiectasis is a classic radiological finding in allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis (ABPA), which should be suspected in asthmatic patients with poor response to standard therapy, elevated IgE, eosinophilia, and characteristic clinical features such as brownish mucus plugs.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_20239", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Central bronchiectasis is described as a classic finding on chest imaging in ABPA"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "diagnostic imaging findings in allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis", "doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_1753", "InternalMed_Harrison_20239", "pubmed23n0052_11549", "pubmed23n0059_2455", "pubmed23n0051_20135", "pubmed23n0034_3594", "pubmed23n0054_6505"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_1753", "InternalMed_Harrison_20239", "pubmed23n0052_11549", "pubmed23n0059_2455", "pubmed23n0051_20135", "pubmed23n0034_3594", "pubmed23n0054_6505"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "exact_match", "score": "1.0", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Asthma Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6692.589417000136, "llm_ms": 2405.7006250000086, "verification_ms": 829.5003749999523, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_1753", "InternalMed_Harrison_20239", "pubmed23n0052_11549", "pubmed23n0059_2455", "pubmed23n0051_20135", "pubmed23n0034_3594", "pubmed23n0054_6505"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 120.0, "generation": 45.0, "verification": 30.0, "llm": 2405.7006250000086}}}
{"topic": "Rheumatoid arthritis", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "A 58-year-old woman with long-standing rheumatoid arthritis presents with progressive joint deformities and functional decline. She has been treated with multiple disease-modifying antirheumatic drugs over the past decade. Which factor is most strongly associated with increased mortality in patients with rheumatoid arthritis?", "options": {"A": "Severity of clinical disease status", "B": "Use of methotrexate therapy", "C": "Body mass index in adolescence", "D": "Compliance with oral contraceptives"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Higher mortality in patients with rheumatoid arthritis is primarily predicted by more severe clinical status rather than drug toxicity or unrelated causes. This is supported by evidence indicating that baseline clinical severity, radiographic progression, and systemic disease activity are key predictors of both morbidity and mortality.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0050_6011", "title": "The paradox of effective therapies but poor long-term outcomes in rheumatoid arthritis.", "span_text": "mortality in RA generally has been attributed to causes unrelated to RA or to drug toxicity, but higher mortality in specific patients is predicted primarily by more severe clinical status;"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "mortality predictors in rheumatoid arthritis", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0050_6011", "pubmed23n0049_8622", "pubmed23n0050_6783", "pubmed23n0052_6909", "pubmed23n0051_11175", "pubmed23n0052_6910", "pubmed23n0047_9315", "pubmed23n0058_11474", "pubmed23n0049_8620", "pubmed23n0047_2331", "pubmed23n0033_9186", "pubmed23n0062_580", "pubmed23n0058_11370", "pubmed23n0050_6015", "pubmed23n0052_15245", "pubmed23n0043_7455", "pubmed23n0004_11403", "pubmed23n0054_9339", "pubmed23n0053_11668", "pubmed23n0047_21697", "pubmed23n0050_7849", "pubmed23n0062_13029", "InternalMed_Harrison_4680", "pubmed23n0001_4408", "pubmed23n0011_13000", "pubmed23n0046_1748", "pubmed23n0027_4668", "pubmed23n0058_12469", "pubmed23n0039_10203", "pubmed23n0024_12081", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2551", "pubmed23n0012_11015", "First_Aid_Step1_536", "pubmed23n0061_3380", "pubmed23n0045_1659", "pubmed23n0052_2450", "pubmed23n0034_2721", "pubmed23n0001_6342", "pubmed23n0016_2968", "pubmed23n0037_389", "pubmed23n0038_1907", "pubmed23n0058_12882", "pubmed23n0016_11161", "pubmed23n0041_9243", "pubmed23n0013_9741", "pubmed23n0051_14920", "pubmed23n0057_14876", "pubmed23n0036_11125", "pubmed23n0047_9312", "pubmed23n0006_4243", "pubmed23n0054_9", "pubmed23n0026_11527", "pubmed23n0044_23263", "pubmed23n0036_8447", "pubmed23n0056_2156", "pubmed23n0012_11018", "pubmed23n0051_9936", "pubmed23n0015_9328"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0050_6011", "pubmed23n0049_8622", "pubmed23n0050_6783", "pubmed23n0052_6909", "pubmed23n0051_11175", "pubmed23n0052_6910", "pubmed23n0047_9315", "pubmed23n0058_11474", "pubmed23n0049_8620", "pubmed23n0047_2331", "pubmed23n0033_9186", "pubmed23n0062_580", "pubmed23n0058_11370", "pubmed23n0050_6015", "pubmed23n0052_15245", "pubmed23n0043_7455", "pubmed23n0004_11403", "pubmed23n0054_9339", "pubmed23n0053_11668", "pubmed23n0047_21697"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "direct_quote_match", "result": "confirmed", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Rheumatoid arthritis Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 10926.25387499993, "llm_ms": 1052.1209999999428, "verification_ms": 1230.8843339999385, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0,