{"topic": "Pancreatitis", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "A 58-year-old male with acute pancreatitis develops severe respiratory distress on the second day of hospitalization. He requires intubation and mechanical ventilation. Which of the following is the most common cause of death in patients with acute pancreatitis who present with respiratory distress?", "options": {"A": "Acute respiratory failure", "B": "Acute renal failure", "C": "Catheter-related sepsis", "D": "Pancreatic pseudocyst rupture"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Respiratory complications are the most common cause of death in acute pancreatitis, accounting for 27% of fatalities. Clinical diagnosis of 'respiratory distress' is associated with a 71% mortality rate, indicating the severity of pulmonary involvement in this condition.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0015_11022", "title": "Predictability of present outcome and future recurrence in acute pancreatitis.", "span_text": "Respiratory complications accounting for 27% of the fatalities were the most common causes of death. The incidence of considerable morbidity was 19.5%. Clinical diagnoses of \"shock\" and \"respiratory distress\" were associated with mortalities of 88% and 71%, respectively."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "respiratory complications mortality acute pancreatitis", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_11022", "pubmed23n0014_6129", "pubmed23n0058_19372", "pubmed23n0048_17520", "Surgery_Schwartz_9923", "pubmed23n0059_757", "Surgery_Schwartz_9671", "Surgery_Schwartz_9672", "pubmed23n0049_6843", "InternalMed_Harrison_24389", "pubmed23n0013_6783", "First_Aid_Step2_354", "pubmed23n0046_12100", "pubmed23n0058_7574", "pubmed23n0054_963", "Pathology_Robbins_4100", "pubmed23n0047_9618", "pubmed23n0061_15536", "pubmed23n0050_4175", "pubmed23n0056_16602", "Surgery_Schwartz_9248", "pubmed23n0062_1500", "pubmed23n0057_24635", "Obstentrics_Williams_7644", "Surgery_Schwartz_9560", "InternalMed_Harrison_24378", "pubmed23n0016_11146", "Surgery_Schwartz_9712", "pubmed23n0060_18331", "pubmed23n0044_23292"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0015_11022", "pubmed23n0014_6129", "pubmed23n0058_19372", "pubmed23n0048_17520", "Surgery_Schwartz_9923", "pubmed23n0059_757", "Surgery_Schwartz_9671", "Surgery_Schwartz_9672", "pubmed23n0049_6843", "InternalMed_Harrison_24389", "pubmed23n0013_6783", "First_Aid_Step2_354", "pubmed23n0046_12100", "pubmed23n0058_7574", "pubmed23n0054_963", "Pathology_Robbins_4100", "pubmed23n0047_9618", "pubmed23n0061_15536", "pubmed23n0050_4175", "pubmed23n0056_16602"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"accuracy": "confirmed", "consistency_with_evidence": "high", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Pancreatitis Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 8157.436041999972, "llm_ms": 3587.166125000067, "verification_ms": 1115.0004580001678, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0015_11022", "pubmed23n0014_6129", "pubmed23n0058_19372", "pubmed23n0048_17520", "Surgery_Schwartz_9923", "pubmed23n0059_757", "Surgery_Schwartz_9671", "Surgery_Schwartz_9672", "pubmed23n0049_6843", "InternalMed_Harrison_24389", "pubmed23n0013_6783", "First_Aid_Step2_354", "pubmed23n0046_12100", "pubmed23n0058_7574", "pubmed23n0054_963", "Pathology_Robbins_4100", "pubmed23n0047_9618", "pubmed23n0061_15536", "pubmed23n0050_4175", "pubmed23n0056_16602"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 120.0, "generation": 65.0, "total": 185.0, "llm": 3587.166125000067, "verification": 1115.0004580001678}}}
{"topic": "Asthma", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A 45-year-old woman with moderate persistent asthma is being evaluated for optimization of her controller therapy. She currently uses a short-acting beta agonist as needed but no daily maintenance medication. Which of the following medications is most appropriate to initiate for long-term control and prevention of asthma exacerbations?", "options": {"A": "Inhaled fluticasone", "B": "Oral theophylline", "C": "Montelukast", "D": "Inhaled ipratropium"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Inhaled corticosteroids such as fluticasone are the preferred first-line therapy for long-term control of asthma due to their potent anti-inflammatory effects and ability to prevent exacerbations. They are recommended for all levels of persistent asthma. Inhaled delivery maximizes airway effects while minimizing systemic toxicity.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_2161", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "CORTICOSTEROIDS, INHALED \u2022FluticasoneAlters gene expression Reduces mediators of inflammation \u2022powerfulprophylaxisofexacerbations Asthma\u2022adjunctinCOPD\u2022hayfever(nasal)Aerosol\u2022durationhours\u2022Toxicity: Limitedbyaerosolapplication\u2022candidalinfection, vocal cord changes"}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "inhaled corticosteroids for asthma prophylaxis", "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_2160", "Pharmacology_Katzung_278", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2162", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1231", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2081", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2161", "pubmed23n0050_11261", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2086", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2119", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3051", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4408"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_2160", "Pharmacology_Katzung_278", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2162", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1231", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2081", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2161", "pubmed23n0050_11261", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2086", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2119", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3051", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4408"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "exact_match", "confirmed_by": "Pharmacology_Katzung_2161", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Asthma Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6954.956000000038, "llm_ms": 1166.1899580001318, "verification_ms": 1427.2719160001088, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_2160", "Pharmacology_Katzung_278", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2162", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1231", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2081", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2161", "pubmed23n0050_11261", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2086", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3959", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2119", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3051", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4408"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 120.0, "generation": 45.0, "verification": 30.0, "llm": 1166.1899580001318}}}
{"topic": "Stroke", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "A 72-year-old man with a history of hypertension, diabetes, and prior ischemic stroke is admitted with an acute intracerebral hemorrhage. Which of the following factors is most strongly associated with increased in-hospital mortality in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Intracerebral hemorrhage as stroke type", "B": "History of smoking", "C": "Obesity", "D": "Sleep apnea"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Intracerebral hemorrhage is independently associated with the highest mortality among stroke types, with a reported in-hospital mortality of 34%. Age, cardiac disease, and diabetes also worsen acute stroke outcome, but stroke type remains a key determinant of prognosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0052_19808", "title": "Acute stroke outcome: effects of stroke type and risk factors.", "span_text": "Mortality was 19% overall, but varied significantly between stroke types, highest in intracerebral haemorrhage (34%), and lowest in lacunar infarction (1%). Age had a marked adverse effect on mortality, independent of stroke type, the probability of death increasing by 3 +/- 0.5% per year from 20-92 years, whereas gender had no effect. Cardiac disease and diabetes were independent adverse prognostic factors (Odds Ratios 1.6 and 1.5 respectively). Cerebral haemorrhage, age, cardiac disease and diabetes all independently worsen acute stroke outcome."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "risk factors for mortality in acute stroke patients", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0018_6422", "pubmed23n0054_778", "pubmed23n0050_211", "pubmed23n0052_19808", "pubmed23n0057_14423", "pubmed23n0049_12951", "Obstentrics_Williams_6591", "pubmed23n0028_4922", "pubmed23n0023_9957", "pubmed23n0054_12486", "Biochemistry_Lippincott_1201", "pubmed23n0060_228", "pubmed23n0050_1238", "First_Aid_Step2_600", "pubmed23n0044_9135", "pubmed23n0063_20280", "pubmed23n0050_13944", "pubmed23n0057_19174", "pubmed23n0063_2773", "Obstentrics_Williams_6905", "pubmed23n0049_16234", "pubmed23n0018_238", "pubmed23n0054_19638", "pubmed23n0052_15590", "pubmed23n0048_4150", "pubmed23n0017_7606", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3692", "Neurology_Adams_6916", "InternalMed_Harrison_19132", "pubmed23n0057_19175", "pubmed23n0005_966", "InternalMed_Harrison_30676", "pubmed23n0061_18584", "Biochemistry_Lippincott_1849", "InternalMed_Harrison_19633", "pubmed23n0048_6215", "pubmed23n0062_585", "pubmed23n0063_9562", "pubmed23n0058_15142", "pubmed23n0036_4718", "pubmed23n0056_4133", "Surgery_Schwartz_13398", "Surgery_Schwartz_13787", "pubmed23n0004_1360", "Pathology_Robbins_4629", "Surgery_Schwartz_6026", "pubmed23n0056_16325"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0018_6422", "pubmed23n0054_778", "pubmed23n0050_211", "pubmed23n0052_19808", "pubmed23n0057_14423", "pubmed23n0049_12951", "Obstentrics_Williams_6591", "pubmed23n0028_4922", "pubmed23n0023_9957", "pubmed23n0054_12486", "Biochemistry_Lippincott_1201", "pubmed23n0060_228", "pubmed23n0050_1238", "First_Aid_Step2_600", "pubmed23n0044_9135", "pubmed23n0063_20280", "pubmed23n0050_13944", "pubmed23n0057_19174", "pubmed23n0063_2773", "Obstentrics_Williams_6905"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "exact_match", "score": "1.0", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Stroke Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9630.391959000008, "llm_ms": 1139.0354580000803, "verification_ms": 847.5813749998906, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [],