{"topic": "Hyperlipidemia", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "In long-term survivors of renal transplantation, which of the following is the leading cause of death?", "options": {"A": "Infection", "B": "Graft rejection", "C": "Malignant disorders", "D": "Cardiovascular disease"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "In long-term survivors of renal transplantation, cardiovascular disease accounts for the majority of patient deaths. This has become the leading cause of mortality, surpassing infection, particularly in the cyclosporine era.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0050_3192", "title": "Hyperlipidemia and transplantation: etiologic factors and therapy.", "span_text": "In long-term survivors of renal transplantation, cardiovascular disease accounts for the majority of patient deaths. In the cyclosporine era, cardiovascular disease has surpassed infection as the number one cause of death."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "leading cause of death in long-term renal transplant survivors with hyperlipidemia", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0050_3192", "pubmed23n0048_967"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0048_967", "pubmed23n0050_3192"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "exact_match", "result": "confirmed", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hyperlipidemia Prognosis prognosis outcomes mortality survival complications disease course recurrence risk stratification severity long-term outcomes quality of life predictors", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9700.640000000249, "llm_ms": 1159.4245830001455, "verification_ms": 0.5480840000018361, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 0, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 1}, "failed_checks": ["evidence_spa