{"topic": "Anemia", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "A 35-year-old woman with sickle cell anemia presents with worsening fatigue, hypertension, and proteinuria. Laboratory studies show elevated serum creatinine. Which of the following is the most significant predictor of progression to end-stage renal failure in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Hypertension, proteinuria, and increasingly severe anemia", "B": "Leukocytosis and thrombocytopenia", "C": "Hyperbilirubinemia and gallstones", "D": "Pulmonary infarction and recurrent pain crises"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "In patients with sickle cell disease, pre-azotemic manifestations such as hypertension, proteinuria, and increasingly severe anemia are significant predictors of chronic renal failure. These factors precede the development of overt renal insufficiency and are associated with a higher risk of progression to end-stage renal disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_6179", "title": "Chronic renal failure in sickle cell disease: risk factors, clinical course, and mortality.", "span_text": "Case-control analysis showed that ineffective erythropoiesis with increasingly severe anemia, hypertension, proteinuria, the nephrotic syndrome, and microscopic hematuria were significant pre-azotemic predictors of chronic renal failure. The risk for sickle renal failure was increased in patients who had inherited the Central African Republic beta s-gene cluster haplotype. The pre-azotemic manifestations of hypertension, proteinuria, and increasingly severe anemia predict end-stage renal failure in patients with sickle cell disease."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "complications of sickle cell anemia related to renal failure", "doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_7738", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1179", "pubmed23n0063_6179", "pubmed23n0046_18126", "pubmed23n0017_2566", "pubmed23n0004_1185", "InternalMed_Harrison_21649", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3345", "pubmed23n0060_15744", "Obstentrics_Williams_8878", "pubmed23n0004_7945", "pubmed23n0044_23031"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Obstentrics_Williams_7738", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1179", "pubmed23n0063_6179", "pubmed23n0046_18126", "pubmed23n0017_2566", "pubmed23n0004_1185", "InternalMed_Harrison_21649", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3345", "pubmed23n0060_15744", "Obstentrics_Williams_8878", "pubmed23n0004_7945", "pubmed23n0044_23031"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"source_confirmed": "true", "accuracy": "high", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Anemia Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7194.51566700036, "llm_ms": 1321.1241670001073, "verification_ms": 0.402332999783539, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 0, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 1}, "failed_checks": ["evidence_span_mismatch"], "failed_checks_all": ["evidence_span_mismatch"], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Obstentrics_Williams_7738", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1179", "pubmed23n0063_6179", "pubmed23n0046_18126", "pubmed23n0017_2566", "pubmed23n0004_1185", "InternalMed_Harrison_21649", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3345", "pubmed23n0060_15744", "Obstentrics_Williams_8878", "pubmed23n0004_7945", "pubmed23n0044_23031"], "evidence_reused": false}, {"attempt": 2, "reason": "v2_requote", "query": "Anemia Complications complications adverse outcomes sequelae comorbidity disease progression risk factors mortality morbidity hospitalization long-term effects severity clinical deterioration", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6947.282749999886, "llm_ms": 1146.675082999