{"topic": "GERD", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "In patients who develop gastroesophageal reflux after sleeve gastrectomy, which of the following outcomes has been reported after magnetic sphincter augmentation (MSA) implantation?", "options": {"A": "More than half of patients no longer require daily proton pump inhibitor (PPI) therapy.", "B": "All patients continue daily PPI therapy.", "C": "There is no change in daily PPI use after MSA.", "D": "Daily PPI use increases after MSA implantation."}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Evidence from a scoping review indicates that after MSA implantation, more than half of patients with reflux following sleeve gastrectomy discontinued daily PPI use, demonstrating a significant reduction in medication dependence.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41527695", "title": "Magnetic Sphincter Augmentation for Gastroesophageal Reflux Following Sleeve Gastrectomy: A Scoping Review and First Asian Case Series", "span_text": "More than half of these patients no longer required daily PPI use after MSA implantation."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "query": "magnetic sphincter augmentation sleeve gastrectomy PPI", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578529", "pubmed_web_41577482", "pubmed_web_41576548", "pubmed_web_41576321", "pubmed_web_41564033", "pubmed_web_41563645", "pubmed_web_41558065", "pubmed_web_41557001", "pubmed_web_41553382", "pubmed_web_41551831", "pubmed_web_41551533", "pubmed_web_41545289", "pubmed_web_41539580", "pubmed_web_41537290", "pubmed_web_41534397", "pubmed_web_41530072", "pubmed_web_41527695", "pubmed_web_41525274", "pubmed_web_41525031", "pubmed_web_41524830"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41545289", "pubmed_web_41539580", "pubmed_web_41537290", "pubmed_web_41534397", "pubmed_web_41530072", "pubmed_web_41527695", "pubmed_web_41525274", "pubmed_web_41525031", "pubmed_web_41524830", "pubmed_web_41578529", "pubmed_web_41577482", "pubmed_web_41576548"