{"topic": "GERD", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "In patients who develop gastroesophageal reflux after sleeve gastrectomy, which intervention has been reported to reduce the need for daily proton pump inhibitor (PPI) therapy in more than half of cases?", "options": {"A": "Magnetic sphincter augmentation (MSA)", "B": "Laparoscopic Nissen fundoplication", "C": "Endoscopic radiofrequency ablation (Stretta)", "D": "High\u2011dose H2\u2011receptor antagonist therapy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The scoping review of studies on magnetic sphincter augmentation after sleeve gastrectomy found that more than half of the patients no longer required daily PPI use following MSA implantation, indicating its effectiveness in reducing medication dependence.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41527695", "title": "Magnetic Sphincter Augmentation for Gastroesophageal Reflux Following Sleeve Gastrectomy: A Scoping Review and First Asian Case Series", "span_text": "The scoping review identified eight studies from the U.S., reporting on 108 patients. More than half of these patients no longer required daily PPI use after MSA implantation."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578529", "pubmed_web_41577482", "pubmed_web_41576548", "pubmed_web_41576321", "pubmed_web_41564033", "pubmed_web_41563645", "pubmed_web_41558065", "pubmed_web_41557001", "pubmed_web_41553382", "pubmed_web_41551831", "pubmed_web_41551533", "pubmed_web_41545289", "pubmed_web_41539580", "pubmed_web_41537290", "pubmed_web_41534397", "pubmed_web_41530072", "pubmed_web_41527695", "pubmed_web_41525274", "pubmed_web_41525031", "pubmed_web_41524830"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41539580", "pubmed_web_41537290", "pubmed_web_41534397", "pubmed_web_41530072", "pubmed_web_41527695", "pubmed_web_41525274", "pubmed_web_41525031", "pubmed_web_41524830", "pubmed_web_41578529", "pubmed_web_41577482", "pubmed_web_41576548", "pubmed_web_41576321", "pubmed_web_4