{"topic": "GERD", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "In adults with gastroesophageal reflux disease experiencing nighttime heartburn, which class of medication has been demonstrated to achieve a higher rate of complete symptom resolution compared with proton pump inhibitors?", "options": {"A": "Potassium\u2011competitive acid blockers (PCABs)", "B": "H2\u2011receptor antagonists", "C": "Prokinetic agents", "D": "Antacids"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "A meta\u2011analysis of randomized controlled trials showed that PCABs significantly increased the likelihood of complete nighttime heartburn resolution compared with PPIs (risk ratio\u202f2.29, 95\u202f%\u202fCI\u202f1.36\u20113.87; p\u202f=\u202f0.002). No significant difference in adverse events was observed, supporting PCABs as the more effective option for nocturnal GERD symptoms.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41524830", "title": "A systematic review and meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials: the effect of potassium-competitive acid blockers on nighttime symptoms of gastroesophageal reflux disease", "span_text": "PCABs significantly increased the likelihood of complete nighttime heartburn resolution compared with PPIs (RR2.29, 95% CI 1.36-3.87; p = 0.002), with no heterogeneity. Safety analysis of the three trials showed no significant difference in TEAE risk (RR0.88, 95% CI 0.53-1.45; p = 0.62)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578529", "pubmed_web_41577482", "pubmed_web_41576548", "pubmed_web_41576321", "pubmed_web_41564033", "pubmed_web_41563645", "pubmed_web_41558065", "pubmed_web_41557001", "pubmed_web_41553382", "pubmed_web_41551831", "pubmed_web_41551533", "pubmed_web_41545289", "pubmed_web_41539580", "pubmed_web_41537290", "pubmed_web_41534397", "pubmed_web_41530072", "pubmed_web_41527695", "pubmed_web_41525274", "pubmed_web_41525031", "pubmed_web_41524830"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41534397", "pubmed_web_41530072", 