{"topic": "GERD", "competency": "Therapy", "stem": "In adults with gastroesophageal reflux disease who experience nighttime heartburn, which of the following statements about potassium\u2011competitive acid blockers (PCABs) compared with proton pump inhibitors (PPIs) is most accurate?", "options": {"A": "PCABs significantly increase the likelihood of complete nighttime heartburn resolution compared with PPIs.", "B": "PCABs have similar efficacy to PPIs for nighttime heartburn resolution.", "C": "PCABs are less effective than PPIs for nighttime heartburn resolution.", "D": "There is no evidence comparing PCABs and PPIs for nighttime heartburn."}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "A meta\u2011analysis of randomized controlled trials found that PCABs significantly increased the proportion of patients achieving complete resolution of nighttime heartburn compared with PPIs (risk ratio 2.29, 95%\u202fCI 1.36\u20113.87; p\u202f=\u202f0.002). Safety profiles were comparable, supporting PCABs as a more effective option for nocturnal GERD symptoms.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41524830", "title": "A systematic review and meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials: the effect of potassium-competitive acid blockers on nighttime symptoms of gastroesophageal reflux disease.", "span_text": "PCABs significantly increased the likelihood of complete nighttime heartburn resolution compared with PPIs (RR2.29, 95% CI 1.36-3.87; p = 0.002), with no heterogeneity."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578529", "pubmed_web_41577482", "pubmed_web_41576548", "pubmed_web_41576321", "pubmed_web_41564033", "pubmed_web_41563645", "pubmed_web_41558065", "pubmed_web_41557001", "pubmed_web_41553382", "pubmed_web_41551831", "pubmed_web_41551533", "pubmed_web_41545289", "pubmed_web_41539580", "pubmed_web_41537290", "pubmed_web_41534397", "pubmed_web_41530072", "pubmed_web_41527695", "pubmed_web_41525274", "pubmed_web_41525031", "pubm