{"topic": "Anxiety Disorders", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "In a clinical study of patients with panic disorder and agoraphobia, what proportion was found to have a comorbid personality disorder?", "options": {"A": "Approximately 10%", "B": "Approximately 25%", "C": "Approximately 50%", "D": "Approximately 75%"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "Research using descriptive\u2011phenomenological diagnostic evaluation showed that almost half of patients with panic disorder and agoraphobia also met criteria for a personality disorder, highlighting the high rate of comorbidity.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0050_16725", "title": "Anxiety disorders--syndrome, personality and relationships. Results of multi-methodology diagnosis", "span_text": "evidence of co-morbidity involving (concomitant?) personality disorders was found in almost 50% of the patients investigated."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword_search", "query": "panic disorder agoraphobia personality disorder co-morbidity", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0050_16725", "InternalMed_Harrison_31620", "pubmed23n0043_17732", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1181", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1599", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_95", "pubmed23n0054_9863", "InternalMed_Harrison_26020", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1187", "InternalMed_Harrison_28583", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_2033", "pubmed23n0050_19193", "Gynecology_Novak_5476", "pubmed23n0052_2977", "pubmed23n0044_23435", "pubmed23n0011_9743", "pubmed23n0015_8564", "pubmed23n0015_4995", "pubmed23n0060_16280", "pubmed23n0058_11835", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1415", "pubmed23n0062_17682", "pubmed23n0003_11516", "pubmed23n0060_19173", "pubmed23n0053_1229", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_522", "pubmed23n0062_1477", "pubmed23n0047_19745", "pubmed23n0012_8787", "pubmed23n0004_8902", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_1168", "pubmed23n0049_4107", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3292", "Neurology_Adams_7841", "InternalMed_Harrison_24082", "pubmed23n0049_15300", "pubmed23n0061_5484", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1158", "Psichiatry_DSM-5_410