{"topic": "Sepsis", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "Which cardiac parameter measured during the early hospital stay of a septic patient is an independent predictor of subsequent major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE)?", "options": {"A": "High left ventricular global longitudinal strain (> -16)", "B": "Low left ventricular ejection fraction", "C": "Elevated serum lactate level", "D": "Persistent thrombocytopenia"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "In a cohort of sepsis survivors, high LV GLS was independently associated with an increased risk of MACE, whereas low LVEF showed no significant association. Therefore, LV GLS is the cardiac measurement that predicts future cardiovascular complications after sepsis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41579501", "title": "Long-term outcomes of abnormal global longitudinal left ventricular strain during sepsis: A retrospective cohort study", "span_text": "LV GLS was an independent predictor of MACE in septic patients, whereas LVEF did not show a significant association."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword_search", "query": "sepsis LV GLS MACE", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41582759", "pubmed_web_41582269", "pubmed_web_41580950", "pubmed_web_41580574", "pubmed_web_41580332", "pubmed_web_41580009", "pubmed_web_41579966", "pubmed_web_41579563", "pubmed_web_41579501", "pubmed_web_41579211", "pubmed_web_41579146", "pubmed_web_41578749", "pubmed_web_41578565", "pubmed_web_41578542", "pubmed_web_41578537", "pubmed_web_41578464", "pubmed_web_41578395", "pubmed_web_41575374", "pubmed_web_41574690", "pubmed_web_41574664"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41579966", "pubmed_web_41579563", "pubmed_web_41579501", "pubmed_web_41579211", "pubmed_web_41579146", "pubmed_web_41578749", "pubmed_web_41578565", "pubmed_web_41578542", "pubmed_web_41578537", "pubmed_web_41578464", "pubmed_web_41578395", "pubmed_web_41575374", "pubmed_web_41574690", "pubmed_web_41574664", "pubmed_web_415