{"topic": "Sepsis", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "In survivors of sepsis, which echocardiographic parameter measured during the early hospital stay is independently associated with an increased risk of major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE)?", "options": {"A": "High left ventricular global longitudinal strain (LV GLS) > -16", "B": "Low left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF)", "C": "Elevated right ventricular systolic pressure", "D": "Increased left atrial volume index"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Studies of septic patients have shown that an abnormal LV GLS (values > -16) predicts future major adverse cardiovascular events, while LVEF does not have a significant association. Therefore, a high LV GLS is the independent echocardiographic predictor of MACE in this population.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41579501", "title": "Long-term outcomes of abnormal global longitudinal left ventricular strain during sepsis: A retrospective cohort study", "span_text": "LV GLS was an independent predictor of MACE in septic patients, whereas LVEF did not show a significant association."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword_search", "query": "sepsis LV GLS MACE", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41582759", "pubmed_web_41582269", "pubmed_web_41580950", "pubmed_web_41580574", "pubmed_web_41580332", "pubmed_web_41580009", "pubmed_web_41579966", "pubmed_web_41579563", "pubmed_web_41579501", "pubmed_web_41579211", "pubmed_web_41579146", "pubmed_web_41578749", "pubmed_web_41578565", "pubmed_web_41578542", "pubmed_web_41578537", "pubmed_web_41578464", "pubmed_web_41578395", "pubmed_web_41575374", "pubmed_web_41574690", "pubmed_web_41574664"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41579501", "pubmed_web_41579211", "pubmed_web_41579146", "pubmed_web_41578749", "pubmed_web_41578565", "pubmed_web_41578542", "pubmed_web_41578537", "pubmed_web_41578464", "pubmed_web_41578395", "pubmed_web_41575374", "pubmed_web_41574690", "pubme