{"topic": "Stroke", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "In patients undergoing transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVR), which oral anticoagulant regimen has been shown to reduce net adverse clinical events compared with vitamin K antagonists?", "options": {"A": "Direct oral anticoagulants (DOACs)", "B": "Vitamin K antagonists (VKAs)", "C": "Low-dose aspirin", "D": "Dual antiplatelet therapy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Meta\u2011analysis of studies after TAVR demonstrated that direct oral anticoagulants were associated with a significantly lower risk of net adverse clinical events (RR\u202f0.84) compared with vitamin K antagonists, indicating superior safety in this setting.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41571953", "title": "The effectiveness and safety of oral anticoagulation therapy in patients undergoing transcatheter aortic valve replacement: a systematic review/meta-analysis", "span_text": "The risk of NACEs (RR: 0.84, 95% CI :0.71-0.99, P = 0.04) and cardiovascular death (RR: 0.78, 95% CI: 0.69-0.87, P < 0.0001) was significantly lower in the DOACs than in the VKAs, but there were no statistically significant differences between the two groups with other outcomes."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41582546", "pubmed_web_41582192", "pubmed_web_41580787", "pubmed_web_41580529", "pubmed_web_41579204", "pubmed_web_41578552", "pubmed_web_41578320", "pubmed_web_41577922", "pubmed_web_41577920", "pubmed_web_41577216", "pubmed_web_41575950", "pubmed_web_41575631", "pubmed_web_41575609", "pubmed_web_41574686", "pubmed_web_41574553", "pubmed_web_41572775", "pubmed_web_41572337", "pubmed_web_41571953", "pubmed_web_41571952", "pubmed_web_41571757"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41575609", "pubmed_web_41574686", "pubmed_web_41574553", "pubmed_web_41572775", "pubmed_web_41572337", "pubmed_web_41571953", "pubmed_web_41571952", "pubmed_web_41571757", "pubmed_web_41582546", "pubmed_web_41582