{"topic": "Pancreatitis", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 5\u00bd\u2011year\u2011old boy is admitted with acute pancreatitis. Which of the following conditions should be included in the differential diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "Kawasaki disease", "B": "Celiac disease", "C": "Crohn disease", "D": "Ulcerative colitis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Kawasaki disease can present shortly after an episode of pancreatitis in children, and case reports have highlighted the need to consider it when evaluating pediatric acute pancreatitis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0047_21213", "title": "Pancreatitis heralding Kawasaki disease", "span_text": "A 5 1/2 year-old boy was hospitalized with clinical and laboratory evidence of pancreatitis. Four days later the classic signs and symptoms of Kawasaki disease developed. This case suggests that Kawasaki disease should be included in the differential diagnosis of acute pancreatitis in children."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0023_5526", "pubmed23n0047_21213", "pubmed23n0013_3149", "InternalMed_Harrison_24368", "pubmed23n0062_1500", "pubmed23n0004_1792", "pubmed23n0062_5886", "InternalMed_Harrison_24307", "pubmed23n0056_18914", "InternalMed_Harrison_24367", "pubmed23n0020_6557", "pubmed23n0034_4853", "Surgery_Schwartz_9644", "Surgery_Schwartz_9662", "InternalMed_Harrison_24327", "pubmed23n0045_14443", "pubmed23n0051_2481", "pubmed23n0012_1885", "pubmed23n0030_8799", "pubmed23n0049_12899", "pubmed23n0024_278", "pubmed23n0016_856", "pubmed23n0026_1400"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0047_21213", "pubmed23n0013_3149", "InternalMed_Harrison_24368", "pubmed23n0062_1500", "pubmed23n0004_1792", "pubmed23n0062_5886", "InternalMed_Harrison_24307", "pubmed23n0056_18914", "InternalMed_Harrison_24367", "pubmed23n0020_6557", "pubmed23n0034_4853", "Surgery_Schwartz_9644", "Surgery_Schwartz_9662", "InternalMed_Harrison_24327", "pubmed23n0045_14443", "pubmed23n0051_2481", "pu