{"topic": "Prostate cancer", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "How can primary prevention of cancer be achieved through lifestyle modifications?", "options": {"A": "By reducing dietary fat intake and increasing consumption of fruits and vegetables", "B": "By increasing exposure to radiation and carcinogens in air and water", "C": "By reducing physical activity and increasing tobacco use", "D": "By decreasing screening for breast and cervical cancer"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Primary prevention of cancer can be achieved through lifestyle modifications, such as reducing dietary fat intake and increasing consumption of fruits and vegetables, which can help reduce the risk of certain types of cancer.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0057_5223", "title": "Epidemiological approaches to primary and secondary prevention of cancer", "span_text": "Dietary factors may be as important, with dietary fat the most important risk factor, vegetables and fruits being protective."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_12794", "pubmed23n0049_13658", "pubmed23n0057_5223", "pubmed23n0053_8349", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "pubmed23n0059_21445", "First_Aid_Step2_237", "pubmed23n0048_17336", "pubmed23n0058_15950", "pubmed23n0058_10943", "pubmed23n0058_3524", "pubmed23n0057_20451", "pubmed23n0058_1366", "pubmed23n0045_15534", "pubmed23n0062_1607", "pubmed23n0055_9924", "pubmed23n0059_2218", "pubmed23n0063_12708", "pubmed23n0052_12796", "pubmed23n0047_5386", "pubmed23n0061_8033", "pubmed23n0047_4505", "pubmed23n0047_4504", "pubmed23n0027_6254", "pubmed23n0050_20552", "InternalMed_Harrison_5956", "pubmed23n0062_20210", "pubmed23n0047_5395", "pubmed23n0055_21461", "pubmed23n0062_2940", "InternalMed_Harrison_6015", "InternalMed_Harrison_322", "pubmed23n0059_13869", "Surgery_Schwartz_2339", "pubmed23n0051_1663", "pubmed23n0058_581", "InternalMed_Harrison_5929", "InternalMed_Harrison_5966", "pubmed23n0054_2279", "p