{"topic": "Heart failure", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the primary goal of treatment in heart failure, according to current understanding?", "options": {"A": "To improve short-term hemodynamic and symptomatic goals", "B": "To manage patients to improve both the quality and quantity of life", "C": "To focus on short-term hemodynamic or symptomatic goals", "D": "To decrease the effects of the sympathetic nervous system only"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The primary goal of treatment in heart failure is to manage patients to improve both the quality and quantity of life, rather than just focusing on short-term hemodynamic or symptomatic goals.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0054_9515", "title": "Long-term strategies in the management of heart failure: looking beyond ventricular function and symptoms", "span_text": "Therapeutic approaches to the management of heart failure have traditionally focused on shortterm hemodynamic and symptomatic goals, but present evidence suggests that most therapeutic decisions have long-term consequences. Treatment may change the rate of disease progression, modify the need for additional therapy, influence the number of hospitalizations, and alter the risk of death."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_5246", "pubmed23n0059_20077", "pubmed23n0054_9515", "pubmed23n0014_2698", "InternalMed_Harrison_18276", "InternalMed_Harrison_18264", "pubmed23n0054_9514", "Obstentrics_Williams_6869", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1331", "pubmed23n0062_743", "InternalMed_Harrison_18263", "InternalMed_Harrison_18590", "pubmed23n0006_10846", "pubmed23n0019_13460", "pubmed23n0051_100", "pubmed23n0023_6700", "Gynecology_Novak_2502", "pubmed23n0051_1059", "pubmed23n0029_9228", "Surgery_Schwartz_6929", "pubmed23n0027_4029", "InternalMed_Harrison_18234", "pubmed23n0058_2514", "pubmed23n0026_5602", "InternalMed_Harrison_18253", "pubmed23n0056_10906", "pubmed23n0012_5617",