{"topic": "Malaria", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is the most reliable and definitive test for the diagnosis of malaria?", "options": {"A": "Differential stained thick and thin blood smear", "B": "Complete blood count with differential", "C": "Measurement of serum electrolytes", "D": "Liver function tests"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The differential stained thick and thin blood smear is the most reliable and definitive test for the diagnosis of malaria because it allows for the direct visualization of the parasites under a microscope.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0060_6118", "title": "Laboratory diagnosis of malaria.", "span_text": "Presently the differential stained thick and thin blood smear, examined under the microscope, remains the most reliable and definitive test for diagnosis of malaria."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"source": "pubmed", "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_12697", "InternalMed_Harrison_16947", "pubmed23n0060_6118", "InternalMed_Harrison_9718"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_12697", "InternalMed_Harrison_16947", "pubmed23n0060_6118", "InternalMed_Harrison_9718"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Malaria Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7474.6788750017, "llm_ms": 1222.816542001965, "verification_ms": 1108.8890829996672, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_i