{"topic": "HIV", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the primary goal of HIV counseling and testing services provided by health departments?", "options": {"A": "To identify HIV-infected persons who can be referred for early medical care and counseled to practice safer behaviors", "B": "To provide treatment for HIV-infected individuals", "C": "To promote health education and risk reduction", "D": "To evaluate existing services"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary goal of HIV counseling and testing services is to identify HIV-infected persons who can be referred for early medical care and counseled to practice safer behaviors, thereby preventing further transmission of the disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0050_5486", "title": "Publicly funded HIV counseling and testing--United States, 1991", "span_text": "The purpose of HIV CT is to 1) reinforce perception of risk by those who are unaware or uninformed, 2) help uninfected persons initiate and sustain behavior changes that reduce their risk for becoming infected, and 3) identify HIV-infected persons who can be referred for early medical care and counseled to practice safer behaviors."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_20690", "First_Aid_Step2_800", "InternalMed_Harrison_10756", "pubmed23n0055_13775", "pubmed23n0055_9279", "pubmed23n0050_5486", "pubmed23n0055_13768", "pubmed23n0048_7714", "pubmed23n0053_8313", "pubmed23n0055_13757", "pubmed23n0054_21402", "pubmed23n0047_2131", "pubmed23n0055_13760", "Gynecology_Novak_728", "Obstentrics_Williams_9092", "pubmed23n0055_13772", "pubmed23n0062_3058", "pubmed23n0063_12968", "Surgery_Schwartz_1282", "pubmed23n0058_16854", "pubmed23n0055_13764", "pubmed23n0047_2145", "pubmed23n0051_1002", "Obstentrics_Williams_9114", "pubmed23n0050_8981", "InternalMed_Harrison_11663", "pubmed23n0062_2547", "pubmed23n0043_15411", "pubmed23n0046_16635", "Gynecology_Novak_733", "pubmed23n0055_1377