{"topic": "Osteoarthritis", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 65-year-old patient presents with joint pain and stiffness. What is the most important factor in diagnosing osteoarthritis in this patient?", "options": {"A": "History and physical examination", "B": "Laboratory and x-ray findings", "C": "Family medical history", "D": "Age and occupation"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The correct diagnosis of osteoarthritis should be suspected from the history and physical examination alone, with laboratory and x-ray findings providing supportive evidence.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0010_6856", "title": "Differential diagnosis of rheumatic disease in the elderly", "span_text": "In each case the correct diagnosis should have been suspected from the history and physical examination alone, with the laboratory and x-ray findings providing supportive evidence."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0010_6856", "pubmed23n0006_238", "InternalMed_Harrison_26220", "pubmed23n0051_16713", "pubmed23n0049_2162"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0010_6856", "pubmed23n0006_238", "InternalMed_Harrison_26220", "pubmed23n0051_16713", "pubmed23n0049_2162"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteoarthritis Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 8177.713459001097, "llm_ms": 1128.0184159986675, "verification_ms": 918.9187090014457, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed