{"topic": "Neonatal sepsis", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the recommended approach for treating neonatal sepsis in an intensive care unit?", "options": {"A": "Early diagnosis and treatment with piperacillin plus cefotaxime", "B": "Surgical intervention as the first line of treatment", "C": "Conservative management awaiting spontaneous improvement", "D": "Administering intramuscular ceftriaxone with outpatient follow-up"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Early diagnosis and treatment with piperacillin plus cefotaxime can improve the results of neonatal sepsis treatment, especially in intensive care patients.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_4311", "title": "Neonatal sepsis in an intensive care unit and results of treatment", "span_text": "Early diagnosis and treatment with piperacillin plus cefotaxime reduced the mortality rate of sepsis to 2%. Sepsis never developed under treatment with piperacillin plus cefotaxime."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0055_7387", "pubmed23n0062_17702", "pubmed23n0053_8023", "pubmed23n0054_18227", "pubmed23n0063_4311", "pubmed23n0053_20250", "pubmed23n0038_11689", "Surgery_Schwartz_1241", "pubmed23n0059_15754", "pubmed23n0025_5242", "pubmed23n0014_9513", "pubmed23n0049_6845", "pubmed23n0047_12115", "pubmed23n0006_4262", "pubmed23n0044_2037", "pubmed23n0047_2992", "pubmed23n0011_11066", "pubmed23n0048_12058", "pubmed23n0037_4049"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0055_7387", "pubmed23n0062_17702", "pubmed23n0053_8023", "pubmed23n0054_18227", "pubmed23n0063_4311", "pubmed23n0053_20250", "pubmed23n0038_11689", "Surgery_Schwartz_1241", "pubmed23n0059_15754", "pubmed23n0025_5242", "pubmed23n0014_9513", "pubmed23n0049_6845", "pubmed23n0047_12115", "pubmed23n0006_4262", "pubmed23n0044_2037", "pubmed23n0047_2992", "pubmed23n0011_11066", "pubmed23n0048_12058", "pubmed23n0037_4049"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {