{"topic": "Asthma", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 30-year-old patient with a history of asthma presents with cough and production of brownish plugs of mucus, and has proven refractory to usual therapy. What is the next step in the diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "Workup for allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis (ABPA)", "B": "Order a chest radiograph", "C": "Perform a sinus computed tomography scan", "D": "Start treatment with oral corticosteroids"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms and history of refractory asthma suggest the possibility of ABPA, which is a distinct diagnosis from simple asthma. A workup for ABPA is necessary to establish sensitivity to Aspergillus antigens and confirm the diagnosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_20239", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis (ABPA) is an eosinophilic pulmonary disorder that occurs in response to allergic sensitization to antigens from Aspergillus species fungi. The predominant clinical presentation of ABPA is an asthmatic phenotype, often accompanied by cough with production of brownish plugs of mucus. ABPA has also been well described as a complication of cystic fibrosis. A workup for ABPA may be beneficial in patients who carry a diagnosis of asthma but have proven refractory to usual therapy."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_1753", "InternalMed_Harrison_20239", "pubmed23n0052_11549", "pubmed23n0059_2455", "pubmed23n0051_20135", "pubmed23n0034_3594", "pubmed23n0054_6505"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_1753", "InternalMed_Harrison_20239", "pubmed23n0052_11549", "pubmed23n0059_2455", "pubmed23n0051_20135", "pubmed23n0034_3594", "pubmed23n0054_6505"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Asthma Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7623.194959000102, "llm_ms": 953.1364169997687, "verification_ms": 4083.160041998781, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_1753", "InternalMed_Harrison_20239", "pubmed23n0052_11549", "pubmed23n0059_2455", "pubmed23n0051_20135", "pubmed23n0034_3594", "pubmed23n0054_6505"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"total": 300.0, "retrieval": 7623.194959000102, "llm": 953.1364169997687, "verification": 4083.160041998781}}}
{"topic": "Sepsis", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the primary cause of mortality in patients with acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS)?", "options": {"A": "Pulmonary causes", "B": "Nonpulmonary causes, including sepsis and organ failure", "C": "Cardiovascular causes", "D": "Neurological causes"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Mortality in ARDS is largely attributable to nonpulmonary causes, with sepsis and nonpulmonary organ failure accounting for >80% of deaths.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_20783", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Of interest, mortality in ARDS is largely attributable to nonpulmonary causes, with sepsis and nonpulmonary organ failure accounting for >80% of deaths."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_8663", "InternalMed_Harrison_20783", "Obstentrics_Williams_7067", "pubmed23n0037_6502", "Gynecology_Novak_3843", "pubmed23n0053_14085", "pubmed23n0058_21152", "Obstentrics_Williams_5951", "pubmed23n0004_3136"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0052_8663", "InternalMed_Harrison_20783", "Obstentrics_Williams_7067", "pubmed23n0037_6502", "Gynecology_Novak_3843", "pubmed23n0053_14085", "pubmed23n0058_21152", "Obstentrics_Williams_5951", "pubmed23n0004_3136"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Sepsis Prognosis prognosis outcomes mortality survival complications disease course recurrence risk stratification severity long-term outcomes quality of life predictors", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 9505.696874999558, "llm_ms": 1523.0241249992105, "verification_ms": 2032.3977499974717, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "IN