{"topic": "Dengue", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is a key factor that contributes to the severity of haematological disease in dengue virus infection?", "options": {"A": "Host immune response to the virus", "B": "Geographical location of the infection", "C": "Presence of an environmental toxin", "D": "Distribution of an infectious agent"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The severity of haematological disease in dengue virus infection is influenced by the host immune response to the virus, as it plays a crucial role in determining the outcome of the infection.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0050_12381", "title": "Viruses and the blood", "span_text": "Severe haematological disease is the exception rather than the rule in dengue virus infection, and probably depends at least in part on the host immune response to the virus."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0050_12381", "pubmed23n0030_5568"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0050_12381", "pubmed23n0030_5568"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Dengue Etiology etiology cause risk factors pathogenesis mechanism underlying cause genetic factors environmental factors predisposing factors associated conditions epidemiology incidence", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6517.622625000513, "llm_ms": 1211.3675420005166, "verification_ms": 924.3717079989437, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0050_12381", "pubmed23n0030_5568"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms":