{"topic": "Heart failure", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "What is a factor that can influence the outcome of patients with heart failure, according to the effect of pharmacologic agents on neurohormonal systems?", "options": {"A": "Drugs that decrease the effects of the sympathetic nervous system", "B": "Drugs that increase the activity of the renin-angiotensin system", "C": "Drugs that exert negative inotropic effects", "D": "Drugs that improve cardiac performance"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The effect of pharmacologic agents on neurohormonal systems, rather than on hemodynamic variables, is a key factor in determining the outcome of patients with heart failure.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0054_9515", "title": "Long-term strategies in the management of heart failure: looking beyond ventricular function and symptoms", "span_text": "In general, drugs that decrease the effects of the sympathetic nervous system (digitalis glycosides) and the renin-angiotensin system (angiotensin-converting enzyme [ACE] inhibitors) reduce the risk of worsening heart failure."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0053_17698", "InternalMed_Harrison_18242", "pubmed23n0054_586", "pubmed23n0053_17697", "pubmed23n0052_8305", "pubmed23n0046_17991", "pubmed23n0054_9515", "pubmed23n0036_11146", "pubmed23n0045_1117", "pubmed23n0048_7202", "pubmed23n0043_106", "Surgery_Schwartz_13389", "pubmed23n0058_8667", "InternalMed_Harrison_18315", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1979", "pubmed23n0057_14423", "pubmed23n0046_12067", "InternalMed_Harrison_21649", "pubmed23n0062_4079", "pubmed23n0047_2331", "pubmed23n0047_11756", "pubmed23n0023_9957", "pubmed23n0050_211", "Surgery_Schwartz_13390", "pubmed23n0030_11320", "pubmed23n0046_18126", "pubmed23n0057_9433", "pubmed23n0052_15611", "pubmed23n0050_2338", "pubmed23n0032_3863", "pubmed23n0047_9521", "pubmed23n0028_9430", "InternalMed_Harrison_19018", "pubmed23n0052_2352", "Obstentrics_Wi