{"topic": "Cirrhosis", "competency": "Prognosis", "stem": "What is the primary factor contributing to the poor prognosis of patients with hepatocellular carcinoma and cirrhosis?", "options": {"A": "Cancer recurrence", "B": "Tumor size", "C": "Liver dysfunction", "D": "Higher carcinogenic potential in cirrhosis"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "The higher carcinogenic potential in cirrhosis is presumed to be the most likely reason for the poorer prognosis after surgery in patients with HCC and cirrhosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0044_10432", "title": "Influence of coexisting cirrhosis on long-term prognosis after surgery in patients with hepatocellular carcinoma", "span_text": "The higher carcinogenic potential in cirrhosis could be presumed to be the most likely reason for the poorer prognosis after surgery in the patients with HCC and cirrhosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_10432", "InternalMed_Harrison_7098", "pubmed23n0046_18230", "pubmed23n0048_18816", "Obstentrics_Williams_7600", "pubmed23n0043_20277", "pubmed23n0036_1940", "pubmed23n0059_9002", "pubmed23n0058_1190", "pubmed23n0054_5644", "pubmed23n0043_19005", "pubmed23n0059_4200", "pubmed23n0056_20815", "pubmed23n0051_4304", "pubmed23n0014_5219", "InternalMed_Harrison_24189", "pubmed23n0002_2921", "InternalMed_Harrison_23987", "pubmed23n0055_13639"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_10432", "InternalMed_Harrison_7098", "pubmed23n0046_18230", "pubmed23n0048_18816", "Obstentrics_Williams_7600", "pubmed23n0043_20277", "pubmed23n0036_1940", "pubmed23n0059_9002", "pubmed23n0058_1190", "pubmed23n0054_5644", "pubmed23n0043_19005", "pubmed23n0059_4200", "pubmed23n0056_20815", "pubmed23n0051_4304", "pubmed23n0014_5219", "InternalMed_Harrison_24189", "pubmed23n0002_2921", "InternalMed_Harrison_23987", "pubmed23n0055_13639"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks":