{"topic": "Dengue Fever", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism of thrombocytopenia in dengue hemorrhagic fever?", "options": {"A": "Increased platelet destruction due to immunologic mechanisms", "B": "Decreased platelet production in the bone marrow", "C": "Sequestration of platelets in the spleen", "D": "Direct infection of platelets by the dengue virus"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The primary mechanism of thrombocytopenia in dengue hemorrhagic fever is increased platelet destruction due to immunologic mechanisms, such as the formation of immune complexes.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0030_5568", "title": "Hemostatic and platelet kinetic studies in dengue hemorrhagic fever", "span_text": "In 11 cases platelet kinetic study revealed increased destruction as a main cause for the thrombocytopenia, most probably due to the underlying immunologic mechanism, i.e., via the immune complexes formed."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0040_11153", "pubmed23n0046_16993", "pubmed23n0008_5019", "pubmed23n0055_23642", "pubmed23n0052_8813", "pubmed23n0062_2052", "pubmed23n0059_10361", "pubmed23n0013_6709", "pubmed23n0043_13850", "pubmed23n0030_5568", "pubmed23n0012_9007", "pubmed23n0060_20230", "pubmed23n0013_5207", "pubmed23n0051_17083", "pubmed23n0038_6601", "InternalMed_Harrison_15707", "pubmed23n0016_1877", "pubmed23n0060_15365", "pubmed23n0060_13708", "pubmed23n0060_12881", "pubmed23n0043_3170", "pubmed23n0054_2558", "pubmed23n0060_7081", "pubmed23n0031_9441", "pubmed23n0045_131", "pubmed23n0051_14352", "pubmed23n0047_3883", "InternalMed_Harrison_15713", "pubmed23n0058_6178", "pubmed23n0013_5033", "InternalMed_Harrison_18726", "pubmed23n0016_1876", "pubmed23n0016_7168", "pubmed23n0050_18125", "pubmed23n0024_11122", "pubmed23n0031_5502", "pubmed23n0058_11190", "pubmed23n0044_24665", "pubmed23n0015_10615", "pubmed23n0059_16593", "pubmed23n0003_76"], "evidence_doc_i