{"topic": "Typhoid", "competency": "Investigation", "stem": "Which laboratory test provides the highest diagnostic sensitivity for confirming typhoid fever?", "options": {"A": "Bone marrow culture", "B": "Blood culture", "C": "Widal agglutination test", "D": "Standard Agglutination Test (SAT)"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Bone marrow culture yields Salmonella typhi more frequently than blood culture, making it the most sensitive diagnostic test for typhoid fever.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0058_8709", "title": "Relative sensitivity of blood and bone marrow cultures in typhoid fever", "span_text": "Forty-four per cent and 59% of the patients yielded S. typhi on blood and bone marrow cultures, respectively. In 31 patients who were investigated by both blood and bone marrow cultures, the yields of S. typhi were 35% and 61% respectively. This difference is statistically significant (P less than 0.05). In this study bone marrow culture proved to be the most sensitive diagnostic test for typhoid fever."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"query": "typhoid bone marrow culture sensitivity", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_10977", "pubmed23n0047_14460", "pubmed23n0014_4025", "pubmed23n0032_10993", "pubmed23n0050_1196", "pubmed23n0029_5015", "pubmed23n0028_8407", "pubmed23n0058_8709", "pubmed23n0020_9619"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_10977", "pubmed23n0047_14460", "pubmed23n0014_4025", "pubmed23n0032_10993", "pubmed23n0050_1196", "pubmed23n0029_5015", "pubmed23n0028_8407", "pubmed23n0058_8709", "pubmed23n0020_9619"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "manual cross\u2011check with source text", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Typhoid Investigation investigation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging workup evaluation differential diagnosis clinical criteria biomarkers screening confirmatory test diagnostic