{"topic": "Hipertensi", "competency": "Monitoring", "stem": "What measures of target-organ damage were examined in the CARDHIAC trial for patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus and hypertension?", "options": {"A": "Left ventricular mass index, carotid intima media thickness, and urinary albumin excretion", "B": "Blood pressure, heart rate, and body mass index", "C": "Glucose levels, kidney function, and liver function", "D": "Lipid profiles, electrocardiogram, and chest X-ray"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The CARDHIAC trial examined the effects of doxazosin and atenolol on left ventricular mass index, carotid intima media thickness, and urinary albumin excretion in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus and hypertension.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_18343246", "title": "Comparison of the effects of doxazosin and atenolol on target organ damage in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus and hypertension in the CARDHIAC study", "span_text": "The CARDHIAC (CARduran en pacientes Diab\u00e9ticos con HIpertensi'on Arterial no Controlada) trial examined the effects of doxazosin gastrointestinal therapeutic system (GITS) and atenolol on 3 separate measures of target-organ damage--left ventricular mass index (LVMI), carotid intima media thickness (IMT), and urinary albumin excretion (UAE)--in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus and hypertension."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "exact match", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_18343246"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_18343246"], "retrieval_mode": "pubmed_web"}, "verification": {"method": "manual review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "pubmed_web_fallback", "query": "Hipertensi Monitoring monitoring follow-up treatment response labs imaging vital signs disease control therapeutic monitoring adverse effects dose adjustment clinical assessment outcome tracking", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 