{"topic": "Anaphylaxis", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism by which omalizumab reduces the risk of allergic reactions in patients with IgE-mediated food allergies?", "options": {"A": "By binding and neutralizing serum IgE antibodies", "B": "By inhibiting the release of histamine from mast cells", "C": "By blocking the action of leukotrienes on airway smooth muscle", "D": "By suppressing the activity of T cells"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Omalizumab is an anti-IgE monoclonal antibody that reduces the body's sensitivity to allergen exposure by binding and neutralizing serum IgE antibodies, thereby increasing the threshold dose of antigen exposure required to trigger an allergic reaction.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41505160", "title": "Omalizumab: First Approved Anti-IgE Therapy for Multiple Food Allergies", "span_text": "By binding and neutralizing serum IgE antibodies, omalizumab reduces the body's sensitivity to allergen exposure, allowing for an increased threshold dose of antigen exposure before an allergic reaction ensues."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"search_terms": ["omalizumab", "IgE-mediated food allergies", "mechanism of action"], "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41562057", "pubmed_web_41560745", "pubmed_web_41538374", "pubmed_web_41521849", "pubmed_web_41514192", "pubmed_web_41510936", "pubmed_web_41510935", "pubmed_web_41510923", "pubmed_web_41508631", "pubmed_web_41505160", "pubmed_web_41489807", "pubmed_web_41475155", "pubmed_web_41475135", "pubmed_web_41465502", "pubmed_web_41459438", "pubmed_web_41429729", "pubmed_web_41429040", "pubmed_web_41428685", "pubmed_web_41420617", "pubmed_web_41418604", "pubmed_web_41412959", "pubmed_web_41408837", "pubmed_web_41405481", "pubmed_web_41401453", "pubmed_web_41399928", "pubmed_web_41355466", "pubmed_web_41344809", "pubmed_web_41343267", "pubmed_web_41339811", "pubmed_web_41324154"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41510935", "p