{"topic": "Anaphylaxis", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A 10-year-old boy with a history of peanut allergy is considering enrolling in an oral immunotherapy program. What is a potential benefit of adding omalizumab to his treatment regimen?", "options": {"A": "Reduced risk of anaphylaxis during the oral immunotherapy program", "B": "Increased risk of anaphylaxis during the oral immunotherapy program", "C": "No effect on the risk of anaphylaxis during the oral immunotherapy program", "D": "Accelerated progression through the oral immunotherapy program"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Omalizumab is an anti-IgE monoclonal antibody that has been shown to reduce the risk of allergic reactions in patients with IgE-mediated food allergies. By adding omalizumab to the oral immunotherapy program, the risk of anaphylaxis during the program may be reduced.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41505160", "title": "Omalizumab: First Approved Anti-IgE Therapy for Multiple Food Allergies", "span_text": "Anti-IgE therapy with omalizumab has recently been approved as an alternative to OIT to reduce the risk of allergic reaction associated with IgE-mediated food allergy."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41562057", "pubmed_web_41560745", "pubmed_web_41538374", "pubmed_web_41521849", "pubmed_web_41514192", "pubmed_web_41510936", "pubmed_web_41510935", "pubmed_web_41510923", "pubmed_web_41508631", "pubmed_web_41505160", "pubmed_web_41489807", "pubmed_web_41475155", "pubmed_web_41475135", "pubmed_web_41465502", "pubmed_web_41459438", "pubmed_web_41429729", "pubmed_web_41429040", "pubmed_web_41428685", "pubmed_web_41420617", "pubmed_web_41418604", "pubmed_web_41412959", "pubmed_web_41408837", "pubmed_web_41405481", "pubmed_web_41401453", "pubmed_web_41399928", "pubmed_web_41355466", "pubmed_web_41344809", "pubmed_web_41343267", "pubmed_web_41339811", "pubmed_web_41324154"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_we