{"topic": "Anaphylaxis", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A 25-year-old woman with a history of cold urticaria is seeking clearance for scientific diving. What is the primary concern regarding her condition in this context?", "options": {"A": "Risk of anaphylaxis", "B": "Increased risk of decompression sickness", "C": "Impaired lung function due to chronic inflammation", "D": "Enhanced risk of nitrogen narcosis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Cold urticaria is a condition that can lead to anaphylaxis, which is a life-threatening allergic reaction. In the context of scientific diving, the risk of anaphylaxis is a primary concern because it can be fatal if not treated promptly and properly.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41429040", "title": "Cold Urticaria Preventing Clearance For Scientific Diving", "span_text": "CU is an uncommon but under-reported and under-recognized condition with potentially fatal consequences for swimmers and divers. Although symptom management focuses on antihistamines, corticosteroids and omalizumab (Xolair\u00ae) may prove helpful. Nonetheless, the risk of anaphylaxis remains, so CU should be a disqualifying condition for divers."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41562057", "pubmed_web_41560745", "pubmed_web_41538374", "pubmed_web_41521849", "pubmed_web_41514192", "pubmed_web_41510936", "pubmed_web_41510935", "pubmed_web_41510923", "pubmed_web_41508631", "pubmed_web_41505160", "pubmed_web_41489807", "pubmed_web_41475155", "pubmed_web_41475135", "pubmed_web_41465502", "pubmed_web_41459438", "pubmed_web_41429729", "pubmed_web_41429040", "pubmed_web_41428685", "pubmed_web_41420617", "pubmed_web_41418604", "pubmed_web_41412959", "pubmed_web_41408837", "pubmed_web_41405481", "pubmed_web_41401453", "pubmed_web_41399928", "pubmed_web_41355466", "pubmed_web_41344809", "pubmed_web_41343267", "pubmed_web_41339811", "pubmed_web_41324154"