{"topic": "Chronic Liver Disease", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "What is the effect of impaired drug metabolism in chronic liver disease on the extrapyramidal effects of phenothiazines and related compounds?", "options": {"A": "It decreases the risk of extrapyramidal effects", "B": "It increases the risk of extrapyramidal effects", "C": "It has no effect on the risk of extrapyramidal effects", "D": "It is unrelated to the extrapyramidal effects"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Impaired drug metabolism in chronic liver disease can increase the risk of extrapyramidal effects of phenothiazines and related compounds.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0029_4831", "title": "Drug-induced extrapyramidal signs in chronic liver disease--a case report", "span_text": "Impaired drug metabolism can occur in chronic liver disease. A case is reported of extra pyramidal signs occurring in a patient with alcoholic liver disease given the antiemetic Ancoloxin in therapeutic dosage."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_5740", "pubmed23n0040_6690", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4057", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1289", "pubmed23n0013_3263", "Pharmacology_Katzung_295", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5758", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5511", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5779", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4003", "Pharmacology_Katzung_437", "pubmed23n0029_4831", "pubmed23n0011_6620", "pubmed23n0060_214", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6114", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6681", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5765", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3994", "Pharmacology_Katzung_453", "pubmed23n0045_12789", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2935", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6757", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3997", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1457", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5278"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0029_4831", "pubmed23n0011_6620", "pubmed23n0060_214", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6114", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6681", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5765", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3994", "Pharmacology_Katzung_453", "pubmed