{"topic": "Chronic Liver Disease", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A patient with chronic liver disease is being treated with leflunomide for rheumatoid arthritis. What is a potential side effect of this medication that can be reduced by decreasing the dose?", "options": {"A": "Elevation in liver enzymes", "B": "Mild alopecia", "C": "Weight gain", "D": "Increased blood pressure"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Leflunomide can cause elevation in liver enzymes, which can be reduced by decreasing the dose of the medication.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_3997", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Elevation in liver enzymes can occur. Both effects can be reduced by decreasing the dose of leflunomide."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 10, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_2935", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1457", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6757", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3997", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5278"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_3997", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5278", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2935", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1457", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6757"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 5, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Chronic Liver Disease Pharmacology pharmacology drug mechanism indication contraindication adverse effects drug interaction dosage pharmacokinetics pharmacodynamics monitoring toxicity therapeutic target", "evidence_top_k": 20, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 22248.65662499724, "llm_ms": 860.4832919991168, "verification_ms": 816.1322079977253, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Pharmacol