{"topic": "Chronic Liver Disease", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A patient with chronic liver disease and hepatic encephalopathy is being considered for treatment with branched-chain amino acids. What is the primary benefit of this treatment?", "options": {"A": "Improved mortality rates", "B": "Reduced risk of liver transplantation", "C": "Beneficial effect on hepatic encephalopathy", "D": "Increased risk of gastrointestinal side effects"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "Branched-chain amino acids have been shown to have a beneficial effect on hepatic encephalopathy in patients with chronic liver disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41542879", "title": "Branched-chain amino acids for people with cirrhosis and hepatic encephalopathy", "span_text": "The previous version of this updated review meta-analysed data from 16 randomised clinical trials on branched-chain amino acids (BCAAs) versus control interventions, and found that BCAAs did not affect mortality but had a beneficial effect on hepatic encephalopathy."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"search_terms": ["branched-chain amino acids", "hepatic encephalopathy", "chronic liver disease"], "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41581330", "pubmed_web_41580527", "pubmed_web_41578796", "pubmed_web_41578751", "pubmed_web_41573556", "pubmed_web_41571146", "pubmed_web_41566055", "pubmed_web_41563900", "pubmed_web_41560793", "pubmed_web_41559682", "pubmed_web_41555805", "pubmed_web_41553611", "pubmed_web_41553253", "pubmed_web_41550876", "pubmed_web_41548202", "pubmed_web_41545323", "pubmed_web_41543328", "pubmed_web_41543167", "pubmed_web_41542879", "pubmed_web_41539296", "pubmed_web_41535725", "pubmed_web_41530074", "pubmed_web_41529611", "pubmed_web_41528557", "pubmed_web_41527692", "pubmed_web_41524429", "pubmed_web_41516226", "pubmed_web_41516127", "pubmed_web_41516036", "pubmed_web_41515159"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41545323", "pubmed_web_41543328", "pubmed_web_4154