{"topic": "Oncology", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A pediatric patient presents with persistent headache, vomiting, and abnormal neurologic findings. What is the most appropriate initial imaging study to order?", "options": {"A": "Head CT or MRI", "B": "Ultrasound or CT of the abdomen", "C": "Plain radiographs of the bones", "D": "Positron emission tomography (PET) scan"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms of persistent headache, vomiting, and abnormal neurologic findings suggest a possible intracranial lesion, making a head CT or MRI the most appropriate initial imaging study to order.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pediatrics_Nelson_3313", "title": "Pediatrics_Nelson", "span_text": "Persistent headache, vomiting, or abnormal neurologic findings should lead to a head CT or MRI."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_3313"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_3313"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Oncology Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 30, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6890.089041997271, "llm_ms": 1620.1592080033151, "verification_ms": 900.1057919958839, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["Pediatrics_Nelson_3313"], "evidence_reused": false}]}, "timings_ms": {"retrieval": 100.0, "verification": 200.0, "llm": 1620.1592080033151}}}
{"topic": "Osteosarcoma", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is the primary method for establishing a definitive diagnosis of osteosarcoma?", "options": {"A": "Carefully placed needle biopsy", "B": "Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)", "C": "Computed tomography (CT) scan", "D": "Radionuclide bone scanning"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The definitive diagnosis of osteosarcoma is often established by carefully placed needle biopsy, which allows for the presence of osteoid and immunohistochemical analysis to confirm the diagnosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pediatrics_Nelson_3397", "title": "Pediatrics_Nelson", "span_text": "Definitive diagnosis of osteosarcoma often is establishedby carefully placed needle biopsy."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_22493", "pubmed23n0051_4745", "pubmed23n0063_560", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3397", "pubmed23n0006_7907", "pubmed23n0035_5690"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_22493", "pubmed23n0051_4745", "pubmed23n0063_560", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3397", "pubmed23n0006_7907", "pubmed23n0035_5690"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Osteosarcoma Diagnosis diagnosis differential diagnosis signs symptoms screening clinical features presentation diagnostic criteria workup evaluation diagnostic test laboratory findings imaging", "evidence_top_k": 30, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 7327.229750000697, "llm_ms": 1261.9917080010055, "verification_ms": 2834.81966600084, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": false, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 0.0}, "status_counts": {"OK": 1, "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 0, "FAILED_VERIFICATION": 0}, "failed_checks": [], "failed_checks_all": [], "evidence_doc_ids_used": ["pubmed23n0044_224