{"topic": "Osteosarcoma", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A patient with a history of radiotherapy presents with a new malignant tumor within the irradiated area. What type of sarcoma is this patient at risk for developing, which can mimic osteosarcoma in its clinical and radiologic features?", "options": {"A": "Post-radiation sarcoma", "B": "Ewing sarcoma", "C": "Chondrosarcoma", "D": "Clear cell myoepithelial carcinoma"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Post-radiation sarcoma is a rare but severe complication following radiotherapy, and it can mimic osteosarcoma in its clinical and radiologic features.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41550183", "title": "A retrospective study of post-radiation sarcoma from three institutions in Japan with a review of the literature", "span_text": "Post-radiation sarcoma is a malignant tumor arising within irradiated areas after a latency period, histologically different from the primary tumor."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41582380", "pubmed_web_41562936", "pubmed_web_41562935", "pubmed_web_41558915", "pubmed_web_41552210", "pubmed_web_41550183", "pubmed_web_41547692", "pubmed_web_41539257", "pubmed_web_41534128", "pubmed_web_41518355", "pubmed_web_41518041", "pubmed_web_41517779", "pubmed_web_41517748", "pubmed_web_41517690", "pubmed_web_41509083", "pubmed_web_41502512", "pubmed_web_41501582", "pubmed_web_41500705", "pubmed_web_41494974", "pubmed_web_41492046", "pubmed_web_41490637", "pubmed_web_41487843", "pubmed_web_41487033", "pubmed_web_41485474", "pubmed_web_41481491", "pubmed_web_41481339", "pubmed_web_41479782", "pubmed_web_41479597", "pubmed_web_41479192", "pubmed_web_41479051"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41552210", "pubmed_web_41550183", "pubmed_web_41547692", "pubmed_web_41539257", "pubmed_web_41534128", "pubmed_web_41518355", "pubmed_web_41518041", "pubmed_web_41517779", "pubmed_web_41517748", "pubmed_web_41517690", "pubmed_we