{"topic": "Neuroblastoma", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "A pediatric patient with a history of high-risk neuroblastoma is being followed up for potential long-term complications. What is the most common type of liver abnormality observed in such patients?", "options": {"A": "Focal liver lesions", "B": "Diffuse parenchymal inhomogeneity", "C": "Liver cysts", "D": "Hepatic calcifications"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The most common type of liver abnormality observed in patients with a history of high-risk neuroblastoma is diffuse parenchymal inhomogeneity, which is often seen on imaging studies.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41518108", "title": "Liver-Related Late Effects in Long-Term Survivors of High-Risk Neuroblastoma: Insights From a Comprehensive Prospective Follow-Up Study", "span_text": "Diffuse parenchymal inhomogeneity was observed in 36 patients out of 47 (76%)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41582754", "pubmed_web_41580800", "pubmed_web_41569474", "pubmed_web_41546455", "pubmed_web_41528631", "pubmed_web_41527496", "pubmed_web_41523735", "pubmed_web_41520034", "pubmed_web_41519468", "pubmed_web_41518108", "pubmed_web_41518041", "pubmed_web_41518036", "pubmed_web_41517599", "pubmed_web_41510400", "pubmed_web_41504043", "pubmed_web_41494662", "pubmed_web_41494248", "pubmed_web_41490991", "pubmed_web_41490581", "pubmed_web_41485549", "pubmed_web_41481409", "pubmed_web_41480378", "pubmed_web_41478971", "pubmed_web_41478460", "pubmed_web_41474309", "pubmed_web_41471039", "pubmed_web_41467146", "pubmed_web_41463147", "pubmed_web_41462603", "pubmed_web_41461538"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41519468", "pubmed_web_41518108", "pubmed_web_41518036", "pubmed_web_41517599", "pubmed_web_41510400", "pubmed_web_41504043", "pubmed_web_41494662", "pubmed_web_41494248", "pubmed_web_41490991", "pubmed_web_41490581", "pubmed_web_41485549", "pubmed_web_41481409", "pubmed_web_41