{"topic": "Neuroblastoma", "competency": "Screening", "stem": "What is the primary role of surgery in the management of neuroblastoma in children?", "options": {"A": "To reduce the risk of recurrence", "B": "To play a pivotal role in the management", "C": "To improve the quality of life", "D": "To increase the survival rate"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Surgery plays a pivotal role in the management of neuroblastoma in children, as it is often used to remove the tumor and improve the chances of survival.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41510400", "title": "Diagnosis and management of neuroblastoma in children", "span_text": "Neuroblastoma constitutes the most common extracranial solid tumor encountered in children under 5 years of age. The clinical course is highly variable, ranging from spontaneous tumor regression in very young infants to a highly aggressive disease in older children. 5-year survival of > 90% in low and intermediate-risk disease compares to < 60% in those with high-risk neuroblastoma despite recent genetic and clinical advances. Treatment strategies vary significantly in intensity depending on the aggressiveness of disease with surgery playing a pivotal role in the management."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41582754", "pubmed_web_41580800", "pubmed_web_41569474", "pubmed_web_41546455", "pubmed_web_41528631", "pubmed_web_41527496", "pubmed_web_41523735", "pubmed_web_41520034", "pubmed_web_41519468", "pubmed_web_41518108", "pubmed_web_41518041", "pubmed_web_41518036", "pubmed_web_41517599", "pubmed_web_41510400", "pubmed_web_41504043", "pubmed_web_41494662", "pubmed_web_41494248", "pubmed_web_41490991", "pubmed_web_41490581", "pubmed_web_41485549", "pubmed_web_41481409", "pubmed_web_41480378", "pubmed_web_41478971", "pubmed_web_41478460", "pubmed_web_41474309", "pubmed_web_41471039", "pubmed_web_41467146", "pubmed_web_41463147", "pubmed_web_41462603", "pubmed_web_