{"topic": "Glioma", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What molecular mechanism is involved in the development and progression of diffuse midline glioma?", "options": {"A": "Histone H3 lysine 27 mutation", "B": "Wnt/\u03b2-catenin/NFATC2 pathway", "C": "CCL5/CCR5-mediated glioma stem cell maintenance", "D": "NSUN5 RNA methyltransferase"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The histone H3 lysine 27 mutation plays a pivotal role in the development and progression of diffuse midline glioma by disrupting histone methylation and acetylation, leading to widespread gene expression abnormalities, tumor aggressiveness, and treatment resistance.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41574724", "title": "Epigenetic mechanisms and therapeutic advances in diffuse midline glioma (Review)", "span_text": "A series of studies have demonstrated that histone modifications, particularly the histone H3 lysine 27 (H3K27)M mutation, play a pivotal role in the development and progression of DMG."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41582518", "pubmed_web_41578499", "pubmed_web_41578162", "pubmed_web_41575610", "pubmed_web_41575548", "pubmed_web_41574724", "pubmed_web_41570802", "pubmed_web_41562896", "pubmed_web_41562049", "pubmed_web_41558658", "pubmed_web_41555554", "pubmed_web_41554079", "pubmed_web_41553075", "pubmed_web_41546701", "pubmed_web_41545304", "pubmed_web_41545301", "pubmed_web_41543195", "pubmed_web_41539178", "pubmed_web_41538469", "pubmed_web_41537310", "pubmed_web_41536151", "pubmed_web_41533777", "pubmed_web_41533587", "pubmed_web_41533333", "pubmed_web_41530397", "pubmed_web_41530365", "pubmed_web_41529664", "pubmed_web_41527794", "pubmed_web_41522810", "pubmed_web_41521799"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41578162", "pubmed_web_41575610", "pubmed_web_41575548", "pubmed_web_41574724", "pubmed_web_41570802", "pubmed_web_41562896", "pubmed_web_41562049", "pubmed_web_41558658", "pubmed_web_41555554", "p