{"topic": "Glioma", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What type of cells have been found to promote glioblastoma progression through CCL5/CCR5-mediated glioma stem cell maintenance?", "options": {"A": "Reactive oligodendrocytes", "B": "Glioma stem cells", "C": "Immune cells", "D": "Neurons"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Reactive oligodendrocytes have been found to secrete pro-tumorigenic cytokines, notably CCL5, that promote GBM tumor cell growth through CCR5 signaling.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41570802", "title": "Reactive oligodendrocytes promote glioblastoma progression through CCL5/CCR5-mediated glioma stem cell maintenance", "span_text": "GBM cells recruit OLs to the tumor border via fractalkine (i.e., CX3CL1/CX3CR1) signaling. A pan-disease human OL meta-atlas and syngeneic mouse models reveal an interferon (IFN)-induced reactive OL state, akin to those seen in demyelinating inflammatory and traumatic injury, which is enriched in central nervous system malignancies."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41582518", "pubmed_web_41578499", "pubmed_web_41578162", "pubmed_web_41575610", "pubmed_web_41575548", "pubmed_web_41574724", "pubmed_web_41570802", "pubmed_web_41562896", "pubmed_web_41562049", "pubmed_web_41558658", "pubmed_web_41555554", "pubmed_web_41554079", "pubmed_web_41553075", "pubmed_web_41546701", "pubmed_web_41545304", "pubmed_web_41545301", "pubmed_web_41543195", "pubmed_web_41539178", "pubmed_web_41538469", "pubmed_web_41537310", "pubmed_web_41536151", "pubmed_web_41533777", "pubmed_web_41533587", "pubmed_web_41533333", "pubmed_web_41530397", "pubmed_web_41530365", "pubmed_web_41529664", "pubmed_web_41527794", "pubmed_web_41522810", "pubmed_web_41521799"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41575548", "pubmed_web_41574724", "pubmed_web_41570802", "pubmed_web_41562896", "pubmed_web_41562049", "pubmed_web_41558658", "pubmed_web_41555554", "pubmed_web_41554079", "pub