{"topic": "Sinusitis", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 35-year-old patient presents with persistent symptoms of purulent nasal discharge, nasal obstruction, and facial pain lasting for 12 days. What is the most likely diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "Acute bacterial sinusitis", "B": "Viral rhinosinusitis", "C": "Chronic sinusitis", "D": "Allergic rhinitis"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms of purulent nasal discharge, nasal obstruction, and facial pain lasting for 12 days are consistent with acute bacterial sinusitis. According to expert panels, this diagnosis is reserved for patients with persistent symptoms lasting more than 10 days in adults, accompanied by the three cardinal signs.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "InternalMed_Harrison_2580", "title": "InternalMed_Harrison", "span_text": "Because acute bacterial sinusitis is uncommon in patients whose symptoms have lasted <10 days, expert panels now recommend reserving this diagnosis for patients with \u201cpersistent\u201d symptoms (i.e., symptoms lasting >10 days in adults or >10\u201314 days in children) accompanied by the three cardinal signs of purulent nasal discharge, nasal obstruction, and facial pain (Table 44-1)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_2580", "pubmed23n0057_21146", "pubmed23n0051_2934", "pubmed23n0051_2935", "pubmed23n0063_18953", "pubmed23n0047_8920", "pubmed23n0060_8214", "Surgery_Schwartz_4216", "pubmed23n0034_6663", "InternalMed_Harrison_1430", "pubmed23n0058_9253", "pubmed23n0051_21563", "InternalMed_Harrison_11639"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["InternalMed_Harrison_2580", "pubmed23n0057_21146", "pubmed23n0051_2934", "pubmed23n0051_2935", "pubmed23n0063_18953", "pubmed23n0047_8920", "pubmed23n0060_8214", "Surgery_Schwartz_4216", "pubmed23n0034_6663", "InternalMed_Harrison_1430", "pubmed23n0058_9253", "pubmed23n0051_21563", "InternalMed_Harrison_11639"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "ver