{"topic": "Asthma", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the first-line therapy for acute asthma attacks?", "options": {"A": "Short-acting inhaled \u03b22-agonists", "B": "Systemic corticosteroids", "C": "Ipratropium", "D": "Magnesium"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Short-acting inhaled \u03b22-agonists are the first-line therapy for acute asthma attacks because they rapidly relax smooth muscle in the airways and are effective for up to 6 hours.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "First_Aid_Step2_1063", "title": "First_Aid_Step2", "span_text": "First_Aid_Step2 TABLE 2.15-3. Acute: O2, bronchodilating agents (short-acting inhaled \u03b22-agonists are f rst-line therapy), ipratropium (never use alone for asthma), systemic corticosteroids, magnesium (for severe exacerbations)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["First_Aid_Step2_1063", "Gynecology_Novak_3798", "pubmed23n0014_2698", "pubmed23n0045_10934", "pubmed23n0049_2331", "pubmed23n0058_459", "Gynecology_Novak_3795", "pubmed23n0040_8607", "pubmed23n0060_3301", "pubmed23n0027_11294", "pubmed23n0060_3302", "pubmed23n0028_10431", "pubmed23n0045_4161", "pubmed23n0051_21249", "pubmed23n0056_1175", "pubmed23n0060_10873", "pubmed23n0027_4029", "pubmed23n0060_1506", "InternalMed_Harrison_20148", "First_Aid_Step2_1061", "pubmed23n0014_8318", "pubmed23n0044_9426", "pubmed23n0046_5572", "pubmed23n0014_2828", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2110", "pubmed23n0001_10283", "pubmed23n0036_6908", "pubmed23n0045_11357", "pubmed23n0050_2993", "pubmed23n0044_15835", "pubmed23n0046_8215", "pubmed23n0048_2494", "pubmed23n0049_8549", "pubmed23n0056_9098", "pubmed23n0061_12104", "pubmed23n0018_6146", "pubmed23n0062_7993", "pubmed23n0044_16056", "pubmed23n0054_18928", "pubmed23n0056_3085", "pubmed23n0044_4340", "pubmed23n0054_5551", "Pediatrics_Nelson_1804", "pubmed23n0048_15488", "pubmed23n0050_18176", "pubmed23n0032_10564", "pubmed23n0058_9876", "pubmed23n0045_4558", "pubmed23n0053_6724", "