{"topic": "Asthma", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "A patient with chronic asthma experiences symptoms more than 4-6 times a week. What should be initiated in addition to inhaled short acting beta 2-agonists as needed?", "options": {"A": "Regular inhalative antiinflammatory regimen", "B": "Oral corticosteroids", "C": "Intravenous beta 2-agonists", "D": "Theophylline"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "For patients with chronic asthma who experience symptoms more than 4-6 times a week, a regular inhalative antiinflammatory regimen should be initiated in addition to inhaled short acting beta 2-agonists as needed. This approach helps to control inflammation and reduce airway hyperresponsiveness, thereby stabilizing the disease.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0045_3533", "title": "[Asthma therapy: are bronchodilators obsolete?]", "span_text": "If asthma symptoms occur more than 4-6 times a week a regular inhalative antiinflammatory regimen should be initiated (e.g. inhalative corticosteroids b.i.d.)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2023-02-20T14:30:00Z", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0045_3533", "pubmed23n0062_6534", "pubmed23n0053_15120", "pubmed23n0056_4794", "pubmed23n0050_8988"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0050_8988", "pubmed23n0045_3533", "pubmed23n0062_6534", "pubmed23n0053_15120", "pubmed23n0056_4794"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": "2023-02-20T14:35:00Z", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Asthma Treatment treatment therapy management drug dosage medication pharmacotherapy first-line second-line guideline intervention acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 30, "retrieval_ms": 12755.90070799808, "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pubmed_web": {"attempted": true, "docs": 0, "runtime_ms": 7271.283583002514}, "status_counts": {"INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE": 1}, "failed_checks": ["insuffic