{"topic": "Appendicitis", "competency": "Clinical Practice", "stem": "A 12-day-old premature infant presents with signs of intestinal obstruction and abdominal tenderness. What is the most likely cause of these symptoms?", "options": {"A": "Intussusception", "B": "Incarcerated inguinal hernia with appendicitis", "C": "Necrotizing enterocolitis", "D": "Meconium ileus"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Neonatal appendicitis is a rare condition, and its presentation can be atypical. The symptoms of intestinal obstruction and abdominal tenderness in a premature infant could be indicative of an incarcerated inguinal hernia with appendicitis, which is a known cause of appendicitis in neonates.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0022_4754", "title": "Neonatal appendicitis: ischemic infarction in incarcerated inguinal hernia", "span_text": "A premature 12-day-old infant with ischemic infarction of the appendix due to hernial incarceration is presented."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0058_9693", "pubmed23n0042_9096", "pubmed23n0033_3448", "pubmed23n0048_15293", "pubmed23n0042_9639", "pubmed23n0022_4754", "pubmed23n0046_12291", "pubmed23n0052_4635", "pubmed23n0013_11618", "Obstentrics_Williams_6431", "pubmed23n0063_345", "pubmed23n0016_13617", "pubmed23n0031_10869", "pubmed23n0053_1397", "Surgery_Schwartz_8858", "pubmed23n0041_8494", "pubmed23n0028_13514", "pubmed23n0059_17717", "pubmed23n0052_19650", "pubmed23n0014_910", "pubmed23n0045_5749", "pubmed23n0016_8223", "pubmed23n0006_13072", "pubmed23n0046_12653", "pubmed23n0013_2579", "pubmed23n0014_10490", "pubmed23n0016_5940", "pubmed23n0041_11346", "pubmed23n0060_11778", "pubmed23n0028_12230", "pubmed23n0059_13611", "pubmed23n0047_18233", "pubmed23n0050_1521", "pubmed23n0054_8565", "pubmed23n0017_7271", "pubmed23n0024_8310", "pubmed23n0032_8174", "pubmed23n0053_10853", "pubmed23n0048_16892", "pubmed23n0062_20088", "pubmed23n0017_6722", "Surgery_Schwartz_88