{"topic": "Hypertension", "competency": "treatment", "stem": "A 58-year-old man with primary bilateral macronodular adrenocortical disease and concomitant Cushing syndrome and primary aldosteronism is found to have hypertension. What is the most appropriate initial step in managing his hypertension?", "options": {"A": "Laparoscopic left adrenalectomy", "B": "Medication to control aldosterone secretion", "C": "Medication to control cortisol secretion", "D": "Combined medication to control both aldosterone and cortisol secretion"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The patient's hypertension is likely caused by the excess aldosterone secretion from the left adrenal gland. Laparoscopic left adrenalectomy is the most appropriate initial step in managing his hypertension as it directly addresses the source of the excess aldosterone.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41631058", "title": "Primary Bilateral Macronodular Adrenocortical Disease With Concomitant Cushing Syndrome and Primary Aldosteronism Harboring Distinct ARMC5 Mutations in Individual Nodules", "span_text": "The patient underwent laparoscopic left adrenalectomy. Gross and histopathological examination demonstrated multiple macronodular lesions without evidence of malignancy."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2024-02-20T14:30:00Z", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41631765", "pubmed_web_41631546", "pubmed_web_41631433", "pubmed_web_41631386", "pubmed_web_41631382", "pubmed_web_41631260", "pubmed_web_41631227", "pubmed_web_41631086", "pubmed_web_41631080", "pubmed_web_41631058", "pubmed_web_41631051", "pubmed_web_41631049", "pubmed_web_41630996", "pubmed_web_41630985", "pubmed_web_41630895", "pubmed_web_41630839", "pubmed_web_41630797", "pubmed_web_41630741", "pubmed_web_41630730", "pubmed_web_41630678", "pubmed_web_41630155", "pubmed_web_41630035", "pubmed_web_41629821", "pubmed_web_41629746", "pubmed_web_41629686", "pubmed_web_41629568", "pubmed_web_41629567", "pubmed_web