{"topic": "Tuberculosis", "competency": "Pathology", "stem": "A patient presents with a lung mass and symptoms resembling a 'flulike' syndrome. Histopathological examination reveals granulomas with central necrosis and giant cells. What is the most likely diagnosis?", "options": {"A": "Sarcoidosis", "B": "Tuberculosis", "C": "Foreign body reaction", "D": "Rheumatoid nodule"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The presence of granulomas with central necrosis and giant cells is characteristic of tuberculosis. The clinical symptoms and signs, such as a lung mass and 'flulike' syndrome, also support this diagnosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pathology_Robbins_3234", "title": "Pathology_Robbins", "span_text": "The primary pulmonary nodules, composed of aggregates of macrophages filled with organisms, are associated with similar lesions in the regional lymph nodes. These lesions evolve into small granulomas complete with giant cells and may develop central necrosis and later fibrosis and calcification."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pathology_Robbins_3234", "Pathology_Robbins_504", "Pathology_Robbins_4694", "Pathology_Robbins_3229", "InternalMed_Harrison_11164", "Pathology_Robbins_3194", "Pediatrics_Nelson_3366", "Pathology_Robbins_4137", "Pathology_Robbins_3749", "Pathology_Robbins_2161", "Pathology_Robbins_4790", "InternalMed_Harrison_20260", "Pathology_Robbins_2996", "InternalMed_Harrison_13295", "Pathology_Robbins_4697", "Pathology_Robbins_3192", "pubmed23n0004_11552", "Pathology_Robbins_2782", "Pathology_Robbins_4136", "Pathology_Robbins_502", "pubmed23n0044_2216", "Pathology_Robbins_3206", "Pathology_Robbins_2179", "Pathology_Robbins_5070", "InternalMed_Harrison_15921", "pubmed23n0043_4481", "pubmed23n0063_19075", "Pathology_Robbins_4199"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pathology_Robbins_3234", "Pathology_Robbins_504", "Pathology_Robbins_4694", "Pathology_Robbins_3229", "InternalMed_Harrison_11164", "Pathology_Rob