{"topic": "Anemia", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A patient with microcytic hypochromic anemia and elevated red cell distribution width is most likely to have which of the following conditions?", "options": {"A": "Iron deficiency anemia", "B": "Alpha-thalassemia", "C": "Beta-thalassemia", "D": "Sideroblastic anemia"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The patient's presentation of microcytic hypochromic anemia and elevated red cell distribution width, along with the absence of hepatosplenomegaly, iron overload, or gallstones, is consistent with alpha-thalassemia.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41634277", "title": "Many faces of non\u2011deletional \u03b1\u2011thalassaemia variants in neonate and early childhood", "span_text": "After the first few months of life, patients typically exhibit mild hypochromic microcytic anemia, elevated red cell distribution width, and reticulocytosis, with basophilic stippling more prominent in Hb CS."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41635834", "pubmed_web_41635391", "pubmed_web_41635378", "pubmed_web_41635041", "pubmed_web_41634502", "pubmed_web_41634406", "pubmed_web_41634383", "pubmed_web_41634277", "pubmed_web_41633330", "pubmed_web_41632990", "pubmed_web_41632717", "pubmed_web_41632448", "pubmed_web_41631231", "pubmed_web_41631168", "pubmed_web_41631088", "pubmed_web_41630562", "pubmed_web_41630338", "pubmed_web_41630307", "pubmed_web_41630156", "pubmed_web_41629758", "pubmed_web_41629110", "pubmed_web_41628927", "pubmed_web_41628562", "pubmed_web_41627676", "pubmed_web_41627544", "pubmed_web_41626911", "pubmed_web_41626659", "pubmed_web_41626634", "pubmed_web_41626618"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41635041", "pubmed_web_41634502", "pubmed_web_41634406", "pubmed_web_41634383", "pubmed_web_41634277", "pubmed_web_41633330", "pubmed_web_41632990", "pubmed_web_41632717", "pubmed_web_41632448", "pubmed_web_41631231", "pubmed_web_41631168", "pubme