{"topic": "Anemia", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "A 66-year-old male patient presents with significantly prolonged activated partial thromboplastin time and microcytic hypochromic anemia. Which of the following is the most likely underlying cause of his condition?", "options": {"A": "Iron deficiency anemia", "B": "High molecular weight kininogen deficiency", "C": "Vitamin B12 deficiency anemia", "D": "Thalassemia"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The patient's presentation of significantly prolonged activated partial thromboplastin time and microcytic hypochromic anemia is consistent with high molecular weight kininogen deficiency, a rare autosomal recessive disorder caused by mutations in the KNG1 gene.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41634406", "title": "Activated partial thromboplastin time prolongation without hemorrhagic dienhesis: a study of a chinese family coexisting with hereditary KNG1 p.Arg240 mutation and --SEA/\u03b1\u03b1 genotype thalassemia", "span_text": "High molecular weight kininogen (HK) deficiency is a rare autosomal recessive disorder caused by mutations in the KNG1 gene. This study reports a 66-year-old male Chinese patient who presented with significantly prolonged activated partial thromboplastin time (aPTT) and microcytic hypochromic anemia."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41635834", "pubmed_web_41635391", "pubmed_web_41635378", "pubmed_web_41635041", "pubmed_web_41634502", "pubmed_web_41634406", "pubmed_web_41634383", "pubmed_web_41634277", "pubmed_web_41633330", "pubmed_web_41632990", "pubmed_web_41632717", "pubmed_web_41632448", "pubmed_web_41631231", "pubmed_web_41631168", "pubmed_web_41631088", "pubmed_web_41630562", "pubmed_web_41630338", "pubmed_web_41630307", "pubmed_web_41630156", "pubmed_web_41629758", "pubmed_web_41629110", "pubmed_web_41628927", "pubmed_web_41628562", "pubmed_web_41627676", "pubmed_web_41627544", "pubmed_web_41626911", "pubm