{"topic": "AIDS", "competency": "Basic Sciences", "stem": "What is the significance of measuring myelin basic protein in the cerebrospinal fluid of patients with AIDS dementia complex?", "options": {"A": "To diagnose opportunistic infections", "B": "To assess the degree of white matter destruction", "C": "To monitor the progression of HIV infection", "D": "To evaluate the effectiveness of antiretroviral therapy"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Measuring myelin basic protein in the cerebrospinal fluid can help assess the degree of white matter destruction in patients with AIDS dementia complex, which can be a predictive marker of myelin injury and neurologic damage.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0045_18621", "title": "Cerebrospinal fluid myelin basic protein as predictive marker of demyelination in AIDS dementia complex", "span_text": "Myelin basic protein (MBP) was measured in cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) of patients with acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS) dementia complex (ADC) in order to investigate the degree of white matter destruction."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_18380", "pubmed23n0051_13265", "pubmed23n0003_8896", "pubmed23n0024_1420", "pubmed23n0045_18621", "pubmed23n0044_8599", "pubmed23n0055_21666", "pubmed23n0022_8476", "pubmed23n0054_2473", "pubmed23n0057_14284", "pubmed23n0042_2240", "pubmed23n0024_4857"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0044_8599", "pubmed23n0055_21666", "pubmed23n0022_8476", "pubmed23n0054_2473", "pubmed23n0057_14284", "pubmed23n0042_2240", "pubmed23n0024_4857", "pubmed23n0049_18380", "pubmed23n0051_13265", "pubmed23n0003_8896", "pubmed23n0024_1420", "pubmed23n0045_18621"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 200, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "AIDS Basic Sciences", "evidence_top_k": 30, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "