{"topic": "AIDS", "competency": "Basic Sciences", "stem": "What is a primary function of the PR enzyme in the viral life cycle of HIV?", "options": {"A": "To cleave various polyproteins into individual components necessary for the formation of mature virions", "B": "To integrate viral DNA into the host genome", "C": "To transcribe viral RNA into host mRNA", "D": "To replicate viral particles"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The PR enzyme is essential for the viral life cycle, and its primary function is to cleave various polyproteins into individual components necessary for the formation of mature, infectious virions.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41555778", "title": "Advancements in development of novel class of HIV protease inhibitors", "span_text": "The PR enzyme is essential for the viral life cycle, as it cleaves various polyproteins into the individual components necessary for the formation of mature, infectious virions."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41632773", "pubmed_web_41627977", "pubmed_web_41626465", "pubmed_web_41619570", "pubmed_web_41618122", "pubmed_web_41608982", "pubmed_web_41601739", "pubmed_web_41588291", "pubmed_web_41576936", "pubmed_web_41574522", "pubmed_web_41555778", "pubmed_web_41554067", "pubmed_web_41532226", "pubmed_web_41525285", "pubmed_web_41513998", "pubmed_web_41503919", "pubmed_web_41501180", "pubmed_web_41492112", "pubmed_web_41480960", "pubmed_web_41476936", "pubmed_web_41467717", "pubmed_web_41467175", "pubmed_web_41457710", "pubmed_web_41449770", "pubmed_web_41449479", "pubmed_web_41449455", "pubmed_web_41448408", "pubmed_web_41446285", "pubmed_web_41425620", "pubmed_web_41419776"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41574522", "pubmed_web_41555778", "pubmed_web_41554067", "pubmed_web_41532226", "pubmed_web_41525285", "pubmed_web_41513998", "pubmed_web_41503919", "pubmed_web_41501180", "pubmed_web_41492112", "pubmed_web_41480960", "pubmed_web_