{"topic": "Migraine", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "What is the recommended approach for treating chronic migraine in patients with comorbid endometriosis?", "options": {"A": "Combined hormonal contraceptives as first-line treatment", "B": "Progestins as first-line treatment due to better tolerability and potential improvement in migraine outcomes", "C": "Gonadotropin-releasing hormone agonists as first-line treatment", "D": "Avoiding hormonal therapies altogether"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Progestins are generally considered to have better tolerability and may improve migraine outcomes, despite potential side effects such as breakthrough bleeding or mood changes, making them a preferable first-line option for treating chronic migraine in patients with comorbid endometriosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41630559", "title": "Safety and efficacy of hormonal therapies used to treat endometriosis in women suffering migraine", "span_text": "Progestins generally show better tolerability and may improve migraine outcomes, despite the occurrence of breakthrough bleeding or mood changes."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "query": "migraine treatment endometriosis", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41634591", "pubmed_web_41633219", "pubmed_web_41630559", "pubmed_web_41630419", "pubmed_web_41630307", "pubmed_web_41630047", "pubmed_web_41629775", "pubmed_web_41628620", "pubmed_web_41628212", "pubmed_web_41628210", "pubmed_web_41628204", "pubmed_web_41627537", "pubmed_web_41626588", "pubmed_web_41623789", "pubmed_web_41620660", "pubmed_web_41619552", "pubmed_web_41619056", "pubmed_web_41616910", "pubmed_web_41615317", "pubmed_web_41615311", "pubmed_web_41615244", "pubmed_web_41615180", "pubmed_web_41614252", "pubmed_web_41614018", "pubmed_web_41613259", "pubmed_web_41613184", "pubmed_web_41613173", "pubmed_web_41612541", "pubmed_web_41609368", "pubmed_web_41609130"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_4