{"topic": "Migraine", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "A patient with chronic migraine is not responding to single calcitonin gene-related peptide therapy. What alternative treatment approach may provide increased synergistic relief?", "options": {"A": "Combining small-molecule antagonists and ligand monoclonal antibodies", "B": "Switching to a different single calcitonin gene-related peptide inhibitor", "C": "Adding a neuromodulation device", "D": "Increasing the dose of the current medication"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Dual calcitonin gene-related peptide therapy, which involves combining small-molecule antagonists and ligand monoclonal antibodies, may provide increased synergistic relief for patients with chronic migraine who are not responding to single calcitonin gene-related peptide therapy.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41628212", "title": "Real-World Insights into Dual Calcitonin Gene-Related Peptide (CGRP) Therapies for Chronic Migraine: A Retrospective Review", "span_text": "Dual-CGRP therapy reduced headache severity by 20%, in contrast to the 10% reduction seen with mono-CGRP therapy (P = 0.039)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41634591", "pubmed_web_41633219", "pubmed_web_41630559", "pubmed_web_41630419", "pubmed_web_41630307", "pubmed_web_41630047", "pubmed_web_41629775", "pubmed_web_41628620", "pubmed_web_41628212", "pubmed_web_41628210", "pubmed_web_41628204", "pubmed_web_41627537", "pubmed_web_41626588", "pubmed_web_41623789", "pubmed_web_41620660", "pubmed_web_41619552", "pubmed_web_41619056", "pubmed_web_41616910", "pubmed_web_41615317", "pubmed_web_41615311", "pubmed_web_41615244", "pubmed_web_41615180", "pubmed_web_41614252", "pubmed_web_41614018", "pubmed_web_41613259", "pubmed_web_41613184", "pubmed_web_41613173", "pubmed_web_41612541", "pubmed_web_41609368", "pubmed_web_41609130"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41630307", "pubmed_web_41630047", "p