{"topic": "Hypertension", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is the most sensitive noninvasive diagnostic test for detecting renal artery stenosis in patients with suspected renovascular hypertension?", "options": {"A": "Doppler ultrasonography", "B": "Magnetic resonance imaging", "C": "Captopril test", "D": "Renography with technetium-99m diethylene triamine penta-acetic acid"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Doppler ultrasonography has been shown to have a high sensitivity for detecting renal artery stenosis, making it a useful noninvasive diagnostic test for suspected renovascular hypertension.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_7473", "title": "[Doppler ultrasound in the diagnosis of renal artery stenosis in hypertensive patients: a prospective study]", "span_text": "Duplex scanning had a sensitivity of 90% and specificity of 96% to detect renal artery stenosis. Diagnostic accuracy was 93% for 50% to 60% stenosis and 100% for occlusion or 60% to 99% renal artery stenosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"method": "keyword search", "query": "renovascular hypertension diagnosis", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0064_316", "pubmed23n0048_14554", "pubmed23n0015_992", "pubmed23n0048_4961", "pubmed23n0063_7473", "pubmed23n0044_5818", "InternalMed_Harrison_23259", "InternalMed_Harrison_26302", "Gynecology_Novak_5295", "pubmed23n0057_22678", "pubmed23n0058_7199", "pubmed23n0008_12394"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0064_316", "pubmed23n0048_14554", "pubmed23n0015_992", "pubmed23n0048_4961", "pubmed23n0063_7473", "pubmed23n0044_5818", "InternalMed_Harrison_23259", "InternalMed_Harrison_26302", "Gynecology_Novak_5295", "pubmed23n0057_22678", "pubmed23n0058_7199", "pubmed23n0008_12394"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"method": "expert review", "result": "verified", "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Hypertension Diagnosis di