{"topic": "Hypertension", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "Which of the following social determinants of health is significantly associated with an increased risk of developing hypertension among adult US women?", "options": {"A": "Food insecurity", "B": "Housing insecurity", "C": "Transportation insecurity", "D": "All of the above"}, "answer_key": "D", "explanation": "The correct answer is supported by evidence that all three types of insecurity (food, housing, and transportation) are significantly associated with chronic conditions, including hypertension, among adult US women.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41636461", "title": "Investigating the Relationship Between Food, Housing, and Transportation Insecurity and Chronic Disease Among US Women Using Nationally Representative Data", "span_text": "Approximately 27% of the sample experienced all three forms of insecurity concurrently. Women with anxiety or depression had elevated levels of food, housing, and transportation insecurity (11.3%, 7.4%, 7.5%) than those with other chronic conditions. Adjusted models indicated that all three types of insecurity were significantly associated with chronic conditions."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2023-02-20T14:30:00Z", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41637013", "pubmed_web_41636996", "pubmed_web_41636870", "pubmed_web_41636707", "pubmed_web_41636461", "pubmed_web_41636435", "pubmed_web_41636195", "pubmed_web_41635670", "pubmed_web_41635579", "pubmed_web_41635567", "pubmed_web_41635563", "pubmed_web_41635378", "pubmed_web_41635343", "pubmed_web_41635286", "pubmed_web_41634178", "pubmed_web_41633645", "pubmed_web_41633620", "pubmed_web_41633425", "pubmed_web_41633376", "pubmed_web_41632932", "pubmed_web_41632717", "pubmed_web_41632705", "pubmed_web_41632493", "pubmed_web_41632337", "pubmed_web_41632311", "pubmed_web_41632160", "pubmed_web_41632142", "pubmed_web_41631990", "pubmed_web_41631433", "pubmed_web_41631227"], "evidence_