{"topic": "Hypertension", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is the significance of diurnal variation in umbilical artery Doppler measurements in pregnancies complicated by hypertensive disorders?", "options": {"A": "It has no significant impact on fetal outcomes", "B": "It is associated with higher rates of cesarean delivery and neonatal intensive care unit admission", "C": "It is only relevant in normotensive pregnancies", "D": "It is not a significant factor in preeclampsia"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Diurnal variation in umbilical artery Doppler measurements is significant in pregnancies complicated by hypertensive disorders, as it is associated with higher rates of cesarean delivery and neonatal intensive care unit admission.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41633376", "title": "Impact of Diurnal Variation on Umbilical Artery Doppler Measurements in Pregnancies Complicated by Hypertensive Disorders", "span_text": "Notably, in the preeclampsia subgroup, the morning S/D values (3.3\u00b11.1 vs. 2.3\u00b10.5, p<0.001) were found to reach the highest levels. Regarding neonatal outcomes, the study group demonstrated significantly higher rates of cesarean delivery (71.7% vs. 33.3%, p<0.001) and neonatal intensive care unit admission (36.7% vs. 6.7%, p<0.001), while birth weight was significantly lower (2724.9\u00b1759.1 g vs. 3241.1\u00b1422.7 g, p<0.001)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41637013", "pubmed_web_41636996", "pubmed_web_41636870", "pubmed_web_41636707", "pubmed_web_41636461", "pubmed_web_41636435", "pubmed_web_41636195", "pubmed_web_41635670", "pubmed_web_41635579", "pubmed_web_41635567", "pubmed_web_41635563", "pubmed_web_41635378", "pubmed_web_41635343", "pubmed_web_41635286", "pubmed_web_41634178", "pubmed_web_41633645", "pubmed_web_41633620", "pubmed_web_41633425", "pubmed_web_41633376", "pubmed_web_41632932", "pubmed_web_41632717", "pubmed_web_41632705", "pu