{"topic": "Diabetes Mellitus", "competency": "Treatment", "stem": "In patients with chronic pancreatitis, what is the primary management approach to address pancreatic insufficiency?", "options": {"A": "Surgery to repair the pancreatic ductal system", "B": "Replacement of pancreatic enzymes and diet supplements", "C": "Insulin therapy to control blood glucose levels", "D": "Pain management with analgesics"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Chronic pancreatitis is most often a result of recurrent attacks of acute pancreatitis, leading to pancreatic destruction and resulting in diabetes and malassimilation. Management consists of replacement of pancreatic enzymes and diet supplements to address the pancreatic insufficiency.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0036_176", "title": "Pancreatic disease", "span_text": "Chronic pancreatitis is most often a result of recurrent attacks of acute pancreatitis. Diabetes and malassimilation become manifest as pancreatic destruction progresses. Management consists of replacement of pancreatic enzymes and diet supplements."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0036_176", "pubmed23n0041_3275", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3156"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0036_176", "pubmed23n0041_3275", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3156"], "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank"}, "verification": {"time": 50, "gate": {"pass": true, "failed_checks": [], "notes": []}, "attempt_history": [{"attempt": 1, "reason": "initial", "query": "Diabetes Mellitus Treatment treatment therapy drug drugs medication pharmacotherapy surgery surgical intervention management dose dosage administration prescription first-line second-line guideline protocol acute management long-term management", "evidence_top_k": 30, "candidate_count": 1, "selected_index": 1, "retrieval_ms": 6528.664332989138, "llm_ms": 1404.3066669837572, "verification_ms": 2367.605791980168, "extra_instructions": "", "retrieval_mode": "hybrid_rerank", "pu