{"topic": "Myocardial Infarction", "competency": "Etiology", "stem": "What is the primary mechanism by which Brilliant Blue G reduces the risk of myocardial infarction in rats?", "options": {"A": "By attenuating inflammation and fibrosis", "B": "By increasing the expression of P2X7 receptors", "C": "By promoting the formation of new coronary arteries", "D": "By reducing the levels of low-density lipoprotein cholesterol"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Brilliant Blue G has been shown to reduce the risk of myocardial infarction in rats by attenuating inflammation and fibrosis, which are key factors in the development of myocardial infarction.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41615556", "title": "Brilliant blue G enhances cardiac function and suppresses ventricular arrhythmias by attenuating inflammation and fibrosis after post-myocardial infarction in rats", "span_text": "BBG treatment significantly reduced ventricular tachycardia induction rates, shortened QT, QTc, and Tpeak-Tend intervals, and improved cardiac function, as evidenced by increased ejection fraction, fractional shortening, and cardiac output. Histological analyses revealed reduced inflammatory cell infiltration, necrosis, and collagen deposition in the MI + BBG group compared to MI groups."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "method": "keyword search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41635670", "pubmed_web_41633605", "pubmed_web_41632477", "pubmed_web_41631724", "pubmed_web_41631049", "pubmed_web_41630293", "pubmed_web_41629182", "pubmed_web_41629127", "pubmed_web_41628974", "pubmed_web_41628730", "pubmed_web_41625718", "pubmed_web_41625238", "pubmed_web_41621906", "pubmed_web_41621021", "pubmed_web_41621009", "pubmed_web_41620890", "pubmed_web_41620233", "pubmed_web_41618755", "pubmed_web_41617364", "pubmed_web_41617356", "pubmed_web_41617253", "pubmed_web_41615556", "pubmed_web_41614508", "pubmed_web_41614487", "pubmed_web_41614370", "pubmed_web_41611310"