{"topic": "Pneumonia", "competency": "Diagnosis", "stem": "What is the most common cause of pneumonia in pediatric patients with severe viral community-acquired pneumonia?", "options": {"A": "Streptococcus pneumoniae", "B": "Haemophilus influenzae", "C": "Adenovirus", "D": "Influenza A virus"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "The most common cause of pneumonia in pediatric patients with severe viral community-acquired pneumonia is adenovirus, as seen in the study where adenovirus predominated in both cohorts.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed_web", "doc_id": "pubmed_web_41630339", "title": "Association between adjunctive corticosteroid therapy and clinical outcomes in children with severe viral community-acquired pneumonia: A retrospective cohort study", "span_text": "Among 129 eligible children, 97 (75.2%) received CSs and 32 (24.8%) received standard therapy. Baseline characteristics demonstrated no significant differences (P > .05). The CS group exhibited significantly higher secondary infection rates (89.9% vs 75.0%, P = .038) and mortality (24.7% vs 6.3%, P = .023). Adenovirus predominated in both cohorts (CS: 50.5%, non-CS: 62.5%), followed by influenza A virus (CS: 37.1%, non-CS: 31.3%)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2024-02-20T14:30:00Z", "doc_ids": ["pubmed_web_41637075", "pubmed_web_41636344", "pubmed_web_41635840", "pubmed_web_41635827", "pubmed_web_41635718", "pubmed_web_41635177", "pubmed_web_41633747", "pubmed_web_41633725", "pubmed_web_41633397", "pubmed_web_41633328", "pubmed_web_41632630", "pubmed_web_41632202", "pubmed_web_41632143", "pubmed_web_41631845", "pubmed_web_41631341", "pubmed_web_41631168", "pubmed_web_41630819", "pubmed_web_41630718", "pubmed_web_41630680", "pubmed_web_41630570", "pubmed_web_41630414", "pubmed_web_41630339", "pubmed_web_41630268", "pubmed_web_41630101", "pubmed_web_41629804", "pubmed_web_41629492", "pubmed_web_41629372", "pubmed_web_41629286", "pubmed_web_41629153", "pubmed_web_41629119"], "evid