{"topic": "Stroke", "competency": "Pathophysiology", "stem": "A patient presents with symptoms of ischemic stroke. What is the role of plasminogen activator inhibitor in the pathophysiology of this condition?", "options": {"A": "It increases the risk of thrombotic events", "B": "It decreases the risk of thrombotic events", "C": "It has no effect on thrombotic events", "D": "It is not related to stroke pathophysiology"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Plasminogen activator inhibitor activity is significantly higher in patients with acute ischemic stroke, suggesting its involvement in the pathophysiology of the condition.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0053_3760", "title": "Involvement of lipid peroxidation in CNS injury", "span_text": "The generation of oxygen radicals and the process of lipid peroxidation have become a focus of attention for investigators in the fields of central nervous system (CNS) injury and stroke (e.g., ischemia)."}, {"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0063_20067", "title": "Plasminogen activator inhibitor in acute stroke", "span_text": "Plasminogen activator inhibitor activity was determined in patients (26 men, 6 women) with acute ischemic stroke (n = 28) and transient ischemic attack (TIA) (n = 4)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Neurology_Adams_6867", "Neurology_Adams_6131", "pubmed23n0050_18622", "pubmed23n0056_16328", "InternalMed_Harrison_3545", "Neurology_Adams_6873", "InternalMed_Harrison_29918", "pubmed23n0058_15052", "InternalMed_Harrison_9311", "pubmed23n0062_4069", "InternalMed_Harrison_20981", "pubmed23n0052_4336", "pubmed23n0042_5041", "pubmed23n0053_7070", "pubmed23n0052_2663", "InternalMed_Harrison_550", "pubmed23n0046_7573", "pubmed23n0054_7260", "InternalMed_Harrison_2242", "pubmed23n0046_13762", "InternalMed_Harrison_9290", "pubmed23n0045_8349", "pubmed23n0049_18948", "pubmed23n0063_20067", "Neurology_Adams_411", "Neurology_Adams_1357", "Obstentrics_Willi