{"topic": "Heart Failure", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A 60-year-old patient with heart failure and reduced ejection fraction is being treated with an ACE inhibitor. Which additional medication has been shown to decrease morbidity and mortality in patients with severe heart failure who are also receiving ACE inhibitors and other standard therapy?", "options": {"A": "Spironolactone", "B": "Furosemide", "C": "Metoprolol", "D": "Hydralazine"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The aldosterone antagonist diuretics, such as spironolactone, have been shown to decrease morbidity and mortality in patients with severe heart failure who are also receiving ACE inhibitors and other standard therapy.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_1293", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Spironolactone and eplerenone, the aldosterone (mineralocorticoid) antagonist diuretics (see Chapter 15), have the additional benefit of decreasing morbidity and mortality in patients with severe heart failure who are also receiving ACE inhibitors and other standard therapy."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_1248", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1244", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1269", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1302", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1833", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1324", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1301", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1592", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1847", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1304", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1265", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1290", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3469", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1475", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1320", "Pharmacology_Katzung_833", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3734", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1306", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1824", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1289", "Pharmacology_Katzung_979", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1465", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1880", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1479", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1432", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1260", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1279", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1293", "Pharmacology