{"topic": "Heart Failure", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A patient with heart failure is being treated with digoxin. What is the appropriate plasma digoxin level to aim for in this patient?", "options": {"A": "1 ng/mL or less", "B": "1.5 ng/mL or more", "C": "2 ng/mL or less", "D": "2.5 ng/mL or more"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "The appropriate plasma digoxin level to aim for in a patient with heart failure is 1 ng/mL or less, as levels higher than this may be associated with increased toxicity.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_1314", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Measurement of plasma digoxin levels is useful in patients who appear unusually resistant or sensitive; a level of 1 ng/mL or less is appropriate; higher levels may be required in patients with atrial fibrillation."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_1555", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2783", "Pharmacology_Katzung_347", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1314", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1472", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1322", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4435", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1846", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1204", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1007", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6565", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1594", "Pharmacology_Katzung_849", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1208", "pubmed23n0056_1248", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1591", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6631", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4548", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1412", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1333", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1399", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1558", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1057", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1443", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1586", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3956", "Pharmacology_Katzung_853", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1546", "pubmed23n0044_20769", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1471"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_347", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1314", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1472", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1322", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4435", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1846", "Pharmacology_Katzung_120