{"topic": "Tuberculosis", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is a key strategy for preventing the spread of tuberculosis in countries with high HIV and tuberculosis prevalence?", "options": {"A": "Improving cure rates through early diagnosis and treatment", "B": "Implementing mass vaccination campaigns with BCG", "C": "Enhancing health education in school collectives", "D": "Conducting regular mass x-ray examinations"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Strengthening tuberculosis control programmes, including improving cure rates through early diagnosis and treatment, is crucial for preventing the spread of tuberculosis in countries with high HIV and tuberculosis prevalence.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0043_6298", "title": "HIV-associated tuberculosis in developing countries: epidemiology and strategies for prevention", "span_text": "In order to respond to this urgent problem, the highest priority must be given to strengthening tuberculosis control programmes in the countries where they are poorly developed and where the prevalence of HIV and tuberculosis infections is high. Besides improving the cure rate by early diagnosis and prompt treatment of patients with tuberculosis, two major strategies that need consideration include BCG vaccination and preventive chemotherapy among HIV-infected individuals."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0049_19893", "pubmed23n0051_16508", "pubmed23n0061_10759", "Obstentrics_Williams_7083", "pubmed23n0055_1539", "pubmed23n0032_4038", "Obstentrics_Williams_7084", "pubmed23n0049_9825", "pubmed23n0060_7675", "pubmed23n0061_22427", "pubmed23n0059_19131", "pubmed23n0002_11683", "pubmed23n0049_8729", "pubmed23n0043_4471", "pubmed23n0053_7099", "pubmed23n0045_11645", "pubmed23n0011_10011", "pubmed23n0059_8624", "InternalMed_Harrison_13258", "pubmed23n0060_6694", "pubmed23n0048_6675", "pubmed23n0059_17812", "pubmed23n0048_14195", "pubmed23n0059_8637", "pubmed23n00