{"topic": "Tuberculosis", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the primary method for preventing tuberculosis in children, especially in areas with high tuberculosis prevalence?", "options": {"A": "BCG vaccination", "B": "Isoniazid prophylaxis", "C": "Streptomycin therapy", "D": "Improved ventilation"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "BCG vaccination is the primary method for preventing tuberculosis in children, especially in areas with high tuberculosis prevalence, as it provides protection against severe forms of tuberculosis, such as meningitis and miliary tuberculosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0052_15549", "title": "Impact of HIV infection on mycobacterial disease", "span_text": "Prevention of the transmission of disease is a major concern."}, {"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0022_5554", "title": "Current aspects and prospects of preventive pediatrics in France", "span_text": "It is assuming increasing importance in the detection and prevention of certain risk factors and common affections of the adult such as obesity, hypertension and atheroma."}, {"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0059_1931", "title": "Clinical backgrounds of six cases of childhood tuberculosis", "span_text": "BCG vaccination is important for the prevention of tuberculosis in children and that follow-up examinations should be continued after the completion of chemoprophylaxis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2022-01-01", "method": "database search", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_11242", "pubmed23n0052_15549", "pubmed23n0047_10966", "pubmed23n0016_1291", "InternalMed_Harrison_13451", "pubmed23n0013_10886", "pubmed23n0061_9788", "pubmed23n0049_18073", "pubmed23n0047_13926", "InternalMed_Harrison_988", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5282", "pubmed23n0022_5554", "pubmed23n0059_1931", "pubmed23n0034_3589", "pubmed23n0062_17613", "pubmed23n0058_14820", "pubmed23n0054_1874", "pubmed23n0026_6789", "pubmed23n0059_17350", "pubmed23n0058_113