{"topic": "Tuberculosis", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "A homeless person presents with a fever and a productive cough of more than 1-3 weeks' duration. What is the most appropriate initial step in managing this patient?", "options": {"A": "Initiate empiric antitubercular therapy", "B": "Perform a tuberculin skin test", "C": "Undertake appropriate diagnostic studies for tuberculosis", "D": "Provide symptomatic treatment only"}, "answer_key": "C", "explanation": "The patient's symptoms suggest tuberculosis, and diagnostic studies are necessary to confirm the diagnosis. This approach allows for appropriate management and prevention of further transmission.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0044_735", "title": "Prevention and control of tuberculosis among homeless persons. Recommendations of the Advisory Council for the Elimination of Tuberculosis", "span_text": "TB should be suspected in any homeless person with a fever and a productive cough of more than 1-3 weeks' duration, and appropriate diagnostic studies should be undertaken."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2023-02-20T14:30:00Z", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0058_14808", "pubmed23n0049_18063", "pubmed23n0027_9892", "pubmed23n0061_22423", "InternalMed_Harrison_13599", "Gynecology_Novak_719", "pubmed23n0052_15678", "pubmed23n0044_735", "pubmed23n0062_17620", "pubmed23n0060_20975", "pubmed23n0051_3597", "pubmed23n0013_5841", "pubmed23n0062_16393", "pubmed23n0051_8653", "pubmed23n0053_12232", "pubmed23n0047_12391", "pubmed23n0007_15596", "pubmed23n0061_11858", "pubmed23n0062_12061", "pubmed23n0059_8939", "pubmed23n0048_1237", "pubmed23n0055_329", "pubmed23n0062_12481", "pubmed23n0042_9089", "pubmed23n0039_11038", "pubmed23n0059_16815", "pubmed23n0014_12622", "pubmed23n0048_20395", "pubmed23n0004_13862", "pubmed23n0048_15841", "pubmed23n0061_5956", "pubmed23n0017_2067", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5203", "pubmed23n0044_23767", "pubmed23n0018_10746", "pubmed23n0063_17499", "pubmed23