{"topic": "Tuberculosis", "competency": "Prevention", "stem": "What is the significance of detecting lipoarabinomannan in human serum samples for the diagnosis of tuberculosis?", "options": {"A": "It has a high specificity but low sensitivity in patients with active pulmonary tuberculosis", "B": "It has a sensitivity of 88% in patients with sputum-smear-positive active pulmonary tuberculosis", "C": "It is only useful for diagnosing tuberculosis in patients with AIDS", "D": "It has no correlation with the presence of Mycobacterium tuberculosis"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "The detection of lipoarabinomannan is an accurate test for the diagnosis of pulmonary tuberculosis, with a sensitivity of 88% in patients with sputum-smear-positive active pulmonary tuberculosis.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0046_22257", "title": "Detection of lipoarabinomannan as a diagnostic test for tuberculosis", "span_text": "The test had a sensitivity of 88% in patients with sputum-smear-positive active pulmonary tuberculosis."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0061_5956", "pubmed23n0044_23767", "pubmed23n0017_2067", "pubmed23n0018_10746", "pubmed23n0044_6742", "pubmed23n0018_10600", "pubmed23n0048_2874", "pubmed23n0063_17499", "pubmed23n0026_11189", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5203", "pubmed23n0027_1721", "pubmed23n0044_23495", "pubmed23n0031_6230", "pubmed23n0022_3225", "pubmed23n0048_4655", "pubmed23n0046_22257", "pubmed23n0015_3230", "pubmed23n0059_14959", "pubmed23n0011_3267", "pubmed23n0049_12876", "pubmed23n0057_20568", "pubmed23n0051_16759", "pubmed23n0043_6308", "pubmed23n0047_7767", "pubmed23n0054_7506", "Pediatrics_Nelson_2605", "pubmed23n0043_6711", "pubmed23n0014_9193", "pubmed23n0059_5777", "pubmed23n0056_21297"], "evidence_doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0063_17499", "pubmed23n0026_11189", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5203", "pubmed23n0027_1721", "pubmed23n0044_23495", "pubmed23n0031_6230", "pubmed23n0022_3225", "pubmed23n00