{"topic": "Atrial Fibrillation", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "A 75-year-old patient with a history of hypertension and nonvalvular atrial fibrillation presents with symptoms of a transient ischemic attack. What is the most significant independent risk factor for systemic embolism in this patient?", "options": {"A": "Left atrial enlargement", "B": "History of coronary artery disease", "C": "Presence of intracardiac thrombi", "D": "Age greater than 70 years"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Left atrial enlargement is a significant independent risk factor for systemic embolism in patients with nonvalvular atrial fibrillation, as it increases the risk of thrombus formation and subsequent embolism.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0054_1577", "title": "Risk factors for systemic embolism in patients with paroxysmal atrial fibrillation", "span_text": "Multiple stepwise logistic regression analysis showed that a history of hypertension and left atrial enlargement on two-dimensional echocardiography were significant independent risk factors for systemic embolism in patients with symptomatic nonvalvular paroxysmal atrial fibrillation."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2023-02-20T14:30:00Z", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0064_377", "pubmed23n0050_18166", "pubmed23n0046_10302", "pubmed23n0037_8656", "pubmed23n0057_854", "pubmed23n0016_125", "pubmed23n0063_20466", "pubmed23n0030_7206", "pubmed23n0017_1015", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1480", "pubmed23n0005_11377", "pubmed23n0062_9052", "pubmed23n0043_12237", "pubmed23n0054_1577", "pubmed23n0058_2113", "pubmed23n0054_3081", "pubmed23n0016_5495", "pubmed23n0056_21706", "pubmed23n0063_15945", "Neurology_Adams_6391", "pubmed23n0019_11942", "pubmed23n0061_7781", "pubmed23n0005_10372", "pubmed23n0027_9496", "pubmed23n0045_4826", "pubmed23n0047_16762", "pubmed23n0005_7381", "pubmed23n0053_12075", "InternalMed_Harrison_18040", "InternalMed_Harrison_18041", "pubmed23n0004_1739", "Surgery_Schwartz