{"topic": "Atrial Fibrillation", "competency": "Complications", "stem": "A patient with atrial fibrillation undergoes transesophageal echocardiography, which reveals left atrial spontaneous echo contrast. What is the clinical significance of this finding?", "options": {"A": "It is a marker of previous thromboembolism in patients with nonvalvular atrial fibrillation", "B": "It is a sign of left ventricular dysfunction", "C": "It is a normal finding in patients with atrial fibrillation", "D": "It is a contraindication for anticoagulant therapy"}, "answer_key": "A", "explanation": "Left atrial spontaneous echo contrast is a marker of blood stasis in the left atrium and is associated with an increased risk of thromboembolism in patients with atrial fibrillation.", "evidence": [{"source": "pubmed", "doc_id": "pubmed23n0062_1992", "title": "Left atrial spontaneous echo contrast: a clinical and echocardiographic analysis", "span_text": "Multivariate analysis in 89 patients with mitral stenosis or mitral valve replacement showed that spontaneous echo contrast was the only independent predictor (p = 0.03) of left atrial thrombus or suspected embolism, or both. In 60 patients with atrial fibrillation of nonvalvular origin, spontaneous echo contrast (p = 0.01) and age (p = 0.03) were the only independent predictors of left atrial thrombus or suspected embolism, or both."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": "2023-02-20T14:30:00Z", "doc_ids": ["pubmed23n0018_9253", "pubmed23n0050_11439", "pubmed23n0029_5006", "pubmed23n0041_11033", "pubmed23n0015_2196", "pubmed23n0021_10087", "pubmed23n0049_607", "pubmed23n0022_10620", "pubmed23n0039_6914", "pubmed23n0021_10990", "pubmed23n0045_18925", "pubmed23n0042_2087", "pubmed23n0062_1992", "pubmed23n0047_1299", "pubmed23n0041_9060", "pubmed23n0038_3725", "pubmed23n0058_16222", "pubmed23n0024_1351", "pubmed23n0047_15369", "pubmed23n0054_17051", "pubmed23n0021_6764", "pubmed23n0045_497", "pubmed23n0049_2389", "pubmed23n0062_154