{"topic": "Depression", "competency": "Pharmacology", "stem": "A 40-year-old patient with bipolar depression is prescribed an antipsychotic. Which of the following antipsychotics is approved by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for the management of bipolar depression?", "options": {"A": "Haloperidol", "B": "Quetiapine", "C": "Risperidone", "D": "Ziprasidone"}, "answer_key": "B", "explanation": "Quetiapine is an antipsychotic that is approved by the FDA for the management of bipolar depression. It is often used as a monotherapy or in combination with other medications to treat depressive episodes in patients with bipolar disorder.", "evidence": [{"source": "textbook", "doc_id": "Pharmacology_Katzung_3148", "title": "Pharmacology_Katzung", "span_text": "Several antipsychotics are now approved by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) in the management of bipolar depression including quetiapine, lurasidone, and olanzapine (in a combination formulation with fluoxetine)."}], "status": "OK", "meta": {"retrieval": {"time": 100, "doc_ids": ["Pharmacology_Katzung_3295", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3318", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6528", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3221", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3273", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2676", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4546", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4367", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2321", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2342", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2674", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3446", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3255", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3246", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3269", "Pharmacology_Katzung_945", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3521", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3249", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2598", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3206", "Pharmacology_Katzung_5453", "Pharmacology_Katzung_1218", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3204", "Pharmacology_Katzung_6764", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3148", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2728", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4400", "Pharmacology_Katzung_2615", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3457", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4576", "Pharmacology_Katzung_3205", "Pharmacology_Katzung_4217", "Pharmacolog